9e","turn_id":"01a16fd6-d88e-7ad0-8956-d61230292d9e","turn_trigger":"goal"}},"retained_context":{"assistant_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016add24539a3c81a09f8d70bd6149b484","order":15670,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a16fd5-e920-74c3-bc97-d41e8ddf08e3","text":"Independent review has now accepted exact commit `ca2865f`: it confirmed that headless egress guidance requires `--yes`, while `--mode auto` remains available for write/exec actions, matching first-use egress prompts. I’m recording the review and checking the requirements gate so the source change’s evidence is accurately represented before handoff for integration.","turn_id":"01a16fcf-b1ad-74b3-9cfe-da9de5b26c39"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016add2483560481a0852a567964bb8350","order":15671,"phase":"final_answer","revision":"retained_01a16fd6-a653-73a1-8778-0164ec06a614","text":"Implemented the startup trust and approval behavior in isolated branch `codex/startup-folder-trust-copy`, commit `ca2865f`.\n\nFolder trust stays separate from tool approvals, and the default approval mode is **review**. In headless mode, egress denials now explain the `--yes` opt-in; `--mode auto` remains guidance for write and exec actions.\n\n**Verification:** 38 focused tests passed, TypeScript check and build passed, and independent review accepted the exact commit. The requirements gate still fails on `REQ-SEC-101` and `REQ-SEC-119`, both marked partial; I left those statuses unchanged.\n\nThe branch is ready for owner integration, but it is not yet on `main`. I did not push it, per the repository’s owner-only push instruction. Nexus acceptance remains **IN_PROGRESS**; no accepted RC or completed release is claimed.","turn_id":"01a16fcf-b1ad-74b3-9cfe-da9de5b26c39"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016add249647e481a097bcded41d4c192f","order":15672,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a16fd6-ed61-7063-8e65-0b9489b68692","text":"This slice has passed independent review, so I’m moving it toward integration rather than leaving it parked. I’ll first refresh `main`, claims, and any active suite ownership, then use the approved PR path if the branch is still based on current `main`; I’ll preserve the dirty shared checkout.","turn_id":"01a16fd6-d88e-7ad0-8956-d61230292d9e"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016add24dde5e481a08140fd9590d5c904","order":15673,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a16fd8-0627-7831-8fce-b2f024fac686","text":"The current `SUITE` lock points to an orphaned full test run: its parent agent is gone, and the exact test process has been idle for over 30 minutes with zero CPU. Project rules prohibit overlapping local tests, and the run has no matching work claim or retained result. I’m recording it as incomplete and clearing only that isolated test process group under your stalled-lane takeover authorization; then I can run this candidate’s full suite without overlap.","turn_id":"01a16fd6-d88e-7ad0-8956-d61230292d9e"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016add24f343dc81a0803b0b9c8dcb627b","order":15674,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a16fd8-5a73-7981-9bd6-3b95b5038d7a","text":"I found the orphan was stuck in `tui_approval_input_e2e.test.ts` with no test timeout, so its run is recorded as **interrupted**, not passed or failed. I ended only that abandoned test process group. This frees the exclusive test lane; I’m now checking whether the two partial security requirements can be evidenced by existing trusted/untrusted and review/auto tests, or whether acceptance coverage is still missing.","turn_id":"01a16fd6-d88e-7ad0-8956-d61230292d9e"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016add25b4dae881a0955dff3bd2befb21","order":15675,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a16fdb-4d95-7a52-adf6-25114b9b80c8","text":"The amended ledger still shows these as partial because their source evidence had not yet been recorded against the new behavior. The focused suite already exercises trust-independent mode selection, verifier approval, and egress denial. I’m adding one explicit trusted/untrusted default-mode regression, then I’ll update the ledger only if the exact tests and enforcement check support “tested”; installed-RC acceptance remains a separate pending gate.","turn_id":"01a16fd6-d88e-7ad0-8956-d61230292d9e"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016add26267e9c81a09ae334c88d5f969d","order":15676,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a16fdd-0959-7cc0-98ad-fc08a043c707","text":"The new trusted/untrusted regression passes, and TypeScript checking is clean. The enforcement checker now confirms the two remaining source rows by name and keeps them partial; it fails on those rows (and on the deliberately uncommitted tree), so I’m not overstating the PTY acceptance that remains. I’m recording that evidence in a small commit, then I’ll request another review of the updated ledger/test slice.","turn_id":"01a16fd6-d88e-7ad0-8956-d61230292d9e"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016add265d313481a0a16f6a7fac16340c","order":15681,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a16fdd-ddee-7f82-bd45-6e5cdecbf114","text":"The reviewer accepted the behavior and agreed the two requirements should remain partial, but found one ledger citation that didn’t support the verifier-specific claim. I’m adding the actual trusted/untrusted verifier prompt test reference, then I’ll recheck the ledger and send the corrected exact revision for review.","turn_id":"01a16fd6-d88e-7ad0-8956-d61230292d9e"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":15682,"sender_deliveries":[{"order":7850,"receiver_message_id":"fco_01a15e0d-46de-72f1-8e85-967b05e2dfc6","receiver_turn_id":"01a15e0b-8f5d-7b40-aa6b-62735e71e8a0","text":"\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES START\nReceived message: fco_01a15e0d-46de-72f1-8e85-967b05e2dfc6\nSource thread: 01a139bf-d0bf-74e0-b969-dd59f0