{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T21:44:21.100Z","ordinal":311124,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a16fdf-336c-7d61-b9d8-528e2157651f","call_id":"call_ed4877fdb88140dd87c0f42c186b6789","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/context_rc_gate_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Recorded the independent **ACCEPT** for `dfb3880d43fb2ba5574c8ac42221cfe4d138fe59`, archived the claim records, and released the slice and test-file claims. `SUITE` is free. No push or merge was performed.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"No change since the prior check at `origin/main@be2cd2f255414f554572c86baa884d9271ff5ea1`: Issue #1 still ends with coordinator comment #6378649211, with no custodian acknowledgment or handoff. PR #16 remains closed with no new custody acceptance, and current claims show no held-out author/custodian owner.\\n\\nThe manifests and historical attestations are unchanged. Qualification remains blocked pending explicit independent custodian ownership and acceptance, plus a custodian-approved T2 compatibility or supersession path. No files or private material were accessed.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — reviewed HEAD `7a43b262975b227b4fb5e0339ab86d2faba60f2b` against base `4b474f1638645258fc6bc696400892feaf3a78d6`. Diff SHA-256: `10be0970043e7a2a17413ce5134ffa12c88232cef7e787a0512fc7a7c73a3730`.\\n\\nThe new trusted/untrusted regression supports REQ-SEC-101’s source behavior, and keeping both REQ-SEC-101 and REQ-SEC-119 **partial** is accurate while their PTY acceptance checks remain pending. The overall trust/approval change is consistent with review-by-default, trust-independent approvals, and the effect-specific headless guidance.\\n\\nOne evidence citation needs correction: [REQUIREMENTS.md:122](/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-folder-trust-copy/docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:122) claims that folder trust alone does not authorize verifier execution. Its cited “folder trust alone keeps an unset permission mode in review” test checks `getApprovalMode()` and denies command/egress calls, but does not exercise verifier execution. The verifier test file does contain trusted and untrusted review-mode cases that prompt before running the verifier and show its script body ([verifier_gating.test.ts:85-141](/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-folder-trust-copy/cli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts:85)); add that test to the row’s evidence.\\n\\nNo tests were run during this review.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16fd6-d88e-7ad0-8956-d61230292d9e","create_time":1792878261.1007457}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
