{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T21:44:43.434Z","ordinal":311149,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a16fdf-8aaa-70c2-a7c0-460c138f1604","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — reviewed HEAD `7ab14b3944919b6fed0cb3553dc816cc548bbd6c` against base `4b474f1638645258fc6bc696400892feaf3a78d6`. Diff SHA-256: `b1e1b501a5fbc1e5b21f197957cb6a69cc2b5ef864e54659c6fbf224d133c10b`.\n\nThe SEC-119 evidence now points to the trusted/untrusted review-mode verifier coverage, and the requirement remains correctly **partial** while PTY ACC-SAFE-09/10 checks are pending. However, the cited test name in [`REQUIREMENTS.md:122`](/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-folder-trust-copy/docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:122) is not an exact test title: the parameterized cases are named **“trusted repo in review mode prompts…”** and **“untrusted repo in review mode prompts…”** in [`verifier_gating.test.ts:85-86`](/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-folder-trust-copy/cli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts:85). Please cite those exact cases, or clearly label the citation as their shared name pattern. No tests were run for this review."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16fd6-d88e-7ad0-8956-d61230292d9e","create_time":1792878283.434567}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":15687}}
