{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T21:44:53.768Z","ordinal":311163,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16fd6-d88e-7ad0-8956-d61230292d9e","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-86b2db65-9fe7-4fba-8863-700752f1ee95","process_id":"8901","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '80,142p' cli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts && git diff --check && git diff -- docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md && git log -5 --oneline"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-folder-trust-copy","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '80,142p' cli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts && git diff --check && git diff -- docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md && git log -5 --oneline"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"    } finally {\n      fs.rmSync(ws, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  });\n\n  for (const trusted of [false, true]) {\n    test(`${trusted ? \"trusted\" : \"untrusted\"} repo in review mode prompts for verifier and script body, writes sentinel only after approval, and caches session decision`, async () => {\n    const savedHome = process.env.HOME;\n    const tempHome = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-vg-home-\"));\n    process.env.HOME = tempHome;\n\n    const { ws, sentinelPath } = setupRepo(`review-${trusted ? \"trusted\" : \"untrusted\"}`);\n    if (trusted) setWorkspaceTrusted(ws, true);\n    const replies = [\n      {\n        kind: \"tools\" as const,\n        calls: [{ name: \"edit_file\", args: { path: \"file.txt\", old_content: \"hello\\n\", new_content: \"world\\n\" } }],\n      },\n      {\n        kind: \"tools\" as const,\n        calls: [{ name: \"task_completed\", args: { summary: \"Finished editing file\" } }],\n      },\n      { kind: \"text\" as const, content: \"Done.\" },\n    ];\n    const gw = await startGateway((n) => replies[Math.min(n, replies.length) - 1]);\n    const agent = new AutonomousAgent({\n      endpoint: gw.url,\n      model: \"m\",\n      workspace: ws,\n      shell: \"bash\",\n      approvalMode: \"review\",\n    } as any);\n\n    const promptLog: Array<{ tool: string; args: any }> = [];\n    try {\n      assert.equal(isWorkspaceTrusted(ws), trusted, `repo trust should be ${trusted}`);\n\n      await agent.runTurn(\"make changes and finish\", async (tool, args) => {\n        promptLog.push({ tool, args });\n        if (tool === \"edit_file\") {\n          // Sentinel must NOT be written before verifier is approved!\n          assert.equal(fs.existsSync(sentinelPath), false, \"sentinel must not exist when edit_file is prompted\");\n          return true;\n        }\n        if (tool === \"verifier\") {\n          // Sentinel must NOT be written before operator confirms verifier!\n          assert.equal(fs.existsSync(sentinelPath), false, \"sentinel must not exist before verifier is confirmed\");\n          assert.equal(args.command, \"npm test\");\n          assert.equal(args.script, \"node test.js\");\n          assert.equal(args.detail, \"package.json:scripts.test\");\n          assert.ok(args.digest, \"digest must be provided\");\n          return true;\n        }\n        return true;\n      });\n\n      // Sentinel was written by the approved verifier execution!\n      assert.equal(fs.existsSync(sentinelPath), true, \"sentinel must be written after verifier was approved and executed\");\n\n      // Verifier should be prompted exactly once because session caching applies\n      const verifierPrompts = promptLog.filter((p) => p.tool === \"verifier\");\n      assert.equal(verifierPrompts.length, 1, \"verifier should only be prompted once during the session\");\n    } finally {\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md b/docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md\nindex be27f5d..258e4b8 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md\n@@ -119,7 +119,7 @@ Every row has status **open** at `db1ca55` unless stated otherwise. In the \"Evid\n | REQ-SEC-101 | Audit; DEC-01 (amended 2026-10-24) | Without operator opt-in, model-initiated exec and egress require the configured permission decision. Folder trust does not select or change approval mode; unset mode defaults to review. | safety | `config.ts`, `sidecar.ts`, `repl.ts`, `index.ts`, `core/approval_policy.ts` | TEST `test:cli/test/approval_policy.test.ts::\"REQ-SEC-101: the unset mode stays review in trusted and untrusted workspaces\"`; `test:cli/test/config.test.ts::\"workspace trust does not select the tool approval mode\"`; PTY ACC-SAFE-01 still pending | partial | ACC-SAFE-01 | **B** | SEC-01, TUI-07 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\n | REQ-SEC-102 | Audit; TOP_TIER B1 | Every capability has an effect class. Review gates every class except read. The gate is enforced at dispatch from the registry. | safety | `core/capabilities.ts`, `agent.ts:3945` | TEST `approval_policy.test.ts` | tested | ACC-SAFE-02 | **B** | HIST-05, SEC-03 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\n | REQ-SEC-103 | Audit | No approval is decided by Enter alone, typed-ahead input, paste, or input inside the grace window, on any surface. | safety | `repl.ts:291-355,444-495`, `tui_approval_input_e2e.test.ts`, `repl_approval_e2e.test.ts` | PTY (ACC-SAFE-03, ACC-SAFE-08) | tested | ACC-SAFE-03, ACC-SAFE-08 | **B** | TUI-02, TUI-03 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\n-| REQ-SEC-119 | Audit; DEC-01 (amended 2026-10-24) | Nexus-initiated verifier runs are `exec` class and follow configured permission mode; review requires a one-time approval showing the script body. Folder trust alone does not authorize execution; all runs are routed through the runner. | safety | `agent.ts:1654,3544,4255`; `tester.ts:145`; `verifier_gating.test.ts` | TEST `test:cli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts::\"repo in review mode prompts for verifier and script body, writes sentinel only after approval, and caches session decision\"`; `test:cli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts::\"denied verifier does not execute verifier and sentinel is not written\"`; `test:cli/test/harness.test.ts::\"run