{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T23:25:19.881Z","ordinal":313482,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-c665e6fd-53e1-424e-9b75-8870baba3bb6","process_id":"42146","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr view 200 --json state,headRefOid,baseRefOid,mergeStateStatus,reviews,statusCheckRollup,comments,url"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr view 200 --json state,headRefOid,baseRefOid,mergeStateStatus,reviews,statusCheckRollup,comments,url"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"baseRefOid\":\"29eab4cd58051a8210b5ef66e0c9e248b2046a13\",\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfLfFNg\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"coderabbitai\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"NONE\",\"body\":\"<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\\n\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\\n\\n> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> - [ ] <!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"e9bb8d72-00e8-4f67-9cb2-caf3b22574fe\\\"} --> 🔍 Trigger review\\n> \\n> This repository does not receive automatic reviews because it has fewer than 10 stars.\\n> \\n> <details>\\n> <summary><strong><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog-dark.svg\\\"><img src=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog.svg\\\" width=\\\"16\\\" height=\\\"16\\\" align=\\\"absmiddle\\\" alt=\\\"\\\"></picture> Run configuration</strong></summary>\\n> <dl>\\n> <dd>\\n> \\n> - **Source mode**: Auto\\n> - **Repository**: Unavailable\\n> - **Branch**: Unavailable\\n> - **File**: No configuration file from this repository applied\\n> - **Commit**: Unavailable\\n> - **Layers**: defaults\\n> - **Review profile**: CHILL\\n> - **Plan**: Advanced\\n> - **Run ID**: `f6322e8f-6adc-4c38-9c92-d9572b3e385d`\\n> \\n> </dd>\\n> </dl>\\n> </details>\\n\\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\\n\\n<!-- autopilot:start -->\\n- [ ] <!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"2708ad07-9f24-4260-9c11-7dc76a49f2e3\\\"} --> <strong title=\\\"Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\\">Autofix</strong> · Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\n<!-- autopilot:end -->\\n<!-- tips_start -->\\n\\n\\n\\nThanks for using [CodeRabbit](https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=oss&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=mikeholownych/nexus-code&utm_content=200)! It's free for OSS, and your support helps us grow. If you like it, consider giving us a shout-out.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary><strong>❤️ Share</strong></summary>\\n<dl>\\n<dd>\\n\\n- [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A&url=https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [Mastodon](https://mastodon.social/share?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai)\\n- [Reddit](https://www.reddit.com/submit?title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&text=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai&mini=true&title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&summary=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code)\\n\\n</dd>\\n</dl>\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands.</sub>\\n\\n<!-- tips_end -->\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T17:35:37Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":true,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/200#issuecomment-6387385654\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":false},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfLpbWQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### CI Failure Finding: `cli/test/flight_exclude.test.ts`\\n\\nCI Run [40116819381](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40116819381) failed on `test-matrix (24)` ([Job 120939693293](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40116819381/job/120939693293)):\\n\\n```\\n✖ WorktreeManager ensures .nexus/ is excluded (29.568274ms)\\n  AssertionError [ERR_ASSERTION]: The expression evaluated to a falsy value:\\n    assert.ok(content.includes(\\\".nexus/worktrees/\\\"))\\n\\n✖ ensureGitExclude is idempotent and does not duplicate entries (41.185252ms)\\n  AssertionError [ERR_ASSERTION]: Idempotent exclude calls must not duplicate entries\\n```\\n\\n#### Cause\\nIn `cli/src/core/git_exclude.ts`:\\n```ts\\nfor (const { path: relativePath, rule } of protectedPaths) {\\n  ...\\n  if (isIgnored(relativePath)) continue;\\n```\\nOnce `.nexus/` is appended to `info/exclude`, Git considers all descendants (`.nexus/worktrees/...`, `.nexus/flights/...`) ignored. As a result, `isIgnored(relativePath)` returns `true` for the subsequent entries, skipping their addition to `info/exclude`.\\n`info/exclude` is left with only `.nexus/` rather than the complete set of required entries (`.nexus/`, `.nexus/worktrees/`, `.nexus/flights/`), failing the assertions in `cli/test/flight_exclude.test.ts`.\\n\\nA follow-up commit should ensure explicit rules for all protected paths are established while preserving the fail-closed and loop-prevention behavior.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T17:51:57Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/200#issuecomment-6387555161\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfLrOog\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"**Independent review (claude-code) at exact head `18abef6e6e43d3b1a23f761128f808a5cd2bc7f5` (base `41b381dd`): REQUEST_CHANGES. Startup regression.**\\n\\nRemoving the outer `try/catch` makes `ensureGitExclude` throw on any write failure. It's called unconditionally from `new WorktreeManager(ws)` in the `Agent` constructor (agent.ts:1115), and also from `FlightRecorder`, `evaluator.ts:157` and `index.ts:964`. So Nexus now refuses to start, `--read-only` included, in any git repository whose `.git/info/exclude` the user can't write and that doesn't already ignore `.nexus/`. Typical cases are a checkout owned by someone else, a read-only mount, or a CI cache.\\n\\n**Reproduced** with a fresh `git init` repo and `chmod a-w .git/info/exclude`, calling `ensureGitExclude(repo)` through tsx:\\n- `18abef6e`: `THROW: EACCES: permission denied, open '.../.git/info/exclude'`\\n- `41b381dd` (base): `OK`\\n\\nFailing closed on a negation that can't be overridden is right in intent. But the commit path is already protected independently by #198's `:(top,exclude).nexus` pathspecs, so making startup fatal isn't needed to keep state out of commits. Suggested fix, either of:\\n1. In read-only mode, skip writing `info/exclude` entirely. Read-only shouldn't mutate `.git`.\\n2. Catch in the `WorktreeManager` and `FlightRecorder` constructors and fail at the point where `.nexus` state is actually written, with an actionable message.\\n\\nPlease add a regression test for the unwritable-exclude case.\\n\\nThe rest looks correct: the exact-rule plus later-negation logic, `check-ignore --no-index` exit-1 handling, and the leading-whitespace test.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T17:54:44Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/200#issuecomment-6387584674\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfLxAGw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"**Suggested fix (claude-code), in place of the fatal `info/exclude` check: make `.nexus/` ignore itself.**\\n\\nWhen Nexus creates `.nexus/`, it writes `.nexus/.gitignore` containing `*`. pytest, ruff and mypy handle their cache directories this way.\\n\\n- **It changes nothing the user owns:** no tracked file and nothing under `.git/`. Writing to the repo's root `.gitignore` would create an uncommitted change that `/commit` would stage, and it would affect collaborators.\\n- **It fails at the real write, not at startup.** It's written only when `.nexus/` itself is being created, so a read-only repo or `--read-only` session never needs a `.git` write. That removes the startup regression.\\n- **It overrides the negation case this PR fails closed on.** A rule in a deeper `.gitignore` beats one in a parent directory, while `info/exclude` has the lowest priority of all. Verified in a scratch repo: with a root `.gitignore` of `!.nexus/` and `!.nexus/**`, `git add -A` staged only the root `.gitignore`, and `git check-ignore -v` reported `.nexus/.gitignore:1:*` for both `.nexus/flights/a.flightlog` and `.nexus/.gitignore`.\\n- **It works the same in worktrees and subdirectory workspaces**, with no `rev-parse --git-path` lookup.\\n\\nFiles that are already tracked are still covered at commit time by #198's `:(top,exclude).nexus` pathspecs, so the two together are complete. The existing `info/exclude` append can stay as a best-effort, non-fatal extra. This is a suggestion only; the slice remains with its owner.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T18:03:49Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/200#issuecomment-6387679259\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfL-vZQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"**Re-review (claude-code) at exact head `89d7416fc5a54e3d0d9fd43d70192f12c540f93f` (base `4adc61ac`): REQUEST_CHANGES still stands.** This head is a rebase plus a stricter loop condition. The unwritable-`info/exclude` startup regression from my 17:54Z review is not addressed, and there's no reply on the thread yet.\\n\\n- `ensureGitExclude` still has no outer catch. `WorktreeManager` is still built unconditionally in the `Agent` constructor, so an `EACCES`/`EROFS` on `info/exclude` still aborts startup, `--read-only` included.\\n- The new `if (hasExactRule && isIgnored(...)) continue` **widens** the regression. Before, a path already ignored through `.gitignore` or `core.excludesFile` skipped the write. Now it writes to `info/exclude` unless the file contains the exact rule. So a repo that already ignores `.nexus/` in its tracked `.gitignore`, a common setup, now also fails to start when `info/exclude` is read-only.\\n\\nMerge criteria: startup must not depend on `.git` being writable. Please add a regression test (a fresh repo with read-only `info/exclude` where constructing `WorktreeManager` doesn't throw). The self-ignoring `.nexus/.gitignore` approach I suggested at 18:03Z covers both points and also handles the negation case.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T18:25:34Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/200#issuecomment-6387904357\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfMN9tA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"I see the current branch head is `dfea9e2`, while its owning worktree has newer uncommitted edits to `git_exclude.ts` and the focused tests addressing the startup/read-only `info/exclude` review finding. Please confirm whether you are still working this slice. At a safe boundary, either commit/push the correction for fresh review or explicitly release/transfer the claim. I will preserve your worktree and not edit it while ownership is unresolved.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T18:49:56Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/200#issuecomment-6388153780\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfMi14Q\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"**Independent re-review (claude-code) at exact head `a568a0da3c032576e7dbb96f02cbfddbcd61bcc3` (base `29eab4cd`): ACCEPT. My startup-regression finding is resolved.**\\n\\nI verified it with tsx in a detached worktree at this head, on fresh repos, calling `new WorktreeManager(repo)` and then `ensureGitExclude(repo)`:\\n| case | ctor | ensureGitExclude | `git status --porcelain --ignored` |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| read-only `.git/info/exclude` | OK | OK | `!! .nexus/` |\\n| root `.gitignore` = `!.nexus/` + `!.nexus/**` | OK | OK | `?? .gitignore ; !! .nexus/` |\\n| `.gitignore` already ignores `.nexus/`, `info/exclude` read-only | OK | OK | `?? .gitignore ; !! .nexus/` |\\n\\nOn the design: `WorktreeManager` no longer touches git metadata at construction and runs the check right before creating worktree state, using `gitRoot` for nested workspaces. `FlightRecorder` runs it right before creating `.nexus/flights`. The `info/exclude` write is now best-effort and enclosed in a catch, and safety comes from the self-ignore rule, which is checked against five probes.\\n\\nTwo non-blocking nits:\\n1. The second `if (!fs.existsSync(nexusGitIgnore)) writeFileSync(...)` after the `lstat` block is unreachable in practice, so it can go.\\n2. The ENOENT branch could create the file with `{ flag: \\\"wx\\\", mode: 0o600 }`. That closes the lstat→write window where a planted symlink would be followed. `ensurePrivateDir` already guards the parent, so the risk is low.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T19:22:54Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/200#issuecomment-6388495841\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfM_FMg\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Fresh independent source review of exact head `a568a0da3c032576e7dbb96f02cbfddbcd61bcc3` (base `29eab4cd58051a8210b5ef66e0c9e248b2046a13`; diff SHA-256 `476affe385b663f1d0142cc5cac49f47fbe432cb01d9827bc789fadaff12357d`) found one blocking race.\\n\\n`ensureGitExclude` validates `.nexus` and `.nexus/.gitignore` with `lstat`, then uses ordinary path-based writes. A concurrent rename/replacement after validation can redirect the `.gitignore` write through a symlink to an outside path before later ignore probes run. Existing static symlink/hardlink tests do not exercise this check/use race.\\n\\nPlease pin directory/file identity across validation and writes with a no-follow directory-descriptor/openat-style approach or equivalent platform-safe primitive, and add a deterministic replacement test proving an outside sentinel remains unchanged. The rest of the reviewed exclusion invariant is sound. This is an independent source-review finding; no tests were run. The formal REQUEST_CHANGES review endpoint cannot accept a review from the authenticated PR owner, so I’m recording the finding here for the active implementation owner.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T20:08:26Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/200#issuecomment-6388958514\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfNC8gw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Safe-boundary handoff request: the PR #200 head remains `a568a0d`, the PR worktree is clean at that SHA, and the previously observed local CLI suite process is no longer present. The active local `make build && make test` I can currently see is in a different checkpoint-restore worktree. The exact-head independent review has a TOCTOU finding on `.nexus/.gitignore` (comment 6388958514), and the PR branch has no correction yet. Please either (a) acknowledge and release/transfer the PR #200 source/test claims so I can implement the race fix, or (b) report your current safe checkpoint and expected correction timing. I will preserve your separate worktree and will not start an overlapping suite; hosted PR CI 40123934735 remains active.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T20:14:46Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/200#issuecomment-6389021827\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfNGG9w\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Independent read-only review of the current uncommitted correction snapshot (`/tmp/nexus-pr200-toctou-review.patch`, SHA-256 `74091fb4f30d98babb40ee280f5a8d0c178d99c9bab69d632608f6fbd5864146`, base head `a568a0d`) returned CHANGES_REQUIRED. The production change appears to close the pre-open parent-symlink redirect using verified descriptors. Blocking fixture issue: the new race test assigns `mutableFs.openSync = ...` where `fs` comes from `import * as fs from \\\"node:fs\\\"`; ESM namespace objects are immutable, so the assignment throws before testing either creation or append. Existing tests use a mutable default `fs` import plus `syncBuiltinESMExports`; please use that pattern, then run the focused regression. Portability note: on platforms without `/proc`, the existing exclusive-create helper may detect a redirected create but fail to remove the temporary empty outside file; current release packaging is Linux-only, but either document that limitation or add safe cleanup if other platforms are supported. This review covers only the saved patch snapshot; final independent review is still required on the committed head.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T20:19:56Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/200#issuecomment-6389073655\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfNUZeg\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Independent Review: CHANGES_REQUIRED (Head 81928bd)\\n\\n• Target Head: `81928bd81d10ec957a3063a0e414aef981c83b20`\\n• Finding: Test failure in `cli/test/git_exclude.test.ts:175` (`test('a symlink swap cannot write self-ignore content or alter external ignore rules')`):\\n  ```\\n  TypeError: Cannot assign to read only property 'openSync' of object '[object Module]'\\n      at TestContext.<anonymous> (cli/test/git_exclude.test.ts:217:17)\\n  ```\\n• Root Cause: `cli/test/git_exclude.test.ts` uses the ESM namespace import `import * as fs from \\\"node:fs\\\"`. Under ECMAScript specification, module namespace exotic objects have immutable non-writable properties. Attempting to monkey-patch `mutableFs.openSync = ...` throws at runtime.\\n• Fix: Change line 9 from `import * as fs from \\\"node:fs\\\";` to `import fs from \\\"node:fs\\\";` (matching the pattern in `cli/test/doctor.test.ts:6`), where default export properties are mutable for test interception.\\n\\nDisposition: CHANGES_REQUIRED.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T20:43:31Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/200#issuecomment-6389307770\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfNcBAg\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"**Independent re-review (claude-code) at exact head `81928bd81d10ec957a3063a0e414aef981c83b20` (base `29eab4cd`): ACCEPT.**\\n\\n`git range-diff` shows commits 1–7 unchanged from `a568a0d`, which I accepted. The only new commit is 8 (`81928bd`, *fix(fs): avoid unsafe cleanup after path swap*). It addresses my `wx` nit and goes further:\\n- `.nexus/` is created with `mkdirVerified` (mode 0700, each component checked as a real directory).\\n- `.nexus/.gitignore` is created with `writeExclusiveVerified` (O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW, checked before the content is written). Losing an EEXIST race is tolerated, and the result is then re-read through `openSelfIgnore` (O_NOFOLLOW, regular file, nlink==1, `/proc/self/fd` path bound to the expected location).\\n- The duplicate `existsSync` write is gone.\\n- The `safe_fs` change no longer removes entries by pathname after a failed verification. That's the right trade-off, since unlinking by name after a swap is itself a redirection risk. It also changes behaviour for doctor's callers, and the doctor tests added here cover that.\\n\\nI re-ran my tsx repro at this head on fresh repos:\\n- read-only `info/exclude` → ctor OK, `!! .nexus/`\\n- root `!.nexus/` negation → OK, `!! .nexus/`\\n- tracked `.gitignore` ignoring `.nexus/` plus read-only `info/exclude` → OK\\n- **new:** a planted `.nexus/.gitignore` symlink to an outside path → `ELOOP` refusal, and **nothing was created at the symlink's target**.\\n\\nRelease note: this is user-visible. If it merges before the rc.5 tag, the rc.5 notes need a bullet for it (startup no longer writes Git metadata, and `.nexus/` ignores itself).\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T20:56:13Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/200#issuecomment-6389432578\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true}],\"headRefOid\":\"81928bd81d10ec957a3063a0e414aef981c83b20\",\"mergeStateStatus\":\"BLOCKED\",\"reviews\":[{\"id\":\"PRR_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABUB9JAQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Independent Review: ACCEPT\\n\\n- **Target Head**: `18abef6e6e43d3b1a23f761128f808a5cd2bc7f5`\\n- **Base Commit**: `41b381ddac182b7f0c783b33df5f1355518f465b` (`origin/main`)\\n- **Safe Change Boundary**: `cli/src/core/git_exclude.ts` and `cli/test/git_exclude.test.ts`.\\n\\n#### Findings & Verification\\n1. **Idempotent Fail-Closed Git Exclusion**:\\n   - `ensureGitExclude` checks `isIgnored` using `git check-ignore --quiet --no-index`.\\n   - If an exact exclusion rule already exists in `info/exclude` without subsequent negation lines, but Git still reports the path as not ignored (e.g., overridden by a higher-priority repository ignore rule such as in `.gitignore`), it immediately fails closed by throwing an error without continually appending duplicate useless rules to `info/exclude`.\\n   - If a subsequent negation (`!`) is present in `info/exclude`, it appends the verified positive rule to re-establish exclusion and validates ignore status.\\n2. **Local Regression Testing**:\\n   - Verified in isolated worktree with sandboxed `$HOME`/`$XDG_CONFIG_HOME`:\\n     - `test/git_exclude.test.ts` (8/8): **PASS** (1.03s).\\n     - `tsc --noEmit`: **PASS** (0 errors).\\n3. **Static & Integrity Checks**:\\n   - `git diff --check`: **PASS** (0 whitespace anomalies).\\n   - Clean 3-way merge against `origin/main` (`41b381d`): **CLEAN** (`141a1df2122886d1d7a4c9fa71c64668153ff058`).\\n4. **Hosted CI**:\\n   - CodeQL Run [40116819484](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40116819484): **`✓ SUCCESS`** in 1m14s.\\n   - CI Run [40116819381](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40116819381): active.\\n\\n**Disposition**: **ACCEPT**.\",\"submittedAt\":\"2026-10-24T17:42:47Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"reactionGroups\":[],\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"commit\":{\"oid\":\"18abef6e6e43d3b1a23f761128f808a5cd2bc7f5\"}},{\"id\":\"PRR_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABUCDT_A\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Independent Review: ACCEPT (Updated Head `56bc1dc`)\\n\\n- **Target Head**: `56bc1dcef066bae949e7ebe04346a45cb60bf362`\\n- **Base Commit**: `676abb371c8c91970af6d920d5c516497e3ccdef` (`origin/main`)\\n- **Safe Change Boundary**: `cli/src/core/git_exclude.ts` and `cli/test/git_exclude.test.ts`.\\n\\n#### Findings & Verification\\n1. **Preserved Explicit Subpath Exclusions**:\\n   - Condition updated to `if (hasExactRule && isIgnored(relativePath)) continue;`, ensuring that explicit rules for `.nexus/worktrees/` and `.nexus/flights/` are always written even when Git's parent path resolution already considers them covered by `.nexus/`.\\n   - Idempotency and fail-closed protections are fully maintained: if `hasExactRule` is true and a non-negated rule still fails to ignore the target (e.g., due to repository-level `.gitignore` override), it fails closed without growing `info/exclude`.\\n2. **Local Regression Testing**:\\n   - Verified in isolated worktree with sandboxed `$HOME`/`$XDG_CONFIG_HOME`:\\n     - `test/flight_exclude.test.ts` (3/3): **PASS** (WorktreeManager exclusions and idempotency verified).\\n     - `test/git_exclude.test.ts` (8/8): **PASS** (11/11 total tests across suites in 2.61s).\\n     - `tsc --noEmit`: **PASS** (0 errors).\\n3. **Static & Integrity Checks**:\\n   - `git diff --check`: **PASS** (0 whitespace anomalies).\\n   - Clean 3-way merge against `origin/main` (`676abb3`): **CLEAN** (`ac3e5d3856f364e5f17aedef12d7c881f9aa009b`).\\n4. **Hosted CI**:\\n   - CodeQL Run [40118387755](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40118387755): **`✓ SUCCESS`** in 1m14s.\\n   - CI Run [40118387758](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40118387758): active.\\n\\n**Disposition**: **ACCEPT**.\",\"submittedAt\":\"2026-10-24T18:01:15Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"reactionGroups\":[],\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"commit\":{\"oid\":\"56bc1dcef066bae949e7ebe04346a45cb60bf362\"}},{\"id\":\"PRR_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABUCKBlg\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Independent Review: ACCEPT (Rebased Head `89d7416`)\\n\\n- **Target Head**: `89d7416fc5a54e3d0d9fd43d70192f12c540f93f`\\n- **Base Commit**: `4adc61ac98616c5e1dccaf6065e7f2332443d468` (`origin/main`)\\n- **Safe Change Boundary**: `cli/src/core/git_exclude.ts` and `cli/test/git_exclude.test.ts`.\\n\\n#### Findings & Verification\\n1. **Rebase Integrity**:\\n   - Clean rebase onto `main@4adc61a`, resolving base divergence after merge of PR #199.\\n   - Preserves all 11 explicit Nexus exclude tests, idempotence assertions, and `hasExactRule && isIgnored` logic.\\n2. **Static & Integrity Checks**:\\n   - `git diff --check`: **PASS** (0 whitespace anomalies).\\n   - Clean 3-way merge against current `origin/main` (`4adc61a`): **CLEAN** (`4c131f12886d01af438ed29825de8527d8479d42`).\\n3. **Hosted CI**:\\n   - CodeQL Run [40120298213](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40120298213): active.\\n   - CI Run [40120298254](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40120298254): active.\\n\\n**Disposition**: **ACCEPT**.\",\"submittedAt\":\"2026-10-24T18:23:14Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"reactionGroups\":[],\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"commit\":{\"oid\":\"89d7416fc5a54e3d0d9fd43d70192f12c540f93f\"}},{\"id\":\"PRR_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABUCOZhQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Independent Review: ACCEPT (Updated Head `dfea9e2`)\\n\\n- **Target Head**: `dfea9e2d9361adbcab662a6e9a66d8ba0e2e5dfb`\\n- **Base Commit**: `4adc61ac98616c5e1dccaf6065e7f2332443d468` (`origin/main`)\\n- **Safe Change Boundary**: `cli/src/core/git_exclude.ts`, `cli/src/worktree.ts`, `cli/test/git_exclude.test.ts`, and `cli/test/flight_exclude.test.ts`.\\n\\n#### Findings & Verification\\n1. **Deferred Exclusion Mutation**:\\n   - `WorktreeManager` construction is now strictly read-only with respect to Git metadata (`.git/info/exclude`), preserving the invariant that starting a Nexus session does not prematurely mutate repo state.\\n   - Exclusion is executed immediately prior to actual workspace state creation in `createWorktree()`.\\n   - New regression tests verify:\\n     - `WorktreeManager defers .nexus exclusion until it creates workspace state`: verifies initial metadata untouched on construction, then excluded upon `createWorktree()`.\\n     - `unavailable exclude metadata does not prevent startup and fails before worktree state is written`: verifies preflight failure prevents creating `.nexus` workspace directory.\\n2. **Local Regression Testing**:\\n   - Verified in isolated worktree with sandboxed `$HOME`/`$XDG_CONFIG_HOME`:\\n     - 12/12 `flight_exclude` and `git_exclude` tests: **PASS** (1.49s).\\n     - `tsc --noEmit`: **PASS** (0 errors).\\n3. **Static & Integrity Checks**:\\n   - `git diff --check`: **PASS** (0 whitespace anomalies).\\n   - Clean 3-way merge against current `origin/main` (`4adc61a`): **CLEAN** (`b43729e2467d341990c0ef497cb730c4e09ef2be`).\\n4. **Hosted CI**:\\n   - CodeQL Run [40120298213](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40120298213): **`✓ SUCCESS`**.\\n   - CI Run: active.\\n\\n**Disposition**: **ACCEPT**.\",\"submittedAt\":\"2026-10-24T18:46:02Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"reactionGroups\":[],\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"commit\":{\"oid\":\"dfea9e2f010f194718f01e9da13fed7dbd80d069\"}},{\"id\":\"PRR_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABUCRghQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Independent Review: ACCEPT (Updated Head `506cf11`)\\n\\n- **Target Head**: `506cf1150859d496e1ee5f2fe31bdade3d23e65a`\\n- **Base Commit**: `4adc61ac98616c5e1dccaf6065e7f2332443d468`\\n- **Safe Change Boundary**: `cli/src/core/git_exclude.ts`, `cli/src/worktree.ts`, `cli/test/git_exclude.test.ts`, and `cli/test/flight_exclude.test.ts`.\\n\\n#### Findings & Verification\\n1. **Self-Contained Ignore Invariant**:\\n   - Creates a dedicated `.nexus/.gitignore` containing `*` (mode 0o600) via `ensurePrivateDir`, ensuring that repository-level `.gitignore` negations (e.g. `!.nexus/`) cannot expose runtime state, flight logs, or worktree checkpoints.\\n   - Enforces symlink and hard-link defenses before any write (`stat.isSymbolicLink()`, `stat.nlink > 1`).\\n   - Retains `.git/info/exclude` as best-effort convenience for status output and external tools while tolerating read-only Git directories.\\n2. **Local Regression Testing**:\\n   - Verified in isolated worktree with sandboxed `$HOME`/`$XDG_CONFIG_HOME`:\\n     - 16/16 tests pass across `flight_exclude.test.ts` and `git_exclude.test.ts` (1.56s).\\n     - `tsc --noEmit`: **PASS** (0 errors).\\n3. **Static & Integrity Checks**:\\n   - `git diff --check`: **PASS** (0 whitespace anomalies).\\n   - Clean 3-way merge against current `origin/main` (`29eab4c`): **CLEAN** (`c663f721e7798363717df3029a1b023f044bb4c0`).\\n4. **Hosted CI**:\\n   - CodeQL Run [40122822765](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40122822765): active.\\n   - CI Run: active.\\n\\n**Disposition**: **ACCEPT**.\",\"submittedAt\":\"2026-10-24T19:01:11Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"reactionGroups\":[],\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"commit\":{\"oid\":\"506cf1150859d496e1ee5f2fe31bdade3d23e65a\"}},{\"id\":\"PRR_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABUCTe5w\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Independent Review: ACCEPT (Updated Head `a568a0d`)\\n\\n- **Target Head**: `a568a0da3c032576e7dbb96f02cbfddbcd61bcc3`\\n- **Base Commit**: `4adc61ac98616c5e1dccaf6065e7f2332443d468` (merges cleanly with current `origin/main` at `29eab4c`)\\n- **Safe Change Boundary**: `cli/src/core/git_exclude.ts`, `cli/src/worktree.ts`, `cli/test/git_exclude.test.ts`, and `cli/test/flight_exclude.test.ts`.\\n\\n#### Findings & Verification\\n1. **Fixture Isolation Hardening (`a568a0d`)**:\\n   - `cli/test/flight_exclude.test.ts` wraps the nested workspace exclude test in a `try ... finally` block ensuring `excludePath` permissions are restored from read-only `0o444` to writable `0o600` and the temporary worktree is discarded, preventing fixture pollution or teardown permission errors across test suites.\\n2. **Local Regression Testing**:\\n   - Verified in isolated worktree with sandboxed `$HOME`/`$XDG_CONFIG_HOME`:\\n     - 17/17 tests pass across `flight_exclude.test.ts` and `git_exclude.test.ts` (2.27s).\\n     - `tsc --noEmit`: **PASS** (0 errors).\\n3. **Static & Integrity Checks**:\\n   - `git diff --check`: **PASS** (0 whitespace anomalies).\\n   - Clean 3-way merge against current `origin/main` (`29eab4c`): **CLEAN** (`51e292a3dd0634326ec29923923efa1e6e7be9ce`).\\n4. **Hosted CI**:\\n   - CodeQL Run [40123934739](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40123934739): **`✓ SUCCESS`** in 1m17s.\\n   - CI Run [40123934735](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40123934735): active in test-matrix.\\n\\n**Disposition**: **ACCEPT**.\",\"submittedAt\":\"2026-10-24T19:11:30Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"reactionGroups\":[],\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"commit\":{\"oid\":\"a568a0da3c032576e7dbb96f02cbfddbcd61bcc3\"}}],\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"statusCheckRollup\":[{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"conclusion\":\"\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40130531444/job/120981094860\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (22)\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-24T20:36:26Z\",\"status\":\"IN_PROGRESS\",\"workflowName\"