ce media=\\\\\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\\\\\" srcset=\\\\\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog-dark.svg\\\\\\\"><img src=\\\\\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog.svg\\\\\\\" width=\\\\\\\"16\\\\\\\" height=\\\\\\\"16\\\\\\\" align=\\\\\\\"absmiddle\\\\\\\" alt=\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"></picture> Run configuration</strong></summary>\\\\n> <dl>\\\\n> <dd>\\\\n> \\\\n> - **Source mode**: Auto\\\\n> - **Repository**: Unavailable\\\\n> - **Branch**: Unavailable\\\\n> - **File**: No configuration file from this repository applied\\\\n> - **Commit**: Unavailable\\\\n> - **Layers**: defaults\\\\n> - **Review profile**: CHILL\\\\n> - **Plan**: Advanced\\\\n> - **Run ID**: `f6322e8f-6adc-4c38-9c92-d9572b3e385d`\\\\n> \\\\n> </dd>\\\\n> </dl>\\\\n> </details>\\\\n\\\\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\\\\n\\\\n<!-- autopilot:start -->\\\\n- [ ] <!-- {\\\\\\\"checkboxId\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"2708ad07-9f24-4260-9c11-7dc76a49f2e3\\\\\\\"} --> <strong title=\\\\\\\"Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\\\\\\">Autofix</strong> · Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\\\n<!-- autopilot:end -->\\\\n<!-- tips_start -->\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nThanks for using [CodeRabbit](https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=oss&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=mikeholownych/nexus-code&utm_content=200)! It's free for OSS, and your support helps us grow. If you like it, consider giving us a shout-out.\\\\n\\\\n<details>\\\\n<summary><strong>❤️ Share</strong></summary>\\\\n<dl>\\\\n<dd>\\\\n\\\\n- [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A&url=https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\\\n- [Mastodon](https://mastodon.social/share?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai)\\\\n- [Reddit](https://www.reddit.com/submit?title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&text=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\\\n- [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai&mini=true&title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&summary=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code)\\\\n\\\\n</dd>\\\\n</dl>\\\\n</details>\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands.</sub>\\\\n\\\\n<!-- tips_end -->\\\",\\\"createdAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T17:35:37Z\\\",\\\"includesCreatedEdit\\\":true,\\\"isMinimized\\\":false,\\\"minimizedReason\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"reactionGroups\\\":[],\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/200#issuecomment-6387385654\\\",\\\"viewerDidAuthor\\\":false},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfLpbWQ\\\",\\\"author\\\":{\\\"login\\\":\\\"mikeholownych\\\"},\\\"authorAssociation\\\":\\\"OWNER\\\",\\\"body\\\":\\\"### CI Failure Finding: `cli/test/flight_exclude.test.ts`\\\\n\\\\nCI Run [40116819381](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40116819381) failed on `test-matrix (24)` ([Job 120939693293](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40116819381/job/120939693293)):\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\n✖ WorktreeManager ensures .nexus/ is excluded (29.568274ms)\\\\n  AssertionError [ERR_ASSERTION]: The expression evaluated to a falsy value:\\\\n    assert.ok(content.includes(\\\\\\\".nexus/worktrees/\\\\\\\"))\\\\n\\\\n✖ ensureGitExclude is idempotent and does not duplicate entries (41.185252ms)\\\\n  AssertionError [ERR_ASSERTION]: Idempotent exclude calls must not duplicate entries\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n#### Cause\\\\nIn `cli/src/core/git_exclude.ts`:\\\\n```ts\\\\nfor (const { path: relativePath, rule } of protectedPaths) {\\\\n  ...\\\\n  if (isIgnored(relativePath)) continue;\\\\n```\\\\nOnce `.nexus/` is appended to `info/exclude`, Git considers all descendants (`.nexus/worktrees/...`, `.nexus/flights/...`) ignored. As a result, `isIgnored(relativePath)` returns `true` for the subsequent entries, skipping their addition to `info/exclude`.\\\\n`info/exclude` is left with only `.nexus/` rather than the complete set of required entries (`.nexus/`, `.nexus/worktrees/`, `.nexus/flights/`), failing the assertions in `cli/test/flight_exclude.test.ts`.\\\\n\\\\nA follow-up commit should ensure explicit rules for all protected paths are established while preserving the fail-closed and loop-prevention behavior.\\\",\\\"createdAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T17:51:57Z\\\",\\\"includesCreatedEdit\\\":false,\\\"isMinimized\\\":false,\\\"minimizedReason\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"reactionGroups\\\":[],\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/200#issuecomment-6387555161\\\",\\\"viewerDidAuthor\\\":true},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfLrOog\\\",\\\"author\\\":{\\\"login\\\":\\\"mikeholownych\\\"},\\\"authorAssociation\\\":\\\"OWNER\\\",\\\"body\\\":\\\"**Independent review (claude-code) at exact head `18abef6e6e43d3b1a23f761128f808a5cd2bc7f5` (base `41b381dd`): REQUEST_CHANGES. Startup regression.**\\\\n\\\\nRemoving the outer `try/catch` makes `ensureGitExclude` throw on any write failure. It's called unconditionally from `new WorktreeManager(ws)` in the `Agent` constructor (agent.ts:1115), and also from `FlightRecorder`, `evaluator.ts:157` and `index.ts:964`. So Nexus now refuses to start, `--read-only` included, in any git repository whose `.git/info/exclude` the user can't write and that doesn't already ignore `.nexus/`. Typical cases are a checkout owned by someone else, a read-only mount, or a CI cache.\\\\n\\\\n**Reproduced** with a fresh `git init` repo and `chmod a-w .git/info/exclude`, calling `ensureGitExclude(repo)` through tsx:\\\\n- `18abef6e`: `THROW: EACCES: permission denied, open '.../.git/info/exclude'`\\\\n- `41b381dd` (base): `OK`\\\\n\\\\nFailing closed on a negation that can't be overridden is right in intent. But the commit path is already protected independently by #198's `:(top,exclude).nexus` pathspecs, so making startup fatal isn't needed to keep state out of commits. Suggested fix, either of:\\\\n1. In read-only mode, skip writing `info/exclude` entirely. Read-only shouldn't mutate `.git`.\\\\n2. Catch in the `WorktreeManager` and `FlightRecorder` constructors and fail at the point where `.nexus` state is actually…4821 tokens truncated…\\\"mikeholownych\\\"},\\\"authorAssociation\\\":\\\"OWNER\\\",\\\"body\\\":\\\"### Independent Review: ACCEPT (Updated Head `dfea9e2`)\\\\n\\\\n- **Target Head**: `dfea9e2d9361adbcab662a6e9a66d8ba0e2e5dfb`\\\\n- **Base Commit**: `4adc61ac98616c5e1dccaf6065e7f2332443d468` (`origin/main`)\\\\n- **Safe Change Boundary**: `cli/src/core/git_exclude.ts`, `cli/src/worktree.ts`, `cli/test/git_exclude.test.ts`, and `cli/test/flight_exclude.test.ts`.\\\\n\\\\n#### Findings & Verification\\\\n1. **Deferred Exclusion Mutation**:\\\\n   - `WorktreeManager` construction is now strictly read-only with respect to Git metadata (`.git/info/exclude`), preserving the invariant that starting a Nexus session does not prematurely mutate repo state.\\\\n   - Exclusion is executed immediately prior to actual workspace state creation in `createWorktree()`.\\\\n   - New regression tests verify:\\\\n     - `WorktreeManager defers .nexus exclusion until it creates workspace state`: verifies initial metadata untouched on construction, then excluded upon `createWorktree()`.\\\\n     - `unavailable exclude metadata does not prevent startup and fails before worktree state is written`: verifies preflight failure prevents creating `.nexus` workspace directory.\\\\n2. **Local Regression Testing**:\\\\n   - Verified in isolated worktree with sandboxed `$HOME`/`$XDG_CONFIG_HOME`:\\\\n     - 12/12 `flight_exclude` and `git_exclude` tests: **PASS** (1.49s).\\\\n     - `tsc --noEmit`: **PASS** (0 errors).\\\\n3. **Static & Integrity Checks**:\\\\n   - `git diff --check`: **PASS** (0 whitespace anomalies).\\\\n   - Clean 3-way merge against current `origin/main` (`4adc61a`): **CLEAN** (`b43729e2467d341990c0ef497cb730c4e09ef2be`).\\\\n4. **Hosted CI**:\\\\n   - CodeQL Run [40120298213](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40120298213): **`✓ SUCCESS`**.\\\\n   - CI Run: active.\\\\n\\\\n**Disposition**: **ACCEPT**.\\\",\\\"submittedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T18:46:02Z\\\",\\\"includesCreatedEdit\\\":false,\\\"reactionGroups\\\":[],\\\"state\\\":\\\"COMMENTED\\\",\\\"commit\\\":{\\\"oid\\\":\\\"dfea9e2f010f194718f01e9da13fed7dbd80d069\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"PRR_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABUCRghQ\\\",\\\"author\\\":{\\\"login\\\":\\\"mikeholownych\\\"},\\\"authorAssociation\\\":\\\"OWNER\\\",\\\"body\\\":\\\"### Independent Review: ACCEPT (Updated Head `506cf11`)\\\\n\\\\n- **Target Head**: `506cf1150859d496e1ee5f2fe31bdade3d23e65a`\\\\n- **Base Commit**: `4adc61ac98616c5e1dccaf6065e7f2332443d468`\\\\n- **Safe Change Boundary**: `cli/src/core/git_exclude.ts`, `cli/src/worktree.ts`, `cli/test/git_exclude.test.ts`, and `cli/test/flight_exclude.test.ts`.\\\\n\\\\n#### Findings & Verification\\\\n1. **Self-Contained Ignore Invariant**:\\\\n   - Creates a dedicated `.nexus/.gitignore` containing `*` (mode 0o600) via `ensurePrivateDir`, ensuring that repository-level `.gitignore` negations (e.g. `!.nexus/`) cannot expose runtime state, flight logs, or worktree checkpoints.\\\\n   - Enforces symlink and hard-link defenses before any write (`stat.isSymbolicLink()`, `stat.nlink > 1`).\\\\n   - Retains `.git/info/exclude` as best-effort convenience for status output and external tools while tolerating read-only Git directories.\\\\n2. **Local Regression Testing**:\\\\n   - Verified in isolated worktree with sandboxed `$HOME`/`$XDG_CONFIG_HOME`:\\\\n     - 16/16 tests pass across `flight_exclude.test.ts` and `git_exclude.test.ts` (1.56s).\\\\n     - `tsc --noEmit`: **PASS** (0 errors).\\\\n3. **Static & Integrity Checks**:\\\\n   - `git diff --check`: **PASS** (0 whitespace anomalies).\\\\n   - Clean 3-way merge against current `origin/main` (`29eab4c`): **CLEAN** (`c663f721e7798363717df3029a1b023f044bb4c0`).\\\\n4. **Hosted CI**:\\\\n   - CodeQL Run [40122822765](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40122822765): active.\\\\n   - CI Run: active.\\\\n\\\\n**Disposition**: **ACCEPT**.\\\",\\\"submittedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T19:01:11Z\\\",\\\"includesCreatedEdit\\\":false,\\\"reactionGroups\\\":[],\\\"state\\\":\\\"COMMENTED\\\",\\\"commit\\\":{\\\"oid\\\":\\\"506cf1150859d496e1ee5f2fe31bdade3d23e65a\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"PRR_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABUCTe5w\\\",\\\"author\\\":{\\\"login\\\":\\\"mikeholownych\\\"},\\\"authorAssociation\\\":\\\"OWNER\\\",\\\"body\\\":\\\"### Independent Review: ACCEPT (Updated Head `a568a0d`)\\\\n\\\\n- **Target Head**: `a568a0da3c032576e7dbb96f02cbfddbcd61bcc3`\\\\n- **Base Commit**: `4adc61ac98616c5e1dccaf6065e7f2332443d468` (merges cleanly with current `origin/main` at `29eab4c`)\\\\n- **Safe Change Boundary**: `cli/src/core/git_exclude.ts`, `cli/src/worktree.ts`, `cli/test/git_exclude.test.ts`, and `cli/test/flight_exclude.test.ts`.\\\\n\\\\n#### Findings & Verification\\\\n1. **Fixture Isolation Hardening (`a568a0d`)**:\\\\n   - `cli/test/flight_exclude.test.ts` wraps the nested workspace exclude test in a `try ... finally` block ensuring `excludePath` permissions are restored from read-only `0o444` to writable `0o600` and the temporary worktree is discarded, preventing fixture pollution or teardown permission errors across test suites.\\\\n2. **Local Regression Testing**:\\\\n   - Verified in isolated worktree with sandboxed `$HOME`/`$XDG_CONFIG_HOME`:\\\\n     - 17/17 tests pass across `flight_exclude.test.ts` and `git_exclude.test.ts` (2.27s).\\\\n     - `tsc --noEmit`: **PASS** (0 errors).\\\\n3. **Static & Integrity Checks**:\\\\n   - `git diff --check`: **PASS** (0 whitespace anomalies).\\\\n   - Clean 3-way merge against current `origin/main` (`29eab4c`): **CLEAN** (`51e292a3dd0634326ec29923923efa1e6e7be9ce`).\\\\n4. **Hosted CI**:\\\\n   - CodeQL Run [40123934739](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40123934739): **`✓ SUCCESS`** in 1m17s.\\\\n   - CI Run [40123934735](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40123934735): active in test-matrix.\\\\n\\\\n**Disposition**: **ACCEPT**.\\\",\\\"submittedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T19:11:30Z\\\",\\\"includesCreatedEdit\\\":false,\\\"reactionGroups\\\":[],\\\"state\\\":\\\"COMMENTED\\\",\\\"commit\\\":{\\\"oid\\\":\\\"a568a0da3c032576e7dbb96f02cbfddbcd61bcc3\\\"}}],\\\"state\\\":\\\"OPEN\\\",\\\"statusCheckRollup\\\":[{\\\"__typename\\\":\\\"CheckRun\\\",\\\"completedAt\\\":\\\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\\\",\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"detailsUrl\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40130531444/job/120981094860\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"test-matrix (22)\\\",\\\"startedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T20:36:26Z\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"IN_PROGRESS\\\",\\\"workflowName\\\":\\\"CI\\\"},{\\\"__typename\\\":\\\"CheckRun\\\",\\\"completedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T20:38:03Z\\\",\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"SUCCESS\\\",\\\"detailsUrl\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40130531552/job/120981094972\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"javascript-typescript\\\",\\\"startedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T20:36:27Z\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"COMPLETED\\\",\\\"workflowName\\\":\\\"CodeQL\\\"},{\\\"__typename\\\":\\\"CheckRun\\\",\\\"completedAt\\\":\\\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\\\",\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"detailsUrl\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40130531444/job/120981094683\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"test-matrix (24)\\\",\\\"startedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T20:36:27Z\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"IN_PROGRESS\\\",\\\"workflowName\\\":\\\"CI\\\"},{\\\"__typename\\\":\\\"CheckRun\\\",\\\"completedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T20:37:56Z\\\",\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"SUCCESS\\\",\\\"detailsUrl\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/runs/120981427339\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"CodeQL\\\",\\\"startedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T20:37:53Z\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"COMPLETED\\\",\\\"workflowName\\\":\\\"\\\"},{\\\"__typename\\\":\\\"StatusContext\\\",\\\"context\\\":\\\"CodeRabbit\\\",\\\"startedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T20:36:28Z\\\",\\\"state\\\":\\\"SUCCESS\\\",\\\"targetUrl\\\":\\\"\\\"}],\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/200\\\"}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0},{\"name\":\"processes\",\"output\":\"1582262    6852 1582262 Ss         00:00 /usr/bin/zsh -c ps -eo pid,ppid,pgid,stat,etime,args | rg '552132|npm test|node.*vitest|vitest|jest' | head -60\\n1582268 1582262 1582262 S          00:00 rg 552132|npm test|node.*vitest|vitest|jest\\n\",\"exit_code\":0},{\"name\":\"rc-readiness\",\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 6536)\\nTotal output lines: 297\\n\\n# Nexus Code v1.0.0: release qualification procedure\\n\\nThis is the procedure that decides whether a release candidate (RC) may become v1.0.0. It defines:\\n\\n- the environments;\\n- the workflow matrix;\\n- the evidence each step must produce;\\n- explicit pass/fail gates.\\n\\nThree separate questions are judged and recorded separately:\\n\\n| Question | Who answers it |\\n|---|---|\\n| **Implementation self-assessment** | Did the implementer's tests pass? |\\n| **Product qualification** | Did the RC meet these gates on real workflows? |\\n| **Independent acceptance** | Did a reviewer other than the implementer agree? |\\n\\nA gate passes only on archived evidence bound to the source commit or installed RC artifact that the gate evaluates. Source-level evidence names the exact source commit; installed-RC evidence names both that commit and the installed package digest. A green test suite alone never qualifies the product.\\n\\n## 1.1 Release-candidate lifecycle and evidence identity\\n\\nThe release sequence has five distinct stages. Passing an earlier stage is a prerequisite for the next stage, not a substitute for it. Every G0–G4 acceptance ID remains mandatory; the stage determines which exact input and evidence it evaluates, not whether the check applies.\\n\\n1. **Pre-RC source gates.** Before creating an RC tag, run required source CI and every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method evaluates source, a source-built test binary, or an environment without requiring a published RC. Record the full commit ID and check results. Source checks do not establish behavior of the installed package.\\n2. **RC artifact construction.** After the required owner authorization, create the version-matched RC tag on that exact source commit and use the repository release workflow to build and publish the RC artifacts. Record the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance. The workflow-produced artifacts are the candidates for qualification; a local build or a different commit is not interchangeable. RC artifact publication is not product qualification or final release acceptance.\\n3. **RC artifact gates.** Before installed-RC product qualification, run every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method requires the RC archive, RC attestation/release, or workflow-produced artifact. This includes ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08. ACC-PKG checks that explicitly require an installed package run against this RC as specified by their test method. Record the RC tag commit, workflow run, artifact digests, and each check result. A source-level analogue does not replace an artifact-bound check.\\n4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\\n5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\\n\\nThe final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\\n\\nExact-RC requirements records identify at least one implementer and an independent reviewer. For a blocking requirement recorded as `tested` instead of `product-qualified`, the cited decision must be explicitly allowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\\n\\nThe post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. At G6, the exact-RC invocation must provide a record meeting the normal B/RR status threshold and digest-bound evidence for every criterion in this table. The table also supplies the criterion mapping for rows whose ledger points to an ACCEPTANCE section instead of naming ACC IDs. The source ledger is never rewritten by the record. Any below-tested required row omitted from this table still fails.\\n\\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:START -->\\n### Qualification-only requirements for exact-RC enforcement\\n\\n| Requirement | Acceptance criteria required in the exact-RC record | Remaining stage |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\\n| REQ-AGT-010 | ACC-TRUST-04 | Independent acceptance of the DEC-04 v1 subset |\\n| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\\n| REQ-REL-005 | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05…3036 tokens truncated…ctory}\\\"\\n  test ! -e \\\"$T2_OUT\\\"\\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json --tasks \\\"$T2_TASKS\\\" --out \\\"$T2_OUT/nexus\\\" --runs 5\\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json --tasks \\\"$T2_TASKS\\\" --out \\\"$T2_OUT/goose\\\" --runs 5\\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json --tasks \\\"$T2_TASKS\\\" --out \\\"$T2_OUT/opencode\\\" --runs 5\\n  node eval/score.mjs --pairs \\\"$T2_OUT/nexus/results.jsonl\\\" \\\"$T2_OUT/goose/results.jsonl\\\" \\\"$T2_OUT/opencode/results.jsonl\\\"\\n  ```\\n\\n  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\\n\\n### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\\n\\n9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC, via `eval/faults/proxy.mjs` and the fixture hooks (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\\n\\n1. refused connection mid-turn\\n2. 5xx / overloaded\\n3. stream cut mid-tool-call\\n4. output-limit truncation\\n5. hanging test command\\n# Nexus Code v1.0.0: audit and planning package\\n\\nThis package is the evidence-based path from `v0.1.0-alpha.2` (audited at `db1ca55`, 2026-10-14) to v1.0.0.\\n\\n**Verdict: v1.0.0 readiness is BLOCKED.** There are 31 blocker requirements, none of them met. Task-quality, standalone and real-terminal qualification are **unverified**: no qualifying evidence exists yet. The contest entry was submitted, is frozen, and is tracked separately.\\n\\n## How to read it\\n\\n| If you want to… | Read |\\n|---|---|\\n| Understand what Nexus is today, what was examined, and what is wrong | [AUDIT.md](AUDIT.md) |\\n| See every requirement (historical and new), its status, blocker class, and how it is accepted | [REQUIREMENTS.md](REQUIREMENTS.md) |\\n| Know the order of work, the effort, and the critical path | [ROADMAP.md](ROADMAP.md) |\\n| Implement a workstream | Its spec in [specs/](specs/), then its plan in [plans/](plans/) |\\n| Qualify a release candidate | [ACCEPTANCE.md](ACCEPTANCE.md) |\\n| Check what was actually run and what it proves | [EVIDENCE.md](EVIDENCE.md) and [evidence/](evidence/) |\\n| See the decisions taken (all resolved under delegated owner authority) and the remaining owner actions | [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md) |\\n| Run several agents on this plan at once without collisions | [CONCURRENCY.md](CONCURRENCY.md) (also referenced from the root `AGENTS.md`) |\\n\\n## Workstreams\\n\\n| # | Workstream | Spec | Plan | Milestone | Blockers |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| 01 | Safe execution defaults and approval integrity | [SPEC-01](specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md) | [PLAN-01](plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md) | M1 | SEC-101, 102, 103, 119 |\\n| 02 | Process ownership, cancellation, resource bounds | [SPEC-02](specs/SPEC-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md) | [PLAN-02](plans/PLAN-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md) | M1 | AGT-109, SEC-106 |\\n| 03 | Untrusted workspace inputs and egress boundary | [SPEC-03](specs/SPEC-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md) | [PLAN-03](plans/PLAN-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md) | M1 | SEC-110, 111, 115, 116 |\\n| 04 | Continuity, resume, durable work units | [SPEC-04](specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md) | [PLAN-04](plans/PLAN-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md) | M3 | AGT-101, 102 |\\n| 05 | Standalone local inference and provider robustness | [SPEC-05](specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md) | [PLAN-05](plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md) | M3/M5 | PRV-101, 102, 106 |\\n| 06 | Packaged product parity, launcher, versioning, doctor | [SPEC-06](specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md) | [PLAN-06](plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md) | M0/M2 | REL-101, 102, 103 |\\n| 07 | Supply chain, compliance, release engineering | [SPEC-07](specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md) | [PLAN-07](plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md) | M2 | REL-107 |\\n| 08 | Persistence hygiene | [SPEC-08](specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md) | [PLAN-08](plans/PLAN-08-persistence-hygiene.md) | M0/M4 | (prerequisite: PER-103) |\\n| 09 | Requirements governance and documentation truth | [SPEC-09](specs/SPEC-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md) | [PLAN-09](plans/PLAN-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md) | M0/M6 | OPS-101, 103 |\\n| 10 | v1 qualification and evaluation | [SPEC-10](specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) | [PLAN-10](plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) | M3/M5 | QUAL-101 to 107 |\\n| 11 | Verification and tool-call integrity | [SPEC-11](specs/SPEC-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md) | [PLAN-11](plans/PLAN-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md) | M1/M3 | AGT-112, 113, 114 |\\n| C1 | Contest (separate product; frozen until judging ends) | [SPEC-C1](specs/SPEC-C1-contest-submission-track.md) | [PLAN-C1](plans/PLAN-C1-contest-submission-track.md) | post-contest | — (not a client gate) |\\n\\n## How to execute\\n\\n0. If more than one agent (or person) will implement in parallel, read [CONCURRENCY.md](CONCURRENCY.md) first. It covers slice claims, worktrees, hot files, the gateway lock and merge order.\\n1. **Start with M0** (ROADMAP). Merge PLAN-08 PR-8a first, so that test runs stop writing into the real `~/.nexus`. Then land PLAN-06 PR-6a (version sync) and PLAN-09 PR-9a (ledger checker, historical banners, cheap doc fixes).\\n2. **M1 is the critical path.** Work through PLAN-01, PLAN-02, PLAN-03 and PLAN-11 PR-11a/b in the PR slices listed. Each plan names its safe change boundary, code locations, tests and rollback.\\n3. **For every PR:**\\n   - update the matching REQUIREMENTS rows (status, test reference, commit);\\n   - keep `scripts/check_requirements.mjs` green;\\n   - run `make test` on a snapshot copy, never while editing (tasks/lessons.md).\\n4. M2 and M4 run in parallel with M1/M3. Held-out task authoring (agent-authored, as authorised) and the standalone proxy start during M1.\\n5. Cut `v1.0.0-rc.1` only when G0–G4 pass. Then run ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 against the **installed** RC.\\n\\n## Conventions\\n\\n- **Requirement IDs.** `REQ-<AREA>-0xx` marks a commitment carried over from history. `REQ-<AREA>-1xx` marks a new v1 requirement.\\n- **Finding IDs.** These are owned by the scoped evidence files: AGT, VER, PRV, SEC, PER, TUI, REL, DX, MNT, HIST, EVL, CON, PERF, DOC.\\n- **Acceptance IDs.** `ACC-<AREA>-NN`. Each is defined in its spec, or in ACCEPTANCE §3.1.\\n- **Evidence labels.** SRC, TEST, RT, MEAS, DOC, HIST, INF, UNV (REQUIREMENTS §1).\\n- **Status ladder.** open → partial → implemented → tested → visually-accepted → product-qualified. Independent acceptance is recorded separately.\\n\\nThis package supersedes the Issue #12 matrices and the PHASE and WP documents as the source of current requirements. Those documents remain as historical record.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0},{\"name\":\"claims-skim\",\"output\":\"---SUITE\\n{\\n  \\\"agent\\\": \\\"codex-root\\\",\\n  \\\"host\\\": \\\"mike-dev\\\",\\n  \\\"branch\\\": \\\"v1/defect-git-exclude-fail-closed\\\",\\n  \\\"worktree\\\": \\\"/var/tmp/nexus-pr200-main-c1b133-candidate\\\",\\n  \\\"base\\\": \\\"c1b13327edf5d3a0c82fb10eb814775fd4953a63\\\",\\n  \\\"head\\\": \\\"REDACTED\\\",\\n  \\\"since\\\": \\\"2026-10-24T23:20:00Z\\\",\\n  \\\"scope\\\": \\\"Focused git_exclude regression tests on immutable PR200 candidate archive with isolated HOME; hosted CI remains separate\\\",\\n  \\\"status\\\": \\\"Previous exact-main CI40140156370 terminal SUCCESS; CodeQL40140156350 SUCCESS. Acquired focused test slot for PR200 candidate; run only test/git_exclude.test.ts, no full suite.\\\",\\n  \\\"workflow_run\\\": \\\"40140156370\\\",\\n  \\\"last_verified_wait\\\": \\\"2026-10-24T23:20:00Z\\\"\\n}\\n---RELEASE_PUBLISHER\\n{\\n  \\\"agent\\\": \\\"/root\\\",\\n  \\\"host\\\": \\\"mike-dev\\\",\\n  \\\"branch\\\": \\\"v1/rc5-version-sync\\\",\\n  \\\"worktree\\\": \\\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc5-version-sync\\\",\\n  \\\"base\\\": \\\"29eab4cd58051a8210b5ef66e0c9e248b2046a13\\\",\\n  \\\"since\\\": \\\"2026-10-23T08:21:16Z\\\",\\n  \\\"scope\\\": \\\"Release coordination and versioning/RC lifecycle preparation; preserve exact-source, installed-RC, independent and human acceptance gates.\\\",\\n  \\\"status\\\": \\\"origin/main 29eab4c exact CI 40123199081 and CodeQL 40123199130 pass; requirements --enforce passed on exact source. PR200 a568a0d remains open with independent ACCEPT and CodeQL pass; Node22/24 full-suite CI 40123934735 still in progress. Local suite process group 361053 is live in defect-doctor-state-dir-snapshot; no overlap or takeover. Ubuntu desktop 10.0.8.3 reachable; terminal versions captured and clean procedure checkout staged at ~/nexus-terminal-acceptance-setup pinned to 29eab4c; no RC installed and no matrix cells run. RC4 remains latest prerelease; acceptance IN_PROGRESS; held-out custody response absent; no RC5 tag or stable release.\\\",\\n  \\\"head\\\": \\\"29eab4cd58051a8210b5ef66e0c9e248b2046a13\\\",\\n  \\\"updated_at\\\": \\\"2026-10-24T19:49:08.456978Z\\\"\\n}\\n\",\"exit_code\":1}]}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","create_time":1792884321.6053698}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
