{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T23:25:30.500Z","ordinal":313495,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-618da6cb-fac1-406e-beea-927b6a3202fd","process_id":"64147","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr checks 200 --json name,state,link,startedAt,completedAt"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr checks 200 --json name,state,link,startedAt,completedAt"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"[{\"completedAt\":\"2026-10-24T20:37:56Z\",\"link\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/runs/120981427339\",\"name\":\"CodeQL\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-24T20:37:53Z\",\"state\":\"SUCCESS\"},{\"completedAt\":\"2026-10-24T20:38:03Z\",\"link\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40130531552/job/120981094972\",\"name\":\"javascript-typescript\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-24T20:36:27Z\",\"state\":\"SUCCESS\"},{\"completedAt\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"link\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40130531444/job/120981094683\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (24)\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-24T20:36:27Z\",\"state\":\"IN_PROGRESS\"},{\"completedAt\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"link\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40130531444/job/120981094860\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (22)\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-24T20:36:26Z\",\"state\":\"IN_PROGRESS\"},{\"completedAt\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"link\":\"\",\"name\":\"CodeRabbit\",\"startedAt\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"state\":\"SUCCESS\"}]\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":615182049}},"started_at_ms":1792884329804,"completed_at_ms":1792884330500}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T23:25:32.247Z","ordinal":313496,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1703b-d6d7-7501-bf84-e6cba4df4e7a","call_id":"call_683d844f57344a8d9c139bac69706ca3","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.8 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"[{\"name\":\"worktree\",\"exit_code\":0,\"output\":\"## v1/defect-git-exclude-fail-closed...origin/v1/defect-git-exclude-fail-closed [ahead 24, behind 8]\\n473103d (HEAD -> v1/defect-git-exclude-fail-closed) fix(git): guard info exclude updates\\n84cdde9 fix(fs): avoid unsafe cleanup after path swap\\n1462dc8 test(worktree): clean up nested workspace fixture\\n\"},{\"name\":\"suite-guide\",\"exit_code\":0,\"output\":\"6:- full test suites were contaminated by edits made mid-run;\\n10:They also follow from audit finding PER-03: the test suite writes into the real `~/.nexus`.\\n12:## 1. Unit of work: one claimed PR slice per agent\\n15:- An agent works on exactly one claimed slice at a time.\\n23:CLAIMS=\\\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\\\"\\n30:  echo \\\"claimed by: $(cat \\\"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\\\")\\\"; exit 1\\n34:- **Release** the claim by deleting its directory (`rm -r \\\"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\\\"`) after the slice merges or is abandoned. Write one line about the outcome to `$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log`.\\n35:- **Hot-file claims** use the same mechanism with the name `FILE_<path with / replaced by _>`, for example `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts`. See §4.\\n36:- **Stale claims.** A claim older than 24 h whose PID is gone may be broken, but only by the owner, or by an agent that first records the broken claim in the log.\\n37:- If the MCP Agent Mail server is available, its file reservations (`file_reservation_paths`) may be used as well. The git-common-dir claim stays authoritative, because every agent can see it without extra tooling.\\n39:## 3. Isolation: worktree, branch, HOME, ports, processes\\n43:| Source | One `git worktree` per claimed slice: `git worktree add ../nexus-wt/<slice> -b v1/<plan>-<slice> origin/main`. Never edit `~/nexus-code` itself. It is the owner's checkout, and `/usr/local/bin/nexus` runs from it. |\\n45:| HOME and state | Until PLAN-08 PR-8a lands, every test, build and probe run sets `HOME=$(mktemp -d)` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\\\"$HOME/.config\\\"`. After PR-8a, the test setup enforces this, but scripts and probes outside `npm test` must still set it. **Never** run anything that writes to the real `~/.nexus` or `~/.config/nexus`. |\\n46:| Test runs | Full suites run on a **snapshot copy** of the worktree (`git worktree add` at the commit under test, or `git archive`), never on the tree being edited. `tsx` reads `src/` live. |\\n50:| Inference | There is one inference host (DEC-16). Any run that uses the gateway takes the claim `GATEWAY` first. That includes eval runs, live checks and stripped-proxy runs. One gateway run at a time, which keeps eval timings valid and prevents overload. Small cloud checks (E5) take `CLOUD` to avoid duplicate spend. |\\n55:These files are touched by several plans. An agent editing one must hold its `FILE_` claim for the **shortest** period: edit, test, push, merge, then release.\\n59:| `cli/src/agent.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 04, 05, 11 | Claim required. Keep each change local to the line ranges the plan names. Rebase immediately before merge and re-run that slice's tests on the rebased snapshot. |\\n68:| `cli/src/tester.ts` | 01, 11 | **PLAN-01 PR-1c lands before PLAN-11 PR-11b/11c.** |\\n69:| `cli/src/core/state.ts` | 04, 08 | **PLAN-08 PR-8a (HOME isolation) lands before everything.** |\\n75:| `docs/USER_MANUAL.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md`, `quickstart.md` | 05, 09 and doc tasks in every plan | Edit only the sections your slice changes. Hold a short `FILE_` claim. |\\n79:A slice changes only the rows for its own requirement IDs: the status, test-reference and evidence cells, in place. It never reorders, adds or removes rows, and never edits another slice's rows. New requirements discovered during work go to §6, not into the ledger. Because rows are independent lines, git merges these edits cleanly. If a conflict appears anyway, resolve it row by row, keeping both changes.\\n85:3. Merge order follows the precedence rules in §4 and the ROADMAP milestone order. Within a milestone, the slice with fewer hot-file claims merges first.\\n86:4. Rebase onto `origin/main` immediately before merging. Re-run the slice's targeted tests, plus `make test`, on a snapshot of the rebased commit. Merge only if both pass.\\n94:| Claims | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` | Who owns which slice or file right now |\\n95:| Claim log | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log` (append-only, one line per event) | Claim, release, broken claim, boundary request |\\n96:| Boundary requests and discovered requirements | The PR description, under the heading `Needs from other slices`. Mirrored as one line in the claim log. | So the owning slice's agent can pick it up. Never fixed silently out of scope. |\\n101:The following groupings can run at the same time with no hot-file contention beyond §4 claims. They are listed by milestone.\\n106:| M1 | (a) PLAN-01 PR-1a → PR-1b → PR-1c (sequential, owns `capabilities.ts`, `agent.ts` dispatch). (b) PLAN-02 PR-2a (Rust only). (c) PLAN-03 PR-3a → PR-3b (config/egress). (d) PLAN-11 PR-11a (`parser.ts`) and PR-11b (`tester.ts`, after PR-1c). Lanes (b), (c) and (d) do not touch `capabilities.ts`. |\\n109:| M4 (alongside M3) | PLAN-08 PR-8b..8e. Coordinate with PLAN-04 on `state.ts` through `FILE_` claims. |\\n110:| M5 | **Serial on `GATEWAY`.** The eval runner, the stripped-proxy runs and the independent reviewer's live task each take the `GATEWAY` claim. The terminal matrix (E3) and the install matrix (E2) can run in parallel with gateway runs. |\\n\"},{\"name\":\"test-scripts\",\"exit_code\":1,\"output\":\"{\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"local-code-harness\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.1.0-alpha.2\\\",\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"module\\\",\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Autonomous local AI coding harness (Codex / Claude-Code style) for LM Studio and vLLM\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/index.js\\\",\\n  \\\"bin\\\": {\\n    \\\"harness\\\": \\\"./dist/index.js\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"tsc && node scripts/write_build_info.mjs\\\",\\n    \\\"test\\\": \\\"tsx --test --test-concurrency=1 test/*.test.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"start\\\": \\\"node dist/index.js\\\",\\n    \\\"dev\\\": \\\"tsx watch src/index.ts\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"keywords\\\": [\\n    \\\"ai\\\",\\n    \\\"coding-agent\\\",\\n    \\\"codex\\\",\\n    \\\"claude-code\\\",\\n    \\\"vllm\\\",\\n    \\\"lm-studio\\\",\\n    \\\"rust\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"author\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"dependencies\\\": {\\n    \\\"commander\\\": \\\"^12.1.0\\\",\\n    \\\"dotenv\\\": \\\"^16.4.5\\\",\\n    \\\"ora\\\": \\\"^8.1.0\\\",\\n    \\\"picocolors\\\": \\\"^1.1.1\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"devDependencies\\\": {\\n    \\\"@types/node\\\": \\\"^22.5.0\\\",\\n    \\\"tsx\\\": \\\"^4.19.0\\\",\\n    \\\"typescript\\\": \\\"^5.5.4\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n\"},{\"name\":\"current-review\",\"exit_code\":0,\"output\":\"[{\\\"completedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T20:37:56Z\\\",\\\"link\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/runs/120981427339\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"CodeQL\\\",\\\"startedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T20:37:53Z\\\",\\\"state\\\":\\\"SUCCESS\\\"},{\\\"completedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T20:38:03Z\\\",\\\"link\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40130531552/job/120981094972\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"javascript-typescript\\\",\\\"startedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T20:36:27Z\\\",\\\"state\\\":\\\"SUCCESS\\\"},{\\\"completedAt\\\":\\\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\\\",\\\"link\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40130531444/job/120981094683\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"test-matrix (24)\\\",\\\"startedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T20:36:27Z\\\",\\\"state\\\":\\\"IN_PROGRESS\\\"},{\\\"completedAt\\\":\\\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\\\",\\\"link\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40130531444/job/120981094860\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"test-matrix (22)\\\",\\\"startedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T20:36:26Z\\\",\\\"state\\\":\\\"IN_PROGRESS\\\"},{\\\"completedAt\\\":\\\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\\\",\\\"link\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"CodeRabbit\\\",\\\"startedAt\\\":\\\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\\\",\\\"state\\\":\\\"SUCCESS\\\"}]\\n\"},{\"name\":\"changed-code\",\"exit_code\":0,\"output\":\"\"}]"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","create_time":1792884332.2475846}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
