v/probe.mts\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/prv/tls.mts\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/repro/agt_repro.test.ts\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:27:4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:28:5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:32:Exact-RC requirements records identify at least one implementer and an independent reviewer. For a blocking requirement recorded as `tested` instead of `product-qualified`, the cited decision must be explicitly allowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:41:| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:45:| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:46:| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:47:| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:48:| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:49:| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:50:| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:51:| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:80:| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:82:| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:113:| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:116:| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:117:| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:118:| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:120:| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:122:## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:141:| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:153:| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:189:### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:191:Terminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:193:For each terminal × size, check:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:200:6. Ctrl-C twice (clean terminal restore: echo on, no stray escape codes).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:203:Record PASS/FAIL per cell, with a screenshot of the approval panel and the post-exit terminal state.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:211:### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:216:- Set `T2_TASKS` to the custodian-approved, sealed task directory and `T2_OUT` to a new, empty, run-specific output directory. Do not use the disclosed `eval/tasks` development set as held-out evidence. Preserve all three outputs and their manifests; never reuse an output directory for a retry.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:232:### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:246:### 6.3 T3 long tasks (ACC-QUAL-T3)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:298:1. An independent re-run of a sample. At minimum:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:310:**Output:** `docs/reviews/<date>-v1-rc-independent-acceptance.md` with an ACCEPT, ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS, or REJECT verdict per area. \"Accept with defects\" needs an owner disposition for every defect, and for a blocker area the only acceptable disposition is a fix.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:331:- [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:332:- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: CI, scripted and manual gates PASS.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:335:- [ ] §8 independent acceptance: ACCEPT, or ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS with owner dispositions and no blocker defects outstanding.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:337:- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:339:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker verifies source/tag/artifact/evidence hash bindings; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:341:- [ ] Release notes state the standalone scope (DEC-16), the provider tiers (DEC-06), the experimental surfaces (DEC-03, DEC-07) and the known limitations.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:344:After G6, complete source checks on the exact stable-version commit before tagging, then complete the stable artifact checks in §1.1 stage 5 before publishing the draft. A failure keeps publication blocked and requires remediation plus the applicable requalification; do not mark the campaign released until published artifacts are independently verified.\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:28:| Live cloud client | Checkout build `db1ca55` (`/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/dist`), using the operator's existing provider connections: ChatGPT via the Codex CLI sign-in; OpenRouter via the crush credential. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:46:| L1 | `nexus providers verify --provider chatgpt -m gpt-6-luna -j` | PASS: streamed completion, tool call, tool-result round trip | `8e910140…`, `1e6c5946…`, `d8595745…` | `evidence/live/verify_chatgpt.json` |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:47:| L2 | `nexus providers verify --provider openrouter -m openrouter/free -j` | PASS. The effective model varied per request (nemotron-3-super, then laguna-xs-2.1, then laguna-s-2.1), which shows `openrouter/free` is unsuitable for matched evaluation. | `49b71fc3…`, `b05711f6…`, `2b9cc6c5…` | `evidence/live/verify_openrouter.json` |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:58:| `evidence/B_providers.md` | Providers and inference | `prv/{probe,tls,err}.mts` against 127.0.0.1 mocks; 125/125 targeted tests |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:60:| `evidence/D_terminal.md` + `evidence/D_pty/` | Terminal | Real-PTY scripts s1–s9 and r1a–r1d against `mockgw.py`; `pyte` screen dumps |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:71:2. **Live provider receipts** were written to `<scratch>/live/.nexus/` and `<scratch>/live/ws1/.nexus/`, not to the repository.\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:97:- **No product qualification exists.** \"Blocked\" is established, from reproduced defects. \"Qualified\" cannot be: there is no held-out, fault-injection or standalone evidence, and the tasks used in the historical pilot were tuned.\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:104:- **Independence:** this audit is one reviewer's evidence pass, assisted by scoped sub-audits from the same reviewer. It is **not** an independent acceptance.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":41973}},"started_at_ms":1792884341960,"completed_at_ms":1792884341960}}
