\\\"\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Post Run actions/checkout@11d5960a326750d5838078e36cf38b85af677262\\\",\\\"number\\\":36,\\\"startedAt\\\":\\\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"pending\\\"}],\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40130531444/job/120981094860\\\"}],\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\",\\\"updatedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T20:36:28Z\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40130531444\\\"}\\n\"},{\"name\":\"pr200-events\",\"exit_code\":0,\"output\":\"{\\\"baseRefOid\\\":\\\"29eab4cd58051a8210b5ef66e0c9e248b2046a13\\\",\\\"commits\\\":[{\\\"authoredDate\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T05:23:25Z\\\",\\\"authors\\\":[{\\\"email\\\":\\\"mike@holownych.com\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\\\",\\\"login\\\":\\\"mikeholownych\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Mike Holownych\\\"}],\\\"committedDate\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T19:03:04Z\\\",\\\"messageBody\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"messageHeadline\\\":\\\"fix(git): verify nexus state exclusions\\\",\\\"oid\\\":\\\"70507de1081dfe0bf64c57fc5e82a1df0bed2bbb\\\"},{\\\"authoredDate\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T17:35:00Z\\\",\\\"authors\\\":[{\\\"email\\\":\\\"mike@holownych.com\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\\\",\\\"login\\\":\\\"mikeholownych\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Mike Holownych\\\"}],\\\"committedDate\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T19:03:05Z\\\",\\\"messageBody\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"messageHeadline\\\":\\\"fix(git): avoid duplicate ineffective exclusion rules\\\",\\\"oid\\\":\\\"646964b8a95bd4c5c259fcffa76b90a539b142c6\\\"},{\\\"authoredDate\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T17:52:25Z\\\",\\\"authors\\\":[{\\\"email\\\":\\\"mike@holownych.com\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\\\",\\\"login\\\":\\\"mikeholownych\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Mike Holownych\\\"}],\\\"committedDate\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T19:03:06Z\\\",\\\"messageBody\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"messageHeadline\\\":\\\"fix(git): preserve explicit Nexus exclude rules\\\",\\\"oid\\\":\\\"0bddc7c2504ff81d7943ee5e75e0473705220fd7\\\"},{\\\"authoredDate\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T18:36:06Z\\\",\\\"authors\\\":[{\\\"email\\\":\\\"mike@holownych.com\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\\\",\\\"login\\\":\\\"mikeholownych\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Mike Holownych\\\"}],\\\"committedDate\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T19:03:06Z\\\",\\\"messageBody\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"messageHeadline\\\":\\\"fix(git): defer exclusion write until needed\\\",\\\"oid\\\":\\\"4d7a5966bef9dbdc90424e09afa2bcb1c48029f6\\\"},{\\\"authoredDate\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T18:56:30Z\\\",\\\"authors\\\":[{\\\"email\\\":\\\"mike@holownych.com\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\\\",\\\"login\\\":\\\"mikeholownych\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Mike Holownych\\\"}],\\\"committedDate\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T19:03:07Z\\\",\\\"messageBody\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"messageHeadline\\\":\\\"fix(git): self-ignore Nexus state safely\\\",\\\"oid\\\":\\\"6352d839dda51a23bdaf6cd4e95c109da727150a\\\"},{\\\"authoredDate\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T19:05:46Z\\\",\\\"authors\\\":[{\\\"email\\\":\\\"mike@holownych.com\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\\\",\\\"login\\\":\\\"mikeholownych\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Mike Holownych\\\"}],\\\"committedDate\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T19:05:46Z\\\",\\\"messageBody\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"messageHeadline\\\":\\\"fix(worktree): ignore state from repository root\\\",\\\"oid\\\":\\\"5068bcf8898267e3c4320ff86ebb808384be6497\\\"},{\\\"authoredDate\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T19:07:25Z\\\",\\\"authors\\\":[{\\\"email\\\":\\\"mike@holownych.com\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\\\",\\\"login\\\":\\\"mikeholownych\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Mike Holownych\\\"}],\\\"committedDate\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T19:07:25Z\\\",\\\"messageBody\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"messageHeadline\\\":\\\"test(worktree): clean up nested workspace fixture\\\",\\\"oid\\\":\\\"a568a0da3c032576e7dbb96f02cbfddbcd61bcc3\\\"},{\\\"authoredDate\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T20:34:36Z\\\",\\\"authors\\\":[{\\\"email\\\":\\\"mike@holownych.com\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\\\",\\\"login\\\":\\\"mikeholownych\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Mike Holownych\\\"}],\\\"committedDate\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T20:34:36Z\\\",\\\"messageBody\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"messageHeadline\\\":\\\"fix(fs): avoid unsafe cleanup after path swap\\\",\\\"oid\\\":\\\"81928bd81d10ec957a3063a0e414aef981c83b20\\\"}],\\\"headRefOid\\\":\\\"81928bd81d10ec957a3063a0e414aef981c83b20\\\",\\\"latestReviews\\\":[],\\\"mergeStateStatus\\\":\\\"BLOCKED\\\",\\\"reviews\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"PRR_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABUB9JAQ\\\",\\\"author\\\":{\\\"login\\\":\\\"mikeholownych\\\"},\\\"authorAssociation\\\":\\\"OWNER\\\",\\\"body\\\":\\\"### Independent Review: ACCEPT\\\\n\\\\n- **Target Head**: `18abef6e6e43d3b1a23f761128f808a5cd2bc7f5`\\\\n- **Base Commit**: `41b381ddac182b7f0c783b33df5f1355518f465b` (`origin/main`)\\\\n- **Safe Change Boundary**: `cli/src/core/git_exclude.ts` and `cli/test/git_exclude.test.ts`.\\\\n\\\\n#### Findings & Verification\\\\n1. **Idempotent Fail-Closed Git Exclusion**:\\\\n   - `ensureGitExclude` checks `isIgnored` using `git check-ignore --quiet --no-index`.\\\\n   - If an exact exclusion rule already exists in `info/exclude` without subsequent negation lines, but Git still reports the path as not ignored (e.g., overridden by a higher-priority repository ignore rule such as in `.gitignore`), it immediately fails closed by throwing an error without continually appending duplicate useless rules to `info/exclude`.\\\\n   - If a subsequent negation (`!`) is present in `info/exclude`, it appends the verified positive rule to re-establish exclusion and validates ignore status.\\\\n2. **Local Regression Testing**:\\\\n   - Verified in isolated worktree with sandboxed `$HOME`/`$XDG_CONFIG_HOME`:\\\\n     - `test/git_exclude.test.ts` (8/8): **PASS** (1.03s).\\\\n     - `tsc --noEmit`: **PASS** (0 errors).\\\\n3. **Static & Integrity Checks**:\\\\n   - `git diff --check`: **PASS** (0 whitespace anomalies).\\\\n   - Clean 3-way merge against `origin/main` (`41b381d`): **CLEAN** (`141a1df2122886d1d7a4c9fa71c64668153ff058`).\\\\n4. **Hosted CI**:\\\\n   - CodeQL Run [40116819484](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40116819484): **`✓ SUCCESS`** in 1m14s.\\\\n   - CI Run [40116819381](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40116819381): active.\\\\n\\\\n**Disposition**: **ACCEPT**.\\\",\\\"submittedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T17:42:47Z\\\",\\\"includesCreatedEdit\\\":false,\\\"reactionGroups\\\":[],\\\"state\\\":\\\"COMMENTED\\\",\\\"commit\\\":{\\\"oid\\\":\\\"18abef6e6e43d3b1a23f761128f808a5cd2bc7f5\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"PRR_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABUCDT_A\\\",\\\"author\\\":{\\\"login\\\":\\\"mikeholownych\\\"},\\\"authorAssociation\\\":\\\"OWNER\\\",\\\"body\\\":\\\"### Independent Review: ACCEPT (Updated Head `56bc1dc`)\\\\n\\\\n- **Target Head**: `56bc1dcef066bae949e7ebe04346a45cb60bf362`\\\\n- **Base Commit**: `676abb371c8c91970af6d920d5c516497e3ccdef` (`origin/main`)\\\\n- **Safe Change Boundary**: `cli/src/core/git_exclude.ts` and `cli/test/git_exclude.test.ts`.\\\\n\\\\n#### Findings & Verification\\\\n1. **Preserved Explicit Subpath Exclusions**:\\\\n   - Condition updated to `if (hasExactRule && isIgnored(relativePath)) continue;`, ensuring that explicit rules for `.nexus/worktrees/` and `.nexus/flights/` are always written even when Git's parent path resolution already considers them covered by `.nexus/`.\\\\n   - Idempotency and fail-closed protections are fully maintained: if `hasExactRule` is true and a non-negated rule still fails to ignore the target (e.g., due to repository-level `.gitignore` override), it fails closed without growing `info/exclude`.\\\\n2. **Local Regression Testing**:\\\\n   - Verified in isolated worktree with sandboxed `$HOME`/`$XDG_CONFIG_HOME`:\\\\n     - `test/flight_exclude.test.ts` (3/3): **PASS** (WorktreeManager exclusions and idempotency verified).\\\\n     - `test/git_exclude.test.ts` (8/8): **PASS** (11/11 total tests across suites in 2.61s).\\\\n     - `tsc --noEmit`: **PASS** (0 errors).\\\\n3. **Static & Integrity Checks**:\\\\n   - `git diff --check`: **PASS** (0 whitespace anomalies).\\\\n   - Clean 3-way merge against `origin/main` (`676abb3`): **CLEAN** (`ac3e5d3856f364e5f17aedef12d7c881f9aa009b`).\\\\n4. **Hosted CI**:\\\\n   - CodeQL Run [40118387755](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40118387755): **`✓ SUCCESS`** in 1m14s.\\\\n   - CI Run [40118387758](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40118387758): active.\\\\n\\\\n**Disposition**: **ACCEPT**.\\\",\\\"submittedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T18:01:15Z\\\",\\\"includesCreatedEdit\\\":false,\\\"reactionGroups\\\":[],\\\"state\\\":\\\"COMMENTED\\\",\\\"commit\\\":{\\\"oid\\\":\\\"56bc1dcef066bae949e7ebe04346a45cb60bf362\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"PRR_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABUCKBlg\\\",\\\"author\\\":{\\\"login\\\":\\\"mikeholownych\\\"},\\\"authorAssociation\\\":\\\"OWNER\\\",\\\"body\\\":\\\"### Independent Review: ACCEPT (Rebased Head `89d7416`)\\\\n\\\\n- **Target Head**: `89d7416fc5a54e3d0d9fd43d70192f12c540f93f`\\\\n- **Base Commit**: `4adc61ac98616c5e1dccaf6065e7f2332443d468` (`origin/main`)\\\\n- **Safe Change Boundary**: `cli/src/core/git_exclude.ts` and `cli/test/git_exclude.test.ts`.\\\\n\\\\n#### Findings & Verification\\\\n1. **Rebase Integrity**:\\\\n   - Clean rebase onto `main@4adc61a`, resolving base divergence after merge of PR #199.\\\\n   - Preserves all 11 explicit Nexus exclude tests, idempotence assertions, and `hasExactRule && isIgnored` logic.\\\\n2. **Static & Integrity Checks**:\\\\n   - `git diff…3752 tokens truncated…eenshot of the approval panel and the post-exit terminal state.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:211:### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:216:- Set `T2_TASKS` to the custodian-approved, sealed task directory and `T2_OUT` to a new, empty, run-specific output directory. Do not use the disclosed `eval/tasks` development set as held-out evidence. Preserve all three outputs and their manifests; never reuse an output directory for a retry.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:232:### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:246:### 6.3 T3 long tasks (ACC-QUAL-T3)\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:298:1. An independent re-run of a sample. At minimum:\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:310:**Output:** `docs/reviews/<date>-v1-rc-independent-acceptance.md` with an ACCEPT, ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS, or REJECT verdict per area. \\\"Accept with defects\\\" needs an owner disposition for every defect, and for a blocker area the only acceptable disposition is a fix.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:331:- [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:332:- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: CI, scripted and manual gates PASS.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:335:- [ ] §8 independent acceptance: ACCEPT, or ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS with owner dispositions and no blocker defects outstanding.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:337:- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:339:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker verifies source/tag/artifact/evidence hash bindings; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:341:- [ ] Release notes state the standalone scope (DEC-16), the provider tiers (DEC-06), the experimental surfaces (DEC-03, DEC-07) and the known limitations.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:344:After G6, complete source checks on the exact stable-version commit before tagging, then complete the stable artifact checks in §1.1 stage 5 before publishing the draft. A failure keeps publication blocked and requires remediation plus the applicable requalification; do not mark the campaign released until published artifacts are independently verified.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:28:| Live cloud client | Checkout build `db1ca55` (`/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/dist`), using the operator's existing provider connections: ChatGPT via the Codex CLI sign-in; OpenRouter via the crush credential. |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:46:| L1 | `nexus providers verify --provider chatgpt -m gpt-6-luna -j` | PASS: streamed completion, tool call, tool-result round trip | `8e910140…`, `1e6c5946…`, `d8595745…` | `evidence/live/verify_chatgpt.json` |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:47:| L2 | `nexus providers verify --provider openrouter -m openrouter/free -j` | PASS. The effective model varied per request (nemotron-3-super, then laguna-xs-2.1, then laguna-s-2.1), which shows `openrouter/free` is unsuitable for matched evaluation. | `49b71fc3…`, `b05711f6…`, `2b9cc6c5…` | `evidence/live/verify_openrouter.json` |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:58:| `evidence/B_providers.md` | Providers and inference | `prv/{probe,tls,err}.mts` against 127.0.0.1 mocks; 125/125 targeted tests |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:60:| `evidence/D_terminal.md` + `evidence/D_pty/` | Terminal | Real-PTY scripts s1–s9 and r1a–r1d against `mockgw.py`; `pyte` screen dumps |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:71:2. **Live provider receipts** were written to `<scratch>/live/.nexus/` and `<scratch>/live/ws1/.nexus/`, not to the repository.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:97:- **No product qualification exists.** \\\"Blocked\\\" is established, from reproduced defects. \\\"Qualified\\\" cannot be: there is no held-out, fault-injection or standalone evidence, and the tasks used in the historical pilot were tuned.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:104:- **Independence:** this audit is one reviewer's evidence pass, assisted by scoped sub-audits from the same reviewer. It is **not** an independent acceptance.\\n\"},{\"name\":\"release-claim-log\",\"exit_code\":0,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 8826)\\nTotal output lines: 80\\n\\n2026-10-24T19:36:11.978863Z POST_CONTEST_DEPENDENCY_REVIEW head=62bf74e4b37c5a8f1a4be33c208d72dc9e15ec4e base=29eab4cd58051a8210b5ef66e0c9e248b2046a13 reviewer=plan05_readonly_review disposition=ACCEPT diff_sha256=ef709167ad941135e3fb2a06ba749bd36c5de4e2d17f2be6780d61ae8d73e8aa.\\n2026-10-24T19:40:00Z SUITE_RELEASE codex-root snapshot=a568a0da3c032576e7dbb96f02cbfddbcd61bcc3; make test progressed through Rust tests and into CLI suite, then session ended with exit 130 and many later Node test files reported Promise resolution pending/event loop resolved; disposition IN