{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T23:32:06.946Z","ordinal":313854,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-6c6f95d1-e506-41f6-8055-68acba1cb01f","process_id":"17934","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n \"ACC-SAFE-01|ACC-SAFE-09|ACC-SAFE-10|trusted and untrusted|script body|verifier|startup_trust\" cli/test docs/v1.0.0/evidence docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | head -180; rg -n \"test:cli/test/(approval_policy|verifier_gating|harness|.*repl.*approval)\" docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'ACC-SAFE-01|ACC-SAFE-09|ACC-SAFE-10|trusted and untrusted|script body|verifier|startup_trust' cli/test docs/v1.0.0/evidence docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md","query":"ACC-SAFE-01|ACC-SAFE-09|ACC-SAFE-10|trusted and untrusted|script body|verifier|startup_trust","path":"test"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'test:cli/test/(approval_policy|verifier_gating|harness|.*repl.*approval)' docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md","query":"test:cli/test/(approval_policy|verifier_gating|harness|.*repl.*approval)","path":"REQUIREMENTS.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:91:| Safety | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-10 | SPEC-01 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:301:   - ACC-SAFE-01, 03, 09;\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:56:| REQ-AGT-002 | quickstart; TOP_TIER B3; EXEC-005 | Truthful outcome taxonomy. VERIFIED requires a passing, deliverable-bound verifier run, plus fail-before/pass-after independence for discovered verifiers. UNVERIFIED, REGRESSION_FREE, BLOCKED and LIMIT_REACHED are distinct, with exit codes 0/2/1/130. | `agent.ts:5726-5764`; `tester.ts:371-430,541-627`; `turn.ts:318-351` | TEST at db1ca55; candidate suite at `6151a23` passes ACC-VER-03/04/09 regression tests. Historical VER-04/05 findings and tuned-set/live evidence remain in [A2_verification.md](evidence/A2_verification.md) and the dated evidence files. | partial | N | M5 false-VERIFIED threshold remains unqualified pending held-out T2/T3/T4 evidence; historical VER-04/05 implementation defects have regression coverage at the candidate. | ACC-VER-03/04/09, ACC-QUAL-T2 | B | SPEC-11 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:119:| REQ-SEC-101 | Audit; DEC-01 (amended 2026-10-24) | Without operator opt-in, model-initiated exec and egress require the configured permission decision. Folder trust does not select or change approval mode; unset mode defaults to review. | safety | `config.ts`, `sidecar.ts`, `repl.ts`, `index.ts`, `core/approval_policy.ts` | TEST `test:cli/test/approval_policy.test.ts::\"REQ-SEC-101: the unset mode stays review in trusted and untrusted workspaces\"`; `test:cli/test/config.test.ts::\"workspace trust does not select the tool approval mode\"`; PTY ACC-SAFE-01 still pending | partial | ACC-SAFE-01 | **B** | SEC-01, TUI-07 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:122:| REQ-SEC-119 | Audit; DEC-01 (amended 2026-10-24) | Nexus-initiated verifier runs are `exec` class and follow configured permission mode; review requires a one-time approval showing the script body. Folder trust alone does not authorize execution; all runs are routed through the runner. | safety | `agent.ts:1654,3544,4255`; `tester.ts:145`; `verifier_gating.test.ts` | TEST `test:cli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts::\"trusted and untrusted repos in review mode prompt for verifier and script body, write sentinel only after approval, and cache session decision\"`; `test:cli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts::\"denied verifier does not execute verifier and sentinel is not written\"`; `test:cli/test/harness.test.ts::\"run_tests keeps repository test side effects inside worktree authority and honors read-only, dry-run, and required sandbox\"`; PTY ACC-SAFE-09/10 still pending | partial | ACC-SAFE-09, ACC-SAFE-10 | **B** | VER-01, VER-14 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:152:| REQ-AGT-116 | Audit | One verifier selector. `run_tests` uses the verifier deadline. | consistency | `tester.ts:19-145`; `tools.ts:1119` | TEST (VER-06; test:cli/test/verification_binding.test.ts::\"ACC-VER-05: discoverVerifier and run_tests return no verifier for Makefile with only pytest: or empty workspace\") | tested | ACC-VER-05 | RR | VER-06 | SPEC-11 / PLAN-11 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:19:| REQ-AGT-05 | EXEC-005 | Model claims/TDD indicators never confer merge authority; authoritative verifier required | P2 §5 | DEMONSTRATED | P | Contradicted 10-12 (A1 false VERIFIED); remediated 3290234/fe576f1; eval rerun 4add897 \"0 false VERIFIED\" (n small) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:33:| REQ-AGT-25..28 | CAND-001..004 | Receipt {candidateId,verifier,status,ts}; invalidate on candidate mutation; merge requires identity equality; clean target root | P2 §11 | DEMONSTRATED (core/candidate.ts; candidate.test) | P (WP04) | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:64:| REQ-AGT-51 | Q2/B3/A1 | VERIFIED only with change-bound, Nexus-independent evidence; else REGRESSION_FREE (exit 2); requirements `verified` only from bound verifier run | TOP_TIER B3; USER_MANUAL §2 Outcomes | Implemented 3290234, fe576f1 (fail-before/pass-after), eval rerun 0 false VERIFIED | N (eval self-run) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:82:| REQ-DX-02 | Outcome honesty | \"VERIFIED only when its selected verifier passes\"; UNVERIFIED/BLOCKED/LIMIT_REACHED distinct | quickstart.md:57 | (as REQ-AGT-51) | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:238:- **Public promises:** one-line installer pinned to v0.1.0-alpha.2 with SHA-256 verification, no root; Linux x86-64 glibc≥2.35 + Node≥20 only; OpenAI-compatible local endpoint first (LM Studio/vLLM), cloud opt-in; honest outcome labels (VERIFIED only from passing verifier); no default step ceiling; secrets tokenized on egress; workspace code needs trust; uninstall keeps user data. Maturity explicitly \"alpha, pre-1.0\".\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:23:| Tests: parser_safety, evaluator, verification_binding, verifier_timeout, independent_verification, candidate, task_class, build_identity | run: 54 tests, 53 pass. The 1 failure is environmental (snap is not a git repo, so build_identity.test.ts:16 `git` fails) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:32:  - pending changes, verifier FAILED or TIMED_OUT → NOT_ESTABLISHED\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:33:  - verifier PASSED and not deliverable-bound → REGRESSION_FREE\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:34:  - discovered verifier, bound, not independent → REGRESSION_FREE\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:35:  - configured verifier and bound, or discovered and bound and independent (fail-before/pass-after with Nexus's own test edits set aside, agent.ts:1622-1638) → VERIFIED\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:36:- **Timeouts.** The oracle and the baseline use `verifierTimeoutSecs`, default 300 s (agent.ts:149), enforced by the runner. A timeout is never a pass (tester.ts:193; verifier_timeout.test.ts passes). The `run_tests` tool hard-codes 120 s (tools.ts:594). `/test` and `nexus eval` use host `execSync` with a 120 s limit, which blocks the event loop (tester.ts:151-156).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:52:| VER-01 | S2 | Any session on a cloned/untrusted repo, including `--approve` review mode | agent.ts:1602-1617 (baseline), 3432-3436 (oracle), 1630 (independence copy run); tester.ts:113-136 | SOURCE. Before the first file edit (agent.ts:4034, after the edit's own approval) and at every `task_completed`, Nexus runs `make test` / `npm test` / `cargo test` / `pytest` through `bridge.executeTool` directly. These run arbitrary repo-defined code with no approval prompt and no workspace-trust check (unlike MCP/plugins, workspace_trust.ts), and unsandboxed unless `--sandbox`. Review mode shows an approval for `edit_file` but never for the hidden repo script that follows. Builds on SEC-01; it is a separate path because it bypasses even review mode. | Cloning a hostile repo and asking for any edit runs its test script on the host without a prompt. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: gate discovered verifiers on workspace trust or a one-time approval of the exact command (shown with its script body), and run them sandboxed when one is available. Document this. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:55:| VER-04 | S2 | Configured-verifier VERIFIED claims; discovered-verifier coverage | tester.ts:356-360 | RUNTIME (tester_probe). `isVerifierDeliverableBound` matches basenames by substring against the command and the output. If `src/a.ts` changed and the output mentions `src/data.ts`, the run counts as bound. If `README.md` changed and the output says \"see README.md\", it counts as bound. Any changed file under `test/` binds the whole change. With a configured verifier, bound means VERIFIED (agent.ts:5124-5146, no independence check). | VERIFIED can rest on a filename coincidence instead of coverage. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: match whole path tokens (boundary-delimited relative paths). Drop basename matching or require a path separator before it. Require a test-path change to be accompanied by executed tests from that file. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:56:| VER-05 | S3 | Zero-test or all-skipped verifier runs | tester.ts:263-282; agent.ts:5126-5135 | RUNTIME (tester_probe). An exit-0 run with no executed tests is labelled REGRESSION_FREE (\"did not cover the modified deliverables\"), and it discharges the unverified-changes obligation (agent.ts:3520). Zero tests is no regression evidence. `hasExecutedTests` false positives: node:test \"ℹ tests 5\" with all skipped → true; jest \"5 skipped, 5 total\" → true; any output line starting `ok ` (go heuristic, e.g. \"ok all good\") → true. False negatives (conservative): mocha \"3 passing\", vitest \"Tests 5 passed (5)\". | REGRESSION_FREE overstates evidence. Exit code 2 is shared with UNVERIFIED, so the automation impact is limited. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: a pass with `!hasExecutedTests` → UNVERIFIED (reason NO_TESTS_EXECUTED), keeping the obligation. Subtract skipped counts. Anchor the go heuristic to `ok\\s+\\S+\\s+(\\d+\\.\\d+s|\\(cached\\))`. Add mocha/vitest parsers. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:57:| VER-06 | S3 | `run_tests` tool, `/test`, TDD, `nexus eval` | tester.ts:21-78 vs 109-138; tools.ts:589; agent.ts:4067-4090 | RUNTIME (tester_probe). `detectTestCommand` diverges from `discoverVerifier`. A Makefile containing only `pytest:` gives `make test` (discover: null). A repo with no manifest gives `npm test` (discover: null). `run_tests` results are recorded as objective verifier attempts under that command, so a nonsense FAILED attempt can mark a requirement's verification failed. `run_tests` uses a fixed 120 s instead of the verifier deadline. | Wrong command runs and is recorded. Long suites time out under run_tests but pass under the oracle. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: one selector (discoverVerifier plus filter); run_tests returns \"no verifier\" when there is none; use `verifierTimeoutSecs`. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:59:| VER-08 | S2 | `--tdd` / `/tdd` | synthesizer.ts:239-326; agent.ts:5236-5255 | SOURCE + INFERENCE. `runAutonomousTdd` never calls `verifyRedPhase` or `verifyGreenPhase`, ignores every `agent.run` result, and contains dead code (266-272). Success is only a full-suite exit 0, with no check that tests executed. Each `agent.run` calls `resetConversation()` (AGT-01), so GREEN starts with no memory of the RED test. The RED prompt asks the model to call `task_completed` with a deliberately failing test, but the completion oracle runs the discovered verifier, which fails → completion refused (INFERENCE). The success summary claims \"RED -> GREEN -> REFACTOR verified\". | The TDD mode advertises a protocol it does not enforce. RED turns likely end in NOT_ESTABLISHED or stagnation. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: enforce the phases (run the repro target and require fail, then pass), carry the conversation between phases, exempt the RED phase from the completion oracle; or mark the mode experimental. Add an e2e test with a mock model. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:65:| VER-14 | S3 | `/test`, `nexus eval` | tester.ts:143-163; repl.ts:1357; slash/workspace_commands.ts:160 | SOURCE. `runTestSuite` uses host `execSync` with a 120 s limit. It bypasses the configured sandbox and the Rust runner, blocks the event loop (no cancel, TUI frozen), and kills only the shell on timeout, not the process tree. | Freezes for up to 2 min. Sandbox users get an unsandboxed run. | Route through the bridge executor with the verifier deadline. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:110:- Pass/fail is exit-code based on the runner envelope. Unknown output is not a pass, and a timeout is never a pass (tester.ts:179-193; verifier_timeout.test.ts).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:112:- Discovered-verifier VERIFIED requires fail-before/pass-after independence, re-running the pre-change tests against the changed code (agent.ts:1622-1638; independent_verification.test.ts).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:113:- Identical-input failed verifiers are not rerun, and the reason is recorded (agent.ts:3412-3428).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:114:- Filtered verifier commands are recognised and cannot clear the full requirement (tester.ts:232-257; core/objective.ts:375).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:128:- **Candidate identity and gitignored inputs.** Confirm that `mutationSeq` and `externalInputsFingerprint` change when only an ignored file (e.g. `.env`) is edited by `run_command`, so a failed verifier is rerun.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:134:| R-VER-1 | Repo-defined verifier commands (discovered) run only in a trusted workspace or after one approval that shows the command and script body. They run sandboxed when a sandbox is available. | safety | RELEASE-REQUIRED | An untrusted temp repo with `\"test\":\"touch /tmp/pwn\"` plus an edit request: no file created without a prompt, in both default and --approve modes. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:137:| R-VER-4 | A passing verifier that executed zero (non-skipped) tests yields UNVERIFIED (NO_TESTS_EXECUTED) and keeps the obligation. | workflow/honesty | RELEASE-REQUIRED | `npm test` = `node -e 0`, after an edit gives outcome UNVERIFIED. node:test all-skipped gives UNVERIFIED. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:139:| R-VER-6 | A single verifier selector everywhere (run_tests, /test, TDD, eval, oracle), with no `npm test` fallback, using the verifier deadline and the bridge executor. | workflow/failure | RELEASE-REQUIRED | Empty repo: run_tests reports \"no verifier\" and records no attempt. /test is cancellable and honours --sandbox. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:151:- `HOME=scratchpad/a2home timeout 600 node_modules/.bin/tsx --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-reporter=spec test/{parser_safety,evaluator,verification_binding,verifier_timeout,independent_verification,candidate,task_class,build_identity}.test.ts` gave 54 tests: 53 pass, 1 environmental failure.\ncli/test/provider_connect.test.ts:130:  test(\"OpenRouter PKCE: callback code + verifier are exchanged for a user key\", async () => {\ncli/test/provider_connect.test.ts:133:      json(res, ok ? 200 : 400, ok ? { key: \"sk-or-ISSUED\", verifier: s.body.code_verifier } : { error: \"bad\" });\ncli/test/provider_connect.test.ts:143:      const verifier = m.seen[0].body.code_verifier;\ncli/test/provider_connect.test.ts:144:      assert.equal(createHash(\"sha256\").update(verifier).digest(\"base64url\"), challenge, \"PKCE S256 holds\");\ncli/test/provider_connect.test.ts:165:      assert.match(m.seen[0].body, /code_verifier=/);\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:34:- Verification gate lives in the `task_completed` handler (3345-3571): open/blocked requirements refuse; configured or discovered verifier runs; prior FAILED on identical inputs is not rerun; discovered-verifier pass is VERIFIED only with fail-before/pass-after independence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:45:| AGT-02 | S2 | `/team`, `nexus operation run/resume` (work units) | agent.ts:3081 (`durableUnit = this.depth === 0`), 3127, 1136-1139, 4389, 1489-1501; operation_runner.ts:559 | SOURCE + DOC-CLAIM. Work units run as `new AutonomousAgent(config, 1)` and ARE durable (resumed via `recoverFromTaskState`), but every depth-gated rule treats depth 1 as a non-durable in-turn subagent: (a) compaction is applied in memory only — no archive append, no checkpoint, never `PERSISTENCE_FAILED`; the next `persistProgress` then writes the compacted conversation and a `committedCompactions` id that has no archive lines, so originals are lost and `read_archive` cannot return them after resume (contradicts COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:145-160 \"Every compaction ... is committed in a fixed order\"); (b) no objective ledger: no requirement gating, no steering, `update_requirements`/`read_objective` not offered; (c) `ExecutionTracker.fresh()` per turn, so loop/stagnation history and cumulative steps reset at every resume/retry; (d) no change baseline / independence judgement (`captureChangeBaseline` depth 0 only, 4034) so discovered-verifier passes are at best REGRESSION_FREE. `runningAsSubagent` already distinguishes the two cases (5003). | Long team/operation units lose compaction originals and convergence history across resume; doc claims overstate durability. | Gate on `runningAsSubagent` (non-durable) instead of `depth`; add a work-unit compaction+resume test asserting archive lines exist. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:81:- Outcome honesty: `buildTurnResult` is the single derivation; invariants forbid VERIFIED/REGRESSION_FREE without PASSED evidence and NOT_REQUIRED with pending changes (turn.ts:318-351). Discovered-verifier passes need fail-before/pass-after independence for VERIFIED (agent.ts:3447, 5136-5145); non-covering passes are REGRESSION_FREE (5126-5135); read-only answers resting on compacted-away output are UNVERIFIED/CONTEXT_EVIDENCE_NOT_RETAINED (5165-5171). `verified` requirements must bind a passing, unfiltered, deliverable-bound, independent run (objective.ts applyRequirementUpdates).\ncli/test/tui_surface_e2e.test.ts:77:      // Finishing through task_completed runs the workspace verifier, which fails once parser.js exists.\ncli/test/tui_surface_e2e.test.ts:96:    // The verifier the agent discovers: fails only once parser.js exists, so earlier edits verify.\ncli/test/evaluator.test.ts:74:      verifierCommand: \"npm test\",\ncli/test/verifier_timeout.test.ts:2: * D3: tool/verifier timeout lifecycle.\ncli/test/verifier_timeout.test.ts:8: *  - the completion verifier has an explicit, configurable deadline and reports VERIFIER_TIMED_OUT\ncli/test/verifier_timeout.test.ts:42:  test(\"verifier result mapping: timeout, ordinary failure and success are three distinct states\", async () => {\ncli/test/verifier_timeout.test.ts:85:    const agent = mute(new AutonomousAgent({ endpoint: gw.url, model: \"m\", maxSteps: 5, temperature: 0, workspace: ws, shell: \"bash\", verifierTimeoutSecs: deadline, approvalMode: \"auto\", fullAccess: true } as any));\ncli/test/verifier_timeout.test.ts:97:  test(\"completion verifier: timeout is VERIFIER_TIMED_OUT with its deadline, distinct from failure, and leaves no process behind\", async () => {\ncli/test/verifier_timeout.test.ts:98:    const { out, cleanup } = await oracleRun(\"(bash -c 'sleep 28.77' &) ; echo verifier-started; sleep 28.77\", 1);\ncli/test/verifier_timeout.test.ts:100:      assert.ok(out.elapsed < 10, `verifier must stop at its deadline, took ${out.elapsed}s`);\ncli/test/verifier_tim