{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T23:35:26.567Z","ordinal":314005,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a17044-e866-7bd3-a1a5-26ba7f79829b","author":"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/current_main_rc_path_audit\nPayload:\n## Release-path audit\n\n**Exact source:** `origin/main` is `c1b13327edf5d3a0c82fb10eb814775fd4953a63`. Exact-main CI run `40140156370` and CodeQL run `40140156350` succeeded.\n\n**Pre-RC gate:** The requirements checker fails on this exact revision: 123 rows; 106 tested, 8 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open. The only enforcement failures are `REQ-SEC-101` and `REQ-SEC-119`, both below the required `tested` status. Their ledger entries say `ACC-SAFE-01` and `ACC-SAFE-09/10` PTY evidence remains pending. `ACCEPTANCE.md` §1.1 requires source-applicable gates and the bare enforcement check to pass before another RC. The 12 explicitly mapped qualification rows are deferred to exact-RC evidence; they are not accepted by that deferral.\n\n**Existing RC4:** The published `v1.0.0-rc.4` targets `57b9285c6cead27b2260bf3113b3fc0b847f8169`, an ancestor of current main. Release workflow `40090364770` succeeded; the archive digest is `07867e26077e5eec6f2cb665c4c34045a116669cacbe7f81f62f40b6fac8b806`. No RC4 qualification record or evidence directory is present.\n\n**Cross-runner gate:** Run `40103980794` rebuilt RC4 successfully on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04, but the comparison failed: the archives differ beginning at byte 19. This leaves `ACC-SUP-08` failed. Acceptance §1.1 places that artifact-bound check before installed-RC qualification. The root cause remains undetermined.\n\n**Other exact-RC evidence:**\n\n- **Provider:** The available record is for RC3, not RC4. It records ChatGPT and pinned OpenRouter verification as passed, while the required live OpenRouter task remains incomplete. No RC4 standalone/provider matrix evidence was found.\n- **Held-out:** The public custody report dated 2026-10-18 records acceptance of a 40-task manifest, but explicitly leaves evaluator-boundary acceptance and host/resource readiness open. It reports no qualification run. The latest readiness document is older than current main and reports runner incompatibility; no newer RC4 qualification evidence was found.\n- **Terminals:** The worksheet is blank. I verified the desktop at `10.0.8.3` has xterm, kitty, tmux 3.6, VS Code, GNOME Terminal, and an active GNOME/Xwayland session. This is setup evidence only: no matrix cells have been run or recorded. §5.3 still requires all five terminals at all three sizes with per-cell results and screenshots.\n\nThe lifecycle is explicit: clear source gates before a new RC; run RC artifact checks, including cross-runner reproducibility, before installed-RC qualification; then complete provider, standalone, held-out, terminal, installation, and independent acceptance gates. G6 and stable publication follow only after those pass. Current status remains **acceptance in progress**; no RC is accepted and no stable release is verified."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","create_time":1792884926.5669837}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":15876}}
