{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T23:35:54.250Z","ordinal":314023,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-f96283a8-64d9-4b1f-ad6f-b3c99705b4d5","process_id":"89318","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '35,135p' /home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md; sed -n '260,325p' /home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md; rg -n 'ACC-SAFE-01|ACC-SAFE-09|ACC-SAFE-10|manual|PTY' /home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01* /home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | head -160; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check status --short --branch; cat /home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/.git 2>/dev/null | head -c 200"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '35,135p' /home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md; sed -n '260,325p' /home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md; rg -n 'ACC-SAFE-01|ACC-SAFE-09|ACC-SAFE-10|manual|PTY' /home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01* /home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | head -160; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check status --short --branch; cat /home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/.git 2>/dev/null | head -c 200"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:START -->\n### Qualification-only requirements for exact-RC enforcement\n\n| Requirement | Acceptance criteria required in the exact-RC record | Remaining stage |\n|---|---|---|\n| REQ-REL-003 | ACC-PLAT | Installed-RC platform and Node-version matrix |\n| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\n| REQ-AGT-010 | ACC-TRUST-04 | Independent acceptance of the DEC-04 v1 subset |\n| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\n| REQ-REL-005 | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | Exact-RC security and dependency artifact checks |\n| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\n| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\n| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\n| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\n| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\n\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\n### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\n\n| Requirement | Approved decision | Scope |\n|---|---|---|\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:END -->\n\n## 1. Rules\n\n1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\n2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n3. Thresholds (DEC-05) are frozen before the first M5 run. A failing gate is fixed in code and the run is repeated as `rc.N+1`. A threshold is never relaxed after results are known.\n4. Evidence goes to `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. The directory contains:\n   - `manifest.json`: commit, package sha256, environment, model fingerprint, dates;\n   - raw outputs;\n   - a `SHA256SUMS` file.\n\n   Secrets are redacted before commit.\n5. Any step that cannot run in the available environment is recorded as **NOT RUN** with its reason. A NOT RUN on a blocker gate fails the gate.\n\n## 2. Environments\n\n| ID | Environment | Used for |\n|---|---|---|\n| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n\n## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\n\nEvery ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\n\n| Gate | Acceptance IDs | Spec |\n|---|---|---|\n| Safety | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-10 | SPEC-01 |\n| Process ownership | ACC-PROC-01 to ACC-PROC-08 (ACC-PROC-07 is the load test, run in E3) | SPEC-02 |\n| Untrusted inputs | ACC-TRUST-01 to ACC-TRUST-09 | SPEC-03 |\n| Continuity | ACC-CONT-01 to ACC-CONT-09 (ACC-CONT-10 is in §8) | SPEC-04 |\n| Inference | ACC-INF-01 to ACC-INF-09 (ACC-INF-10 is in §4) | SPEC-05 |\n| Packaging | ACC-PKG-01 to ACC-PKG-09 | SPEC-06 |\n| Supply chain | ACC-SUP-01 to ACC-SUP-08 (artifact-bound ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08 after RC construction) | SPEC-07 |\n| Persistence | ACC-PER-01 to ACC-PER-07 | SPEC-08 |\n| Governance | ACC-GOV-01 to ACC-GOV-06 | SPEC-09 |\n| Verification | ACC-VER-01 to ACC-VER-09 | SPEC-11 |\n| Upgrade | ACC-UPG-01 to ACC-UPG-14 | SPEC-12 |\n\n\n### 3.1 Acceptance IDs defined in this file\n\nThese are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\n\n| ID | Check | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\n| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\n| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\n| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\n| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\n| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\n| ACC-PLAT | E2 matrix, §7 | All rows pass. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\n\n## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n\n### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\n\n1. `export HOME=$(mktemp -d)`.\n2. Install the RC with the documented command.\n3. Create `~/.config/nexus/config.env` containing only:\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:<proxy>/v1`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=<id as listed by the proxy>`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=REDACTED\n\n   No gateway token file, no homelab paths, no `NODE_*` overrides.\n4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\n| T4 truthful outcome | = 100% |\n| T4 hang beyond budget + 5 min | = 0 |\n| T3 false-absence | = 0 |\n| T3 false-presence | = 0 |\n| T3 steering honoured | ≥ 95% |\n| Operator interventions in `run` mode | = 0 |\n\nThe scorer output `verdict.md` lists each metric with its Wilson 95% interval, along with the infrastructure reruns and the excluded contaminated runs.\n\n## 7. Install, upgrade, rollback, uninstall (ACC-PLAT; E2)\n\n| Case | Command | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| Fresh install, each image with Node ≥ 22 | Documented one-line command with `NEXUS_VERSION=<rc>`, then the no-version command after v1.0.0 is published | Installed. `nexus --version` equals the RC. `nexus doctor` shows no version warning and an empty stderr. |\n| No Node / Node 20 | Same | Clear prerequisite message before download or state change. HOME untouched. |\n| Upgrade alpha.2 → RC | Same, with the tag | Symlink swapped. Old version retained. User state intact. |\n| Rollback RC → alpha.2 | Same, with the old tag | Works. |\n| Repair | Delete a file in the version dir, then reinstall | Repaired (REQ-REL-105). Same-version reinstall preserves working files if package fails verification. |\n| Uninstall (documented manual) | Commands from the quickstart | Only Nexus-owned paths removed. `~/.config/nexus` and `~/.nexus` retained. |\n| Checksum tamper | installer-smoke | Refused. The existing install is unchanged. |\n| Attestation | `gh attestation verify <tarball> -R mikeholownych/nexus-code` | PASS |\n| Upgrade self-test failure | `nexus upgrade` (broken candidate package) | Refused. Staging verified before switch; if post-switch verification fails, launcher atomically rolls back to previous target and journal records `rolled_back`. |\n| Upgrade crash recovery | `nexus upgrade --recover` | Idempotent recovery. Cleans incomplete staging, restores unverified launcher symlink, verifies functional installation. |\n| Backup restore | `nexus upgrade --restore-backup <state-backup-directory>` | Snapshot of configuration and complete durable state restored from a recognized private backup directory (`backup.json`, `state/`, optional `config/`), with strict 0600 file / 0700 directory modes. A canonical `config.env.bak.*` path restores configuration only. Arbitrary files and tar archives are rejected. Run it through the stable `nexus` launcher; close existing legacy clients, then keep version-pinned legacy binaries and direct old entry points offline until the durable restore journal is cleared. |\n| Incompatible downgrade | `nexus upgrade --version <v> --allow-downgrade` (incompatible state schema) | Refused fail-closed with actionable state schema explanation. Existing installation unchanged. |\n\n## 8. Independent acceptance (REQ-AGT-110, ACC-CONT-10)\n\nThe reviewer is supplied by the owner (X5) and did not implement the work under review.\n\nThe reviewer receives:\n\n- the RC package;\n- this file;\n- the REQUIREMENTS ledger;\n- SPEC-04;\n- read access to the evidence directory.\n\nThe reviewer performs:\n\n1. An independent re-run of a sample. At minimum:\n   - ACC-SAFE-01, 03, 09;\n   - ACC-PROC-02;\n   - ACC-TRUST-01, 02;\n   - ACC-CONT-01, 03;\n   - ACC-VER-01, 03;\n   - ACC-PKG-01;\n   - 5 random T2 tasks;\n   - 2 T4 classes.\n2. One live long task (≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions) on the RC through the gateway, including one kill and resume.\n3. A review of the scorer verdict and of contamination handling.\n\n**Output:** `docs/reviews/<date>-v1-rc-independent-acceptance.md` with an ACCEPT, ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS, or REJECT verdict per area. \"Accept with defects\" needs an owner disposition for every defect, and for a blocker area the only acceptable disposition is a fix.\n\n## 9. Contest (separate product; not a client gate)\n\nThe contest submission is complete and judging has concluded. No contest freeze applies (DEC-13 status amendment); post-contest hardening is tracked separately from client v1.0.0 acceptance and is accepted by:\n\n| ID | Check |\n|---|---|\n| CON-A1 | Ordinary maintained package/experiment checks build `agent-collab-worker`. `worker.config.json` has the configured name, and the bundle contains the `/work-state` handler. Do not restore the retired `cloudflare-contest-contract` status check. |\n| CON-A2 | Broker negative tests: caller-supplied env paths and URLs are ignored. A host outside `*.artifacts.cloudflare.net` is refused. |\n| CON-A3 | On a clean VM, `install.sh --fresh` followed by `post-install-qualify.py` passes. |\n| CON-A4 | `sudo -l` for the demo user shows only fixed argv. `sudo setpriv --reuid=0 id` is denied. |\n| CON-A5 | One clean-account `--mode cloudflare --agents real` run, with a committed, redacted run record. |\n| CON-A6 | The video source commits are tagged and published, or the docs state that they are unpublished. |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:10:| Acceptance | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-06 in [ACCEPTANCE.md](../ACCEPTANCE.md) |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:30:- A lone Enter approves the action (TUI-02, reproduced in a PTY).\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:48:| TUI-02 Enter approves | RUNTIME (PTY r1a) | evidence/D_terminal.md §4 |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:49:| TUI-03 typed-ahead approves | RUNTIME (PTY r1d) | D §4 |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:52:| TUI guard strength | RUNTIME (PTY s2/s3) | D §5 |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:170:| ACC-SAFE-01 | Fresh HOME; run `nexus` and `nexus repl` in both trusted and untrusted fixture workspaces with explicit `--mode review` and `--mode auto`. A mock gateway calls `run_command \"echo x > ../outside\"`: review asks in both folders; auto permits according to the configured execution boundary in both folders. With no mode configured, both folders default to review. Trust affects only project instruction/integration loading. | PTY |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:172:| ACC-SAFE-03 | REPL PTY: lone Enter → DENIED. `y` typed before the prompt + Enter → DENIED. Paste `y\\n` → DENIED. Deliberate `y` + Enter after 500 ms → APPROVED. | PTY (r1a/r1d scripts) |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:175:| ACC-SAFE-06 | Startup screen of both surfaces shows mode/sandbox/trust. Doctor JSON contains `posture`. | PTY + unit |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:177:| ACC-SAFE-08 | Existing `tui_approval_input_e2e` stays green. | PTY (CI) |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:178:| ACC-SAFE-09 | Fixture repo whose `package.json` `scripts.test` writes a sentinel file. In review mode, the sentinel is not written until a verifier approval is given, and the approval panel shows `npm test` and the script body, regardless of folder trust. In auto mode, execution follows the configured permission mode regardless of folder trust. | integration + PTY |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:179:| ACC-SAFE-10 | `/test` runs through the runner: Esc cancels it within 5 s, and in sandbox mode it runs inside bwrap (`/proc/self/mountinfo` probe). | PTY |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:51:| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:65:2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:79:| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:91:| Safety | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-10 | SPEC-01 |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:110:| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:111:| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:161:### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:174:- new: the package PTY smoke\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:176:### 5.2 Scripted PTY scenarios against the installed RC (E3, mock gateway)\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:278:| Uninstall (documented manual) | Commands from the quickstart | Only Nexus-owned paths removed. `~/.config/nexus` and `~/.nexus` retained. |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:301:   - ACC-SAFE-01, 03, 09;\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:334:- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: CI, scripted and manual gates PASS.\n## HEAD (no branch)\ngitdir: /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/worktrees/startup-trust-main-check\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":30572}},"started_at_ms":1792884954249,"completed_at_ms":1792884954249}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T23:35:55.156Z","ordinal":314024,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17045-5814-7682-b481-e475defe3cdf","call_id":"call_bae56afe3d9e4443a2028fc75d95b27d","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:START -->\n### Qualification-only requirements for exact-RC enforcement\n\n| Requirement | Acceptance criteria required in the exact-RC record | Remaining stage |\n|---|---|---|\n| REQ-REL-003 | ACC-PLAT | Installed-RC platform and Node-version matrix |\n| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\n| REQ-AGT-010 | ACC-TRUST-04 | Independent acceptance of the DEC-04 v1 subset |\n| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\n| REQ-REL-005 | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | Exact-RC security and dependency artifact checks |\n| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\n| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\n| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\n| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\n| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\n\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\n### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\n\n| Requirement | Approved decision | Scope |\n|---|---|---|\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:END -->\n\n## 1. Rules\n\n1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\n2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n3. Thresholds (DEC-05) are frozen before the first M5 run. A failing gate is fixed in code and the run is repeated as `rc.N+1`. A threshold is never relaxed after results are known.\n4. Evidence goes to `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. The directory contains:\n   - `manifest.json`: commit, package sha256, environment, model fingerprint, dates;\n   - raw outputs;\n   - a `SHA256SUMS` file.\n\n   Secrets are redacted before commit.\n5. Any step that cannot run in the available environment is recorded as **NOT RUN** with its reason. A NOT RUN on a blocker gate fails the gate.\n\n## 2. Environments\n\n| ID | Environment | Used for |\n|---|---|---|\n| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n\n## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\n\nEvery ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\n\n| Gate | Acceptance IDs | Spec |\n|---|---|---|\n| Safety | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-10 | SPEC-01 |\n| Process ownership | ACC-PROC-01 to ACC-PROC-08 (ACC-PROC-07 is the load test, run in E3) | SPEC-02 |\n| Untrusted inputs | ACC-TRUST-01 to ACC-TRUST-09 | SPEC-03 |\n| Continuity | ACC-CONT-01 to ACC-CONT-09 (ACC-CONT-10 is in §8) | SPEC-04 |\n| Inference | ACC-INF-01 to ACC-INF-09 (ACC-INF-10 is in §4) | SPEC-05 |\n| Packaging | ACC-PKG-01 to ACC-PKG-09 | SPEC-06 |\n| Supply chain | ACC-SUP-01 to ACC-SUP-08 (artifact-bound ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08 after RC construction) | SPEC-07 |\n| Persistence | ACC-PER-01 to ACC-PER-07 | SPEC-08 |\n| Governance | ACC-GOV-01 to ACC-GOV-06 | SPEC-09 |\n| Verification | ACC-VER-01 to ACC-VER-09 | SPEC-11 |\n| Upgrade | ACC-UPG-01 to ACC-UPG-14 | SPEC-12 |\n\n\n### 3.1 Acceptance IDs defined in this file\n\nThese are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\n\n| ID | Check | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\n| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\n| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\n| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\n| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\n| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\n| ACC-PLAT | E2 matrix, §7 | All rows pass. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\n\n## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n\n### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\n\n1. `export HOME=$(mktemp -d)`.\n2. Install the RC with the documented command.\n3. Create `~/.config/nexus/config.env` containing only:\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:<proxy>/v1`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=<id as listed by the proxy>`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=REDACTED\n\n   No gateway token file, no homelab paths, no `NODE_*` overrides.\n4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\n| T4 truthful outcome | = 100% |\n| T4 hang beyond budget + 5 min | = 0 |\n| T3 false-absence | = 0 |\n| T3 false-presence | = 0 |\n| T3 steering honoured | ≥ 95% |\n| Operator interventions in `run` mode | = 0 |\n\nThe scorer output `verdict.md` lists each metric with its Wilson 95% interval, along with the infrastructure reruns and the excluded contaminated runs.\n\n## 7. Install, upgrade, rollback, uninstall (ACC-PLAT; E2)\n\n| Case | Command | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| Fresh install, each image with Node ≥ 22 | Documented one-line command with `NEXUS_VERSION=<rc>`, then the no-version command after v1.0.0 is published | Installed. `nexus --version` equals the RC. `nexus doctor` shows no version warning and an empty stderr. |\n| No Node / Node 20 | Same | Clear prerequisite message before download or state change. HOME untouched. |\n| Upgrade alpha.2 → RC | Same, with the tag | Symlink swapped. Old version retained. User state intact. |\n| Rollback RC → alpha.2 | Same, with the old tag | Works. |\n| Repair | Delete a file in the version dir, then reinstall | Repaired (REQ-REL-105). Same-version reinstall preserves working files if package fails verification. |\n| Uninstall (documented manual) | Commands from the quickstart | Only Nexus-owned paths removed. `~/.config/nexus` and `~/.nexus` retained. |\n| Checksum tamper | installer-smoke | Refused. The existing install is unchanged. |\n| Attestation | `gh attestation verify <tarball> -R mikeholownych/nexus-code` | PASS |\n| Upgrade self-test failure | `nexus upgrade` (broken candidate package) | Refused. Staging verified before switch; if post-switch verification fails, launcher atomically rolls back to previous target and journal records `rolled_back`. |\n| Upgrade crash recovery | `nexus upgrade --recover` | Idempotent recovery. Cleans incomplete staging, restores unverified launcher symlink, verifies functional installation. |\n| Backup restore | `nexus upgrade --restore-backup <state-backup-directory>` | Snapshot of configuration and complete durable state restored from a recognized private backup directory (`backup.json`, `state/`, optional `config/`), with strict 0600 file / 0700 directory modes. A canonical `config.env.bak.*` path restores configuration only. Arbitrary files and tar archives are rejected. Run it through the stable `nexus` launcher; close existing legacy clients, then keep version-pinned legacy binaries and direct old entry points offline until the durable restore journal is cleared. |\n| Incompatible downgrade | `nexus upgrade --version <v> --allow-downgrade` (incompatible state schema) | Refused fail-closed with actionable state schema explanation. Existing installation unchanged. |\n\n## 8. Independent acceptance (REQ-AGT-110, ACC-CONT-10)\n\nThe reviewer is supplied by the owner (X5) and did not implement the work under review.\n\nThe reviewer receives:\n\n- the RC package;\n- this file;\n- the REQUIREMENTS ledger;\n- SPEC-04;\n- read access to the evidence directory.\n\nThe reviewer performs:\n\n1. An independent re-run of a sample. At minimum:\n   - ACC-SAFE-01, 03, 09;\n   - ACC-PROC-02;\n   - ACC-TRUST-01, 02;\n   - ACC-CONT-01, 03;\n   - ACC-VER-01, 03;\n   - ACC-PKG-01;\n   - 5 random T2 tasks;\n   - 2 T4 classes.\n2. One live long task (≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions) on the RC through the gateway, including one kill and resume.\n3. A review of the scorer verdict and of contamination handling.\n\n**Output:** `docs/reviews/<date>-v1-rc-independent-acceptance.md` with an ACCEPT, ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS, or REJECT verdict per area. \"Accept with defects\" needs an owner disposition for every defect, and for a blocker area the only acceptable disposition is a fix.\n\n## 9. Contest (separate product; not a client gate)\n\nThe contest submission is complete and judging has concluded. No contest freeze applies (DEC-13 status amendment); post-contest hardening is tracked separately from client v1.0.0 acceptance and is accepted by:\n\n| ID | Check |\n|---|---|\n| CON-A1 | Ordinary maintained package/experiment checks build `agent-collab-worker`. `worker.config.json` has the configured name, and the bundle contains the `/work-state` handler. Do not restore the retired `cloudflare-contest-contract` status check. |\n| CON-A2 | Broker negative tests: caller-supplied env paths and URLs are ignored. A host outside `*.artifacts.cloudflare.net` is refused. |\n| CON-A3 | On a clean VM, `install.sh --fresh` followed by `post-install-qualify.py` passes. |\n| CON-A4 | `sudo -l` for the demo user shows only fixed argv. `sudo setpriv --reuid=0 id` is denied. |\n| CON-A5 | One clean-account `--mode cloudflare --agents real` run, with a committed, redacted run record. |\n| CON-A6 | The video source commits are tagged and published, or the docs state that they are unpublished. |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:10:| Acceptance | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-06 in [ACCEPTANCE.md](../ACCEPTANCE.md) |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:30:- A lone Enter approves the action (TUI-02, reproduced in a PTY).\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:48:| TUI-02 Enter approves | RUNTIME (PTY r1a) | evidence/D_terminal.md §4 |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:49:| TUI-03 typed-ahead approves | RUNTIME (PTY r1d) | D §4 |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:52:| TUI guard strength | RUNTIME (PTY s2/s3) | D §5 |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:170:| ACC-SAFE-01 | Fresh HOME; run `nexus` and `nexus repl` in both trusted and untrusted fixture workspaces with explicit `--mode review` and `--mode auto`. A mock gateway calls `run_command \"echo x > ../outside\"`: review asks in both folders; auto permits according to the configured execution boundary in both folders. With no mode configured, both folders default to review. Trust affects only project instruction/integration loading. | PTY |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:172:| ACC-SAFE-03 | REPL PTY: lone Enter → DENIED. `y` typed before the prompt + Enter → DENIED. Paste `y\\n` → DENIED. Deliberate `y` + Enter after 500 ms → APPROVED. | PTY (r1a/r1d scripts) |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:175:| ACC-SAFE-06 | Startup screen of both surfaces shows mode/sandbox/trust. Doctor JSON contains `posture`. | PTY + unit |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:177:| ACC-SAFE-08 | Existing `tui_approval_input_e2e` stays green. | PTY (CI) |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:178:| ACC-SAFE-09 | Fixture repo whose `package.json` `scripts.test` writes a sentinel file. In review mode, the sentinel is not written until a verifier approval is given, and the approval panel shows `npm test` and the script body, regardless of folder trust. In auto mode, execution follows the configured permission mode regardless of folder trust. | integration + PTY |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:179:| ACC-SAFE-10 | `/test` runs through the runner: Esc cancels it within 5 s, and in sandbox mode it runs inside bwrap (`/proc/self/mountinfo` probe). | PTY |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:51:| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:65:2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:79:| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:91:| Safety | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-10 | SPEC-01 |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:110:| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:111:| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:161:### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:174:- new: the package PTY smoke\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:176:### 5.2 Scripted PTY scenarios against the installed RC (E3, mock gateway)\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:278:| Uninstall (documented manual) | Commands from the quickstart | Only Nexus-owned paths removed. `~/.config/nexus` and `~/.nexus` retained. |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:301:   - ACC-SAFE-01, 03, 09;\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-trust-main-check/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:334:- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: CI, scripted and manual gates PASS.\n## HEAD (no branch)\ngitdir: /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/worktrees/startup-trust-main-check\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","create_time":1792884955.1565528}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
