{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T23:37:31.924Z","ordinal":314116,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016add413af79881a090ca2cff8349d165","status":"completed","call_id":"call_ee0812ba9bc741618329bbb49b8d4a0a","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md | sed -n '1,240p'; git show origin/main:AGENTS.md | sed -n '1,180p'; cat .git/nexus-claims.log 2>/dev/null | tail -50; tar --version | head -1; gzip --version | head -1; docker --version 2>&1; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/git-exclude-fail-closed show-ref --heads | rg 'defect-git-exclude'\",\"workdir\":\"/home/mike/nexus-code\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":5000});\ntext(r.output)\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","create_time":1792885050.9693573}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T23:37:32.008Z","ordinal":314117,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016add412fd6f481a096eedf6c648cdf55","usage":{"input_tokens":132955,"cached_input_tokens":127488,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1506,"reasoning_output_tokens":1335,"total_tokens":134461},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":10387606,"cached_input_tokens":10153216,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":54560,"reasoning_output_tokens":35326,"total_tokens":10442166},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":5695604784,"cached_input_tokens":5634202496,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":16148008,"reasoning_output_tokens":9272525,"total_tokens":5711752792}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T23:37:33.222Z","ordinal":314118,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-a2d1e6aa-ed01-46d3-8aa1-518379efe3e8","process_id":"57828","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md | sed -n '1,240p'; git show origin/main:AGENTS.md | sed -n '1,180p'; cat .git/nexus-claims.log 2>/dev/null | tail -50; tar --version | head -1; gzip --version | head -1; docker --version 2>&1; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/git-exclude-fail-closed show-ref --heads | rg 'defect-git-exclude'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md | sed -n '1,240p'; git show origin/main:AGENTS.md | sed -n '1,180p'; cat .git/nexus-claims.log 2>/dev/null | tail -50; tar --version | head -1; gzip --version | head -1; docker --version 2>&1; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/git-exclude-fail-closed show-ref --heads | rg 'defect-git-exclude'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# Running multiple agents on this plan without collisions\n\nThese rules apply to every agent (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Nexus itself, or a human) that implements any part of this package at the same time as another. The repository's root `AGENTS.md` points here. The rules come from incidents recorded in `tasks/lessons.md`:\n\n- a concurrent agent overwrote newer evidence;\n- full test suites were contaminated by edits made mid-run;\n- `pkill -f` killed the agent's own shell;\n- HEAD moved during a pause.\n\nThey also follow from audit finding PER-03: the test suite writes into the real `~/.nexus`.\n\n## 1. Unit of work: one claimed PR slice per agent\n\n- The unit of concurrent work is **one PR slice** from a plan, for example `PLAN-01/PR-1a`. Every slice lists its tasks and its safe change boundary in its plan.\n- An agent works on exactly one claimed slice at a time.\n- An agent must not edit files outside its slice's boundary. The exceptions are the ledger rows and the shared files covered by §4. If the work needs a file outside the boundary, the agent stops and records a **boundary request** (§6). It does not edit the file.\n\n## 2. Claiming a slice (atomic and machine-local)\n\nClaims live in the repository's shared git directory. They are visible to every worktree, and they are never committed.\n\n```sh\nCLAIMS=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"\nmkdir -p \"$CLAIMS\"\nSLICE=\"PLAN-01_PR-1a\"\nif mkdir \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\" 2>/dev/null; then          # mkdir is atomic: exactly one agent wins\n  printf '{\"agent\":\"%s\",\"branch\":\"%s\",\"since\":\"%s\",\"pid\":%s}\\n' \\\n    \"$AGENT_NAME\" \"v1/plan-01-pr-1a\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" \"$$\" > \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\"\nelse\n  echo \"claimed by: $(cat \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\")\"; exit 1\nfi\n```\n\n- **Release** the claim by deleting its directory (`rm -r \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\"`) after the slice merges or is abandoned. Write one line about the outcome to `$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log`.\n- **Hot-file claims** use the same mechanism with the name `FILE_<path with / replaced by _>`, for example `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts`. See §4.\n- **Stale claims.** A claim older than 24 h whose PID is gone may be broken, but only by the owner, or by an agent that first records the broken claim in the log.\n- If the MCP Agent Mail server is available, its file reservations (`file_reservation_paths`) may be used as well. The git-common-dir claim stays authoritative, because every agent can see it without extra tooling.\n\n## 3. Isolation: worktree, branch, HOME, ports, processes\n\n| Resource | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| Source | One `git worktree` per claimed slice: `git worktree add ../nexus-wt/<slice> -b v1/<plan>-<slice> origin/main`. Never edit `~/nexus-code` itself. It is the owner's checkout, and `/usr/local/bin/nexus` runs from it. |\n| Branch | `v1/plan-NN-pr-Nx`. One branch per slice. Never commit to `main` directly. |\n| HOME and state | Until PLAN-08 PR-8a lands, every test, build and probe run sets `HOME=$(mktemp -d)` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"$HOME/.config\"`. After PR-8a, the test setup enforces this, but scripts and probes outside `npm test` must still set it. **Never** run anything that writes to the real `~/.nexus` or `~/.config/nexus`. |\n| Test runs | Full suites run on a **snapshot copy** of the worktree (`git worktree add` at the commit under test, or `git archive`), never on the tree being edited. `tsx` reads `src/` live. |\n| Builds | Each worktree builds into its own `core/target`, and `cli/dist` is per worktree. To share the Rust build cache, set `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` per worktree, never to one shared directory. |\n| Ports | Mock servers bind `127.0.0.1:0` (an ephemeral port) and publish the chosen port to a file. Fixed ports are forbidden. |\n| Processes | Kill only PIDs you started, taken from `$!` or `ps -eo pid,args \\| grep -v grep`. **Never `pkill -f` or `killall`.** Long background jobs are stopped through the agent's own task controls. |\n| Full test suites | The PTY and provider tests are timing-sensitive. Take the claim `SUITE` before running a full suite (`make test`, or `npm test` over all files). While anyone holds `SUITE`, nobody runs other suites or targeted test files on the same machine. Concurrent load caused a false failure on 2026-10-15: `cloud_providers` saw an extra provider request after a load-induced timeout. Release the claim when the run ends. |\n| Inference | There is one inference host (DEC-16). Any run that uses the gateway takes the claim `GATEWAY` first. That includes eval runs, live checks and stripped-proxy runs. One gateway run at a time, which keeps eval timings valid and prevents overload. Small cloud checks (E5) take `CLOUD` to avoid duplicate spend. |\n| Credentials | Agents never read or copy `~/.config/nexus/credentials.json`, `config.env` values, or gateway tokens. The stripped proxy reads the token file itself. |\n\n## 4. Hot files: serialise, do not merge blindly\n\nThese files are touched by several plans. An agent editing one must hold its `FILE_` claim for the **shortest** period: edit, test, push, merge, then release.\n\n| File | Plans that touch it | Rule |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cli/src/agent.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 04, 05, 11 | Claim required. Keep each change local to the line ranges the plan names. Rebase immediately before merge and re-run that slice's tests on the rebased snapshot. |\n| `cli/src/index.ts` | 01, 03, 04, 06, 08, 10, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-06 PR-6b (unified launcher) lands first.** Other plans add commands and flags afterwards. |\n| `cli/src/tools.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 06, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-02 PR-2b (signal plumbing) lands before PLAN-03 PR-3c (`safeFetch`)**. |\n| `cli/src/sidecar.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 05, 08 | Claim required |\n| `cli/src/doctor.ts` | 01, 03, 05, 06, 08 | Claim required. Each plan adds **new check functions** in separate blocks. Only PLAN-06 PR-6d changes existing checks. |\n| `cli/src/client.ts` | 03, 05, 08, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-03 PR-3a (env layering) lands before any PLAN-05 slice.** |\n| `cli/src/repl.ts` | 01, 05, 08 | Claim required |\n| `cli/src/config.ts`, `security.ts`, `sandbox.ts`, `mcp.ts`, `plugins.ts` | 01, 03 | Claim required. PLAN-01 PR-1e and PLAN-03 must not run at the same time on `sandbox.ts` or `security.ts`. |\n| `cli/src/core/capabilities.ts` | 01, 02 | **PLAN-01 PR-1a (effect classes) lands first.** PLAN-02 PR-2c adds schema fields afterwards. |\n| `cli/src/tester.ts` | 01, 11 | **PLAN-01 PR-1c lands before PLAN-11 PR-11b/11c.** |\n| `cli/src/core/state.ts` | 04, 08 | **PLAN-08 PR-8a (HOME isolation) lands before everything.** |\n| `core/src/runner.rs`, `core/src/main.rs` | 01, 02, 06 | Claim required. The protocol version number is owned by PLAN-02 PR-2a. PLAN-06 PR-6c only reads it. |\n| `core/src/bin/nexus_tui/{live_state,live_view}.rs` | 01, 02 | Claim required |\n| `package.json`, `cli/package.json`, `core/Cargo.toml`, lockfiles | 01, 06, 07, 08 | **Only one agent at a time.** Version fields are written only by `scripts/sync-version.mjs`. Dependency changes are separate commits that touch only the lockfile and manifest. |\n| `harness.sh`, `install.sh`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `.github/workflows/*` | 05, 06, 07, 09, C1 | Claim required. Workflow edits are separate commits. |\n| `cli/dist/**` | all, while tracked | Do not commit `cli/dist` from slices. PLAN-07 PR-7d untracks it (DEC-10). Until that merges, only the merging agent rebuilds and commits dist, in a final separate commit, after rebasing. |\n| `docs/USER_MANUAL.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md`, `quickstart.md` | 05, 09 and doc tasks in every plan | Edit only the sections your slice changes. Hold a short `FILE_` claim. |\n\n### Ledger updates (`docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md`)\n\nA slice changes only the rows for its own requirement IDs: the status, test-reference and evidence cells, in place. It never reorders, adds or removes rows, and never edits another slice's rows. New requirements discovered during work go to §6, not into the ledger. Because rows are independent lines, git merges these edits cleanly. If a conflict appears anyway, resolve it row by row, keeping both changes.\n\n## 5. Commit and merge discipline\n\n1. Before **every** commit, compare `git rev-parse HEAD` with the commit you last made. Then run `git log <yours>..HEAD` on the branch. If anything foreign appears, stop and reconcile. Never commit generated artifacts (evidence, dist, lockfiles) over a branch that moved (lessons 2026-10-13).\n2. Commits are scoped to the slice. Do not reformat or clean up files outside the boundary.\n3. Merge order follows the precedence rules in §4 and the ROADMAP milestone order. Within a milestone, the slice with fewer hot-file claims merges first.\n4. Rebase onto `origin/main` immediately before merging. Re-run the slice's targeted tests, plus `make test`, on a snapshot of the rebased commit. Merge only if both pass.\n5. Pushing, tagging, publishing and changing GitHub state (issues, milestones, releases) are **owner-approved actions** (DECISIONS X-list). Agents prepare them and do not perform them.\n6. Preserve unrelated user work: the untracked `nexus-continuity-validation/`, the stashes, and any dirty files you did not create. Never stash, reset, clean or check out over them.\n\n## 6. Coordination records\n\n| Record | Where | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| Claims | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` | Who owns which slice or file right now |\n| Claim log | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log` (append-only, one line per event) | Claim, release, broken claim, boundary request |\n| Boundary requests and discovered requirements | The PR description, under the heading `Needs from other slices`. Mirrored as one line in the claim log. | So the owning slice's agent can pick it up. Never fixed silently out of scope. |\n| Slice evidence | `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/<plan>-<slice>/` (new directory per slice) | No shared evidence files, so agents cannot overwrite each other's evidence |\n\n## 7. Safe parallel lanes\n\nThe following groupings can run at the same time with no hot-file contention beyond §4 claims. They are listed by milestone.\n\n| Phase | Parallel lanes |\n|---|---|\n| M0 | (a) PLAN-08 PR-8a, which must merge first. Then in parallel: (b) PLAN-06 PR-6a, (c) PLAN-09 PR-9a. |\n| M1 | (a) PLAN-01 PR-1a → PR-1b → PR-1c (sequential, owns `capabilities.ts`, `agent.ts` dispatch). (b) PLAN-02 PR-2a (Rust only). (c) PLAN-03 PR-3a → PR-3b (config/egress). (d) PLAN-11 PR-11a (`parser.ts`) and PR-11b (`tester.ts`, after PR-1c). Lanes (b), (c) and (d) do not touch `capabilities.ts`. |\n| M2 (alongside M1) | (a) PLAN-07 PR-7a/7b/7c (workflows, scripts). (b) PLAN-06 PR-6b after PLAN-01 PR-1b (shares `index.ts` flags). |\n| M3 | (a) PLAN-04 (`agent.ts` turn, operation runner). (b) PLAN-05 (`client.ts`, provider modules). (c) PLAN-10 harness (`eval/`, no product files). (d) Held-out task authoring by the agent author, **outside the repository**: no access to Nexus source or the development set (DEC-05). |\n| M4 (alongside M3) | PLAN-08 PR-8b..8e. Coordinate with PLAN-04 on `state.ts` through `FILE_` claims. |\n| M5 | **Serial on `GATEWAY`.** The eval runner, the stripped-proxy runs and the independent reviewer's live task each take the `GATEWAY` claim. The terminal matrix (E3) and the install matrix (E2) can run in parallel with gateway runs. |\n\n## 8. Independence constraints\n\n- The held-out task author must not see Nexus source, the development tasks or tuning history. It runs in a separate session with only the task schema and external repositories. Its output is sealed by a sha256 manifest committed before RC1.\n- The independent reviewer in ACCEPTANCE §8 must not be the agent or session that implemented the slices under review.\n- An implementing agent never edits `eval/heldout-manifest.json`, scorer thresholds or ACCEPTANCE §6.4 after the freeze.\n# Project Guidelines & Agent Instructions\n\n## Commands\n- Build: `make build` or `cargo build` or `npm run build`\n- Test: `make test` or `cargo test` or `npm test`\n- Lint: `cargo clippy` or `npm run lint`\n\n## Code Conventions\n- Maintain documentation integrity and keep existing comments.\n- Always run tests after making changes to verify correctness.\n- Keep functions modular and clearly typed.\n\n## v1.0.0 work and concurrent agents\n- The v1.0.0 plan is in `docs/v1.0.0/` (start at `docs/v1.0.0/README.md`). Implement one claimed PR slice at a time, within the safe change boundary in its plan.\n- When more than one agent may be working, follow `docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md`. In short:\n  - Claim the slice atomically under `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/`.\n  - Use one worktree and branch per slice; never edit `~/nexus-code` directly.\n  - Isolate `HOME` for every test or probe run.\n  - Claim hot files before editing them.\n  - Take the `GATEWAY` claim for any inference run.\n  - Never use `pkill -f`.\n  - Check `git log` for foreign commits before every commit.\n  - Leave push, tag and publish to the owner.\n2026-10-24T21:18:00Z SAFE_BOUNDARY_STATUS_REQUEST: Foreign make test PID850189 has been live >15 min with full CLI test child PID868748 in ep_poll and 0 CPU across repeated checks; cwd=/home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-latest-resume-corruption-snapshot at 27415c892fe0e20188b38a1653090b8c231ff788. Codex PR200 suite was stopped after detecting overlap (exit130, incomplete). No process was signaled. Please record current test case, expected completion, and SUITE claim ownership at the next safe boundary; until then no local suite will run.\n2026-10-24T21:20:07Z MERGED PR=#203 merge=4b474f1638645258fc6bc696400892feaf3a78d6 head=ef40498 exact_CI_all_success independent_review=ACCEPT claims_released post_merge_CI_pending\n2026-10-24T21:27:00Z STARTUP_FOLDER_TRUST_COPY_20261024 REGRESSION: Added targeted test in claimed cli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts; isolated `node scripts/run_tests.mjs test/verifier_gating.test.ts` on candidate branch confirms trusted workspace with unset approvalMode returns `auto` instead of required `review` (1 intended failure, 8 other tests pass). Exact-main run40133356557 still in npm CLI test on Node22/24; CodeQL40133356577 success. Re-requested safe-boundary FILE_cli_src_agent.ts release/transfer on merged PR203 comment6389662191; no response yet. Protected file remains untouched.\n2026-10-24T21:22:00Z NODE22_DECISION_VERIFIED: User-selected Node>=22 policy is already merged in PR150 at 1da67c3622f7290944a496a58965606961a5afc0; exact candidate c638da0 is ancestor of current origin/main 29eab4c. Current package.json engines >=22; CI matrix [22,24]; PR150 exact Node22, Node24, Linux package, CodeQL all SUCCESS. PR137 and PR146 closed/superseded; no additional edit needed.\n2026-10-24T21:21:36Z LOG_TIMESTAMP_NOTE: The immediately preceding NODE22_DECISION_VERIFIED entry carries an approximate timestamp 30 seconds later than the live `date -u` check (21:21:30Z); its verified state is accurate.\n2026-10-24T21:27:34Z claude-code ENFORCE main=4b474f1638645258fc6bc696400892feaf3a78d6 (PR203 merge) clean detached worktree, isolated HOME/XDG: requirements --enforce exit 0; 123 rows (108 tested / 6 partial / 2 implemented / 7 open; 12 exact-RC deferrals), unchanged. RC5 NOTES ACTION for /root: PR203 is now on main, so notes 010ccb9 need a bullet before tagging, e.g. 'An explicit --read-only launch stays read-only for the whole session: /mode, \"always\" approval and TUI always-approve can no longer lower it.' Notes re-review required after the edit. PR200 (accepted at 81928bd) still pending; same rule applies.\n2026-10-24T21:31:20Z VERIFIED_WAIT: host=mike-dev boot=8928bf1f; foreign make test PID850189/CLI PID868748 remains live in defect-latest-resume-corruption-snapshot@27415c892fe0e20188b38a1653090b8c231ff788; PR200 81928bd exact CI Node22/24 in progress, CodeQL pass. No test rerun, no signaling, no handoff received.\n2026-10-24T21:32:30Z FOREIGN_SUITE_ORPHAN_RECHECK: Parent agent PID1969096 is absent; make test PID850189 and test runner PID868748 remain live under PID1 on boot 8928bf1f, cwd defect-latest-resume-corruption-snapshot@27415c892fe0e20188b38a1653090b8c231ff788. No claim matches this snapshot. No process signaled or adopted. SUITE coordination lock remains.\n2026-10-24T21:34:02Z STARTUP_FOLDER_TRUST_COPY_20261024 CHECKPOINT: exact branch head ca2865fcf5251015f8eba05525d53b6fe1b96243 on base origin/main=4b474f1638645258fc6bc696400892feaf3a78d6. Effect-specific headless egress guidance + regression test. Focused approval/config/startup/verifier tests 38/38 PASS under isolated HOME; tsc --noEmit PASS; npm run build PASS; diff-check PASS. Independent read-only review ACCEPT exact HEAD by plan05_readonly_review, diff SHA-256 3492fafded257cba75428f1ab66fcc700c9e99372a68fad72d73018d313684c3. Requirements --enforce still fails only REQ-SEC-101 and REQ-SEC-119, both partial; narrow test evidence does not promote them. Hot-file claim FILE_cli_src_agent.ts released after review. Candidate ready for owner integration; no push, PR, or release action taken.\n2026-10-24T21:42:00Z STARTUP_FOLDER_TRUST_COPY_20261024 REVIEW_FIX: amended SEC-119 citations to exact trusted/untrusted parameterized verifier test names; committed 5b8f4ebf68fd9c5d016f342a1a7c5e948e20b16f. Source unchanged from prior focused test run. Diff-check clean. Exact-commit independent review requested; no push/PR/tag/publication.\n2026-10-24T21:47:00Z STARTUP_FOLDER_TRUST_COPY_20261024 REVIEW_ACCEPT: exact HEAD 5b8f4ebf68fd9c5d016f342a1a7c5e948e20b16f against main 4b474f1638645258fc6bc696400892feaf3a78d6; independent ACCEPT by plan05_readonly_review, diff SHA-256 e07d47052ecc8ef37f5ad5c0d9d174de0a289f19d0c6e87e216bd3591c647251. Clean isolated requirements enforcement still fails only SEC-101/119 as partial (PTY acceptance pending). Main CI40133356557 Node22/24 passed; linux-x86_64 remains in progress. Hold PR CI start until exact-main full workflow finishes to avoid overlapping full suites.\n2026-10-24T21:49:00Z STARTUP_FOLDER_TRUST_COPY_20261024 PUSH: pushed accepted candidate 5b8f4ebf68fd9c5d016f342a1a7c5e948e20b16f to new branch codex/startup-folder-trust-copy-20261024 using normal fast-forward. No PR opened yet because exact-main CI40133356557 linux-x86_64 is still running npm CLI suite; avoid overlapping full-suite executions.\n2026-10-24T21:50:00Z SUITE_RECOVERY: verified on mike-dev that the previously reported local make test PID850189 and runner PID868748 are absent; classify that run INCOMPLETE, not pass/fail. Updated SUITE ownership to track exact-main CI40133356557 at 4b474f1638645258fc6bc696400892feaf3a78d6; Node22/24 passed, linux-x86_64 still running npm CLI test. No overlapping candidate suite launched.\n2026-10-24T21:51:19Z claude-code INDEPENDENT_REVIEW STARTUP_FOLDER_TRUST_COPY_20261024 head=5b8f4ebf68fd9c5d016f342a1a7c5e948e20b16f (branch codex/startup-folder-trust-copy-20261024, base 4b474f1): REQUEST_CHANGES (gate only; code reviewed and sound). CODE: trust no longer selects approval mode (config/repl/sidecar/doctor/agent default to review unless fullAccess); auto mode no longer asks for exec in untrusted workspaces; context_inject is now gated only by isUntrustedSource (which no caller in cli/src sets), BUT untrusted-workspace skills stay hard-denied at agent.ts:4251/4504 (UNTRUSTED_WORKSPACE_SKILL), so activate_skill in an untrusted folder can only load user-home skills. Net: defaults are stricter (trusted no longer = auto); the only widening is explicit --mode auto in an untrusted folder, which matches the amended DEC-01. GATE FAILS: requirements --enforce at this exact head in a clean worktree with isolated HOME exits 1 (106 tested / 8 partial): (a) REQ-SEC-119 cites 'trusted repo in review mode…' and 'untrusted repo in review mode…', but verifier_gating.test.ts:85-86 generates those names from a template literal inside for(const trusted of [false,true]), so the checker cannot resolve them; unroll into two literal test() calls or cite resolvable names. (b) REQ-SEC-101 and REQ-SEC-119 were downgraded tested→partial ('PTY ACC-SAFE-01 still pending'). Blocking rows must stay ≥tested under --enforce, so either provide tested evidence for the amended wording or keep the ledger honest and do not merge before RC5 (an unenforced gate would be a weakened threshold). DECISION PROVENANCE: DECISIONS.md says 'operator direction 2026-10-24'; claude-code is asking the owner to confirm directly. SCOPE: user-visible; it changes DEC-01 defaults and needs an RC5 notes bullet if merged before the tag.\n2026-10-24T21:54:00Z MAIN_CI_TERMINAL: CI40133356557 SUCCESS exact main 4b474f1638645258fc6bc696400892feaf3a78d6; Node22/24 and linux-x86_64 all success. CodeQL40133356577 SUCCESS. Opened PR204 for accepted candidate 5b8f4ebf68fd9c5d016f342a1a7c5e948e20b16f against exact main. PR CI40136152410 queued/in progress, CodeQL40136152442 in progress. SUITE exclusive ownership moved to PR204 exact-head checks.\n2026-10-24T21:57:00Z PR204_REMEDIATION: CI40136152410 failed at requirements report before suites; validator could not resolve dynamic template test names, no tests ran. Replaced dynamic cases with literal test title spanning both trust states; focused test 8/8 PASS; clean candidate checker now flags only SEC-101/119 partial. Pushed normal fast-forward 5b8f4eb..29891188. Exact CI40136337984 and CodeQL40136337957 active; independent re-review requested.\n2026-10-24T21:58:00Z PR204_REVIEW_ACCEPT: independent ACCEPT exact HEAD 29891188e580c774194f68ef006415183a1c27cf by plan05_readonly_review, diff SHA-256 5a3e5a97575fa8dad526cef5dda26d5a53f231a20c84ef8accb273293e163a4e. Reviewer confirms literal evidence title matches and covers both trust states; claims remain partial pending PTY. Exact CI40136337984/CodeQL40136337957 active.\n2026-10-24T22:01:41Z POST_MERGE PR=#203 merge=4b474f1 CI=40133356557_success CodeQL=40133356577_success; read-only sidecar mode escalation fixed. KNOWN_NEXT: REPL /init and /skill init (and other mutating slash commands) still bypass explicit --read-only via direct scaffolding; reviewer finding from PR203; needs a REPL read-only gate and PTY regression.\n2026-10-24T22:01:51Z CLAIM DEFECT_REPL_READONLY_20261024 repl.ts + repl_approval_e2e/driver base=4b474f1 scope=repl-readonly-slash-bypass\n2026-10-24T22:02:02Z CLAIM_WITHDRAWN DEFECT_REPL_READONLY_20261024: FILE_cli_src_repl.ts is actively claimed by codex-root (startup-folder-trust-copy, since 20:25Z, scope touches approval decisions); no takeover and no edit. REPL read-only slash bypass remains an unowned follow-up once that claim releases.\n2026-10-24T22:02:30Z CLAIM DEFECT_TAR_AMBIENT_ENV_20261024 tar_safety.ts/test base=4b474f1 scope=tar-PATH-and-TAR_OPTIONS-ambient-exec\n2026-10-24T22:03:53Z CLAIM_UPDATE DEFECT_TAR_AMBIENT_ENV_20261024 PR=#205 head=2247540bf0e8d4fbaf24746d06de2d7464c72101 focused_tar_6_pass tsc_pass pre_fix_both_markers_confirmed independent_review=pending\n2026-10-24T22:07:00Z UPDATE DEFECT_TAR_AMBIENT_ENV_20261024 head=010caad29b9653ef13b8728e3cf85e3a20113c00 review_REJECT_addressed: PATH_gzip_shim_sanitized, no_tar_PATH_fallback, explicit_skips, README corrected; 3 ambient tests fail base, 7/7 now; re_review_pending\n2026-10-24T22:15:43Z PR200_TAKEOVER user_authorized=true old_pid=1999482 old_pid_state=absent host=mike-dev boot=8928bf1f-8ae0-441b-8070-f05ef8823a5e branch=v1/defect-git-exclude-fail-closed head=81928bd81d10ec957a3063a0e414aef981c83b20 PR_CI=40130531444_IN_PROGRESS SUITE=PR204_40136337984_ACTIVE claims=PR200_GIT_EXCLUDE_FAIL_CLOSED,FILE_cli_src_core_git_exclude.ts,FILE_cli_test_flight_exclude.test.ts,FILE_cli_test_git_exclude.test.ts\n2026-10-24T22:17:34Z PR200_SCOPE_FOLLOWUP local_uncommitted=info_exclude_nofollow_and_hardlink_guard REDACTED diff_check=PASS\n2026-10-24T22:30:29Z PR200_LIVE_WAIT CI40130531444=IN_PROGRESS_Node22_Node24_CLI_tests REDACTED SUITE=held_by_PR204 local_changes=uncommitted_unverified\n2026-10-24T22:34:30Z STARTUP_FOLDER_TRUST_COPY_20261024 CLAIM_RELEASE: PR204 merged as 2ab20cdc7db52d5f2306f2f49f4138fcfe74d52f after exact-head CI40136337984 all required jobs SUCCESS, CodeQL40136337957 SUCCESS, and independent ACCEPT. Released slice and file claims: FILE_cli_src_agent.ts, FILE_cli_src_config.ts, FILE_cli_src_core_approval_policy.ts, FILE_cli_src_doctor.ts, FILE_cli_src_index.ts, FILE_cli_src_repl.ts, FILE_cli_src_sidecar.ts, FILE_cli_src_startup_trust.ts, FILE_cli_src_types.ts, FILE_cli_test_approval_policy.test.ts, FILE_cli_test_config.test.ts, FILE_cli_test_startup_trust_prompt.test.ts, FILE_cli_test_verifier_gating.test.ts, FILE_docs_ARCHITECTURE.md, FILE_docs_USER_MANUAL.md, FILE_docs_releases_v1.0.0.md, FILE_docs_v1.0.0_DECISIONS.md, FILE_docs_v1.0.0_REQUIREMENTS.md, FILE_docs_v1.0.0_plans_PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md, FILE_docs_v1.0.0_specs_SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md, FILE_quickstart.md. Post-merge CI40139114804 and CodeQL40139114781 are now tracked under SUITE; no acceptance status promoted, SEC-101/119 remain partial pending PTY.\n2026-10-24T22:34:00Z PR204_TERMINAL_MERGED merge=2ab20cdc7db52d5f2306f2f49f4138fcfe74d52f checks=CI40136337984_SUCCESS_CodeQL40136337957_SUCCESS postmerge=CI40139114804_ACTIVE_CodeQL40139114781_ACTIVE SUITE_claim=retained_by_RELEASE_PUBLISHER; PR200 candidate patch applies cleanly to 2ab20cd in /var/tmp/nexus-pr200-main-2ab20cd-candidate; tests not run pending SUITE release.\n2026-10-24T22:35:00Z PR200_CURRENT_MAIN_TSC PASS snapshot=/var/tmp/nexus-pr200-main-2ab20cd-candidate base=2ab20cdc7db52d5f2306f2f49f4138fcfe74d52f PR200_committed_diff=clean_apply local_followup=clean_apply HOME_XDG=isolated no_tests_run SUITE=main_CI40139114804_active\n2026-10-24T22:37:00Z MAIN_POST_PR204_CODEQL CodeQL40139114781=SUCCESS CI40139114804=IN_PROGRESS_Node22_Node24 SUITE_claim=RELEASE_PUBLISHER; PR200_CI40130531444=IN_PROGRESS_Node22_Node24_CLI; current-main PR200 typecheck PASS on archive snapshot 2ab20cd, no tests.\n2026-10-24T22:42:49Z PR200_MAIN_SNAPSHOT_UPDATE base=2ab20cdc7db52d5f2306f2f49f4138fcfe74d52f committed_patch=3bd2245f532151c94bac0ebf71ede8706d0609598f8b94e9cdee6ed640fa42b8 clean_apply followup_patch=64b2c51215d421c6f180893b402abb991a7dda7aa4a032f06ff3e7cfa0064d56 clean_sequential_apply snapshot=/var/tmp/nexus-pr200-main-2ab20cd-candidate2 isolated_tsc=PASS tests=NOT_RUN_SUITE_MAIN40139114804_ACTIVE\n2026-10-24T22:49:31Z MERGED PR=#205 merge=c1b13327edf5d3a0c82fb10eb814775fd4953a63 head=010caad exact_CI_all_success independent_review=ACCEPT_after_REJECT_round claims_released post_merge_CI_pending\n2026-10-24T22:49:51Z CLAIM DEFECT_REPL_READONLY_20261024 repl.ts + repl_approval_e2e/driver base=c1b1332 scope=repl-readonly-slash-bypass\n2026-10-24T22:56:23Z PR200_LIVE_WAIT REDACTED:54:00Z main_Code