CC-SAFE-01 | **B** | SEC-01, TUI-07 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\n120-| REQ-SEC-102 | Audit; TOP_TIER B1 | Every capability has an effect class. Review gates every class except read. The gate is enforced at dispatch from the registry. | safety | `core/capabilities.ts`, `agent.ts:3945` | TEST `approval_policy.test.ts` | tested | ACC-SAFE-02 | **B** | HIST-05, SEC-03 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\n121-| REQ-SEC-103 | Audit | No approval is decided by Enter alone, typed-ahead input, paste, or input inside the grace window, on any surface. | safety | `repl.ts:291-355,444-495`, `tui_approval_input_e2e.test.ts`, `repl_approval_e2e.test.ts` | PTY (ACC-SAFE-03, ACC-SAFE-08) | tested | ACC-SAFE-03, ACC-SAFE-08 | **B** | TUI-02, TUI-03 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\n122:| REQ-SEC-119 | Audit; DEC-01 (amended 2026-10-24) | Nexus-initiated verifier runs are `exec` class and follow configured permission mode; review requires a one-time approval showing the script body. Folder trust alone does not authorize execution; all runs are routed through the runner. | safety | `agent.ts:1654,3544,4255`; `tester.ts:145`; `verifier_gating.test.ts` | TEST `test:cli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts::\"trusted and untrusted repos in review mode prompt for verifier and script body, write sentinel only after approval, and cache session decision\"`; `test:cli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts::\"denied verifier does not execute verifier and sentinel is not written\"`; `test:cli/test/harness.test.ts::\"run_tests keeps repository test side effects inside worktree authority and honors read-only, dry-run, and required sandbox\"`; PTY ACC-SAFE-09/10 still pending | partial | ACC-SAFE-09, ACC-SAFE-10 | **B** | VER-01, VER-14 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\n123-| REQ-SEC-104 | Audit | `--read-only` cannot read outside the workspace through commands. HOME is masked. | safety | `sandbox.ts`, `core/authority.ts:44-136` | RT (SEC-04) | tested | ACC-SAFE-04 | RR | SEC-04 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\n124-| REQ-TUI-102 | Audit | The startup banner states mode, sandbox and trust. Doctor reports the posture. | safety / UX | `sidecar.ts`, `live_view.rs`, `repl.ts`, `doctor.ts` | TEST `tui_surface_e2e.test.ts`, `doctor.test.ts` | tested | ACC-SAFE-06 | RR | TUI-07 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\n125-| REQ-SEC-108 | Audit | The command denylist is labelled a tripwire, and its false positives are fixed. | honesty / workflow | `security.ts`, `runner.rs:64-107` | RT (SEC-02) | tested | ACC-SAFE-07 | RR | SEC-02, DOC-01 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\n--\n274-| Group | Rows | Breakdown |\n275-|---|---|---|\n276:| New v1 rows (§3) | 92 | **31 B**, 58 RR, 3 P. 79 open, 9 partial (REQ-SEC-118, REQ-PRV-101, REQ-PRV-103, REQ-PRV-105, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-PER-106, REQ-OPS-101, REQ-QUAL-108, REQ-QUAL-110), 1 implemented (REQ-OPS-103), 4 tested (REQ-SEC-103, REQ-SEC-119, REQ-PER-101, REQ-PER-102). |\n277-| Carried rows (§2.1) | 29 | 14 tested and unchanged (Keep). 1 visually-accepted (REQ-TUI-001). The rest are partial, or have open items mapped to §3. |\n278-| Contest rows (§4) | 7 | Separate product. |\n279-\n88-\n89-| Gate | Acceptance IDs | Spec |\n90-|---|---|---|\n91:| Safety | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-10 | SPEC-01 |\n92-| Process ownership | ACC-PROC-01 to ACC-PROC-08 (ACC-PROC-07 is the load test, run in E3) | SPEC-02 |\n93-| Untrusted inputs | ACC-TRUST-01 to ACC-TRUST-09 | SPEC-03 |\n94-| Continuity | ACC-CONT-01 to ACC-CONT-09 (ACC-CONT-10 is in §8) | SPEC-04 |\n95-| Inference | ACC-INF-01 to ACC-INF-09 (ACC-INF-10 is in §4) | SPEC-05 |\n--\n298-The reviewer performs:\n299-\n300-1. An independent re-run of a sample. At minimum:\n301:   - ACC-SAFE-01, 03, 09;\n302-   - ACC-PROC-02;\n303-   - ACC-TRUST-01, 02;\n304-   - ACC-CONT-01, 03;\n305-   - ACC-VER-01, 03;\n1-// Checks docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md against the rest of the repository (REQ-OPS-102).\n2://   report mode (default): every B/RR row links a spec, a plan and an acceptance ID; every ACC id it names is defined\n3://     (in a spec table, a spec's \"ACC-X-01 to ACC-X-NN\" range, or ACCEPTANCE.md); every `test:<file>::\"<name>\"` reference\n4-//     in a row names an existing test file that contains <name>.\n5-//   --enforce (pre-RC source gate): every B/RR row is at least `tested`, except rows explicitly\n6://     mapped to post-RC qualification in ACCEPTANCE.md. Those rows remain deferred, not accepted.\n7-//     Exact-RC enforcement requires a qualification record with after-RC evidence for every mapped row.\n8-// Exit 1 on any problem; prints a summary table either way. `--ledger <file>` checks another ledger (used by its test).\n9-import fs from \"node:fs\";\n10-import path from \"node:path\";\n11-import { createHash } from \"node:crypto\";\n12-import { execFileSync } from \"node:child_process\";\n13-import { fileURLToPath } from \"node:url\";\n14-\n15-const root = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), \"..\");\n16-const args = process.argv.slice(2);\n17-const enforce = args.includes(\"--enforce\");\n18-const ledgerArg = args.indexOf(\"--ledger\");\n--\n23-const pkg = path.join(root, \"docs\", \"v1.0.0\");\n24-const ledgerPath = ledgerArg >= 0 ? path.resolve(args[ledgerArg + 1]) : path.join(pkg, \"REQUIREMENTS.md\");\n25-\n26-const read = (p) => fs.readFileSync(p, \"utf8\");\n27-const specs = fs.readdirSync(path.join(pkg, \"specs\")).map((f) => read(path.join(pkg, \"specs\", f)));\n28:const acceptance = read(path.join(pkg, \"ACCEPTANCE.md\"));\n29-const decisions = read(path.join(pkg, \"DECISIONS.md\"));\n30-\n31-function accDefined(id) {\n32-  const cell = new RegExp(`\\\\|\\\\s*${id}\\\\s*\\\\|`);\n33:  if (specs.some((s) => cell.test(s)) || cell.test(acceptance)) return true;\n34-  const m = /^ACC-([A-Z0-9]+)-(\\d+)$/.exec(id);\n35-  if (!m) return false;\n36-  const range = new RegExp(`ACC-${m[1]}-(\\\\d+) to ACC-${m[1]}-(\\\\d+)`, \"g\");\n37-  return specs.some((s) => [...s.matchAll(range)].some((r) => Number(r[1]) <= Number(m[2]) && Number(m[2]) <= Number(r[2])));\n38-}\n39-\n40-function testExists(file, name) {\n41-  const p = path.join(root, file);\n42-  return fs.existsSync(p) && read(p).includes(name);\n43-}\n44-\n45:function acceptanceIds(value) {\n46-  const ids = new Set(value.match(/(?<![A-Za-z0-9_-])ACC-[A-Z0-9]+(?:-[A-Z0-9]+)*(?![A-Za-z0-9_-])/g) ?? []);\n47-  const ranges = /ACC-([A-Z0-9]+)-(\\d+)\\s+to\\s+ACC-\\1-(\\d+)/g;\n48-  for (const [, family, first, last] of value.matchAll(ranges)) {\n49-    for (let number = Number(first); number <= Number(last); number++) ids.add(`ACC-${family}-${String(number).padStart(first.length, \"0\")}`);\n50-  }\n51-  return [...ids];\n52-}\n53-\n54-function decisionSection(decision) {\n55-  if (typeof decision !== \"string\" || !/^DEC-\\d{2}$/.test(decision)) return \"\";\n56-  const heading = new RegExp(`^## ${decision}:[^\\\\n]*`, \"m\").exec(decisions);\n57-  if (!heading) return \"\";\n--\n59-  const remaining = decisions.slice(start);\n60-  const nextHeading = /^## /m.exec(remaining);\n61-  return remaining.slice(0, nextHeading ? nextHeading.index : remaining.length);\n62-}\n63-\n64:const RANK = { open: 0, partial: 1, implemented: 2, tested: 3, \"visually-accepted\": 4, \"product-qualified\": 5 };\n65-const problems = [];\n66-const counts = {};\n67-const requiredRows = new Map();\n68-const seenRequirementIds = new Set();\n69-const deferredQualificationRows = [];\n70-let rows = 0;\n71-let header = null;\n72-for (const line of read(ledgerPath).split(\"\\n\")) {\n73-  if (!line.startsWith(\"|\")) { header = null; continue; }\n74-  const cells = line.slice(1, -1).split(\"|\").map((c) => c.trim());\n75-  if (cells[0] === \"ID\") { header = cells; continue; }\n76-  if (!header || !/^REQ-[A-Z]+-\\d+[a-z]?$/.test(cells[0])) continue;\n77-  const col = (name) => cells[header.findIndex((h) => h.startsWith(name))] ?? \"\";\n78-  const id = cells[0];\n79-  const cls = col(\"Class\");\n80:  const status = col(\"Status\").split(/[\\s(]/)[0];\n81:  const acc = col(\"Acceptance\");\n82-  const links = col(\"Spec\") || col(\"Links\");\n83-  co