{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T00:41:55.270Z","ordinal":316006,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016add504e49ec81a0be670f26bb5732f5","usage":{"input_tokens":121970,"cached_input_tokens":120960,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":533,"reasoning_output_tokens":516,"total_tokens":122503},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":52291817,"cached_input_tokens":51667968,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":162720,"reasoning_output_tokens":101873,"total_tokens":52454537},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":5737508995,"cached_input_tokens":5675717248,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":16256168,"reasoning_output_tokens":9339072,"total_tokens":5753765163}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T00:41:56.205Z","ordinal":316007,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a17081-c8ed-75d3-87df-b5aaae61aaa4","call_id":"call_59391027d54c436cbafdffb2db24f980","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — no blocking findings in the four-file diff. The worktree is at the requested base, contains only the expected changes, and passes `git diff --check`. The workflow pins the RC source and verifies the packaging tool against the reviewed workflow commit; the repro identity checks fail closed on source, tool, and artifact mismatches. No tests or suites were run, as instructed.\\n\\nOne reporting caveat: the workflow compares six selected reproducibility assets, while the RC4 release has nine assets. The tarball comparison supports the documented cross-runner claim; clarify that the six are selected assets or compare the remaining three too.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/pr207_independent_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"The repository does not explicitly promise isolation from a hostile process running as the same UID. `safe_fs.ts` describes ownership checks and descriptor verification, but not a separate same-UID security boundary. A same-UID process has the owner’s filesystem authority; a different UID is constrained by directory permissions.\\n\\nFor protection from different-UID actors, the smallest robust change is to verify ownership and write permissions across the parent directories before mutation, including `.nexus` and `.git/info`, and fail closed when another principal can rename those paths. Add a distinct-UID or equivalent permission-based adversarial fixture. The current descriptor checks still help reject symlink redirection.\\n\\nIf protection from hostile same-UID processes is required, this cannot be guaranteed with a final path recheck or ordinary Node `fs` calls. Node 22 exposes path-based opens and descriptor-based I/O, but no dirfd-relative `openat`/`openat2` API ([Node 22 filesystem docs](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-jod/docs/api/fs.html)). A native Linux `openat2` helper can constrain path lookup, but it cannot stop a same-UID process from moving the opened directory afterward ([openat2(2)](https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/openat2.2.html)). That requires a real OS boundary, such as separate UIDs or constrained task execution.\\n\\nSo the post-open rename is a merge blocker only if PR #207 claims protection against arbitrary same-UID concurrent mutation. Otherwise, narrow the documentation and tests to the supported different-principal boundary and record same-UID relocation as a limitation. v1 supports Linux x86-64/glibc, so any native Linux mechanism would also need an explicit kernel requirement and fail-closed preflight.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","create_time":1792888916.2050786}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
