|\n36-| B | Auto with an enforced sandbox by default | Few prompts. bwrap is unavailable on some hosts (WSL, rootless containers), and the Docker fallback is unpinned and networked. Egress is unsolved. |\n37:| **C (original choice; amended 2026-10-24)** | Permission mode controls approvals independently of workspace trust. The default is `review`. `--mode auto` permits writes and commands regardless of folder trust and keeps first-use egress approval per origin. `--yes` and `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` select full access and bypass confirmation prompts, including egress. | Folder trust is a separate choice for loading project instructions and workspace integrations. |\n38-| D | Keep auto | Contradicts REQ-SEC-101; rejected. |\n39-\n40-**Rationale.** Folder trust protects project instructions and workspace integrations from being loaded before the operator approves those sources. Tool authority is governed by the operator's permission settings and must not change when a folder is trusted. A configured `auto` mode remains the operator's choice; when no permission mode is configured, Nexus defaults to `review`.\n41-\n42:**Amendment (2026-10-24, operator direction).** This supersedes the original trust-derived mode and approval behavior. Trust affects project instruction and integration loading only; it does not select or change tool approval mode. Approval behavior follows the configured permission mode, with `review` as the unconfigured default.\n43-\n44-**Further rules:**\n45-- Headless `nexus run` with no TTY: decision-required calls are DENIED with a typed reason unless `--ye…482 tokens truncated…racter.codePointAt(0)!;\n      if (character === \"\\u200d\" || /[\\p{Mark}\\p{Format}]/u.test(character)) return 0;\n      return point >= 0x1100 && (\n        point <= 0x115f || point === 0x2329 || point === 0x232a ||\n        (point >= 0x2e80 && point <= 0xa4cf && point !== 0x303f) ||\n        (point >= 0xac00 && point <= 0xd7a3) || (point >= 0xf900 && point <= 0xfaff) ||\n        (point >= 0xfe10 && point <= 0xfe19) || (point >= 0xfe30 && point <= 0xfe6f) ||\n        (point >= 0xff00 && point <= 0xff60) || (point >= 0xffe0 && point <= 0xffe6) ||\n        (point >= 0x1f000 && point <= 0x1faff) || (point >= 0x20000 && point <= 0x3fffd)\n      ) ? 2 : 1;\n    });\n    width += Math.max(0, ...widths);\n  }\n  return width;\n}\n\ntest(\"trust prompt offers explicit trust, continue-untrusted, and exit choices\", async () => {\n  const workspace = workspaceWithInstructions();\n  const terminal = mockTerminal(true, 40);\n  let trusted = false;\n  try {\n    const decision = promptWorkspaceTrust(workspace, {\n      ...terminal,\n      trustStore: {\n        isTrusted: () => trusted,\n        trust: () => { trusted = true; },\n      },\n    });\n    await new Promise((resolve) => setImmediate(resolve));\n    const rendered = terminal.text.replace(/\\u001b\\[[0-9;?]*[A-Za-z]/g, \"\");\n    assert.match(rendered, /Trust this folder\\?/);\n    assert.match(rendered, /AGENTS\\.md/);\n    assert.match(rendered, /Trust and continue/);\n    assert.match(rendered, /Continue without trusting/);\n    assert.match(rendered, /Exit/);\n    assert.match(rendered, /Trust remembered for this folder/);\n    assert.match(rendered, /Includes future project config changes/);\n    assert.match(rendered, /Tool approvals use permission settings/);\n    assert.match(rendered, /Folder trust doesn't change approvals/);\n    assert.ok(rendered.split(\"\\n\").every((line) => displayWidth(line) <= 40), rendered);\n\n    terminal.input.emit(\"keypress\", undefined, { name: \"down\" });\n    terminal.input.emit(\"keypress\", \"\\r\", { name: \"return\" });\n    assert.equal(await decision, \"untrusted\");\n    assert.equal(trusted, false);\n    assert.equal(terminal.input.isRaw, false);\n  } finally {\n    fs.rmSync(workspace, { recursive: true, force: true });\n  }\n});\n\ntest(\"trust prompt neutralizes bidi controls and fits wide Unicode paths by terminal cells\", async () => {\n  const parent = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-trust-bidi-\"));\n  const workspace = path.join(parent, `項目-${\"界\".repeat(30)}-\\u202eabc-\\u200bdef-\\u2060ghi`);\n  fs.mkdirSync(workspace);\n  const terminal = mockTerminal(true, 40);\n  try {\n    const decision = promptWorkspaceTrust(workspace, {\n      ...terminal,\n      trustStore: { isTrusted: () => false, trust: () => {} },\n    });\n    await new Promise((resolve) => setImmediate(resolve));\n    const rendered = terminal.text.replace(/\\u001b\\[[0-9;?]*[A-Za-z]/g, \"\");\n    assert.equal(rendered.includes(\"\\u202e\"), false);\n    assert.match(rendered, /�abc/);\n    assert.equal(rendered.includes(\"\\u200b\"), false);\n    assert.equal(rendered.includes(\"\\u2060\"), false);\n    assert.match(rendered, /�def/);\n    assert.match(rendered, /�ghi/);\n    assert.ok(rendered.split(\"\\n\").every((line) => displayWidth(line) <= 40), rendered);\n    terminal.input.emit(\"keypress\", \"\\u001b\", { name: \"escape\" });\n    assert.equal(await decision, \"exit\");\n  } finally {\n    fs.rmSync(parent, { recursive: true, force: true });\n  }\n});\n\ntest(\"trust choice persists workspace trust and returns trusted\", async () => {\n  const workspace = workspaceWithInstructions();\n  const terminal = mockTerminal();\n  let trusted = false;\n  try {\n    const decision = promptWorkspaceTrust(workspace, {\n      ...terminal,\n      trustStore: {\n        isTrusted: () => trusted,\n        trust: () => { trusted = true; },\n      },\n    });\n    terminal.input.emit(\"keypress\", \"\\r\", { name: \"return\" });\n    assert.equal(await decision, \"trusted\");\n    assert.equal(trusted, true);\n  } finally {\n    fs.rmSync(workspace, { recursive: true, force: true });\n  }\n});\n\ntest(\"a trust-store write failure leaves the operator free to continue without trust\", async () => {\n  const workspace = workspaceWithInstructions();\n  const terminal = mockTerminal();\n  try {\n    const decision = promptWorkspaceTrust(workspace, {\n      ...terminal,\n      trustStore: {\n        isTrusted: () => false,\n        trust: () => { throw new Error(\"store unavailable\"); },\n      },\n    });\n    terminal.input.emit(\"keypress\", \"\\r\", { name: \"return\" });\n    await new Promise((resolve) => setImmediate(resolve));\n    assert.match(terminal.text, /Trust was not saved: store unavailable/);\n    terminal.input.emit(\"keypress\", \"\\u001b[B\", { name: \"down\" });\n    terminal.input.emit(\"keypress\", \"\\r\", { name: \"return\" });\n    assert.equal(await decision, \"untrusted\");\n  } finally {\n    fs.rmSync(workspace, { recursive: true, force: true });\n  }\n});\n\ntest(\"escape exits without recording trust\", async () => {\n  const workspace = workspaceWithInstructions();\n  const terminal = mockTerminal();\n  let trusted = false;\n  try {\n    const decision = promptWorkspaceTrust(workspace, {\n      ...terminal,\n119:| REQ-SEC-101 | Audit; DEC-01 (amended 2026-10-24) | Without operator opt-in, model-initiated exec and egress require the configured permission decision. Folder trust does not select or change approval mode; unset mode defaults to review. | safety | `config.ts`, `sidecar.ts`, `repl.ts`, `index.ts`, `core/approval_policy.ts` | TEST `test:cli/test/approval_policy.test.ts::\"REQ-SEC-101: the unset mode stays review in trusted and untrusted workspaces\"`; `test:cli/test/config.test.ts::\"workspace trust does not select the tool approval mode\"`; PTY ACC-SAFE-01 still pending | partial | ACC-SAFE-01 | **B** | SEC-01, TUI-07 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\n122:| REQ-SEC-119 | Audit; DEC-01 (amended 2026-10-24) | Nexus-initiated verifier runs are `exec` class and follow configured permission mode; review requires a one-time approval showing the script body. Folder trust alone does not authorize execution; all runs are routed through the runner. | safety | `agent.ts:1654,3544,4255`; `tester.ts:145`; `verifier_gating.test.ts` | TEST `test:cli/test/veri