{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T01:03:35.594Z","ordinal":316656,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-846542c8-6fb0-4d03-be9d-5c804b2c99d4","process_id":"67968","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","nl -ba /home/mike/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | sed -n '777,808p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"nl -ba /home/mike/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | sed -n '777,808p'","name":"MEMORY.md","path":"/home/mike/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"   777\t# Task Group: Nexus v1 CI prerequisite integration and release qualification handoff\n   778\tscope: Integrate reviewed CI prerequisites and accurately track Nexus v1 release gates, claims, and held-out boundaries; use for `v1/integration` readiness work, not as a substitute for exact-RC qualification.\n   779\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/mike/nexus-code (worktree used: /home/mike/nexus-wt/p10g-rebased); reuse_rule=recheck integration HEAD, claim ownership/staleness, exact CI, acceptance documents, and release state; recorded alpha.2 status and blockers are time-specific.\n   780\t\n   781\t## Task 1: Monitor exact-head CI/reviews and merge PR #10 without calling it a release, success for integration; partial for qualification\n   782\t\n   783\t### rollout_summary_files\n   784\t\n   785\t- rollout_summaries/2026-10-16T01-45-07-stRS-t5820_assessment_and_nexus_v1_release_monitoring.md (cwd=/home/mike/Projects/aihost, rollout_path=/home/mike/.codex/sessions/2026/10/16/rollout-2026-10-16T01-45-07-01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-18T01:41:41+00:00, thread_id=01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0, PR #10 integrated; qualification blocked)\n   786\t\n   787\t### keywords\n   788\t\n   789\t- Nexus v1, PR #10, bdc705e593def11ee5e44a6ebd0703b57e5953a0, CI 39085388798, v1/integration, 2c70d39ad4f9c29cff04c909eef9de6d2a29bdb2, check_requirements.mjs --enforce, REQ-QUAL-101, ACCEPTANCE.md, CONCURRENCY.md\n   790\t\n   791\t## Task 2: Record readiness status while the claim is active, success\n   792\t\n   793\t### rollout_summary_files\n   794\t\n   795\t- rollout_summaries/2026-10-16T01-45-07-stRS-t5820_assessment_and_nexus_v1_release_monitoring.md (cwd=/home/mike/Projects/aihost, rollout_path=/home/mike/.codex/sessions/2026/10/16/rollout-2026-10-16T01-45-07-01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-18T01:41:41+00:00, thread_id=01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0, held-out payload preserved; readiness files untouched)\n   796\t\n   797\t### keywords\n   798\t\n   799\t- FILE_docs_v1.0.0_READINESS.md, PLAN-10_READINESS_T2, nexus-claims, stale claim, 24-hour threshold, PR #9, held-out, fresh branch CI\n   800\t\n   801\t## User preferences\n   802\t\n   803\t- reviewers and the release workflow distinguish source/CI acceptance from RC/product qualification -> never call a green CI run a release. [Task 1]\n   804\t- when shared readiness/governance files are claimed, coordinate claim release or wait for the documented stale threshold; do not access held-out payloads or edit the artifact meanwhile. [Task 2]\n   805\t\n   806\t## Reusable knowledge\n   807\t\n   808\t- PR #10 exact head `bdc705e593def11ee5e44a6ebd0703b57e5953a0` passed CI run `39085388798` (contest contract, Node 20/22/24, Linux package/reproducibility) and three independent reviews accepted the code diff. It merged normally to `v1/integration` as `2c70d39ad4f9c29cff04c909eef9de6d2a29bdb2`; the candidate is an ancestor. [Task 1]\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":41466}},"started_at_ms":1792890215593,"completed_at_ms":1792890215594}}
