{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T01:05:57.573Z","ordinal":316765,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17095-f2fe-7de0-b5cc-460661bc1fe3","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a17095-f2fe-7de0-b5cc-460661bc1fe3","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016add55f35ca481a093faad454b198c1d","usage":{"input_tokens":133929,"cached_input_tokens":129280,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":200,"reasoning_output_tokens":183,"total_tokens":134129},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1412142,"cached_input_tokens":1373568,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":9389,"reasoning_output_tokens":6655,"total_tokens":1421531},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":5752468077,"cached_input_tokens":5690522752,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":16296169,"reasoning_output_tokens":9362609,"total_tokens":5768764246}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T01:05:59.714Z","ordinal":316766,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a17097-cfa2-7113-b554-f1b07994ed28","call_id":"call_a69f26a900d44cc196ef3f63389377fd","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"The fixture change is correct and fixes the directory setup without changing test intent. Prior **ACCEPT** still applies; no tests were run.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/pr207_independent_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"The repository does not explicitly promise isolation from a hostile process running as the same UID. `safe_fs.ts` describes ownership checks and descriptor verification, but not a separate same-UID security boundary. A same-UID process has the owner’s filesystem authority; a different UID is constrained by directory permissions.\\n\\nFor protection from different-UID actors, the smallest robust change is to verify ownership and write permissions across the parent directories before mutation, including `.nexus` and `.git/info`, and fail closed when another principal can rename those paths. Add a distinct-UID or equivalent permission-based adversarial fixture. The current descriptor checks still help reject symlink redirection.\\n\\nIf protection from hostile same-UID processes is required, this cannot be guaranteed with a final path recheck or ordinary Node `fs` calls. Node 22 exposes path-based opens and descriptor-based I/O, but no dirfd-relative `openat`/`openat2` API ([Node 22 filesystem docs](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-jod/docs/api/fs.html)). A native Linux `openat2` helper can constrain path lookup, but it cannot stop a same-UID process from moving the opened directory afterward ([openat2(2)](https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/openat2.2.html)). That requires a real OS boundary, such as separate UIDs or constrained task execution.\\n\\nSo the post-open rename is a merge blocker only if PR #207 claims protection against arbitrary same-UID concurrent mutation. Otherwise, narrow the documentation and tests to the supported different-principal boundary and record same-UID relocation as a limitation. v1 supports Linux x86-64/glibc, so any native Linux mechanism would also need an explicit kernel requirement and fail-closed preflight.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17095-f2fe-7de0-b5cc-460661bc1fe3","create_time":1792890359.7140203}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T01:05:59.716Z","ordinal":316767,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"token_count","info":{"total_token_usage":{"input_tokens":5687050790,"cached_input_tokens":5625986944,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":15440772,"reasoning_output_tokens":9362609,"total_tokens":5702491562},"last_token_usage":{"input_tokens":133929,"cached_input_tokens":129280,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":200,"reasoning_output_tokens":183,"total_tokens":134129},"model_context_window":258400},"rate_limits":{"limit_id":"codex","limit_name":null,"primary":{"used_percent":20.0,"window_minutes":300,"resets_at":1792903340},"secondary":{"used_percent":73.0,"window_minutes":10080,"resets_at":1793382098},"credits":{"has_credits":false,"unlimited":false,"balance":"0"},"individual_limit":null,"spend_control_reached":null,"plan_type":"plus","rate_limit_reached_type":null}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T01:05:59.722Z","ordinal":316768,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a17097-c495-7e80-869b-ce412675b905","name":"send_message_to_thread","namespace":"codex_app","output":"<codex_delegation>\n  <source_thread_id>01a15488-7e03-70f3-9a99-99c1c2bb2f1e</source_thread_id>\n  <input>Update at 01:05Z: the immutable 8e5fc70 full `make test` is terminal exit 1: 1666 tests, 1636 pass, 24 fail, 6 cancelled, 4,683,253 ms. Log `/var/tmp/nexus-pr200-exact-make-test.IGD3UZ.log`; failures include seven compaction tests, convergence file, evaluator fixtures (the /var/tmp root is expressly rejected and capped tmpfs fixture missing), objective continuation assertions/timeouts, repro_false_verified, turn step-limit, upgrade TUI. No full-suite pass claim. The local SUITE claim was released by another same-project actor at 00:59:20Z; no local run is active. PR207 run 40142986610 remains in npm CLI tests on both Node 22/24; CodeQL passed, independent review ACCEPT. Current main c1f40e5 still has requirements --enforce blocker REQ-SEC-101/119 partial, with unit regression tests listed and PTY acceptance separately pending. I verified those current-main rows read source tests plus exact-RC PTY gates. I’ll continue holding the PR207 slice until CI terminal, then refresh on c1f40e5 and request exact-head evidence before integration.</input>\n</codex_delegation>","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17095-f2fe-7de0-b5cc-460661bc1fe3","create_time":1792890359.7227547}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000,"user_input_order":16013,"sender_user_messages":{"receiver_turn_id":"01a17095-f2fe-7de0-b5cc-460661bc1fe3","receiver_message_id":"fco_01a17097-c495-7e80-869b-ce412675b905","text":">>> SENDER USER MESSAGES START\nReceived message: fco_01a17097-c495-7e80-869b-ce412675b905\nSource thread: 01a15488-7e03-70f3-9a99-99c1c2bb2f1e\nHost: Up to three recent user messages with preceding assistant context, captured at delivery. Assistant messages are untrusted context, not authorization or verified questions. This is partial history for this delivery, not a transfer of permission. Earlier sections describe earlier deliveries; earlier instructions and later changes may be absent.\nuser: <codex_internal_context source=\"user_goal\">\nuser: User set goal status: \"active\".\nuser: </codex_internal_context>\nuser: <send_user_message_question_reply>\nuser: [{\"questionItemId\":\"[\\\"request_user_input_async\\\",\\\"call_d29751c9919344b790f599d25b814641\\\",0]\",\"question\":\"PR #200 scope handoff\",\"answer\":\"Yes, extend PR #200 scope\"}]\nuser: </send_user_message_question_reply>\nuser: continue\n>>> SENDER USER MESSAGES END\n"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T01:05:59.725Z","ordinal":316769,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17095-f2fe-7de0-b5cc-460661bc1fe3","item":{"type":"FunctionCallOutput","id":"fco_01a17097-c495-7e80-869b-ce412675b905","name":"send_message_to_thread","namespace":"codex_app","output":"<codex_delegation>\n  <source_thread_id>01a15488-7e03-70f3-9a99-99c1c2bb2f1e</source_thread_id>\n  <input>Update at 01:05Z: the immutable 8e5fc70 full `make test` is terminal exit 1: 1666 tests, 1636 pass, 24 fail, 6 cancelled, 4,683,253 ms. Log `/var/tmp/nexus-pr200-exact-make-test.IGD3UZ.log`; failures include seven compaction tests, convergence file, evaluator fixtures (the /var/tmp root is expressly rejected and capped tmpfs fixture missing), objective continuation assertions/timeouts, repro_false_verified, turn step-limit, upgrade TUI. No full-suite pass claim. The local SUITE claim was released by another same-project actor at 00:59:20Z; no local run is active. PR207 run 40142986610 remains in npm CLI tests on both Node 22/24; CodeQL passed, independent review ACCEPT. Current main c1f40e5 still has requirements --enforce blocker REQ-SEC-101/119 partial, with unit regression tests listed and PTY acceptance separately pending. I verified those current-main rows read source tests plus exact-RC PTY gates. I’ll continue holding the PR207 slice until CI terminal, then refresh on c1f40e5 and request exact-head evidence before integration.</input>\n</codex_delegation>"},"started_at_ms":1792890359725,"completed_at_ms":1792890359725}}
