{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T01:06:19.008Z","ordinal":316787,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17095-f2fe-7de0-b5cc-460661bc1fe3","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-1c8ca86a-8e5c-458c-a04e-7048b409b6cd","process_id":"98120","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git ls-tree -r --name-only origin/main scripts/terminal-acceptance docs/v1.0.0 | rg 'terminal|ACCEPTANCE|READINESS|REQUIREMENTS|SPEC-01' | head -50; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | rg -n -A72 -B4 '^### 5\\.3|^## 5|Terminal matrix' | head -100; git show origin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md 2>/dev/null | sed -n '1,180p'; git show origin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh 2>/dev/null | sed -n '1,160p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git ls-tree -r --name-only origin/main scripts/terminal-acceptance docs/v1.0.0 | rg 'terminal|ACCEPTANCE|READINESS|REQUIREMENTS|SPEC-01' | head -50; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | rg -n -A72 -B4 '^### 5\\.3|^## 5|Terminal matrix' | head -100; git show origin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md 2>/dev/null | sed -n '1,180p'; git show origin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh 2>/dev/null | sed -n '1,160p'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/mockgw.py\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/scope-procs.sh\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/summarize.mjs\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh\n77-| ID | Environment | Used for |\n78-|---|---|---|\n79-| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n80-| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n81:| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n82-| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n83-| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n84-\n85-## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\n86-\n87-Every ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\n88-\n89-| Gate | Acceptance IDs | Spec |\n90-|---|---|---|\n91-| Safety | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-10 | SPEC-01 |\n92-| Process ownership | ACC-PROC-01 to ACC-PROC-08 (ACC-PROC-07 is the load test, run in E3) | SPEC-02 |\n93-| Untrusted inputs | ACC-TRUST-01 to ACC-TRUST-09 | SPEC-03 |\n94-| Continuity | ACC-CONT-01 to ACC-CONT-09 (ACC-CONT-10 is in §8) | SPEC-04 |\n95-| Inference | ACC-INF-01 to ACC-INF-09 (ACC-INF-10 is in §4) | SPEC-05 |\n96-| Packaging | ACC-PKG-01 to ACC-PKG-09 | SPEC-06 |\n97-| Supply chain | ACC-SUP-01 to ACC-SUP-08 (artifact-bound ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08 after RC construction) | SPEC-07 |\n98-| Persistence | ACC-PER-01 to ACC-PER-07 | SPEC-08 |\n99-| Governance | ACC-GOV-01 to ACC-GOV-06 | SPEC-09 |\n100-| Verification | ACC-VER-01 to ACC-VER-09 | SPEC-11 |\n101-| Upgrade | ACC-UPG-01 to ACC-UPG-14 | SPEC-12 |\n102-\n103-\n104-### 3.1 Acceptance IDs defined in this file\n105-\n106-These are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\n107-\n108-| ID | Check | Pass condition |\n109-|---|---|---|\n110-| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\n111-| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\n112-| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\n113-| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\n114-| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\n115-| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\n116-| ACC-PLAT | E2 matrix, §7 | All rows pass. |\n117-| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n118-| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n119-| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n120-| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n121-| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\n122-\n123-## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n124-\n125-### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\n126-\n127-1. `export HOME=$(mktemp -d)`.\n128-2. Install the RC with the documented command.\n129-3. Create `~/.config/nexus/config.env` containing only:\n130-   - `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:<proxy>/v1`\n131-   - `LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=<id as listed by the proxy>`\n132-   - `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=REDACTED\n133-\n134-   No gateway token file, no homelab paths, no `NODE_*` overrides.\n135-4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\n136-5. Run `nexus doctor --json` and archive it. It must report the server kind and context source with no `gateway` capability.\n137-\n138-### 4.2 Standalone matrix\n139-\n140-| Profile | What Nexus sees | Runs | Pass condition |\n141-|---|---|---|---|\n142-| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\n143-| P-llamacpp | Emulated llama.cpp `/props` and overflow body | Same tasks × 1 run; plus the forced-overflow case (context limit set to 8k) | Context discovered from `/props`. Overflow gives one compact-and-retry, then success or an actionable error. |\n144-| P-vllm | Emulated `max_model_len` and vLLM overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `max_model_len` |\n145-| P-ollama | Emulated `/api/show` and Ollama overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `ollama_show` |\n146-| Conformance | CI fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama shapes | CI | All pass (ACC-INF-01, -02, -05) |\n147-\n148-ACC-INF-10 passes only when every row passes. The release notes state the scope in the form required by DEC-16.\n149-\n150-### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\n151-\n152-| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\n153-|---|---|---|\n--\n155-| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\n156-| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\n157-| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\n158-\n159:## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n160-\n161-### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\n162-\n163-These must pass:\n164-\n165-- `tui_approval_input_e2e`\n166-- `tui_diff_e2e`\n167-- `tui_maturity_e2e`\n168-- `tui_model_picker_e2e`\n169-- `tui_multiline_e2e`\n170-- `tui_surface_e2e`\n171-- new: `repl_approval_e2e`\n172-- new: `process_lifecycle_e2e`\n173-- new: `startup_unreachable_e2e`\n174-- new: the package PTY smoke\n175-\n176-### 5.2 Scripted PTY scenarios against the installed RC (E3, mock gateway)\n# Manual real-terminal matrix (ACCEPTANCE §5.3, REQ-QUAL-108)\n\nA human runs this procedure against the **installed RC**. Automated PTY suites (§5.1, §5.2) do not replace it.\n\n**Cells:** five terminals, each at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60, giving 15 cells.\n- xterm\n- kitty, with the kitty keyboard protocol on\n- tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal\n- the VS Code integrated terminal\n- GNOME Terminal\n\n**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6. Any other FAIL needs a written disposition.\n\n## Before you start\n\n1. Install the RC with the documented one-line command. `nexus --version` must print the RC version, and `nexus` must\n   not resolve into a checkout.\n2. Choose a new evidence directory, `OUT=docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/terminal`, and use it for every cell.\n3. You need a screenshot tool, and `python3` and `git` on `PATH`. No inference is used: a local mock gateway\n   (`mockgw.py`) answers every request.\n\n## Each cell\n\nOpen the terminal and resize it to the cell's size. For tmux, start tmux inside GNOME Terminal. For kitty, enable the\nkeyboard protocol. Then run:\n\n```sh\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh --rc <rc> --terminal <xterm|kitty|tmux-gnome|vscode|gnome> --size <WxH> --out \"$OUT\"\n```\n\nThe script refuses to start in these cases: the wrong RC, a checkout build, the wrong size, not inside tmux for\n`tmux-gnome`, or a cell already recorded. It creates an isolated HOME and workspace and starts the mock. Then it opens\nthe TUI twice, once normally and once with `NO_COLOR=1`, and prompts you through checks 1–7:\n\n| # | You do | You judge |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | The TUI opens | It renders correctly at this size |\n| 2 | Prompt `approve`. At each approval panel, type continuously, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key | No decision is made by the stray input, and the deliberate key decides. **Screenshot the panel.** |\n| 3 | Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter while composing | It inserts a newline and does not submit |\n| 4 | Prompt `stream`, then resize while it streams and restore the size | Layout recovers and nothing is garbled or lost |\n| 5 | Prompt `sleep`, then press Esc while `sleep 30` runs | Cancel is acknowledged, and nothing survives |\n| 6 | Press Ctrl-C twice to quit | The terminal is restored: echo on, no stray escape codes. **Screenshot the terminal after exit.** |\n| 7 | Second launch, with `NO_COLOR=1` | The TUI is readable without colour |\n\nThe script also **measures** two things:\n- whether `stty` state after each exit equals the state before it;\n- any process started from the cell's HOME that is still running after exit.\n\nA measured survivor or unavailable systemd-scope measurement fails check 5, and an unrestored terminal fails check 6, whatever you recorded. A zero survivor count is recorded only when the scope's `cgroup.procs` file was readable or systemd confirmed the scope stopped or disappeared. Missing or unreadable scope data while the unit is active is recorded as unavailable and fails the matrix gate. Each cell writes\n`cell-<terminal>-<size>.json` with the RC version, binary path and SHA-256, terminal environment, measurements, your\nresults and notes, screenshot hashes, and the mock request log. A cell is recorded once. To retry, keep the failed\nattempt and use a new evidence directory.\n\n## Gate\n\nThe deterministic systemd-scope measurement fixtures run as part of `npm test` in `cli/`. They cover empty and\npopulated cgroups, stopped and missing units, unavailable or malformed measurements, and the summary gate's response\nto an unavailable measurement.\n\n```sh\n# MANIFEST_SHA: sha256 of MANIFEST.sha256 inside the RC archive, e.g.\n#   tar -xzOf nexus-linux-x86_64-<rc>.tar.gz --wildcards '*/MANIFEST.sha256' | sha256sum\nnode scripts/terminal-acceptance/summarize.mjs \"$OUT\" --rc <rc> --manifest-sha256 \"$MANIFEST_SHA\" [--dispositions dispositions.json]\n```\n\nThe summarizer prints the 15-cell table and writes `matrix-summary.json`. **PASS** requires all of the following:\n- every cell is present (a missing cell is NOT RUN);\n- every attempt names the given RC, and its installed package manifest equals the archive's;\n- checks 2, 5 and 6 have no FAIL;\n- every other FAIL has an entry `\"<cell>:<check>\": \"<fix or documented known limitation>\"` in the dispositions file;\n- every aborted attempt (a `.partial` file, which holds the measurements taken before it was abandoned) has an entry\n  `\"<cell>:partial-<n>\"`.\n\nThe record hashes prove that files are unchanged since recording, not who recorded them. Commit the evidence directory\nto the qualification evidence PR to make it authoritative.\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# One cell of the manual real-terminal matrix (ACCEPTANCE §5.3), run by a human INSIDE the terminal under test, sized\n# to the cell. It verifies the installed RC package and the terminal, launches the TUI against a deterministic local\n# mock from an isolated HOME and a whitelisted environment, and captures what can be measured:\n#   - terminal state (stty) before and after each exit;\n#   - processes from the cell (by HOME or workspace cwd) that survive an exit, with a planted positive control;\n#   - the mock's request log, which proves which scenarios ran.\n# The human records PASS/FAIL per check and two screenshots. Every attempt is kept. Usage:\n#   scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh --rc v1.0.0-rc.N --terminal <xterm|kitty|tmux-gnome|vscode|gnome> \\\n#     --size <80x24|40x14|200x60> --out <evidence dir>\nset -euo pipefail\n\nHERE=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd)\"\nreadonly HERE\nsource \"$HERE/scope-procs.sh\"\nrc=\"\" terminal=\"\" size=\"\" out=\"\"\nwhile [[ $# -gt 0 ]]; do\n  case \"$1\" in\n    --rc) rc=\"$2\"; shift 2 ;;\n    --terminal) terminal=\"$2\"; shift 2 ;;\n    --size) size=\"$2\"; shift 2 ;;\n    --out) out=\"$2\"; shift 2 ;;\n    *) echo \"unknown argument $1\" >&2; exit 2 ;;\n  esac\ndone\n[[ \"$rc\" =~ ^v[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+-rc\\.[0-9]+$ ]] || { echo \"--rc must be an RC tag, vX.Y.Z-rc.N\" >&2; exit 2; }\n[[ \"$terminal\" =~ ^(xterm|kitty|tmux-gnome|vscode|gnome)$ ]] || { echo \"--terminal must be xterm|kitty|tmux-gnome|vscode|gnome\" >&2; exit 2; }\n[[ \"$size\" =~ ^(80x24|40x14|200x60)$ ]] || { echo \"--size must be 80x24|40x14|200x60\" >&2; exit 2; }\n[[ -n \"$out\" ]] || { echo \"--out is required\" >&2; exit 2; }\n[[ -t 0 && -t 1 ]] || { echo \"run this interactively in the terminal under test\" >&2; exit 2; }\n\n# Identity: the installed RC package (VERSION and its own MANIFEST.sha256), never a checkout build.\nnexus_bin=\"$(command -v nexus)\" || { echo \"nexus is not on PATH; install the RC with the documented one-line command\" >&2; exit 2; }\nnexus_real=\"$(readlink -f \"$nexus_bin\")\"\npackage=\"$(dirname \"$(dirname \"$nexus_real\")\")\"\n[[ \"$(cat \"$package/VERSION\" 2>/dev/null)\" == \"$rc\" ]] || { echo \"nexus resolves to $nexus_real, which is not an installed $rc package\" >&2; exit 2; }\n(cd \"$package\" && sha256sum --check --status MANIFEST.sha256) || { echo \"installed package at $package fails its MANIFEST.sha256\" >&2; exit 2; }\n# The manifest must also list every file: an extra file in the package would pass sha256sum --check.\ndiff <(cd \"$package\" && find . -type f ! -name MANIFEST.sha256 | sed 's|^\\./||' | LC_ALL=C sort) \\\n     <(sed -E 's/^[0-9a-f]{64} [ *]//; s|^\\./||' \"$package/MANIFEST.sha256\" | LC_ALL=C sort) >/dev/null \\\n  || { echo \"installed package at $package has files its MANIFEST.sha256 does not list\" >&2; exit 2; }\nmanifest_sha=\"$(sha256sum \"$package/MANIFEST.sha256\" | cut -d' ' -f1)\"\nversion_line=\"$(nexus --version 2>&1 | head -n 1)\"\n[[ \"$(grep -oE '[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+(-[0-9A-Za-z.]+)?' <<< \"$version_line\" | head -n 1)\" == \"${rc#v}\" ]] || { echo \"nexus reports '$version_line', not exactly ${rc#v}\" >&2; exit 2; }\n\n# Terminal: the cell's size, and environment consistent with the claimed terminal.\nwant_cols=\"${size%x*}\" want_rows=\"${size#*x}\"\nread -r rows cols < <(stty size)\n[[ \"$cols\" == \"$want_cols\" && \"$rows\" == \"$want_rows\" ]] || { echo \"terminal is ${cols}x${rows}; resize it to $size first\" >&2; exit 2; }\ntmux_version=\"\"\ncase \"$terminal\" in\n  xterm) [[ -n \"${XTERM_VERSION:-}\" && -z \"${TMUX:-}\" ]] || { echo \"XTERM_VERSION unset or inside tmux: not xterm\" >&2; exit 2; } ;;\n  kitty) [[ -n \"${KITTY_WINDOW_ID:-}\" && -z \"${TMUX:-}\" ]] || { echo \"KITTY_WINDOW_ID unset or inside tmux: not kitty\" >&2; exit 2; } ;;\n  vscode) [[ \"${TERM_PROGRAM:-}\" == vscode ]] || { echo \"TERM_PROGRAM is not vscode\" >&2; exit 2; } ;;\n  gnome) [[ -n \"${GNOME_TERMINAL_SCREEN:-}${GNOME_TERMINAL_SERVICE:-}\" && -z \"${TMUX:-}\" ]] || { echo \"GNOME_TERMINAL_SCREEN/SERVICE unset or inside tmux: not GNOME Terminal\" >&2; exit 2; } ;;\n  tmux-gnome)\n    [[ -n \"${TMUX:-}\" && -n \"${GNOME_TERMINAL_SCREEN:-}${GNOME_TERMINAL_SERVICE:-}\" ]] || { echo \"run inside tmux inside GNOME Terminal\" >&2; exit 2; }\n    tmux_version=\"$(tmux -V)\"; [[ \"$tmux_version\" =~ ^tmux\\ 3\\. ]] || { echo \"need tmux 3.x, have $tmux_version\" >&2; exit 2; } ;;\nesac\nkitty_protocol=\"\"\nif [[ \"$terminal\" == kitty ]]; then\n  read -r -p \"Is the kitty keyboard protocol enabled for this window? (yes/no) \" kitty_protocol\n  [[ \"$kitty_protocol\" == yes ]] || { echo \"enable the kitty keyboard protocol first\" >&2; exit 2; }\nfi\n\n# The scope-based survivor check needs the user's systemd manager.\nsystemd-run --user --scope --quiet -- true || { echo \"systemd user scopes are unavailable in this session\" >&2; exit 2; }\n\n# Attempts are numbered in one directory and never overwritten; the gate counts every attempt, including aborted ones.\ncell=\"$terminal-$size\"\nmkdir -p \"$out\"\nattempt=1\nwhile [[ -e \"$out/cell-$cell.attempt-$attempt.json\" || -e \"$out/cell-$cell.attempt-$attempt.partial\" ]]; do attempt=$((attempt + 1)); done\nstem=\"$out/cell-$cell.attempt-$attempt\"\nattempt_start=\"$(date +%s)\"\n: > \"$stem.partial\"\n\n# Isolated HOME and workspace; nothing touches the operator's ~/.nexus or ~/.config/nexus.\ncell_home=\"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/nexus-terminal-$cell.XXXXXX\")\"\nws=\"$cell_home/workspace\"\nmkdir -p \"$ws\" \"$cell_home/.config/nexus\"\ngit -C \"$ws\" init -q\nprintf 'terminal matrix workspace\\n' > \"$ws/README.md\"\nmock_log=\"$cell_home/mock.log\"\npython3 \"$HERE/mockgw.py\" \"$cell_home/port\" \"$mock_log\" &\nmock_pid=$!\ncanary_pid=\"\"\ncleanup() { kill \"$mock_pid\" ${canary_pid:+\"$canary_pid\"} 2>/dev/null || true; rm -rf \"$cell_home\"; }\ntrap cleanup EXIT\nfor _ in $(seq 50); do [[ -s \"$cell_home/port\" ]] && break; sleep 0.1; done\nport=\"$(cat \"$cell_home/port\")\"\nprintf 'LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:%s/v1\\nLOCAL_LLM_MODEL=terminal-matrix\\n' \"$port\" > \"$cell_home/.config/nexus/config.env\"\n\n# The TUI sees only a whitelisted environment, so operator gateway or API settings cannot redirect it.\nlaunch_env=(env -i PATH=\"$PATH\" HOME=\"$cell_home\" XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"$cell_home/.config\" XDG_DATA_HOME=\"$cell_home/.local/share\"\n  XDG_STATE_HOME=\"$cell_home/.local/state\" XDG_CACHE_HOME=\"$cell_home/.cache\" LANG=\"${LANG:-C.UTF-8}\")\nfor var in TERM COLORTERM TERM_PROGRAM TERM_PROGRAM_VERSION VTE_VERSION KITTY_WINDOW_ID TMUX TMUX_PANE XTERM_VERSION DISPLAY WAYLAND_DISPLAY XDG_RUNTIME_DIR DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS; do\n  [[ -n \"${!var:-}\" ]] && launch_env+=(\"$var=${!var}\")\ndone\n\n# Processes from this cell: HOME is the cell's HOME, or the working directory is inside the cell workspace.\ncell_processes() {\n  local pid\n  for pid in $(pgrep -u \"$(id -u)\"); do\n    [[ \"$pid\" == \"$mock_pid\" || \"$pid\" == \"$$\" || \"$pid\" == \"$BASHPID\" ]] && continue\n    if tr '\\0' '\\n' < \"/proc/$pid/environ\" 2>/dev/null | grep -qx \"HOME=$cell_home\" || [[ \"$(readlink \"/proc/$pid/cwd\" 2>/dev/null)\" == \"$ws\"* ]]; then\n      echo \"$pid\"\n    fi\n  done\n}\n# Positive control: the scan must find a planted process before it is trusted to report zero.\n(cd \"$ws\" && exec env HOME=\"$cell_home\" sleep 600) &\ncanary_pid=$!\nsleep 0.3\ncell_processes | grep -qx \"$canary_pid\" || { echo \"survivor scan cannot see a planted cell process; refusing to measure\" >&2; exit 1; }\nkill \"$canary_pid\"; wait \"$canary_pid\" 2>/dev/null || true; canary_pid=\"\"\n\n# Each launch runs in its own transient systemd user scope. The cgroup probe\n# reports zero only for a readable empty cgroup or a scope systemd confirms is\n# stopped/gone; missing data while active remains an explicit failed measure.\nlaunch() {\n  local label=\"$1\"; shift\n  local before after status=0 survivors scoped scope_measurement=verified unit=\"nexus-terminal-$cell-$attempt-$label\"\n  before=\"$(stty -g)\"\n  (cd \"$ws\" && systemd-run --user --scope --quiet --unit=\"$unit\" -- \"${launch_env[@]}\" \"$@\" nexus) || status=$?\n  after=\"$(stty -g)\"\n  sleep 2\n  if ! scoped=\"$(nexus_terminal_scope_procs \"$unit\")\"; then\n    scoped=0\n    scope_measurement=unavailable\n  fi\n  survivors=\"$(cell_processes | wc -l)\"\n  (( scoped > survivors )) && survivors=\"$scoped\"\n  [[ \"$survivors\" == 0 && \"$scope_measurement\" == verified ]] || { cell_processes | xargs -r ps -o pid=,args= -p >&2; systemctl --user kill --signal=KILL \"$unit.scope\" 2>/dev/null || true; }\n  printf '%s\\t%s\\t%s\\t%s\\t%s\\t%s\\n' \"$label\" \"$status\" \"$([[ \"$before\" == \"$after\" ]] && echo true || echo false)\" \"$survivors\" \"$scope_measurement\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" >> \"$cell_home/exits.tsv\"\n  # Measurements reach the evidence directory as they happen, so an attempt abandoned later still shows them.\n  cp \"$cell_home/exits.tsv\" \"$stem.partial\"\n}\n\ncat <<EOF\n\n=== Cell $cell, attempt $attempt ($rc, package $package) ===\nIn the TUI that opens next (the first word of each prompt selects the mock scenario):\n  1  It launches and shows the TUI.\n  2  Prompt \"approve\". While each of the two approval panels is open, type continuously, paste 3 lines, then\n     approve with a deliberate key. Screenshot an approval panel.\n  3  Enter a multiline prompt with Shift+Enter (or Alt+Enter).\n  4  Prompt \"stream\" and resize the window while it streams; restore $size afterwards.\n  5  Prompt \"sleep\" and press Esc while \"sleep 30\" runs.\n  6  Quit with Ctrl-C twice. Screenshot the terminal after exit.\nPress Enter to launch.\nEOF\nread -r _\nlaunch main\ncat <<EOF\n\n7  NO_COLOR: the TUI opens again with NO_COLOR=1. Check that it is readable without colour, then quit with Ctrl-C twice.\nPress Enter to launch.\nEOF\nread -r _\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":28160}},"started_at_ms":1792890379007,"completed_at_ms":1792890379008}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T01:06:20.252Z","ordinal":316788,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17098-1fdc-74a3-8481-6939354c7674","call_id":"call_3e23abcd19d24a489b85f8d99012bd2b","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 5524)\nTotal output lines: 346\n\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/mockgw.py\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/scope-procs.sh\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/summarize.mjs\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh\n77-| ID | Environment | Used for |\n78-|---|---|---|\n79-| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n80-| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n81:| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n82-| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n83-| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n84-\n85-## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\n86-\n87-Every ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\n88-\n89-| Gate | Acceptance IDs | Spec |\n90-|---|---|---|\n91-| Safety | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-10 | SPEC-01 |\n92-| Process ownership | ACC-PROC-01 to ACC-PROC-08 (ACC-PROC-07 is the load test, run in E3) | SPEC-02 |\n93-| Untrusted inputs | ACC-TRUST-01 to ACC-TRUST-09 | SPEC-03 |\n94-| Continuity | ACC-CONT-01 to ACC-CONT-09 (ACC-CONT-10 is in §8) | SPEC-04 |\n95-| Inference | ACC-INF-01 to ACC-INF-09 (ACC-INF-10 is in §4) | SPEC-05 |\n96-| Packaging | ACC-PKG-01 to ACC-PKG-09 | SPEC-06 |\n97-| Supply chain | ACC-SUP-01 to ACC-SUP-08 (artifact-bound ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08 after RC construction) | SPEC-07 |\n98-| Persistence | ACC-PER-01 to ACC-PER-07 | SPEC-08 |\n99-| Governance | ACC-GOV-01 to ACC-GOV-06 | SPEC-09 |\n100-| Verification | ACC-VER-01 to ACC-VER-09 | SPEC-11 |\n101-| Upgrade | ACC-UPG-01 to ACC-UPG-14 | SPEC-12 |\n102-\n103-\n104-### 3.1 Acceptance IDs defined in this file\n105-\n106-These are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\n107-\n108-| ID | Check | Pass condition |\n109-|---|---|---|\n110-| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\n111-| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\n112-| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\n113-| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\n114-| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\n115-| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\n116-| ACC-PLAT | E2 matrix, §7 | All rows pass. |\n117-| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n118-| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n119-| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n120-| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n121-| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\n122-\n123-## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n124-\n125-### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\n126-\n127-1. `export HOME=$(mktemp -d)`.\n128-2. Install the RC with the documented command.\n129-3. Create `~/.config/nexus/config.env` containing only:\n130-   - `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:<proxy>/v1`\n131-   - `LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=<id as listed by the proxy>`\n132-   - `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=REDACTED\n133-\n134-   No gateway token file, no homelab paths, no `NODE_*` overrides.\n135-4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\n136-5. Run `nexus doctor --json` and archive it. It must report the server kind and context source with no `gateway` capability.\n137-\n138-### 4.2 Standalone matrix\n139-\n140-| Profile | What Nexus sees | Runs | Pass condition |\n141-|---|---|---|---|\n142-| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\n143-| P-llamacpp | Emulated llama.cpp `/props` and overflow body | Same tasks…2324 tokens truncated… Terminal: the cell's size, and environment consistent with the claimed terminal.\nwant_cols=\"${size%x*}\" want_rows=\"${size#*x}\"\nread -r rows cols < <(stty size)\n[[ \"$cols\" == \"$want_cols\" && \"$rows\" == \"$want_rows\" ]] || { echo \"terminal is ${cols}x${rows}; resize it to $size first\" >&2; exit 2; }\ntmux_version=\"\"\ncase \"$terminal\" in\n  xterm) [[ -n \"${XTERM_VERSION:-}\" && -z \"${TMUX:-}\" ]] || { echo \"XTERM_VERSION unset or inside tmux: not xterm\" >&2; exit 2; } ;;\n  kitty) [[ -n \"${KITTY_WINDOW_ID:-}\" && -z \"${TMUX:-}\" ]] || { echo \"KITTY_WINDOW_ID unset or inside tmux: not kitty\" >&2; exit 2; } ;;\n  vscode) [[ \"${TERM_PROGRAM:-}\" == vscode ]] || { echo \"TERM_PROGRAM is not vscode\" >&2; exit 2; } ;;\n  gnome) [[ -n \"${GNOME_TERMINAL_SCREEN:-}${GNOME_TERMINAL_SERVICE:-}\" && -z \"${TMUX:-}\" ]] || { echo \"GNOME_TERMINAL_SCREEN/SERVICE unset or inside tmux: not GNOME Terminal\" >&2; exit 2; } ;;\n  tmux-gnome)\n    [[ -n \"${TMUX:-}\" && -n \"${GNOME_TERMINAL_SCREEN:-}${GNOME_TERMINAL_SERVICE:-}\" ]] || { echo \"run inside tmux inside GNOME Terminal\" >&2; exit 2; }\n    tmux_version=\"$(tmux -V)\"; [[ \"$tmux_version\" =~ ^tmux\\ 3\\. ]] || { echo \"need tmux 3.x, have $tmux_version\" >&2; exit 2; } ;;\nesac\nkitty_protocol=\"\"\nif [[ \"$terminal\" == kitty ]]; then\n  read -r -p \"Is the kitty keyboard protocol enabled for this window? (yes/no) \" kitty_protocol\n  [[ \"$kitty_protocol\" == yes ]] || { echo \"enable the kitty keyboard protocol first\" >&2; exit 2; }\nfi\n\n# The scope-based survivor check needs the user's systemd manager.\nsystemd-run --user --scope --quiet -- true || { echo \"systemd user scopes are unavailable in this session\" >&2; exit 2; }\n\n# Attempts are numbered in one directory and never overwritten; the gate counts every attempt, including aborted ones.\ncell=\"$terminal-$size\"\nmkdir -p \"$out\"\nattempt=1\nwhile [[ -e \"$out/cell-$cell.attempt-$attempt.json\" || -e \"$out/cell-$cell.attempt-$attempt.partial\" ]]; do attempt=$((attempt + 1)); done\nstem=\"$out/cell-$cell.attempt-$attempt\"\nattempt_start=\"$(date +%s)\"\n: > \"$stem.partial\"\n\n# Isolated HOME and workspace; nothing touches the operator's ~/.nexus or ~/.config/nexus.\ncell_home=\"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/nexus-terminal-$cell.XXXXXX\")\"\nws=\"$cell_home/workspace\"\nmkdir -p \"$ws\" \"$cell_home/.config/nexus\"\ngit -C \"$ws\" init -q\nprintf 'terminal matrix workspace\\n' > \"$ws/README.md\"\nmock_log=\"$cell_home/mock.log\"\npython3 \"$HERE/mockgw.py\" \"$cell_home/port\" \"$mock_log\" &\nmock_pid=$!\ncanary_pid=\"\"\ncleanup() { kill \"$mock_pid\" ${canary_pid:+\"$canary_pid\"} 2>/dev/null || true; rm -rf \"$cell_home\"; }\ntrap cleanup EXIT\nfor _ in $(seq 50); do [[ -s \"$cell_home/port\" ]] && break; sleep 0.1; done\nport=\"$(cat \"$cell_home/port\")\"\nprintf 'LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:%s/v1\\nLOCAL_LLM_MODEL=terminal-matrix\\n' \"$port\" > \"$cell_home/.config/nexus/config.env\"\n\n# The TUI sees only a whitelisted environment, so operator gateway or API settings cannot redirect it.\nlaunch_env=(env -i PATH=\"$PATH\" HOME=\"$cell_home\" XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"$cell_home/.config\" XDG_DATA_HOME=\"$cell_home/.local/share\"\n  XDG_STATE_HOME=\"$cell_home/.local/state\" XDG_CACHE_HOME=\"$cell_home/.cache\" LANG=\"${LANG:-C.UTF-8}\")\nfor var in TERM COLORTERM TERM_PROGRAM TERM_PROGRAM_VERSION VTE_VERSION KITTY_WINDOW_ID TMUX TMUX_PANE XTERM_VERSION DISPLAY WAYLAND_DISPLAY XDG_RUNTIME_DIR DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS; do\n  [[ -n \"${!var:-}\" ]] && launch_env+=(\"$var=${!var}\")\ndone\n\n# Processes from this cell: HOME is the cell's HOME, or the working directory is inside the cell workspace.\ncell_processes() {\n  local pid\n  for pid in $(pgrep -u \"$(id -u)\"); do\n    [[ \"$pid\" == \"$mock_pid\" || \"$pid\" == \"$$\" || \"$pid\" == \"$BASHPID\" ]] && continue\n    if tr '\\0' '\\n' < \"/proc/$pid/environ\" 2>/dev/null | grep -qx \"HOME=$cell_home\" || [[ \"$(readlink \"/proc/$pid/cwd\" 2>/dev/null)\" == \"$ws\"* ]]; then\n      echo \"$pid\"\n    fi\n  done\n}\n# Positive control: the scan must find a planted process before it is trusted to report zero.\n(cd \"$ws\" && exec env HOME=\"$cell_home\" sleep 600) &\ncanary_pid=$!\nsleep 0.3\ncell_processes | grep -qx \"$canary_pid\" || { echo \"survivor scan cannot see a planted cell process; refusing to measure\" >&2; exit 1; }\nkill \"$canary_pid\"; wait \"$canary_pid\" 2>/dev/null || true; canary_pid=\"\"\n\n# Each launch runs in its own transient systemd user scope. The cgroup probe\n# reports zero only for a readable empty cgroup or a scope systemd confirms is\n# stopped/gone; missing data while active remains an explicit failed measure.\nlaunch() {\n  local label=\"$1\"; shift\n  local before after status=0 survivors scoped scope_measurement=verified unit=\"nexus-terminal-$cell-$attempt-$label\"\n  before=\"$(stty -g)\"\n  (cd \"$ws\" && systemd-run --user --scope --quiet --unit=\"$unit\" -- \"${launch_env[@]}\" \"$@\" nexus) || status=$?\n  after=\"$(stty -g)\"\n  sleep 2\n  if ! scoped=\"$(nexus_terminal_scope_procs \"$unit\")\"; then\n    scoped=0\n    scope_measurement=unavailable\n  fi\n  survivors=\"$(cell_processes | wc -l)\"\n  (( scoped > survivors )) && survivors=\"$scoped\"\n  [[ \"$survivors\" == 0 && \"$scope_measurement\" == verified ]] || { cell_processes | xargs -r ps -o pid=,args= -p >&2; systemctl --user kill --signal=KILL \"$unit.scope\" 2>/dev/null || true; }\n  printf '%s\\t%s\\t%s\\t%s\\t%s\\t%s\\n' \"$label\" \"$status\" \"$([[ \"$before\" == \"$after\" ]] && echo true || echo false)\" \"$survivors\" \"$scope_measurement\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" >> \"$cell_home/exits.tsv\"\n  # Measurements reach the evidence directory as they happen, so an attempt abandoned later still shows them.\n  cp \"$cell_home/exits.tsv\" \"$stem.partial\"\n}\n\ncat <<EOF\n\n=== Cell $cell, attempt $attempt ($rc, package $package) ===\nIn the TUI that opens next (the first word of each prompt selects the mock scenario):\n  1  It launches and shows the TUI.\n  2  Prompt \"approve\". While each of the two approval panels is open, type continuously, paste 3 lines, then\n     approve with a deliberate key. Screenshot an approval panel.\n  3  Enter a multiline prompt with Shift+Enter (or Alt+Enter).\n  4  Prompt \"stream\" and resize the window while it streams; restore $size afterwards.\n  5  Prompt \"sleep\" and press Esc while \"sleep 30\" runs.\n  6  Quit with Ctrl-C twice. Screenshot the terminal after exit.\nPress Enter to launch.\nEOF\nread -r _\nlaunch main\ncat <<EOF\n\n7  NO_COLOR: the TUI opens again with NO_COLOR=1. Check that it is readable without colour, then quit with Ctrl-C twice.\nPress Enter to launch.\nEOF\nread -r _\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17095-f2fe-7de0-b5cc-460661bc1fe3","create_time":1792890380.2528152}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
