reference validation, effective access separation, and current custody acceptance remain unverified here. No payload, validator, reference solution, or hidden answer was accessed, and no held-out run has started.\n- **Other qualification gates:** No installed-RC provider or standalone matrix, T2/T3/T4 scored qualification, exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility, or independent RC acceptance exists. `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3 and `scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md` define the human five-environment × three-size matrix and evidence capture; all 15 real-terminal cells remain unrun because no RC is installed. Automated PTY results do not replace those operator results.\n- **Version, RC, and publication:** Root and CLI package versions remain `0.1.0-alpha.2`. GitHub currently lists only alpha pre-releases `v0.1.0-alpha.1` and `v0.1.0-alpha.2`; no `v1.0.0-rc.N` artifact/tag or stable v1.0.0 tag, npm package, or GitHub release exists. Follow the staged lifecycle in `ACCEPTANCE.md`: pre-RC source gates, RC construction, artifact-bound RC gates, installed-RC qualification and independent G6 acceptance, then stable promotion/publication and post-publication verification.\n\nThe 2026-10-18 checkpoint sections below remain historical evidence. The previously closed PR #46 was never merged; its two readiness commits remain available on the preserved closed-PR branch, not in this reconciliation branch's history, and are superseded by this exact `8f4504e` update.\n\n## Publication status correction (2026-10-18 17:25 UTC)\n\nThe 17:16 checkpoint's phrase “nothing has been tagged or published” was too broad. GitHub lists the existing pre-releases `v0.1.0-alpha.1` and `v0.1.0-alpha.2`, with corresponding tags `7e46bb0da88d06552a66ef703f53a05d1de1f37d` and `c3dcafac93b5f52d913b4dfb6eb292bbcede4566`. Post-merge CI run `39146982849` and CodeQL passed on exact integration `6a16cb60635c9182f13be1635d5f44eddebdcde0`. No v1.0.0 release candidate or stable v1.0.0 publication exists. The superseded 17:16 text below is retained verbatim as historical evidence; this correction is authoritative for current release status.\n\n## Current state update (2026-10-18 17:16 UTC, `6a16cb6`)\n\n- **Authoritative integration and CI:** `origin/v1/integration` is `6a16cb60635c9182f13be1635d5f44eddebdcde0`, merge commit for PR #45, whose only changed file was `docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md`. PR #45 exact-head CI run `39144798481` and CodeQL run `39144798415` passed; independent read-only review accepted exact head `8041c0dbe1a982b2a9e275083f336eb4c5b768b3`. Post-merge CodeQL run `39146982807` passed. Post-merge CI run `39146982849` is in progress on exact `6a16cb6`: Cloudflare and Node 20/22/24 passed; Linux `linux-x86_64` is still executing the CLI suite. This checkpoint does not combine its status with results from another revision.\n- **PR and evaluator state:** PRs #9, #13, #15, #16, #44, and #45 are integrated. PR #33 remains open at `0ca77e5ee64f80db02e2b16178c5be551ce5de0c` on stale base `faf95803714a3c543f5c59bc0610ca6291a6184d`. Its exact CI run `39141771002` passed on that old head, but independent review found qualification preflight does not account for host-source mounts created unconditionally by `agentSandboxArgv`. The finding is recorded in comment `6252102243`; a read-only source inventory and shared-mount-plan remediation target are in comment `6252621855`. Owner handoff request `6252543078` has no response as of this checkpoint. The evaluator claim remains protected. Do not execute held-out tasks until this boundary is fixed, exact-head validated, and independently accepted.\n- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` ran in a detached worktree at exact `6a16cb60635c9182f13be1635d5f44eddebdcde0` with isolated `HOME` and failed as required. It reports 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open) and 11 below threshold: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. The exact result is recorded in the claims log and was sent to the ledger owner in PR #17 comment `6252582027`; no ledger status changed.\n- **Held-out custody and qualification:** The custodian previously accepted the sealed 40-task manifest identity `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b` and its private digest/reference validation. This does not establish evaluator acceptance or T2 qualification. The implementing agent has not accessed private payloads. No held-out run has started because evaluator confidentiality preflight remains unaccepted and corpus/evaluator schema compatibility is unresolved.\n- **Other qualification and release gates:** Provider/standalone, T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, qualification-host validation, and human five-environment × three-size terminal acceptance remain incomplete. Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`; no RC artifact/tag, stable tag, npm publication, or GitHub release exists. Publication authorization remains granted but gated on accepted exact-RC evidence.\n\nThe 16:19 UTC `4bce876` checkpoint below remains as historical evidence for that revision.\n\n## Historical current state update (2026-10-18 16:19 UTC, `4bce876`)\n\n\n**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\n\n## 6. Task-quality qualification (REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-109)\n\nEnvironment: E4 (gateway direct), serial runs, with matched model fingerprint, budgets and env (REQ-QUAL-102).\n\n### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\n\n- 40 sealed tasks. The manifest is committed before RC1, and authorship is recorded (agent-authored, DEC-05).\n- 5 runs × {Nexus RC, Goose, OpenCode}.\n- Before execution, freeze three qualification configs at `eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json`, `eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json`, and `eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json`. Each must set `qualification: true`, identify the same model fingerprint and sampling settings, and record equal context/output and task budgets; the Nexus config must identify the installed RC and its package digest. Do not derive these files from the pilot configs by silently inheriting or changing settings.\n- Set `T2_TASKS` to the custodian-approved, sealed task directory and `T2_OUT` to a new, empty, run-specific output directory. Do not use the disclosed `eval/tasks` development set as held-out evidence. Preserve all three outputs and their manifests; never reuse an output directory for a retry.\n- Run each config serially, with identical task selection and five runs per task:\n\n  ```bash\n  set -euo pipefail\n  : \"${T2_TASKS:?set the sealed task directory}\"\n  : \"${T2_OUT:?set a new unique output directory}\"\n  test ! -e \"$T2_OUT\"\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/nexus\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/goose\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/opencode\" --runs 5\n  node eval/score.mjs --pairs \"$T2_OUT/nexus/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/goose/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/opencode/results.jsonl\"\n  ```\n\n  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\n\n### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\n\n9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\n\n1. refused connection mid-turn\n2. 5xx / overloaded\n3. stream cut mid-tool-call\n4. output-limit truncation\n5. hanging test command\n6. disk full\n7. context overflow at 32k\n8. malformed tool-call JSON\n9. SIGTERM then `run --resume`\n\n### 6.3 T3 long tasks (ACC-QUAL-T3)\n\n- 8 tasks × 5 runs. Each run must have ≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions and scripted steering.\n\n### 6.4 Thresholds (DEC-05; all must hold)\n\n| Metric | Gate |\n|---|---|\n| False VERIFIED (T2 + T3 + T4) | **= 0** |\n| T2 pooled hidden-test correctness | ≥ 60% and ≥ best matched peer − 10 pts |\n| T2 per class (bugfix, feature, refactor, debug) | ≥ 40% |\n| Crash rate (all Nexus runs) | ≤ 2% |\n| Regression rate | ≤ 5% |\n| T4 truthful outcome | = 100% |\n| T4 hang beyond budget + 5 min | = 0 |\n| T3 false-absence | = 0 |\n| T3 false-presence | = 0 |\n| T3 steering honoured | ≥ 95% |\n| Operator interventions in `run` mode | = 0 |\n\nThe scorer output `verdict.md` lists each metric with its Wilson 95% interval, along with the infrastructure reruns and the excluded contaminated runs.\n\n## 7. Install, upgrade, rollback, uninstall (ACC-PLAT; E2)\n\n| Case | Command | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| Fresh install, each image with Node ≥ 22 | Documented one-line command with `NEXUS_VERSION=<rc>`, then the no-version command after v1.0.0 is published | Installed. `nexus --version` equals the RC. `nexus doctor` shows no version warning and an empty stderr. |\n| No Node / Node 20 | Same | Clear prerequisite message before download or state change. HOME untouched. |\n| Upgrade alpha.2 → RC | Same, with the tag | Symlink swapped. Old version retained. User state intact. |\n| Rollback RC → alpha.2 | Same, with the old tag | Works. |\n| Repair | Delete a file in the version dir, then reinstall | Repaired (REQ-REL-105). Same-version reinstall preserves working files if package fails verification. |\n| Uninstall (documented manual) | Commands from the quickstart | Only Nexus-owned paths removed. `~/.config/nexus` and `~/.nexus` retained. |\n| Checksum tamper | installer-smoke | Refused. The existing install is unchanged. |\n| Attestation | `gh attestation verify <tarball> -R mikeholownych/nexus-code` | PASS |\n| Upgrade self-test failure | `nexus upgrade` (broken candidate package) | Refused. Staging verified before switch; if post-switch verification fails, launcher atomically rolls back to previous target and journal records `rolled_back`. |\n| Upgrade crash recovery | `nexus upgrade --recover` | Idempotent recovery. Cleans incomplete staging, restores unverified launcher symlink, verifies functional installation. |\n| Backup restore | `nexus upgrade --restore-backup <state-backup-directory>` | Snapshot of configuration and complete durable state restored from a recognized private backup directory (`backup.json`, `state/`, optional `config/`), with strict 0600 file / 0700 directory modes. A canonical `config.env.bak.*` path restores configuration only. Arbitrary files and tar archives are rejected. Run it through the stable `nexus` launcher; close existing legacy clients, then keep version-pinned legacy binaries and direct old entry points offline until the durable restore journal is cleared. |\n| Incompatible downgrade | `nexus upgrade --version <v> --allow-downgrade` (incompatible state schema) | Refused fail-closed with actionable state schema explanation. Existing installation unchanged. |\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":28617}},"started_at_ms":1792890399969,"completed_at_ms":1792890399969}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T01:06:41.025Z","ordinal":316806,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17098-7101-7f83-a66a-0cfdfadd9308","call_id":"call_b286f83da4564ed59ac4bbd0ceed5a01","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 12090)\nTotal output lines: 241\n\n# v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\n\n## Current release convergence status (observed 2026-10-23 13:35 UTC at `1f3c655`)\n\n**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `1f3c655971ade086f55347926db16cf2ecd52d1f`, merging PR #161's pinned Linux builder/reproducibility changes. Exact-main CI [39957281380](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39957281380) completed successfully: Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 jobs all passed, including the full CLI suite, security gates, requirements check, reproducible package builds, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke. Exact-main CodeQL [39957281390](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39957281390) also passed. On a clean detached checkout of this exact SHA with isolated HOME/XDG, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 explicit exact-RC qualification deferrals. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` reports all components at `1.0.0-rc.3`. These are source-gate results; the CI package is validation output, not a new published RC.\n\n**Distribution scope:** The release owner confirmed the supported distribution target is the GitHub installer/archive only; npm publication is inapplicable. The current release workflow is the authority for published assets.\n\n**RC3, checkpoint choice, and Doctor:** RC3 remains the latest published prerelease, tagged at `1b9791f07d301c885fe48f04a796203583ab5a5c`; its archive digest and provenance are recorded in the snapshot below. The operator's `Sensitive content prevents durable persistence to checkpoint` failure occurred on immutable RC1, which predates the interactive choice flow. RC3 source contains the five choices: read-only, continue in the configured mode without a rollback checkpoint, create a checkpoint with the sensitivity risk acknowledged, cancel, or re-enter the instruction. Current RC3 source also scans saved-state metadata asynchronously in bounded batches, accepts schema-2 task `messageLog` records, and treats a configured model absent from `/models` as unverified rather than unavailable; a `--deep` inference probe can verify it. The interrupted-write temporary file reported by Doctor is a separate real warning and is not automatically repaired. These source checks and existing tests do not substitute for exercising the exact installed candidate on the operator's own state.\n\n**Qualification evidence and blockers:** The RC3 provider record `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023.json` was independently accepted: ChatGPT sign-in streaming/tool round trip passed; OpenRouter failed authentication and its live task remains outstanding. Public Issue #1 remains open; its latest visible update is coordinator-authored at 10:23 UTC, with no custodian response. The sealed legacy `hidden.command` corpus is not accepted by the current `blackbox-v1` runner; no held-out qualification has started and no private payload was accessed. T2/T3/T4, long-task and fault-injection qualification, exact-candidate cross-runner reproducibility, all 15 human terminal cells, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete.\n\n**Human terminal matrix:** The required environments remain xterm, kitty with keyboard protocol, tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal, and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14, and 200×60, with the two required screenshots for each cell. This coordination session is on `mike-dev`, an Ubuntu 24.04 remote TTY with no