{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T01:07:22.661Z","ordinal":316842,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17095-f2fe-7de0-b5cc-460661bc1fe3","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-f2c72b7b-e8ab-44bd-8af1-f19b85d5d9f5","process_id":"69064","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md | rg -n -A8 -B4 'ACC-SAFE-01|ACC-SAFE-09|ACC-SAFE-10'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '208,280p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md | sed -n '114,124p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md | rg -n -A8 -B4 'ACC-SAFE-01|ACC-SAFE-09|ACC-SAFE-10'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '208,280p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md | sed -n '114,124p'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"6-| Release class | **BLOCKER** |\n7-| Requirements | REQ-SEC-101, REQ-SEC-102, REQ-SEC-103, REQ-SEC-104, REQ-TUI-102, REQ-SEC-108, REQ-SEC-109, REQ-SEC-119 |\n8-| Findings | SEC-01, VER-01, HIST-05, TUI-07, TUI-02, TUI-03, TUI-12, SEC-02, SEC-04, SEC-10, VER-14, TUI-09, TUI-10 |\n9-| Plan | [PLAN-01](../plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md) |\n10:| Acceptance | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-06 in [ACCEPTANCE.md](../ACCEPTANCE.md) |\n11-\n12-## 1. Original finding (historical baseline)\n13-\n14-The observations in this section describe the original audit baseline and are not assertions about the amended DEC-01 behavior. In particular, the reported trust-derived `auto` default was the defect identified by SEC-01; DEC-01 was amended on 2026-10-24 to make permission mode independent of folder trust and default to `review`.\n15-\n16-Nexus's default interactive mode is `auto` on both surfaces (`cli/src/sidecar.ts:935`, `cli/src/index.ts:93,115`, `cli/src/repl.ts:69`). In `auto`:\n17-\n18-- `run_command` executes `bash -c <string>` on the host as the user (`core/src/runner.rs:116-157`). The only confinement is the working directory. No sandbox is applied unless `--sandbox` is passed (`cli/src/config.ts:107`).\n--\n166-## 10. Acceptance criteria\n167-\n168-| ID | Check | Type |\n169-|---|---|---|\n170:| ACC-SAFE-01 | Fresh HOME; run `nexus` and `nexus repl` in both trusted and untrusted fixture workspaces with explicit `--mode review` and `--mode auto`. A mock gateway calls `run_command \"echo x > ../outside\"`: review asks in both folders; auto permits according to the configured execution boundary in both folders. With no mode configured, both folders default to review. Trust affects only project instruction/integration loading. | PTY |\n171-| ACC-SAFE-02 | Capability × mode matrix test: enumerate the registry. For each mode, the expected decision matches §5.1 for every capability, including MCP and plugin-registered tools. | unit |\n172-| ACC-SAFE-03 | REPL PTY: lone Enter → DENIED. `y` typed before the prompt + Enter → DENIED. Paste `y\\n` → DENIED. Deliberate `y` + Enter after 500 ms → APPROVED. | PTY (r1a/r1d scripts) |\n173-| ACC-SAFE-04 | `--read-only` + `run_command \"cat ~/.ssh/id_rsa\"` with a fixture HOME → refused, or fails with \"No such file\" inside the masked home. | integration |\n174-| ACC-SAFE-05 | Sandbox with workspace path `/tmp/a b/'q` → sandboxed `pwd` prints the path. | integration |\n175-| ACC-SAFE-06 | Startup screen of both surfaces shows mode/sandbox/trust. Doctor JSON contains `posture`. | PTY + unit |\n176-| ACC-SAFE-07 | Tripwire tests: the false-positive list passes, the documented bypass list is asserted as \"not blocked (by design)\". | unit |\n177-| ACC-SAFE-08 | Existing `tui_approval_input_e2e` stays green. | PTY (CI) |\n178:| ACC-SAFE-09 | Fixture repo whose `package.json` `scripts.test` writes a sentinel file. In review mode, the sentinel is not written until a verifier approval is given, and the approval panel shows `npm test` and the script body, regardless of folder trust. In auto mode, execution follows the configured permission mode regardless of folder trust. | integration + PTY |\n179:| ACC-SAFE-10 | `/test` runs through the runner: Esc cancels it within 5 s, and in sandbox mode it runs inside bwrap (`/proc/self/mountinfo` probe). | PTY |\n180-\n181-## 11. Dependencies and open decisions\n182-\n183-- **DEC-01** is resolved as amended: review by default; explicit permission mode controls approvals independently of folder trust. Nothing in this spec is blocked by the decision.\n184-- **DEC-02** is resolved: the REPL stays a supported secondary surface, so §5.3 is required.\n185-- SPEC-03 provides the trust state for skills and knowledge (`context_inject`).\n186-- SPEC-06 makes the TUI the packaged default, which reduces exposure to the REPL but does not remove it.\n## 6. Task-quality qualification (REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-109)\n\nEnvironment: E4 (gateway direct), serial runs, with matched model fingerprint, budgets and env (REQ-QUAL-102).\n\n### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\n\n- 40 sealed tasks. The manifest is committed before RC1, and authorship is recorded (agent-authored, DEC-05).\n- 5 runs × {Nexus RC, Goose, OpenCode}.\n- Before execution, freeze three qualification configs at `eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json`, `eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json`, and `eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json`. Each must set `qualification: true`, identify the same model fingerprint and sampling settings, and record equal context/output and task budgets; the Nexus config must identify the installed RC and its package digest. Do not derive these files from the pilot configs by silently inheriting or changing settings.\n- Set `T2_TASKS` to the custodian-approved, sealed task directory and `T2_OUT` to a new, empty, run-specific output directory. Do not use the disclosed `eval/tasks` development set as held-out evidence. Preserve all three outputs and their manifests; never reuse an output directory for a retry.\n- Run each config serially, with identical task selection and five runs per task:\n\n  ```bash\n  set -euo pipefail\n  : \"${T2_TASKS:?set the sealed task directory}\"\n  : \"${T2_OUT:?set a new unique output directory}\"\n  test ! -e \"$T2_OUT\"\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/nexus\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/goose\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/opencode\" --runs 5\n  node eval/score.mjs --pairs \"$T2_OUT/nexus/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/goose/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/opencode/results.jsonl\"\n  ```\n\n  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\n\n### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\n\n9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\n\n1. refused connection mid-turn\n2. 5xx / overloaded\n3. stream cut mid-tool-call\n4. output-limit truncation\n5. hanging test command\n6. disk full\n7. context overflow at 32k\n8. malformed tool-call JSON\n9. SIGTERM then `run --resume`\n\n### 6.3 T3 long tasks (ACC-QUAL-T3)\n\n- 8 tasks × 5 runs. Each run must have ≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions and scripted steering.\n\n### 6.4 Thresholds (DEC-05; all must hold)\n\n| Metric | Gate |\n|---|---|\n| False VERIFIED (T2 + T3 + T4) | **= 0** |\n| T2 pooled hidden-test correctness | ≥ 60% and ≥ best matched peer − 10 pts |\n| T2 per class (bugfix, feature, refactor, debug) | ≥ 40% |\n| Crash rate (all Nexus runs) | ≤ 2% |\n| Regression rate | ≤ 5% |\n| T4 truthful outcome | = 100% |\n| T4 hang beyond budget + 5 min | = 0 |\n| T3 false-absence | = 0 |\n| T3 false-presence | = 0 |\n| T3 steering honoured | ≥ 95% |\n| Operator interventions in `run` mode | = 0 |\n\nThe scorer output `verdict.md` lists each metric with its Wilson 95% interval, along with the infrastructure reruns and the excluded contaminated runs.\n\n## 7. Install, upgrade, rollback, uninstall (ACC-PLAT; E2)\n\n| Case | Command | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| Fresh install, each image with Node ≥ 22 | Documented one-line command with `NEXUS_VERSION=<rc>`, then the no-version command after v1.0.0 is published | Installed. `nexus --version` equals the RC. `nexus doctor` shows no version warning and an empty stderr. |\n| No Node / Node 20 | Same | Clear prerequisite message before download or state change. HOME untouched. |\n| Upgrade alpha.2 → RC | Same, with the tag | Symlink swapped. Old version retained. User state intact. |\n| Rollback RC → alpha.2 | Same, with the old tag | Works. |\n| Repair | Delete a file in the version dir, then reinstall | Repaired (REQ-REL-105). Same-version reinstall preserves working files if package fails verification. |\n| Uninstall (documented manual) | Commands from the quickstart | Only Nexus-owned paths removed. `~/.config/nexus` and `~/.nexus` retained. |\n| Checksum tamper | installer-smoke | Refused. The existing install is unchanged. |\n| Attestation | `gh attestation verify <tarball> -R mikeholownych/nexus-code` | PASS |\n\n### 3.1 Safety and execution boundary\n\n| ID | Source | Requirement (short; full text in spec) | Rationale | Implementation location | Evidence | Status | Acceptance | Class | Finding | Spec / Plan |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| REQ-SEC-101 | Audit; DEC-01 (amended 2026-10-24) | Without operator opt-in, model-initiated exec and egress require the configured permission decision. Folder trust does not select or change approval mode; unset mode defaults to review. | safety | `config.ts`, `sidecar.ts`, `repl.ts`, `index.ts`, `core/approval_policy.ts` | TEST `test:cli/test/approval_policy.test.ts::\"REQ-SEC-101: the unset mode stays review in trusted and untrusted workspaces\"`; `test:cli/test/config.test.ts::\"workspace trust does not select the tool approval mode\"`; PTY ACC-SAFE-01 still pending | partial | ACC-SAFE-01 | **B** | SEC-01, TUI-07 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\n| REQ-SEC-102 | Audit; TOP_TIER B1 | Every capability has an effect class. Review gates every class except read. The gate is enforced at dispatch from the registry. | safety | `core/capabilities.ts`, `agent.ts:3945` | TEST `approval_policy.test.ts` | tested | ACC-SAFE-02 | **B** | HIST-05, SEC-03 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\n| REQ-SEC-103 | Audit | No approval is decided by Enter alone, typed-ahead input, paste, or input inside the grace window, on any surface. | safety | `repl.ts:291-355,444-495`, `tui_approval_input_e2e.test.ts`, `repl_approval_e2e.test.ts` | PTY (ACC-SAFE-03, ACC-SAFE-08) | tested | ACC-SAFE-03, ACC-SAFE-08 | **B** | TUI-02, TUI-03 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\n| REQ-SEC-119 | Audit; DEC-01 (amended 2026-10-24) | Nexus-initiated verifier runs are `exec` class and follow configured permission mode; review requires a one-time approval showing the script body. Folder trust alone does not authorize execution; all runs are routed through the runner. | safety | `agent.ts:1654,3544,4255`; `tester.ts:145`; `verifier_gating.test.ts` | TEST `test:cli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts::\"trusted and untrusted repos in review mode prompt for verifier and script body, write sentinel only after approval, and cache session decision\"`; `test:cli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts::\"denied verifier does not execute verifier and sentinel is not written\"`; `test:cli/test/harness.test.ts::\"run_tests keeps repository test side effects inside worktree authority and honors read-only, dry-run, and required sandbox\"`; PTY ACC-SAFE-09/10 still pending | partial | ACC-SAFE-09, ACC-SAFE-10 | **B** | VER-01, VER-14 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\n| REQ-SEC-104 | Audit | `--read-only` cannot read outside the workspace through commands. HOME is masked. | safety | `sandbox.ts`, `core/authority.ts:44-136` | RT (SEC-04) | tested | ACC-SAFE-04 | RR | SEC-04 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\n| REQ-TUI-102 | Audit | The startup banner states mode, sandbox and trust. Doctor reports the posture. | safety / UX | `sidecar.ts`, `live_view.rs`, `repl.ts`, `doctor.ts` | TEST `tui_surface_e2e.test.ts`, `doctor.test.ts` | tested | ACC-SAFE-06 | RR | TUI-07 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":43988}},"started_at_ms":1792890442660,"completed_at_ms":1792890442660}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T01:07:23.733Z","ordinal":316843,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17099-17d5-7fe3-8500-40707781930d","call_id":"call_d0a4528b388c404a9b9d07bca288f88a","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"6-| Release class | **BLOCKER** |\n7-| Requirements | REQ-SEC-101, REQ-SEC-102, REQ-SEC-103, REQ-SEC-104, REQ-TUI-102, REQ-SEC-108, REQ-SEC-109, REQ-SEC-119 |\n8-| Findings | SEC-01, VER-01, HIST-05, TUI-07, TUI-02, TUI-03, TUI-12, SEC-02, SEC-04, SEC-10, VER-14, TUI-09, TUI-10 |\n9-| Plan | [PLAN-01](../plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md) |\n10:| Acceptance | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-06 in [ACCEPTANCE.md](../ACCEPTANCE.md) |\n11-\n12-## 1. Original finding (historical baseline)\n13-\n14-The observations in this section describe the original audit baseline and are not assertions about the amended DEC-01 behavior. In particular, the reported trust-derived `auto` default was the defect identified by SEC-01; DEC-01 was amended on 2026-10-24 to make permission mode independent of folder trust and default to `review`.\n15-\n16-Nexus's default interactive mode is `auto` on both surfaces (`cli/src/sidecar.ts:935`, `cli/src/index.ts:93,115`, `cli/src/repl.ts:69`). In `auto`:\n17-\n18-- `run_command` executes `bash -c <string>` on the host as the user (`core/src/runner.rs:116-157`). The only confinement is the working directory. No sandbox is applied unless `--sandbox` is passed (`cli/src/config.ts:107`).\n--\n166-## 10. Acceptance criteria\n167-\n168-| ID | Check | Type |\n169-|---|---|---|\n170:| ACC-SAFE-01 | Fresh HOME; run `nexus` and `nexus repl` in both trusted and untrusted fixture workspaces with explicit `--mode review` and `--mode auto`. A mock gateway calls `run_command \"echo x > ../outside\"`: review asks in both folders; auto permits according to the configured execution boundary in both folders. With no mode configured, both folders default to review. Trust affects only project instruction/integration loading. | PTY |\n171-| ACC-SAFE-02 | Capability × mode matrix test: enumerate the registry. For each mode, the expected decision matches §5.1 for every capability, including MCP and plugin-registered tools. | unit |\n172-| ACC-SAFE-03 | REPL PTY: lone Enter → DENIED. `y` typed before the prompt + Enter → DENIED. Paste `y\\n` → DENIED. Deliberate `y` + Enter after 500 ms → APPROVED. | PTY (r1a/r1d scripts) |\n173-| ACC-SAFE-04 | `--read-only` + `run_command \"cat ~/.ssh/id_rsa\"` with a fixture HOME → refused, or fails with \"No such file\" inside the masked home. | integration |\n174-| ACC-SAFE-05 | Sandbox with workspace path `/tmp/a b/'q` → sandboxed `pwd` prints the path. | integration |\n175-| ACC-SAFE-06 | Startup screen of both surfaces shows mode/sandbox/trust. Doctor JSON contains `posture`. | PTY + unit |\n176-| ACC-SAFE-07 | Tripwire tests: the false-positive list passes, the documented bypass list is asserted as \"not blocked (by design)\". | unit |\n177-| ACC-SAFE-08 | Existing `tui_approval_input_e2e` stays green. | PTY (CI) |\n178:| ACC-SAFE-09 | Fixture repo whose `package.json` `scripts.test` writes a sentinel file. In review mode, the sentinel is not written until a verifier approval is given, and the approval panel shows `npm test` and the script body, regardless of folder trust. In auto mode, execution follows the configured permission mode regardless of folder trust. | integration + PTY |\n179:| ACC-SAFE-10 | `/test` runs through the runner: Esc cancels it within 5 s, and in sandbox mode it runs inside bwrap (`/proc/self/mountinfo` probe). | PTY |\n180-\n181-## 11. Dependencies and open decisions\n182-\n183-- **DEC-01** is resolved as amended: review by default; explicit permission mode controls approvals independently of folder trust. Nothing in this spec is blocked by the decision.\n184-- **DEC-02** is resolved: the REPL stays a supported secondary surface, so §5.3 is required.\n185-- SPEC-03 provides the trust state for skills and knowledge (`context_inject`).\n186-- SPEC-06 makes the TUI the packaged default, which reduces exposure to the REPL but does not remove it.\n## 6. Task-quality qualification (REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-109)\n\nEnvironment: E4 (gateway direct), serial runs, with matched model fingerprint, budgets and env (REQ-QUAL-102).\n\n### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\n\n- 40 sealed tasks. The manifest is committed before RC1, and authorship is recorded (agent-authored, DEC-05).\n- 5 runs × {Nexus RC, Goose, OpenCode}.\n- Before execution, freeze three qualification configs at `eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json`, `eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json`, and `eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json`. Each must set `qualification: true`, identify the same model fingerprint and sampling settings, and record equal context/output and task budgets; the Nexus config must identify the installed RC and its package digest. Do not derive these files from the pilot configs by silently inheriting or changing settings.\n- Set `T2_TASKS` to the custodian-approved, sealed task directory and `T2_OUT` to a new, empty, run-specific output directory. Do not use the disclosed `eval/tasks` development set as held-out evidence. Preserve all three outputs and their manifests; never reuse an output directory for a retry.\n- Run each config serially, with identical task selection and five runs per task:\n\n  ```bash\n  set -euo pipefail\n  : \"${T2_TASKS:?set the sealed task directory}\"\n  : \"${T2_OUT:?set a new unique output directory}\"\n  test ! -e \"$T2_OUT\"\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/nexus\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/goose\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/opencode\" --runs 5\n  node eval/score.mjs --pairs \"$T2_OUT/nexus/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/goose/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/opencode/results.jsonl\"\n  ```\n\n  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\n\n### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\n\n9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\n\n1. refused connection mid-turn\n2. 5xx / overloaded\n3. stream cut mid-tool-call\n4. output-limit truncation\n5. hanging test command\n6. disk full\n7. context overflow at 32k\n8. malformed tool-call JSON\n9. SIGTERM then `run --resume`\n\n### 6.3 T3 long tasks (ACC-QUAL-T3)\n\n- 8 tasks × 5 runs. Each run must have ≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions and scripted steering.\n\n### 6.4 Thresholds (DEC-05; all must hold)\n\n| Metric | Gate |\n|---|---|\n| False VERIFIED (T2 + T3 + T4) | **= 0** |\n| T2 pooled hidden-test correctness | ≥ 60% and ≥ best matched peer − 10 pts |\n| T2 per class (bugfix, feature, refactor, debug) | ≥ 40% |\n| Crash rate (all Nexus runs) | ≤ 2% |\n| Regression rate | ≤ 5% |\n| T4 truthful outcome | = 100% |\n| T4 hang beyond budget + 5 min | = 0 |\n| T3 false-absence | = 0 |\n| T3 false-presence | = 0 |\n| T3 steering honoured | ≥ 95% |\n| Operator interventions in `run` mode | = 0 |\n\nThe scorer output `verdict.md` lists each metric with its Wilson 95% interval, along with the infrastructure reruns and the excluded contaminated runs.\n\n## 7. Install, upgrade, rollback, uninstall (ACC-PLAT; E2)\n\n| Case | Command | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| Fresh install, each image with Node ≥ 22 | Documented one-line command with `NEXUS_VERSION=<rc>`, then the no-version command after v1.0.0 is published | Installed. `nexus --version` equals the RC. `nexus doctor` shows no version warning and an empty stderr. |\n| No Node / Node 20 | Same | Clear prerequisite message before download or state change. HOME untouched. |\n| Upgrade alpha.2 → RC | Same, with the tag | Symlink swapped. Old version retained. User state intact. |\n| Rollback RC → alpha.2 | Same, with the old tag | Works. |\n| Repair | Delete a file in the version dir, then reinstall | Repaired (REQ-REL-105). Same-version reinstall preserves working files if package fails verification. |\n| Uninstall (documented manual) | Commands from the quickstart | Only Nexus-owned paths removed. `~/.config/nexus` and `~/.nexus` retained. |\n| Checksum tamper | installer-smoke | Refused. The existing install is unchanged. |\n| Attestation | `gh attestation verify <tarball> -R mikeholownych/nexus-code` | PASS |\n\n### 3.1 Safety and execution boundary\n\n| ID | Source | Requirement (short; full text in spec) | Rationale | Implementation location | Evidence | Status | Acceptance | Class | Finding | Spec / Plan |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| REQ-SEC-101 | Audit; DEC-01 (amended 2026-10-24) | Without operator opt-in, model-initiated exec and egress require the configured permission decision. Folder trust does not select or change approval mode; unset mode defaults to review. | safety | `config.ts`, `sidecar.ts`, `repl.ts`, `index.ts`, `core/approval_policy.ts` | TEST `test:cli/test/approval_policy.test.ts::\"REQ-SEC-101: the unset mode stays review in trusted and untrusted workspaces\"`; `test:cli/test/config.test.ts::\"workspace trust does not select the tool approval mode\"`; PTY ACC-SAFE-01 still pending | partial | ACC-SAFE-01 | **B** | SEC-01, TUI-07 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\n| REQ-SEC-102 | Audit; TOP_TIER B1 | Every capability has an effect class. Review gates every class except read. The gate is enforced at dispatch from the registry. | safety | `core/capabilities.ts`, `agent.ts:3945` | TEST `approval_policy.test.ts` | tested | ACC-SAFE-02 | **B** | HIST-05, SEC-03 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\n| REQ-SEC-103 | Audit | No approval is decided by Enter alone, typed-ahead input, paste, or input inside the grace window, on any surface. | safety | `repl.ts:291-355,444-495`, `tui_approval_input_e2e.test.ts`, `repl_approval_e2e.test.ts` | PTY (ACC-SAFE-03, ACC-SAFE-08) | tested | ACC-SAFE-03, ACC-SAFE-08 | **B** | TUI-02, TUI-03 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\n| REQ-SEC-119 | Audit; DEC-01 (amended 2026-10-24) | Nexus-initiated verifier runs are `exec` class and follow configured permission mode; review requires a one-time approval showing the script body. Folder trust alone does not authorize execution; all runs are routed through the runner. | safety | `agent.ts:1654,3544,4255`; `tester.ts:145`; `verifier_gating.test.ts` | TEST `test:cli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts::\"trusted and untrusted repos in review mode prompt for verifier and script body, write sentinel only after approval, and cache session decision\"`; `test:cli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts::\"denied verifier does not execute verifier and sentinel is not written\"`; `test:cli/test/harness.test.ts::\"run_tests keeps repository test side effects inside worktree authority and honors read-only, dry-run, and required sandbox\"`; PTY ACC-SAFE-09/10 still pending | partial | ACC-SAFE-09, ACC-SAFE-10 | **B** | VER-01, VER-14 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\n| REQ-SEC-104 | Audit | `--read-only` cannot read outside the workspace through commands. HOME is masked. | safety | `sandbox.ts`, `core/authority.ts:44-136` | RT (SEC-04) | tested | ACC-SAFE-04 | RR | SEC-04 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\n| REQ-TUI-102 | Audit | The startup banner states mode, sandbox and trust. Doctor reports the posture. | safety / UX | `sidecar.ts`, `live_view.rs`, `repl.ts`, `doctor.ts` | TEST `tui_surface_e2e.test.ts`, `doctor.test.ts` | tested | ACC-SAFE-06 | RR | TUI-07 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17095-f2fe-7de0-b5cc-460661bc1fe3","create_time":1792890443.7334137}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
