{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T01:07:28.416Z","ordinal":316852,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a17099-2a20-7692-b78a-6fc800bd781e","author":"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/current_main_rc_path_audit\nPayload:\n**Disposition: keep REQ-SEC-101 and REQ-SEC-119 `partial` at c1f40e51b4d29b7110456b80e71984a31020eef3.** Their unit and integration tests cover important behavior, but the mapped acceptance criteria still require source-applicable PTY evidence before RC construction.\n\n- **REQ-SEC-101:** The policy, config, and headless-dispatch tests cover the review default and trust independence. They do not cover all of ACC-SAFE-01’s required combinations: both `nexus` and `nexus repl`, trusted and untrusted workspaces, review and auto modes, and the mock command.\n- **REQ-SEC-119:** The verifier and harness tests cover review approval, script details, sentinel behavior, auto mode, and execution boundaries. ACC-SAFE-09 still requires PTY evidence for the approval panel; ACC-SAFE-10 requires `/test` cancellation within five seconds and a bwrap mount-info probe through PTY.\n\n`ACCEPTANCE.md` §1.1 makes source-applicable criteria pre-RC gates, and PLAN-01 calls for ACC-SAFE-01–10 to pass in CI. That is separate from the installed-RC manual terminal matrix. DEC-01 does not exempt either criterion. Next, obtain exact-revision evidence for ACC-SAFE-01 and ACC-SAFE-09/10, then review and update the ledger. No tests were run."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17095-f2fe-7de0-b5cc-460661bc1fe3","create_time":1792890448.4167628}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":16017}}
