 tripwire.\n62-6. **PR-1f** (tasks 13-14): TUI polish and docs.\n63-\n64:## Tests and fixtures\n65-\n66-- **Unit:**\n67-  - `approval_policy.test.ts`: registry × mode matrix with trust-independence assertions; fails on an unclassified capability.\n68-  - `security.test.ts`: tripwire false positives and documented bypasses.\n69-- **Integration:**\n70:  - Extend `verifier_gating.test.ts` to cover trusted and untrusted fixtures with sentinel `scripts.test`, for both review and explicitly configured auto behavior under ACC-SAFE-09.\n71-  - `readonly_home.test.ts`: fixture HOME with `.ssh/id_rsa`, covering ACC-SAFE-04.\n72-  - `sandbox_quoting.test.ts`, covering ACC-SAFE-05.\n73-- **PTY:**\n74-  - Port `evidence/D_pty/r1_repl.py` and `r1d.py` into `cli/test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts`, using the existing PTY helper in `cli/test/helpers/fixtures.ts`. Covers ACC-SAFE-03.\n75-  - Add a startup-banner assertion to `tui_surface_e2e`. Covers ACC-SAFE-06.\n76-  - Keep `tui_approval_input_e2e` green (ACC-SAFE-08).\n77-- **Live (M5):** one standalone session per server kind verifies the banner and the first-verifier approval.\n78-\n79-## Documentation and packaging\n80-\n81-- Add a release-notes entry for the default change and for `--yes` in scripts and CI.\n82-- The quickstart gains a \"Trust your own repository\" step: `nexus trust .`.\n83-\n84-## Rollback\n85-\n86-- Each PR reverts independently.\n87-- PR-1b is the posture behavior change. Reverting the amended mode resolution would restore the original trust-derived behavior while keeping the classes and gate.\n88-- The `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` escape hatch remains for users after release.\n89-\n90:## Definition of done\n91-\n92:- ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-10 pass in CI. The PTY tests run in CI (they already run in `linux-x86_64`).\n93-- REQUIREMENTS.md rows REQ-SEC-101/102/103/104/108/109/119 and REQ-TUI-102 show status `tested`, with test references.\n94-- `make test` passes on a clean snapshot.\n95-- The docs checklist items for SPEC-01 are done.\ncli/test/approval_policy.test.ts\ncli/test/approval_review.test.ts\ncli/test/helpers/repl_approval_driver.py\ncli/test/helpers/tui_approval_driver.py\ncli/test/helpers/tui_approval_typing_driver.py\ncli/test/helpers/tui_pty_driver.py\ncli/test/helpers/tui_surface_driver.py\ncli/test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts\ncli/test/tui_approval_input_e2e.test.ts\ncli/test/tui_surface_e2e.test.ts\ncli/src/sidecar.ts:859:/** Milestones the agent recorded in its own durable task state (update_plan completions); empty when unreadable. */\ncli/src/sidecar.ts:869:/** Prompt history from the REPL's file, redacted; empty when the file is missing or unreadable. */\ncli/src/file_diff.ts:50:  /** Unified diff of the operation (headers `--- a/` `+++ b/`), or empty when line detail is unavailable. */\ncli/src/browser.ts:299:    if (!this.domContent) return \"(empty page)\";\ncli/src/repl.ts:902:                  console.log(pc.dim(\"Empty message, commit cancelled.\\n\"));\ncli/src/repl.ts:969:                console.log(pc.dim(\"Empty server name. Wizard cancelled.\\n\"));\ncli/src/repl.ts:980:                  console.log(pc.dim(\"Empty command. Wizard cancelled.\\n\"));\ncli/src/repl.ts:989:                  console.log(pc.dim(\"Empty URL. Wizard cancelled.\\n\"));\ncli/src/repl.ts:1201:              console.log(pc.red(`Clipboard error: ${res.error || \"Clipboard is empty\"}\\n`));\ncli/src/evidence.ts:130:  /** Why the section is empty, or a footnote. */\ncli/src/tokens.ts:109:  const emptyChars = Math.max(0, barWidth - filledChars);\ncli/src/tokens.ts:118:  const bar = barColor(\"█\".repeat(filledChars)) + pc.dim(\"░\".repeat(emptyChars));\ncli/test/provider_recovery.test.ts:3: * client's failover / empty-stream behaviour when a request's execution status is unknown.\ncli/test/provider_recovery.test.ts:299:// ---------------------------------------------------------------- client: failover and empty stream\ncli/test/provider_recovery.test.ts:301:describe(\"clien