{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T01:10:41.418Z","ordinal":317005,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17095-f2fe-7de0-b5cc-460661bc1fe3","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-debd8e61-7e11-4bd6-8c06-da0a47859c60","process_id":"17917","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '75,145p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md; sed -n '285,320p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md; sed -n '1,260p' cli/test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts; sed -n '1,260p' cli/test/helpers/repl_approval_driver.py; rg -n \"ACC-SAFE-01|ACC-SAFE-09|ACC-SAFE-10\" docs/v1.0.0/plans docs/v1.0.0/specs docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/sec101-119-pty-followup","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '75,145p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md","name":"ACCEPTANCE.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '285,320p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md","name":"ACCEPTANCE.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,260p' cli/test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts","name":"repl_approval_e2e.test.ts","path":"cli/test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,260p' cli/test/helpers/repl_approval_driver.py","name":"repl_approval_driver.py","path":"cli/test/helpers/repl_approval_driver.py"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'ACC-SAFE-01|ACC-SAFE-09|ACC-SAFE-10' docs/v1.0.0/plans docs/v1.0.0/specs docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md","query":"ACC-SAFE-01|ACC-SAFE-09|ACC-SAFE-10","path":"plans"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"## 2. Environments\n\n| ID | Environment | Used for |\n|---|---|---|\n| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n\n## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\n\nEvery ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\n\n| Gate | Acceptance IDs | Spec |\n|---|---|---|\n| Safety | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-10 | SPEC-01 |\n| Process ownership | ACC-PROC-01 to ACC-PROC-08 (ACC-PROC-07 is the load test, run in E3) | SPEC-02 |\n| Untrusted inputs | ACC-TRUST-01 to ACC-TRUST-09 | SPEC-03 |\n| Continuity | ACC-CONT-01 to ACC-CONT-09 (ACC-CONT-10 is in §8) | SPEC-04 |\n| Inference | ACC-INF-01 to ACC-INF-09 (ACC-INF-10 is in §4) | SPEC-05 |\n| Packaging | ACC-PKG-01 to ACC-PKG-09 | SPEC-06 |\n| Supply chain | ACC-SUP-01 to ACC-SUP-08 (artifact-bound ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08 after RC construction) | SPEC-07 |\n| Persistence | ACC-PER-01 to ACC-PER-07 | SPEC-08 |\n| Governance | ACC-GOV-01 to ACC-GOV-06 | SPEC-09 |\n| Verification | ACC-VER-01 to ACC-VER-09 | SPEC-11 |\n| Upgrade | ACC-UPG-01 to ACC-UPG-14 | SPEC-12 |\n\n\n### 3.1 Acceptance IDs defined in this file\n\nThese are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\n\n| ID | Check | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\n| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\n| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\n| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\n| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\n| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\n| ACC-PLAT | E2 matrix, §7 | All rows pass. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\n\n## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n\n### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\n\n1. `export HOME=$(mktemp -d)`.\n2. Install the RC with the documented command.\n3. Create `~/.config/nexus/config.env` containing only:\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:<proxy>/v1`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=<id as listed by the proxy>`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=REDACTED\n\n   No gateway token file, no homelab paths, no `NODE_*` overrides.\n4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\n5. Run `nexus doctor --json` and archive it. It must report the server kind and context source with no `gateway` capability.\n\n### 4.2 Standalone matrix\n\n| Profile | What Nexus sees | Runs | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\n| P-llamacpp | Emulated llama.cpp `/props` and overflow body | Same tasks × 1 run; plus the forced-overflow case (context limit set to 8k) | Context discovered from `/props`. Overflow gives one compact-and-retry, then success or an actionable error. |\n| P-vllm | Emulated `max_model_len` and vLLM overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `max_model_len` |\n| P-ollama | Emulated `/api/show` and Ollama overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `ollama_show` |\n\n## 8. Independent acceptance (REQ-AGT-110, ACC-CONT-10)\n\nThe reviewer is supplied by the owner (X5) and did not implement the work under review.\n\nThe reviewer receives:\n\n- the RC package;\n- this file;\n- the REQUIREMENTS ledger;\n- SPEC-04;\n- read access to the evidence directory.\n\nThe reviewer performs:\n\n1. An independent re-run of a sample. At minimum:\n   - ACC-SAFE-01, 03, 09;\n   - ACC-PROC-02;\n   - ACC-TRUST-01, 02;\n   - ACC-CONT-01, 03;\n   - ACC-VER-01, 03;\n   - ACC-PKG-01;\n   - 5 random T2 tasks;\n   - 2 T4 classes.\n2. One live long task (≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions) on the RC through the gateway, including one kill and resume.\n3. A review of the scorer verdict and of contamination handling.\n\n**Output:** `docs/reviews/<date>-v1-rc-independent-acceptance.md` with an ACCEPT, ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS, or REJECT verdict per area. \"Accept with defects\" needs an owner disposition for every defect, and for a blocker area the only acceptable disposition is a fix.\n\n## 9. Contest (separate product; not a client gate)\n\nThe contest submission is complete and judging has concluded. No contest freeze applies (DEC-13 status amendment); post-contest hardening is tracked separately from client v1.0.0 acceptance and is accepted by:\n\n| ID | Check |\n|---|---|\n| CON-A1 | Ordinary maintained package/experiment checks build `agent-collab-worker`. `worker.config.json` has the configured name, and the bundle contains the `/work-state` handler. Do not restore the retired `cloudflare-contest-contract` status check. |\n/**\n * ACC-SAFE-03 & ACC-SAFE-08: REPL approval hardening e2e in a real pseudo-terminal (PTY).\n *\n * Verifies:\n * 1. Lone Enter at approval prompt -> DENIED (returns false, file not written)\n * 2. Keystrokes typed ahead before approval prompt -> cleared with Ctrl-U and line buffer reset, DENIED\n * 3. Paste within the 400ms grace window -> discarded, not approved\n * 4. Deliberate 'y' after 500ms -> APPROVED (action executed)\n * 5. 'a' (always allow session) requires explicit confirmation typing 'all';\n *    unconfirmed cancels and reprompts, confirmed switches session to auto-approve.\n */\n\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport os from \"node:os\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport { spawn } from \"node:child_process\";\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \"node:url\";\nimport { startGateway, makeRepo, makeHome, trustWorkspace, Reply, ptyTest } from \"./helpers/fixtures.js\";\n\nconst here = path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\nconst ROOT = path.resolve(here, \"..\");\nconst INDEX = path.join(ROOT, \"dist/index.js\");\nconst DRIVER = path.join(here, \"helpers/repl_approval_driver.py\");\n\nfunction script(_n: number, body: any): Reply {\n  const messages: any[] = body?.messages ?? [];\n  let lastUserIdx = -1;\n  let filename = \"target.txt\";\n\n  for (let i = messages.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\n    if (messages[i].role === \"user\") {\n      lastUserIdx = i;\n      const text = typeof messages[i].content === \"string\" ? messages[i].content : \"\";\n      const m = text.match(/create\\s+([a-zA-Z0-9_\\-\\.]+)/i);\n      if (m) filename = m[1];\n      break;\n    }\n  }\n\n  const toolsSinceUser = lastUserIdx >= 0\n    ? messages.slice(lastUserIdx).filter((m) => m.role === \"tool\").length\n    : 0;\n\n  if (toolsSinceUser === 0) {\n    return {\n      kind: \"tools\",\n      calls: [{ name: \"write_file\", args: { path: filename, content: `content for ${filename}\\n` } }],\n      delayMs: 500, // delay allows typed-ahead input to land mid-turn\n    };\n  }\n  return { kind: \"text\", content: `Finished handling ${filename}.` };\n}\n\nasync function runScenario(scenario: string): Promise<any> {\n  const repo = makeRepo();\n  const home = makeHome();\n  trustWorkspace(home, repo);\n  const gw = await startGateway(script);\n  const plan = {\n    node: process.execPath,\n    index: INDEX,\n    args: [\"repl\", \"--approve\", \"-w\", repo, \"-e\", gw.url, \"-m\", \"m\"],\n    ws: repo,\n    home,\n    scenario,\n    env: {\n      HOME: home,\n      NEXUS_DEBUG: \"0\",\n    },\n  };\n  const planFile = path.join(home, \"plan.json\");\n  fs.writeFileSync(planFile, JSON.stringify(plan));\n\n  let driverShutdownConfirmed = false;\n  try {\n    const { code, out, err } = await new Promise<{ code: number | null; out: string; err: string }>((resolve) => {\n      const child = spawn(\"python3\", [DRIVER, planFile], { stdio: [\"ignore\", \"pipe\", \"pipe\"] });\n      let out = \"\";\n      let err = \"\";\n      child.stdout.on(\"data\", (c) => (out += c));\n      child.stderr.on(\"data\", (c) => (err += c));\n      child.on(\"close\", (c) => resolve({ code: c, out, err }));\n    });\n    // The driver exits successfully only after its finally block confirms that\n    // the PTY process group has stopped. Preserve the fixture on every other\n    // exit so a surviving child cannot write into a HOME being removed here.\n    driverShutdownConfirmed = code === 0;\n    assert.equal(code, 0, `driver failed for scenario '${scenario}':\\n${err}\\n${out}`);\n    const lastLine = out.trim().split(\"\\n\").pop() || \"{}\";\n    return JSON.parse(lastLine);\n  } finally {\n    await gw.close();\n    if (driverShutdownConfirmed) {\n      fs.rmSync(repo, { recursive: true, force: true });\n      fs.rmSync(home, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nptyTest(\"REPL approval hardening (ACC-SAFE-03): lone Enter, typed-ahead, paste, deliberate approval, and session confirmation\", { timeout: 180_000 }, async () => {\n  assert.ok(fs.existsSync(INDEX), `missing ${INDEX} (run npm run build)`);\n  assert.ok(fs.existsSync(DRIVER), `missing ${DRIVER}`);\n\n  // 1. Lone Enter -> DENIED\n  const r1 = await runScenario(\"lone_enter\");\n  assert.equal(r1.file_created, false, \"lone Enter must NOT approve the action\");\n  assert.equal(r1.passed, true);\n\n  // 2. Typed ahead mid-turn -> DISCARDED & DENIED\n  const r2 = await runScenario(\"typed_ahead\");\n  assert.equal(r2.file_created, false, \"typed-ahead input must be discarded and NOT approve\");\n  assert.equal(r2.passed, true);\n\n  // 3. Paste during grace window -> DISCARDED & NOT APPROVED\n  const r3 = await runScenario(\"paste\");\n  assert.equal(r3.created_during_grace, false, \"burst/paste during grace window must NOT approve\");\n  assert.equal(r3.created_after_deny, false);\n  assert.equal(r3.passed, true);\n\n  // 4. Deliberate 'y' after grace window -> APPROVED\n  const r4 = await runScenario(\"deliberate\");\n  assert.equal(r4.file_created, true, \"deliberate 'y' after grace window MUST approve\");\n  assert.equal(r4.passed, true);\n\n  // 5. 'a' confirmation: unconfirmed cancels, 'all' enables auto-mode\n  const r5 = await runScenario(\"confirm_a\");\n  assert.equal(r5.auto1_cancelled, true, \"unconfirmed 'a' must cancel auto-approval\");\n  assert.equal(r5.auto1_created, true, \"confirmed 'a' with 'all' must approve initial action\");\n  assert.equal(r5.auto2_created, true, \"subsequent actions must run in auto mode without prompt\");\n  assert.equal(r5.passed, true);\n});\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Approval input safety driver for the REPL (ACC-SAFE-03).\nRuns node repl in a pseudo-terminal (PTY) and tests:\n1. Lone Enter at approval prompt -> DENIED\n2. Keystrokes typed ahead before approval prompt -> DISCARDED / DENIED\n3. Paste within the 400ms grace window -> DISCARDED / DENIED\n4. Deliberate 'y' after 500ms grace window -> APPROVED\n5. Always allow ('a') requires explicit 'all' confirmation; unconfirmed cancels, confirmed enables auto-mode.\n\nUsage: repl_approval_driver.py PLAN.json\n\"\"\"\nimport fcntl\nimport json\nimport os\nimport pty\nimport re\nimport select\nimport signal\nimport struct\nimport sys\nimport termios\nimport time\n\nCSI = re.compile(r\"\\x1b\\[[0-9;?<>=]*[ -/]*[@-~]|\\x1b\\][^\\x07\\x1b]*(?:\\x07|\\x1b\\\\)|\\x1b[()][0-9A-Za-z]|\\x1b[=>78]\")\n\n\nclass ReplSession:\n    def __init__(self, argv, env, cwd, cols=100, rows=30):\n        self.cols, self.rows = cols, rows\n        self.pid, self.fd = pty.fork()\n        self.reaped = False\n        if self.pid == 0:\n            os.chdir(cwd)\n            os.execvpe(argv[0], argv, env)\n        self.out = \"\"\n        self.raw = b\"\"\n        fcntl.ioctl(self.fd, termios.TIOCSWINSZ, struct.pack(\"HHHH\", rows, cols, 0, 0))\n\n    def pump(self, seconds=0.2):\n        deadline = time.monotonic() + seconds\n        got = b\"\"\n        while True:\n            left = deadline - time.monotonic()\n            if left <= 0:\n                break\n            ready, _, _ = select.select([self.fd], [], [], left)\n            if not ready:\n                continue\n            try:\n                chunk = os.read(self.fd, 65536)\n            except OSError:\n                break\n            if not chunk:\n                break\n            got += chunk\n        if got:\n            self.raw += got\n            self.out += got.decode(\"utf-8\", \"replace\")\n        return got\n\n    def clean_text(self):\n        return CSI.sub(\"\", self.out)\n\n    def wait_text(self, text, timeout=25):\n        deadline = time.monotonic() + timeout\n        while text not in self.clean_text():\n            if time.monotonic() > deadline:\n                raise TimeoutError(f\"never saw {text!r}; clean text:\\n{self.clean_text()[-1000:]}\")\n            self.pump(0.05)\n\n    def send(self, data: bytes, settle=0.1):\n        os.write(self.fd, data)\n        if settle > 0:\n            self.pump(settle)\n\n    def close(self):\n        try:\n            # pty.fork makes the child a session/process-group leader. Stop the\n            # whole REPL tree so a sidecar cannot keep writing session state\n            # while the parent test removes its temporary HOME.\n            try:\n                os.killpg(self.pid, signal.SIGTERM)\n            except ProcessLookupError:\n                pass\n\n            if not self._wait_for_group_exit(10.0):\n                try:\n                    os.killpg(self.pid, signal.SIGKILL)\n                except ProcessLookupError:\n                    pass\n                if not self._wait_for_group_exit(5.0):\n                    raise RuntimeError(f\"REPL process group {self.pid} did not exit after SIGKILL\")\n        finally:\n            try:\n                os.close(self.fd)\n            except OSError:\n                pass\n\n    def _wait_for_group_exit(self, timeout):\n        deadline = time.monotonic() + timeout\n        while True:\n            if not self.reaped:\n                try:\n                    pid, _ = os.waitpid(self.pid, os.WNOHANG)\n                    self.reaped = pid == self.pid\n                except ChildProcessError:\n                    self.reaped = True\n\n            group_alive = False\n            try:\n                os.killpg(self.pid, 0)\n                group_alive = True\n            except ProcessLookupError:\n                pass\n            except PermissionError:\n                group_alive = True\n\n            if self.reaped and not group_alive:\n                return True\n            if time.monotonic() >= deadline:\n                return False\n            time.sleep(0.05)\n\n\ndef main():\n    if len(sys.argv) < 2:\n        print(\"Usage: repl_approval_driver.py PLAN.json\", file=sys.stderr)\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n    plan = json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))\n    argv = [plan[\"node\"], plan[\"index\"]] + plan[\"args\"]\n    env = {\n        **os.environ,\n        **plan.get(\"env\", {}),\n        \"TERM\": \"xterm-256color\",\n        \"COLORTERM\": \"truecolor\",\n        \"LANG\": \"C.UTF-8\",\n    }\n    ws = plan[\"ws\"]\n    scenario = plan.get(\"scenario\", \"lone_enter\")\n\n    s = ReplSession(argv, env, ws)\n    result = {}\n\n    try:\n        s.wait_text(\"❯\", timeout=25)\n\n        if scenario == \"lone_enter\":\n            s.send(b\"create lone_enter.txt\\r\", settle=0.3)\n            s.wait_text(\"[y/N/d/a]\", timeout=20)\n            # Lone Enter at prompt\n            s.send(b\"\\r\", settle=2.5)\n            created = os.path.exists(os.path.join(ws, \"lone_enter.txt\"))\n            result = {\n                \"scenario\": scenario,\n                \"file_created\": created,\n                \"passed\": not created,\n            }\n\n        elif scenario == \"typed_ahead\":\n            s.send(b\"create typed_ahead.txt\\r\", settle=0.2)\n            # Send 'y\\r' mid-turn while model is processing, before approval prompt appears\n            s.send(b\"y\\r\", settle=0.4)\n            s.wait_text(\"[y/N/d/a]\", timeout=20)\n            # The typed ahead 'y\\r' must have been cleared / discarded; send Enter\n            s.send(b\"\\r\", settle=2.5)\n            created = os.path.exists(os.path.join(ws, \"typed_ahead.txt\"))\n            result = {\n                \"scenario\": scenario,\n                \"file_created\": created,\n                \"passed\": not created,\n            }\n\n        elif scenario == \"paste\":\n            s.send(b\"create paste.txt\\r\", settle=0.3)\n            s.wait_text(\"[y/N/d/a]\", timeout=20)\n            # Immediately send burst / paste during grace window (<400ms)\n            s.send(b\"y\\r\", settle=1.2)\n            created_during_grace = os.path.exists(os.path.join(ws, \"paste.txt\"))\n            # Settle and deny with 'n'\n            s.send(b\"n\\r\", settle=2.0)\n            created_after_deny = os.path.exists(os.path.join(ws, \"paste.txt\"))\n            result = {\n                \"scenario\": scenario,\n                \"created_during_grace\": created_during_grace,\n                \"created_after_deny\": created_after_deny,\n                \"passed\": not created_during_grace and not created_after_deny,\n            }\n\n        elif scenario == \"deliberate\":\n            s.send(b\"create deliberate.txt\\r\", settle=0.3)\n            s.wait_text(\"[y/N/d/a]\", timeout=20)\n            # Wait 600ms (> 400ms grace window)\n            time.sleep(0.6)\n            s.send(b\"y\\r\", settle=2.5)\n            created = os.path.exists(os.path.join(ws, \"deliberate.txt\"))\n            result = {\n                \"scenario\": scenario,\n                \"file_created\": created,\n                \"passed\": created,\n            }\n\n        elif scenario == \"confirm_a\":\n            s.send(b\"create auto1.txt\\r\", settle=0.3)\n            s.wait_text(\"[y/N/d/a]\", timeout=20)\n            time.sleep(0.6)\n            s.send(b\"a\\r\", settle=0.3)\n            s.wait_text(\"Type 'all' to confirm\", timeout=15)\n            time.sleep(0.6)\n            # Send 'no' to cancel\n            s.send(b\"no\\r\", settle=1.0)\n            s.wait_text(\"cancelled\", timeout=15)\n            auto1_cancelled = not os.path.exists(os.path.join(ws, \"auto1.txt\"))\n\n            # Approval prompt appears again\n            s.wait_text(\"[y/N/d/a]\", timeout=15)\n            time.sleep(0.6)\n            s.send(b\"a\\r\", settle=0.3)\n            s.wait_text(\"Type 'all' to confirm\", timeout=15)\n            time.sleep(0.6)\n            s.send(b\"all\\r\", settle=1.0)\n            s.wait_text(\"Finished handling auto1.txt\", timeout=20)\n            auto1_created = os.path.exists(os.path.join(ws, \"auto1.txt\"))\n\n            # Next action should now auto-approve without prompt\n            time.sleep(0.5)\n            s.send(b\"create auto2.txt\\r\", settle=1.0)\n            s.wait_text(\"Finished handling auto2.txt\", timeout=20)\n            auto2_created = os.path.exists(os.path.join(ws, \"auto2.txt\"))\n\n            result = {\n                \"scenario\": scenario,\n                \"auto1_cancelled\": auto1_cancelled,\n                \"auto1_created\": auto1_created,\n                \"auto2_created\": auto2_created,\n                \"passed\": auto1_cancelled and auto1_created and auto2_created,\n            }\n\n        elif scenario == \"readonly_slash\":\n            # A mode change is allowed but must not unlock direct slash scaffolding.\n            s.send(b\"/mode auto\\r\", settle=1.0)\n            s.wait_text(\"❯\", timeout=15)\n            s.send(b\"/skill init leaked\\r\", settle=1.5)\n            s.wait_text(\"❯\", timeout=15)\n            skill_created = os.path.exists(os.path.join(ws, \".nexus\", \"skills\", \"leaked\", \"SKILL.md\"))\n            s.send(b\"/init\\r\", settle=1.5)\n            s.wait_text(\"❯\", timeout=15)\n            agents_created = os.path.exists(os.path.join(ws, \"AGENTS.md\"))\n            result = {\n                \"scenario\": scenario,\n                \"skill_created\": skill_created,\n                \"agents_created\": agents_created,\n                \"passed\": not skill_created and not agents_created,\n            }\n\n        elif scenario == \"readonly_mode_slash\":\n            s.send(b\"/mode read-only\\r\", settle=1.0)\n            s.wait_text(\"❯\", timeout=15)\n            s.send(b\"/init\\r\", settle=1.5)\n            s.wait_text(\"❯\", timeout=15)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:91:| Safety | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-10 | SPEC-01 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:301:   - ACC-SAFE-01, 03, 09;\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:10:| Acceptance | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-06 in [ACCEPTANCE.md](../ACCEPTANCE.md) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:170:| ACC-SAFE-01 | Fresh HOME; run `nexus` and `nexus repl` in both trusted and untrusted fixture workspaces with explicit `--mode review` and `--mode auto`. A mock gateway calls `run_command \"echo x > ../outside\"`: review asks in both folders; auto permits according to the configured execution boundary in both folders. With no mode configured, both folders default to review. Trust affects only project instruction/integration loading. | PTY |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:178:| ACC-SAFE-09 | Fixture repo whose `package.json` `scripts.test` writes a sentinel file. In review mode, the sentinel is not written until a verifier approval is given, and the approval panel shows `npm test` and the script body, regardless of folder trust. In auto mode, execution follows the configured permission mode regardless of folder trust. | integration + PTY |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:179:| ACC-SAFE-10 | `/test` runs through the runner: Esc cancels it within 5 s, and in sandbox mode it runs inside bwrap (`/proc/self/mountinfo` probe). | PTY |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:70:  - Extend `verifier_gating.test.ts` to cover trusted and untrusted fixtures with sentinel `scripts.test`, for both review and explicitly configured auto behavior under ACC-SAFE-09.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:92:- ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-10 pass in CI. The PTY tests run in CI (they already run in `linux-x86_64`).\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":848337301}},"started_at_ms":1792890640569,"completed_at_ms":1792890641418}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T01:10:42.412Z","ordinal":317006,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1709c-1fec-7192-aa8a-b2d4cb6427bf","call_id":"call_6fd004f7dee34ea6bc0fd8af5c99fc11","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"## 2. Environments\n\n| ID | Environment | Used for |\n|---|---|---|\n| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n\n## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\n\nEvery ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\n\n| Gate | Acceptance IDs | Spec |\n|---|---|---|\n| Safety | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-10 | SPEC-01 |\n| Process ownership | ACC-PROC-01 to ACC-PROC-08 (ACC-PROC-07 is the load test, run in E3) | SPEC-02 |\n| Untrusted inputs | ACC-TRUST-01 to ACC-TRUST-09 | SPEC-03 |\n| Continuity | ACC-CONT-01 to ACC-CONT-09 (ACC-CONT-10 is in §8) | SPEC-04 |\n| Inference | ACC-INF-01 to ACC-INF-09 (ACC-INF-10 is in §4) | SPEC-05 |\n| Packaging | ACC-PKG-01 to ACC-PKG-09 | SPEC-06 |\n| Supply chain | ACC-SUP-01 to ACC-SUP-08 (artifact-bound ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08 after RC construction) | SPEC-07 |\n| Persistence | ACC-PER-01 to ACC-PER-07 | SPEC-08 |\n| Governance | ACC-GOV-01 to ACC-GOV-06 | SPEC-09 |\n| Verification | ACC-VER-01 to ACC-VER-09 | SPEC-11 |\n| Upgrade | ACC-UPG-01 to ACC-UPG-14 | SPEC-12 |\n\n\n### 3.1 Acceptance IDs defined in this file\n\nThese are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\n\n| ID | Check | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\n| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\n| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\n| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\n| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\n| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\n| ACC-PLAT | E2 matrix, §7 | All rows pass. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\n\n## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n\n### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\n\n1. `export HOME=$(mktemp -d)`.\n2. Install the RC with the documented command.\n3. Create `~/.config/nexus/config.env` containing only:\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:<proxy>/v1`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=<id as listed by the proxy>`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=REDACTED\n\n   No gateway token file, no homelab paths, no `NODE_*` overrides.\n4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\n5. Run `nexus doctor --json` and archive it. It must report the server kind and context source with no `gateway` capability.\n\n### 4.2 Standalone matrix\n\n| Profile | What Nexus sees | Runs | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\n| P-llamacpp | Emulated llama.cpp `/props` and overflow body | Same tasks × 1 run; plus the forced-overflow case (context limit set to 8k) | Context discovered from `/props`. Overflow gives one compact-and-retry, then success or an actionable error. |\n| P-vllm | Emulated `max_model_len` and vLLM overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `max_model_len` |\n| P-ollama | Emulated `/api/show` and Ollama overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `ollama_show` |\n\n## 8. Independent acceptance (REQ-AGT-110, ACC-CONT-10)\n\nThe reviewer is supplied by the owner (X5) and did not implement the work under review.\n\nThe reviewer receives:\n\n- the RC package;\n- this file;\n- the REQUIREMENTS ledger;\n- SPEC-04;\n- read access to the evidence directory.\n\nThe reviewer performs:\n\n1. An independent re-run of a sample. At minimum:\n   - ACC-SAFE-01, 03, 09;\n   - ACC-PROC-02;\n   - ACC-TRUST-01, 02;\n   - ACC-CONT-01, 03;\n   - ACC-VER-01, 03;\n   - ACC-PKG-01;\n   - 5 random T2 tasks;\n   - 2 T4 classes.\n2. One live long task (≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions) on the RC through the gateway, including one kill and resume.\n3. A review of the scorer verdict and of contamination handling.\n\n**Output:** `docs/reviews/<date>-v1-rc-independent-acceptance.md` with an ACCEPT, ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS, or REJECT verdict per area. \"Accept with defects\" needs an owner disposition for every defect, and for a blocker area the only acceptable disposition is a fix.\n\n## 9. Contest (separate product; not a client gate)\n\nThe contest submission is complete and judging has concluded. No contest freeze applies (DEC-13 status amendment); post-contest hardening is tracked separately from client v1.0.0 acceptance and is accepted by:\n\n| ID | Check |\n|---|---|\n| CON-A1 | Ordinary maintained package/experiment checks build `agent-collab-worker`. `worker.config.json` has the configured name, and the bundle contains the `/work-state` handler. Do not restore the retired `cloudflare-contest-contract` status check. |\n/**\n * ACC-SAFE-03 & ACC-SAFE-08: REPL approval hardening e2e in a real pseudo-terminal (PTY).\n *\n * Verifies:\n * 1. Lone Enter at approval prompt -> DENIED (returns false, file not written)\n * 2. Keystrokes typed ahead before approval prompt -> cleared with Ctrl-U and line buffer reset, DENIED\n * 3. Paste within the 400ms grace window -> discarded, not approved\n * 4. Deliberate 'y' after 500ms -> APPROVED (action executed)\n * 5. 'a' (always allow session) requires explicit confirmation typing 'all';\n *    unconfirmed cancels and reprompts, confirmed switches session to auto-approve.\n */\n\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport os from \"node:os\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport { spawn } from \"node:child_process\";\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \"node:url\";\nimport { startGateway, makeRepo, makeHome, trustWorkspace, Reply, ptyTest } from \"./helpers/fixtures.js\";\n\nconst here = path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\nconst ROOT = path.resolve(here, \"..\");\nconst INDEX = path.join(ROOT, \"dist/index.js\");\nconst DRIVER = path.join(here, \"helpers/repl_approval_driver.py\");\n\nfunction script(_n: number, body: any): Reply {\n  const messages: any[] = body?.messages ?? [];\n  let lastUserIdx = -1;\n  let filename = \"target.txt\";\n\n  for (let i = messages.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\n    if (messages[i].role === \"user\") {\n      lastUserIdx = i;\n      const text = typeof messages[i].content === \"string\" ? messages[i].content : \"\";\n      const m = text.match(/create\\s+([a-zA-Z0-9_\\-\\.]+)/i);\n      if (m) filename = m[1];\n      break;\n    }\n  }\n\n  const toolsSinceUser = lastUserIdx >= 0\n    ? messages.slice(lastUserIdx).filter((m) => m.role === \"tool\").length\n    : 0;\n\n  if (toolsSinceUser === 0) {\n    return {\n      kind: \"tools\",\n      calls: [{ name: \"write_file\", args: { path: filename, content: `content for ${filename}\\n` } }],\n      delayMs: 500, // delay allows typed-ahead input to land mid-turn\n    };\n  }\n  return { kind: \"text\", content: `Finished handling ${filename}.` };\n}\n\nasync function runScenario(scenario: string): Promise<any> {\n  const repo = makeRepo();\n  const home = makeHome();\n  trustWorkspace(home, repo);\n  const gw = await startGateway(script);\n  const plan = {\n    node: process.execPath,\n    index: INDEX,\n    args: [\"repl\", \"--approve\", \"-w\", repo, \"-e\", gw.url, \"-m\", \"m\"],\n    ws: repo,\n    home,\n    scenario,\n    env: {\n      HOME: home,\n      NEXUS_DEBUG: \"0\",\n    },\n  };\n  const planFile = path.join(home, \"plan.json\");\n  fs.writeFileSync(planFile, JSON.stringify(plan));\n\n  let driverShutdownConfirmed = false;\n  try {\n    const { code, out, err } = await new Promise<{ code: number | null; out: string; err: string }>((resolve) => {\n      const child = spawn(\"python3\", [DRIVER, planFile], { stdio: [\"ignore\", \"pipe\", \"pipe\"] });\n      let out = \"\";\n      let err = \"\";\n      child.stdout.on(\"data\", (c) => (out += c));\n      child.stderr.on(\"data\", (c) => (err += c));\n      child.on(\"close\", (c) => resolve({ code: c, out, err }));\n    });\n    // The driver exits successfully only after its finally block confirms that\n    // the PTY process group has stopped. Preserve the fixture on every other\n    // exit so a surviving child cannot write into a HOME being removed here.\n    driverShutdownConfirmed = code === 0;\n    assert.equal(code, 0, `driver failed for scenario '${scenario}':\\n${err}\\n${out}`);\n    const lastLine = out.trim().split(\"\\n\").pop() || \"{}\";\n    return JSON.parse(lastLine);\n  } finally {\n    await gw.close();\n    if (driverShutdownConfirmed) {\n      fs.rmSync(repo, { recursive: true, force: true });\n      fs.rmSync(home, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nptyTest(\"REPL approval hardening (ACC-SAFE-03): lone Enter, typed-ahead, paste, deliberate approval, and session confirmation\", { timeout: 180_000 }, async () => {\n  assert.ok(fs.existsSync(INDEX), `missing ${INDEX} (run npm run build)`);\n  assert.ok(fs.existsSync(DRIVER), `missing ${DRIVER}`);\n\n  // 1. Lone Enter -> DENIED\n  const r1 = await runScenario(\"lone_enter\");\n  assert.equal(r1.file_created, false, \"lone Enter must NOT approve the action\");\n  assert.equal(r1.passed, true);\n\n  // 2. Typed ahead mid-turn -> DISCARDED & DENIED\n  const r2 = await runScenario(\"typed_ahead\");\n  assert.equal(r2.file_created, false, \"typed-ahead input must be discarded and NOT approve\");\n  assert.equal(r2.passed, true);\n\n  // 3. Paste during grace window -> DISCARDED & NOT APPROVED\n  const r3 = await runScenario(\"paste\");\n  assert.equal(r3.created_during_grace, false, \"burst/paste during grace window must NOT approve\");\n  assert.equal(r3.created_after_deny, false);\n  assert.equal(r3.passed, true);\n\n  // 4. Deliberate 'y' after grace window -> APPROVED\n  const r4 = await runScenario(\"deliberate\");\n  assert.equal(r4.file_created, true, \"deliberate 'y' after grace window MUST approve\");\n  assert.equal(r4.passed, true);\n\n  // 5. 'a' confirmation: unconfirmed cancels, 'all' enables auto-mode\n  const r5 = await runScenario(\"confirm_a\");\n  assert.equal(r5.auto1_cancelled, true, \"unconfirmed 'a' must cancel auto-approval\");\n  assert.equal(r5.auto1_created, true, \"confirmed 'a' with 'all' must approve initial action\");\n  assert.equal(r5.auto2_created, true, \"subsequent actions must run in auto mode without prompt\");\n  assert.equal(r5.passed, true);\n});\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Approval input safety driver for the REPL (ACC-SAFE-03).\nRuns node repl in a pseudo-terminal (PTY) and tests:\n1. Lone Enter at approval prompt -> DENIED\n2. Keystrokes typed ahead before approval prompt -> DISCARDED / DENIED\n3. Paste within the 400ms grace window -> DISCARDED / DENIED\n4. Deliberate 'y' after 500ms grace window -> APPROVED\n5. Always allow ('a') requires explicit 'all' confirmation; unconfirmed cancels, confirmed enables auto-mode.\n\nUsage: repl_approval_driver.py PLAN.json\n\"\"\"\nimport fcntl\nimport json\nimport os\nimport pty\nimport re\nimport select\nimport signal\nimport struct\nimport sys\nimport termios\nimport time\n\nCSI = re.compile(r\"\\x1b\\[[0-9;?<>=]*[ -/]*[@-~]|\\x1b\\][^\\x07\\x1b]*(?:\\x07|\\x1b\\\\)|\\x1b[()][0-9A-Za-z]|\\x1b[=>78]\")\n\n\nclass ReplSession:\n    def __init__(self, argv, env, cwd, cols=100, rows=30):\n        self.cols, self.rows = cols, rows\n        self.pid, self.fd = pty.fork()\n        self.reaped = False\n        if self.pid == 0:\n            os.chdir(cwd)\n            os.execvpe(argv[0], argv, env)\n        self.out = \"\"\n        self.raw = b\"\"\n        fcntl.ioctl(self.fd, termios.TIOCSWINSZ, struct.pack(\"HHHH\", rows, cols, 0, 0))\n\n    def pump(self, seconds=0.2):\n        deadline = time.monotonic() + seconds\n        got = b\"\"\n        while True:\n            left = deadline - time.monotonic()\n            if left <= 0:\n                break\n            ready, _, _ = select.select([self.fd], [], [], left)\n            if not ready:\n                continue\n            try:\n                chunk = os.read(self.fd, 65536)\n            except OSError:\n                break\n            if not chunk:\n                break\n            got += chunk\n        if got:\n            self.raw += got\n            self.out += got.decode(\"utf-8\", \"replace\")\n        return got\n\n    def clean_text(self):\n        return CSI.sub(\"\", self.out)\n\n    def wait_text(self, text, timeout=25):\n        deadline = time.monotonic() + timeout\n        while text not in self.clean_text():\n            if time.monotonic() > deadline:\n                raise TimeoutError(f\"never saw {text!r}; clean text:\\n{self.clean_text()[-1000:]}\")\n            self.pump(0.05)\n\n    def send(self, data: bytes, settle=0.1):\n        os.write(self.fd, data)\n        if settle > 0:\n            self.pump(settle)\n\n    def close(self):\n        try:\n            # pty.fork makes the child a session/process-group leader. Stop the\n            # whole REPL tree so a sidecar cannot keep writing session state\n            # while the parent test removes its temporary HOME.\n            try:\n                os.killpg(self.pid, signal.SIGTERM)\n            except ProcessLookupError:\n                pass\n\n            if not self._wait_for_group_exit(10.0):\n                try:\n                    os.killpg(self.pid, signal.SIGKILL)\n                except ProcessLookupError:\n                    pass\n                if not self._wait_for_group_exit(5.0):\n                    raise RuntimeError(f\"REPL process group {self.pid} did not exit after SIGKILL\")\n        finally:\n            try:\n                os.close(self.fd)\n            except OSError:\n                pass\n\n    def _wait_for_group_exit(self, timeout):\n        deadline = time.monotonic() + timeout\n        while True:\n            if not self.reaped:\n                try:\n                    pid, _ = os.waitpid(self.pid, os.WNOHANG)\n                    self.reaped = pid == self.pid\n                except ChildProcessError:\n                    self.reaped = True\n\n            group_alive = False\n            try:\n                os.killpg(self.pid, 0)\n                group_alive = True\n            except ProcessLookupError:\n                pass\n            except PermissionError:\n                group_alive = True\n\n            if self.reaped and not group_alive:\n                return True\n            if time.monotonic() >= deadline:\n                return False\n            time.sleep(0.05)\n\n\ndef main():\n    if len(sys.argv) < 2:\n        print(\"Usage: repl_approval_driver.py PLAN.json\", file=sys.stderr)\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n    plan = json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))\n    argv = [plan[\"node\"], plan[\"index\"]] + plan[\"args\"]\n    env = {\n        **os.environ,\n        **plan.get(\"env\", {}),\n        \"TERM\": \"xterm-256color\",\n        \"COLORTERM\": \"truecolor\",\n        \"LANG\": \"C.UTF-8\",\n    }\n    ws = plan[\"ws\"]\n    scenario = plan.get(\"scenario\", \"lone_enter\")\n\n    s = ReplSession(argv, env, ws)\n    result = {}\n\n    try:\n        s.wait_text(\"❯\", timeout=25)\n\n        if scenario == \"lone_enter\":\n            s.send(b\"create lone_enter.txt\\r\", settle=0.3)\n            s.wait_text(\"[y/N/d/a]\", timeout=20)\n            # Lone Enter at prompt\n            s.send(b\"\\r\", settle=2.5)\n            created = os.path.exists(os.path.join(ws, \"lone_enter.txt\"))\n            result = {\n                \"scenario\": scenario,\n                \"file_created\": created,\n                \"passed\": not created,\n            }\n\n        elif scenario == \"typed_ahead\":\n            s.send(b\"create typed_ahead.txt\\r\", settle=0.2)\n            # Send 'y\\r' mid-turn while model is processing, before approval prompt appears\n            s.send(b\"y\\r\", settle=0.4)\n            s.wait_text(\"[y/N/d/a]\", timeout=20)\n            # The typed ahead 'y\\r' must have been cleared / discarded; send Enter\n            s.send(b\"\\r\", settle=2.5)\n            created = os.path.exists(os.path.join(ws, \"typed_ahead.txt\"))\n            result = {\n                \"scenario\": scenario,\n                \"file_created\": created,\n                \"passed\": not created,\n            }\n\n        elif scenario == \"paste\":\n            s.send(b\"create paste.txt\\r\", settle=0.3)\n            s.wait_text(\"[y/N/d/a]\", timeout=20)\n            # Immediately send burst / paste during grace window (<400ms)\n            s.send(b\"y\\r\", settle=1.2)\n            created_during_grace = os.path.exists(os.path.join(ws, \"paste.txt\"))\n            # Settle and deny with 'n'\n            s.send(b\"n\\r\", settle=2.0)\n            created_after_deny = os.path.exists(os.path.join(ws, \"paste.txt\"))\n            result = {\n                \"scenario\": scenario,\n                \"created_during_grace\": created_during_grace,\n                \"created_after_deny\": created_after_deny,\n                \"passed\": not created_during_grace and not created_after_deny,\n            }\n\n        elif scenario == \"deliberate\":\n            s.send(b\"create deliberate.txt\\r\", settle=0.3)\n            s.wait_text(\"[y/N/d/a]\", timeout=20)\n            # Wait 600ms (> 400ms grace window)\n            time.sleep(0.6)\n            s.send(b\"y\\r\", settle=2.5)\n            created = os.path.exists(os.path.join(ws, \"deliberate.txt\"))\n            result = {\n                \"scenario\": scenario,\n                \"file_created\": created,\n                \"passed\": created,\n            }\n\n        elif scenario == \"confirm_a\":\n            s.send(b\"create auto1.txt\\r\", settle=0.3)\n            s.wait_text(\"[y/N/d/a]\", timeout=20)\n            time.sleep(0.6)\n            s.send(b\"a\\r\", settle=0.3)\n            s.wait_text(\"Type 'all' to confirm\", timeout=15)\n            time.sleep(0.6)\n            # Send 'no' to cancel\n            s.send(b\"no\\r\", settle=1.0)\n            s.wait_text(\"cancelled\", timeout=15)\n            auto1_cancelled = not os.path.exists(os.path.join(ws, \"auto1.txt\"))\n\n            # Approval prompt appears again\n            s.wait_text(\"[y/N/d/a]\", timeout=15)\n            time.sleep(0.6)\n            s.send(b\"a\\r\", settle=0.3)\n            s.wait_text(\"Type 'all' to confirm\", timeout=15)\n            time.sleep(0.6)\n            s.send(b\"all\\r\", settle=1.0)\n            s.wait_text(\"Finished handling auto1.txt\", timeout=20)\n            auto1_created = os.path.exists(os.path.join(ws, \"auto1.txt\"))\n\n            # Next action should now auto-approve without prompt\n            time.sleep(0.5)\n            s.send(b\"create auto2.txt\\r\", settle=1.0)\n            s.wait_text(\"Finished handling auto2.txt\", timeout=20)\n            auto2_created = os.path.exists(os.path.join(ws, \"auto2.txt\"))\n\n            result = {\n                \"scenario\": scenario,\n                \"auto1_cancelled\": auto1_cancelled,\n                \"auto1_created\": auto1_created,\n                \"auto2_created\": auto2_created,\n                \"passed\": auto1_cancelled and auto1_created and auto2_created,\n            }\n\n        elif scenario == \"readonly_slash\":\n            # A mode change is allowed but must not unlock direct slash scaffolding.\n            s.send(b\"/mode auto\\r\", settle=1.0)\n            s.wait_text(\"❯\", timeout=15)\n            s.send(b\"/skill init leaked\\r\", settle=1.5)\n            s.wait_text(\"❯\", timeout=15)\n            skill_created = os.path.exists(os.path.join(ws, \".nexus\", \"skills\", \"leaked\", \"SKILL.md\"))\n            s.send(b\"/init\\r\", settle=1.5)\n            s.wait_text(\"❯\", timeout=15)\n            agents_created = os.path.exists(os.path.join(ws, \"AGENTS.md\"))\n            result = {\n                \"scenario\": scenario,\n                \"skill_created\": skill_created,\n                \"agents_created\": agents_created,\n                \"passed\": not skill_created and not agents_created,\n            }\n\n        elif scenario == \"readonly_mode_slash\":\n            s.send(b\"/mode read-only\\r\", settle=1.0)\n            s.wait_text(\"❯\", timeout=15)\n            s.send(b\"/init\\r\", settle=1.5)\n            s.wait_text(\"❯\", timeout=15)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:91:| Safety | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-10 | SPEC-01 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:301:   - ACC-SAFE-01, 03, 09;\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:10:| Acceptance | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-06 in [ACCEPTANCE.md](../ACCEPTANCE.md) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:170:| ACC-SAFE-01 | Fresh HOME; run `nexus` and `nexus repl` in both trusted and untrusted fixture workspaces with explicit `--mode review` and `--mode auto`. A mock gateway calls `run_command \"echo x > ../outside\"`: review asks in both folders; auto permits according to the configured execution boundary in both folders. With no mode configured, both folders default to review. Trust affects only project instruction/integration loading. | PTY |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:178:| ACC-SAFE-09 | Fixture repo whose `package.json` `scripts.test` writes a sentinel file. In review mode, the sentinel is not written until a verifier approval is given, and the approval panel shows `npm test` and the script body, regardless of folder trust. In auto mode, execution follows the configured permission mode regardless of folder trust. | integration + PTY |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:179:| ACC-SAFE-10 | `/test` runs through the runner: Esc cancels it within 5 s, and in sandbox mode it runs inside bwrap (`/proc/self/mountinfo` probe). | PTY |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:70:  - Extend `verifier_gating.test.ts` to cover trusted and untrusted fixtures with sentinel `scripts.test`, for both review and explicitly configured auto behavior under ACC-SAFE-09.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:92:- ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-10 pass in CI. The PTY tests run in CI (they already run in `linux-x86_64`).\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17095-f2fe-7de0-b5cc-460661bc1fe3","create_time":1792890642.4125874}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
