` | Would make read-only mode refuse web search, which is a legitimate read-only research workflow. It conflates two axes. |\n| Improve the denylist into a boundary | Not achievable with string matching. Approval or sandbox is the boundary. |\n\n## 10. Acceptance criteria\n\n| ID | Check | Type |\n|---|---|---|\n| ACC-SAFE-01 | Fresh HOME; run `nexus` and `nexus repl` in both trusted and untrusted fixture workspaces with explicit `--mode review` and `--mode auto`. A mock gateway calls `run_command \"echo x > ../outside\"`: review asks in both folders; auto permits according to the configured execution boundary in both folders. With no mode configured, both folders default to review. Trust affects only project instruction/integration loading. | PTY |\n| ACC-SAFE-02 | Capability × mode matrix test: enumerate the registry. For each mode, the expected decision matches §5.1 for every capability, including MCP and plugin-registered tools. | unit |\n| ACC-SAFE-03 | REPL PTY: lone Enter → DENIED. `y` typed before the prompt + Enter → DENIED. Paste `y\\n` → DENIED. Deliberate `y` + Enter after 500 ms → APPROVED. | PTY (r1a/r1d scripts) |\n| ACC-SAFE-04 | `--read-only` + `run_command \"cat ~/.ssh/id_rsa\"` with a fixture HOME → refused, or fails with \"No such file\" inside the masked home. | integration |\n| ACC-SAFE-05 | Sandbox with workspace path `/tmp/a b/'q` → sandboxed `pwd` prints the path. | integration |\n| ACC-SAFE-06 | Startup screen of both surfaces shows mode/sandbox/trust. Doctor JSON contains `posture`. | PTY + unit |\n| ACC-SAFE-07 | Tripwire tests: the false-positive list passes, the documented bypass list is asserted as \"not blocked (by design)\". | unit |\n| ACC-SAFE-08 | Existing `tui_approval_input_e2e` stays green. | PTY (CI) |\n| ACC-SAFE-09 | Fixture repo whose `package.json` `scripts.test` writes a sentinel file. In review mode, the sentinel is not written until a verifier approval is given, and the approval panel shows `npm test` and the script body, regardless of folder trust. In auto mode, execution follows the configured permission mode regardless of folder trust. | integration + PTY |\n| ACC-SAFE-10 | `/test` runs through the runner: Esc cancels it within 5 s, and in sandbox mode it runs inside bwrap (`/proc/self/mountinfo` probe). | PTY |\n\n## 11. Dependencies and open decisions\n\n- **DEC-01** is resolved as amended: review by default; explicit permission mode controls approvals independently of folder trust. Nothing in this spec is blocked by the decision.\n- **DEC-02** is resolved: the REPL stays a supported secondary surface, so §5.3 is required.\n- SPEC-03 provides the trust state for skills and knowledge (`context_inject`).\n\n### 3.2 Completion truth, continuity and recovery\n\n| ID | Source | Requirement | Rationale | Location | Evidence | Status | Acceptance | Class | Finding | Spec / Plan |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| REQ-AGT-114 | quickstart promise | Deliverable binding uses path tokens, not basename substrings. | outcome honesty (false VERIFIED) | `tester.ts:488-570` | TEST (ACC-VER-03; test:cli/test/verification_binding.test.ts, test:cli/test/repro_false_verified.test.ts) | tested | ACC-VER-03 | **B** | VER-04 | SPEC-11 / PLAN-11 |\n| REQ-AGT-115 | Audit | A zero-executed-tests pass is UNVERIFIED (NO_TESTS_EXECUTED) and keeps the obligation. | honesty | `tester.ts:356-430`; `agent.ts:3516-3675,5360-5410` | TEST (ACC-VER-04; test:cli/test/verification_binding.test.ts) | tested | ACC-VER-04 | RR | VER-05 | SPEC-11 / PLAN-11 |\n| REQ-AGT-116 | Audit | One verifier selector. `run_tests` uses the verifier deadline. | consistency | `tester.ts:19-145`; `tools.ts:1119` | TEST (VER-06; test:cli/test/verification_binding.test.ts::\"ACC-VER-05: discoverVerifier and run_tests return no verifier for Makefile with only pytest: or empty workspace\") | tested | ACC-VER-05 | RR | VER-06 | SPEC-11 / PLAN-11 |\n| REQ-AGT-118 | Audit | Conservative token estimation; `/tokenize` used when available. | failure (context overflow) | `tokens.ts`, `client.ts`, `agent.ts` | TEST (VER-09; test:cli/test/tokens.test.ts; fixture measured on llama.cpp worker b0-live-llama-worker1, limits_version a3c2fcbc2f2b977c). 12/14 corpora within the 1.5x band (max non-floor over-estimate 1.428x, base64); 4 corpora under-estimate within the 0.8x conservative guard (worst 601/748 = 1.245x, whitespace-indented code); the 2 floor-bound exceptions are recorded per DEC-17. **Amended (DEC-17, 2026-10-17):** the ≥1 token/char floor (admission safety) takes precedence over ACC-VER-07's accuracy band for merging scripts (CJK word composition, Hangul syllables); the floor-driven over-estimate (CJK 2.00x, Hangul 1.67x) is preserved as recorded, failed accuracy evidence. Executed: `tokens.test.ts` 3/3 on snapshot `8cf3e82` and post-merge on `f771a3c` (GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS test-evidence record); independent coordinator rerun 3/3 at exact `2c70d39` with independent reviewer **ACCEPT** (docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-11_PR-11d_REVIEW_AGT-118/independent-review.md, branch v1/review-plan-11-pr-11d-ag118 @ bc9fd2c). Floor-bound accuracy exceptions preserved as recorded evidence; reconciled 2026-10-18. | tested | ACC-VER-07 | RR | VER-09 | SPEC-11 / PLAN-11 |\n| REQ-AGT-119 | DEC-07 | Experimental surfaces are labelled. `nexus eval` never mutates the operator checkout. Reviewer and researcher roles are read-only. | honesty / safety | `index.ts`, `evaluator.ts`, `roles.ts`, `agent.ts` | TEST (ACC-VER-08; test:cli/test/experimental_and_readonly.test.ts) | tested | ACC-VER-08 | RR | VER-07, VER-08, VER-13 | SPEC-11 / PLAN-11 |\n| REQ-AGT-101 | USER_MANUAL; CLIENT_GUIDE (resume) | `run --resume <id>` continues the conversation, objective and id. A bare `--resume` resolves the latest task. | workflow | `agent.ts:5236`; `app.ts:174`; `index.ts:176` | RT (AGT-01; test:cli/test/durable_continuity.test.ts) | tested | ACC-CONT-01, ACC-CONT-02 | **B** | AGT-01 | SPEC-04 / PLAN-04 |\n| REQ-AGT-102 | COMPA