{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T01:28:48.842Z","ordinal":317971,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a170ac-b3c9-77b2-b706-551841641637","author":"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/current_main_rc_path_audit\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED.** The actual-launch ACC-SAFE-01 matrix covers the 12 required surface, trust, and mode combinations. The verifier scenarios cover review approval details, auto mode, the sandbox mount-info probe, and Escape return within five seconds.\n\nThe ACC-SAFE-10 cancellation case does not establish that the verifier’s child process stopped. It records the `sleep 30` PID, but checks only that the command returned quickly and `finished` was not written. The child could remain alive and write that file later. Add a post-cancel liveness check for the recorded PID before accepting this criterion.\n\nREQ-SEC-101 can be marked source-tested once its exact-revision evidence is archived. Keep REQ-SEC-119 partial until the cancellation evidence gap is closed and archived. No tests were run during this review."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17095-f2fe-7de0-b5cc-460661bc1fe3","create_time":1792891728.8416808}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":16033}}
