his supersedes the original trust-derived mode and approval behavior. Trust affects project instruction and integration loading only; it does not select or change tool approval mode. Approval behavior follows the configured permission mode, with `review` as the unconfigured default.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:77:| CTX-001 (per-item provenance for injected context) | **Partially implement**: skills, knowledge and other injected context carry source path and trust state (SPEC-03 §3.4). The full provenance graph is post-v1. | The risky injected sources are covered. A full implementation is a large redesign with low marginal safety benefit once trust gating exists. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:78:| CTX-002 (freshness and version applicability of knowledge) | **Descoped to post-v1**, with this written rationale: auto-extraction is off by default (DEC-15) and knowledge is trust-gated, so stale knowledge can only come from the operator's own explicit saves. | Accepted risk, recorded. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:184:**Chosen:** off by default; opt-in with `NEXUS_KNOWLEDGE_AUTOEXTRACT=1`, with a visible notice each time a rule is saved. Workspace knowledge is loaded only when the workspace is trusted.\ncli/src/agent.ts:19:import { isWorkspaceTrusted } from \"./workspace_trust.js\";\ncli/src/agent.ts:46:import { trustedProjectRules } from \"./startup_trust.js\";\ncli/src/agent.ts:59:import { judgeWithoutCopy, prepareBaselineTestsCopy, requiresWorkspaceVerifierDefinitionBinding, trustedDeliverablesFromBaseline, testsChangedSince, snapshotTests, snapshotVerifierDefinition, verifierDefinitionChangedSince, type ChangeBaseline, type Independence } from \"./core/independent_check.js\";\ncli/src/agent.ts:155:import { untrustedWorkspaceExtensions } from \"./workspace_trust.js\";\ncli/src/agent.ts:860:  /** A persisted baseline retained only as untrusted continuity evidence after recovery. */\ncli/src/agent.ts:861:  private untrustedRecoveredBaseline?: DurableTaskState[\"changeBaseline\