{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T01:34:20.742Z","ordinal":318222,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a170b1-c446-79b0-9515-48b3aeceb4c6","author":"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/current_main_rc_path_audit\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED.** The updated fixture now checks that the canary is visible before Escape, fails closed when `/proc` is inaccessible, checks for it afterward, and attempts cleanup.\n\nOne false-pass remains: the scan accepts any process whose argv contains the canary. The transient `bash -c` launcher contains it before `exec -a` starts `sleep`. If that exec fails or exits early, the test could mistake the launcher for the long-running child and measure an already-failed verifier as a successful cancellation. Require the post-exec process shape—such as argv[0] equal to the canary and argv[1] equal to `30`—before sending Escape. No tests were run."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17095-f2fe-7de0-b5cc-460661bc1fe3","create_time":1792892060.742059}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":16046}}
