{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T01:38:44.632Z","ordinal":318429,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016add5da0a65881a0acfc4db31a6d4d92","status":"completed","call_id":"call_a9c5a536750b456485dd6917485b2610","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/sec101-119-pty-followup/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md\\n+# Source evidence: REQ-SEC-101 and REQ-SEC-119\\n+\\n+## Candidate identity\\n+\\n+- Source commit: `3ec79ce0f1b6053752c942f1465221465350085c`\\n+- Branch: `v1/plan-01-sec101-119-pty-followup`\\n+- Package version: `1.0.0-rc.4` (build metadata only; no RC artifact was created)\\n+- Independent source review: **ACCEPT**, reviewer `current_main_rc_path_audit`\\n+\\n+## Evidence\\n+\\n+All commands ran in the isolated candidate worktree with a temporary `HOME` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`.\\n+\\n+- `npm run build` in `cli/`: passed on the candidate commit.\\n+- `node --import=tsx --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern='ACC-SAFE-01' test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts` in `cli/`: 1 test passed. The test launches the actual `nexus` TUI and `nexus repl` in trusted and untrusted workspaces with explicit `review`, explicit `auto`, and unset mode. It verifies that unset mode prompts in both trust states, auto mode executes, review mode denies without approval, and project instructions load only after trust.\\n+- `node --import=tsx --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern='ACC-SAFE-09/10' test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts` in `cli/`: 1 test passed. It verifies `/test` approval disclosure, trust-independent review and auto behavior, actual bwrap workspace mounting, and Escape cancellation. Before cancellation the driver confirms the unique `sleep 30` descendant is visible in the host `/proc` by exact argv and process name; after Escape the test requires the process to disappear within three seconds. The fixture terminates any remaining canary before cleanup if an assertion fails.\\n+- `python3 -m py_compile cli/test/helpers/startup_permission_driver.py`: passed.\\n+- `git diff --check`: passed.\\n+\\n+The source tests cover the applicable source acceptance criteria. They do not claim installed-RC qualification, held-out qualification, cross-runner qualification, or human terminal acceptance. Those release gates remain pending.\\n+\\n+## Disposition\\n+\\n+Source behavior for REQ-SEC-101 and REQ-SEC-119 is tested at the exact candidate tree. The evidence does not promote either requirement to product-qualified status.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17095-f2fe-7de0-b5cc-460661bc1fe3","create_time":1792892320.65193}}}
