{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T01:47:17.832Z","ordinal":318861,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17095-f2fe-7de0-b5cc-460661bc1fe3","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-0b29d219-a9e8-42ba-ba83-7b33f16cccd1","process_id":"95927","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr view 208 --json author,title,body,commits,files"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/sec101-119-pty-followup","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr view 208 --json author,title,body,commits,files"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"author\":{\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"is_bot\":false,\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nCross-runner RC reproduction previously executed the packaging script from the RC checkout. That lets an older RC packaging script and runner-specific host tools affect the output, even though the workflow itself is reviewed on `main`.\\n\\nThis change keeps product source bound to the peeled RC tag commit while running the package builder from the exact reviewed workflow commit. It records both identities, verifies the script bytes and SHA-256, and rejects a package-source override that points outside the current Git worktree. The report wording now describes the six selected reproducibility artifacts accurately.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- Focused `repro_identity.test.ts`: 6/6 passed on commit `f7747fada2ca9afd636bc41bac0f8f9a8b888487`.\\n- `bash -n scripts/package-linux.sh`: passed.\\n- `node --check scripts/repro-identity.mjs`: passed.\\n- `actionlint .github/workflows/repro.yml`: passed.\\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\\n- Independent source review: ACCEPT; reviewer did not run tests.\\n\\nNo cross-runner qualification is claimed by this PR. Exact-head hosted checks remain required. A separate full suite ran on stale PR #207 candidate `8e5fc70` and ended with failures; it is not evidence for this head.\\n\",\"commits\":[{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-25T01:00:58Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-25T01:00:58Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"fix(release): bind repro builds to reviewed package tool\",\"oid\":\"f7747fada2ca9afd636bc41bac0f8f9a8b888487\"}],\"files\":[{\"path\":\".github/workflows/repro.yml\",\"additions\":15,\"deletions\":3,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"cli/test/repro_identity.test.ts\",\"additions\":35,\"deletions\":4,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"scripts/package-linux.sh\",\"additions\":12,\"deletions\":1,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"scripts/repro-identity.mjs\",\"additions\":15,\"deletions\":3,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"}],\"title\":\"fix(release): pin RC reproduction to reviewed packaging tool\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":266964947}},"started_at_ms":1792892836565,"completed_at_ms":1792892837832}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T01:47:18.798Z","ordinal":318862,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a170bd-a38e-7873-a79a-1438616fc638","call_id":"call_66d43005649f4e32b3ee497aaf942037","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"author\":{\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"is_bot\":false,\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nCross-runner RC reproduction previously executed the packaging script from the RC checkout. That lets an older RC packaging script and runner-specific host tools affect the output, even though the workflow itself is reviewed on `main`.\\n\\nThis change keeps product source bound to the peeled RC tag commit while running the package builder from the exact reviewed workflow commit. It records both identities, verifies the script bytes and SHA-256, and rejects a package-source override that points outside the current Git worktree. The report wording now describes the six selected reproducibility artifacts accurately.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- Focused `repro_identity.test.ts`: 6/6 passed on commit `f7747fada2ca9afd636bc41bac0f8f9a8b888487`.\\n- `bash -n scripts/package-linux.sh`: passed.\\n- `node --check scripts/repro-identity.mjs`: passed.\\n- `actionlint .github/workflows/repro.yml`: passed.\\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\\n- Independent source review: ACCEPT; reviewer did not run tests.\\n\\nNo cross-runner qualification is claimed by this PR. Exact-head hosted checks remain required. A separate full suite ran on stale PR #207 candidate `8e5fc70` and ended with failures; it is not evidence for this head.\\n\",\"commits\":[{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-25T01:00:58Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-25T01:00:58Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"f