\n{\"comments\":[{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only compatibility follow-up (no private store, task payload, validator, answer, or author log accessed).\\n\\nThe current public evaluator contract does not define a generic, semantics-preserving adapter from legacy `hidden.command`/`hidden.dir` tasks to `blackbox-v1`. Its documented migration path requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, independent revalidation, repeat custody checks, and a new immutable manifest identity.\\n\\nPlease answer only as safe status metadata:\\n\\n1. Can the sealed task validators be represented losslessly by `blackbox-v1` without changing covered behavior?\\n2. If yes, is the independent custodian authoring and revalidating a new immutable manifest, and what is the status/ETA?\\n3. If no, should the release record mark this corpus incompatible and awaiting custodian-authored replacement?\\n\\nNo task identifiers, objectives, source URLs, payloads, patches, validator details, answers, or credentials are needed. Qualification remains closed until custodian acceptance and compatibility evidence are recorded.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-22T22:08:34Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only custody follow-up, current source `main@1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145` (no private corpus material accessed).\\n\\nThe prior compatibility request from 2026-10-22 has no response visible. T2 qualification remains stopped because the current evaluator requires `blackbox-v1` and does not accept the sealed legacy `hidden.command` format. Please provide a safe status update covering:\\n\\n- Whether the designated independent author/custodian is actively progressing the corpus and who currently owns the custody lane.\\n- Whether a custodian-verified, semantics-preserving conversion is possible, or whether a new immutable corpus version is required; include an ETA for the next public metadata checkpoint.\\n- Whether the custodian can provide a separate acceptance attestation for completeness/coverage, setup and reference validation, payload/validator digest derivation, access controls and author-session independence, without disclosing payloads or answers to implementers.\\n- If the current owner is unavailable, whether an explicit safe-boundary handoff to another authorized custodian can be arranged.\\n\\nNo qualification run will use the corpus until the custodian accepts its custody and integrity. Please keep private task content, validators, answers and author logs out of this public thread.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-23T03:46:59Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only checkpoint request for the independent held-out custodian. No private corpus material has been accessed.\\n\\nRC3 (`v1.0.0-rc.3`) is published, but no held-out qualification has started. The public 40-task manifest still uses the legacy `hidden.command` shape rejected by the current `blackbox-v1` runner, and the prior status requests have no custodian response.\\n\\nPlease provide only safe status metadata:\\n- current author/custodian owner and claim or handoff reference;\\n- whether lossless conversion is being done by the custodian or a new immutable manifest is needed, with next checkpoint/ETA;\\n- whether completeness, coverage, setup/reference validation, integrity, access controls, and author-session independence have been independently accepted;\\n- if no custodian is active, confirm that so an authorized replacement can be assigned.\\n\\nPlease do not include task content, objectives, validators, answers, patches, author logs, credentials, or private digests. Qualification remains closed until custody acceptance and runner compatibility are documented.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-23T10:23:00Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only custody checkpoint from the release coordinator. I found no current held-out author/custodian claim in the shared claim ledger; the last public custodian response request was October 23 10:23 UTC. Please reply only with safe status metadata: (1) current independent author and custodian, including the acknowledged claim/handoff; (2) whether the 40-task corpus and setup/reference validation are complete; (3) whether the legacy runner-format incompatibility has a custodian-approved immutable resolution; and (4) whether access separation, digests, independence, and custody have been accepted. If the current custodian is unavailable, please state that explicitly and identify the authorized handoff needed. Do not post task payloads, answers, validators, author logs, credentials, or private digests. Qualification remains closed until independent custody acceptance.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T00:19:17Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only custody status request: please confirm the current author/custodian owner and progress toward the 40-task corpus, including coverage/validation counts, setup and reference-validation status, private digest re-derivation, store and parent access controls, exposure-history review, immutable seal status, and expected custody acceptance. Please do not post task prompts, answers, validators, or other protected payloads here. Held-out qualification remains blocked until the independent custodian verifies completeness, coverage, integrity, and execution-boundary separation.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T02:16:57Z\"}],\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"PLAN-10 task 8: finish and seal the held-out T2/T3 corpus\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-24T02:16:57Z\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":2,"nanos":336076691}},"started_at_ms":1792893258428,"completed_at_ms":1792893260765}}
