{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T02:07:30.860Z","ordinal":319594,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17095-f2fe-7de0-b5cc-460661bc1fe3","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016add6460331081a08dc58d9b999a63a6","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"**NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE — acceptance remains IN_PROGRESS.** No RC has been accepted and v1.0.0 has not been released.\n\nPR #209 is now at `9a27e194050aa8089de4fe28537e5f8e564b7452`, based on current `main` at `19b30a4c92b8dd2c891c5b7a5b67db319ee9ee7f`. Its evidence amendment received independent ACCEPT. The clean-tree requirements gate passed: 123 rows, with 12 explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification. Focused PTY checks and the build passed on the rebased candidate. **CodeQL passed** for the PR head; its Node 22/24 full suites are still running. The post-merge checks for PR #208 are also still running, so I have not merged #209 or combined results from different revisions.\n\nThe Ubuntu desktop at `10.0.8.3` is reachable. All five required terminal applications are installed, and an active Wayland session is present. Nexus is not installed there yet, so no manual matrix cells have been run; those checks must use the exact RC.\n\nThe separate PR #207 lane has reported a fresh rebase onto `19b30a4`; it has not yet reported tests or a push. I’m leaving its claims and work to that active lane. The held-out custodian still has not replied to the metadata-only status requests, so held-out qualification remains blocked.\n\n**Next:** reconcile the running CI results, then merge only if the exact-head checks remain green and the base has not advanced. After that, continue RC qualification. No action is needed from you right now."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1792894048225,"completed_at_ms":1792894050860}}
