 SPEC-01 §3 rule 8 & ACC-SAFE-09: Verifier executions that Nexus initiates itself\ncli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts:45:describe(\"ACC-SAFE-09: Verifier Gating\", () => {\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:178:| ACC-SAFE-09 | Fixture repo whose `package.json` `scripts.test` writes a sentinel file. In review mode, the sentinel is not written until a verifier approval is given, and the approval panel shows `npm test` and the script body, regardless of folder trust. In auto mode, execution follows the configured permission mode regardless of folder trust. | integration + PTY |\ncli/test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts:134:const STARTUP_DRIVER = path.join(here, \"helpers/startup_permission_driver.py\");\ncli/test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts:324:ptyTest(\"ACC-SAFE-09/10: /test approval, trust independence, sandbox and cancellation\", { timeout: 360_000 }, async () => {\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:70:  - Extend `verifier_gating.test.ts` to cover trusted and untrusted fixtures with sentinel `scripts.test`, for both review and explicitly configured auto behavior under ACC-SAFE-09.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md:16:- `node --import=tsx --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern='ACC-SAFE-09/10' test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts` in `cli/`: 1 test passed. It verifies `/test` approval disclosure, trust-independent review and auto behavior, actual bwrap workspace mounting, and Escape cancellation. Before cancellation the driver confirms the unique `sleep 30` descendant is visible in the host `/proc` by exact argv and process name; after Escape the test requires the process to disappear within three seconds. The fixture terminates any remaining canary before cleanup if an assertion fails.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md:17:- `python3 -m py_compile cli/test/helpers/startup_permission_driver.py`: passed.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md:30: