{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T02:19:25.630Z","ordinal":320110,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a170d0-7672-79e2-b11d-117e84b3ea44","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a170d0-7672-79e2-b11d-117e84b3ea44","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016add672b58e481a0bab1815a9de0a3d4","usage":{"input_tokens":84392,"cached_input_tokens":79232,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":220,"reasoning_output_tokens":203,"total_tokens":84612},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":9277976,"cached_input_tokens":9208960,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":25329,"reasoning_output_tokens":12042,"total_tokens":9303305},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":5817939482,"cached_input_tokens":5755390208,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":16473985,"reasoning_output_tokens":9465847,"total_tokens":5834413467}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T02:19:26.656Z","ordinal":320111,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a170db-0e40-71f2-8dd8-f0bcfcbe78b0","call_id":"call_eb1643059d09454e9351a8a196dcd558","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT.** Result matching now starts at the `/test` invocation or immediately before Escape, so earlier PTY output cannot combine with the result phrase. Cancellation still requires the explicit “Test suite failed.” result within five seconds, with the existing pre-Escape check and live descendant canary intact.\\n\\nRead-only review; no tests were run.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/pr207_independent_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"The repository does not explicitly promise isolation from a hostile process running as the same UID. `safe_fs.ts` describes ownership checks and descriptor verification, but not a separate same-UID security boundary. A same-UID process has the owner’s filesystem authority; a different UID is constrained by directory permissions.\\n\\nFor protection from different-UID actors, the smallest robust change is to verify ownership and write permissions across the parent directories before mutation, including `.nexus` and `.git/info`, and fail closed when another principal can rename those paths. Add a distinct-UID or equivalent permission-based adversarial fixture. The current descriptor checks still help reject symlink redirection.\\n\\nIf protection from hostile same-UID processes is required, this cannot be guaranteed with a final path recheck or ordinary Node `fs` calls. Node 22 exposes path-based opens and descriptor-based I/O, but no dirfd-relative `openat`/`openat2` API ([Node 22 filesystem docs](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-jod/docs/api/fs.html)). A native Linux `openat2` helper can constrain path lookup, but it cannot stop a same-UID process from moving the opened directory afterward ([openat2(2)](https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/openat2.2.html)). That requires a real OS boundary, such as separate UIDs or constrained task execution.\\n\\nSo the post-open rename is a merge blocker only if PR #207 claims protection against arbitrary same-UID concurrent mutation. Otherwise, narrow the documentation and tests to the supported different-principal boundary and record same-UID relocation as a limitation. v1 supports Linux x86-64/glibc, so any native Linux mechanism would also need an explicit kernel requirement and fail-closed preflight.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a170d0-7672-79e2-b11d-117e84b3ea44","create_time":1792894766.6562185}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
