{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T02:22:07.909Z","ordinal":320305,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a170dd-8424-77e3-9ef1-b3bb0f277bb2","author":"/root/pr207_independent_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/pr207_independent_review\nPayload:\n**PR #207 re-review: CHANGES_REQUIRED**\n\nReviewed `f2d7b7d03efbc3e6e3186a9d82c5c5fed2d44f14` against `19b30a4`.\n\nThe same-UID post-open rename is not a defect against the stated `REQ-PER-105` acceptance; arbitrary same-UID isolation is not promised. It remains a limitation of any stronger path-location guarantee.\n\nA separate fail-open case does violate `REQ-PER-105`: [git_exclude.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/git-exclude-fail-closed/cli/src/core/git_exclude.ts:135) returns before creating the self-ignore file if Git lookup fails and `.git/info` is absent. A linked worktree uses a `.git` file, so with Git unavailable the fallback misses it; `FlightRecorder` can then write committable telemetry. The tests cover normal repositories with Git available, not this case. Enforce the self-ignore rule before that return, or fail closed when a `.git` marker exists and verification is unavailable; add a focused regression fixture.\n\nNo files were edited and no tests were run."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a170d0-7672-79e2-b11d-117e84b3ea44","create_time":1792894927.90873}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":16127}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T02:22:10.560Z","ordinal":320306,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a170d0-7672-79e2-b11d-117e84b3ea44","item":{"type":"Reasoning","id":"rs_060b64278a9dfb15016add67d248f881a08298391f817a0277","summary_text":[],"raw_content":[]},"started_at_ms":1792894930350,"completed_at_ms":1792894930560}}
