{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T02:22:11.310Z","ordinal":320308,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a170d0-7672-79e2-b11d-117e84b3ea44","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016add67d289f081a09814beea2ecdf6a2","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The fresh PR #207 review found a concrete fail-open case: when Git is unavailable in a linked worktree, an early return skips the `.nexus/.gitignore` protection, so flight logs could later be committed. This is actionable and within the existing PR claim. I’m extending that claim, adding a focused regression, and will send the fix back for independent review."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1792894930567,"completed_at_ms":1792894931310}}
