{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T02:26:55.979Z","ordinal":320676,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a170d0-7672-79e2-b11d-117e84b3ea44","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-727b2a0b-8064-41b9-b1b3-9057b1c49304","process_id":"28604","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -F 'Sensitive content prevents durable persistence to checkpoint' cli core docs && rg -n 'sensitive.*checkpoint|checkpoint.*sensitive|redactForCheckpoint|durable persistence' cli/src cli/test core/src"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/sec101-119-pty-followup","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n -F 'Sensitive content prevents durable persistence to checkpoint' cli core docs","query":"Sensitive content prevents durable persistence to checkpoint","path":"cli"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'sensitive.*checkpoint|checkpoint.*sensitive|redactForCheckpoint|durable persistence' cli/src cli/test core/src","query":"sensitive.*checkpoint|checkpoint.*sensitive|redactForCheckpoint|durable persistence","path":"cli"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:9:**RC3, checkpoint choice, and Doctor:** RC3 remains the latest published prerelease, tagged at `1b9791f07d301c885fe48f04a796203583ab5a5c`; its archive digest and provenance are recorded in the snapshot below. The operator's `Sensitive content prevents durable persistence to checkpoint` failure occurred on immutable RC1, which predates the interactive choice flow. RC3 source contains the five choices: read-only, continue in the configured mode without a rollback checkpoint, create a checkpoint with the sensitivity risk acknowledged, cancel, or re-enter the instruction. Current RC3 source also scans saved-state metadata asynchronously in bounded batches, accepts schema-2 task `messageLog` records, and treats a configured model absent from `/models` as unverified rather than unavailable; a `--deep` inference probe can verify it. The interrupted-write temporary file reported by Doctor is a separate real warning and is not automatically repaired. These source checks and existing tests do not substitute for exercising the exact installed candidate on the operator's own state.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:49:**Checkpoint failure and remediation:** The operator reports every launch attempt on installed RC1 fails before the turn starts with `Sensitive content prevents durable persistence to checkpoint`. This is confirmed as an RC1 limitation: immutable RC1 source predates the checkpoint-choice flow. PR #153 integrates that flow in current main, offering read-only, continue without a rollback checkpoint, create the checkpoint despite sensitive content, cancel, or re-enter the instruction. This is source-integrated behavior only; the installed candidate must exercise the prompt and selected actions before acceptance. RC1 and RC2 remain unchanged and do not contain this behavior.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:65:**Checkpoint failure and remediation:** The operator reports that every attempt to start Nexus RC1 fails with `Sensitive content prevents durable persistence to checkpoint`. This is consistent with RC1's exact source predating PR #147's checkpoint-choice flow. PR #147 is integrated in current main and its exact-head CI and CodeQL passed; the interactive TUI now offers read-only, continue without a rollback checkpoint, create the checkpoint anyway with a sensitivity warning, cancel, or re-enter the instruction. RC1 and RC2 are immutable and do not contain this behavior. The next candidate must include the fix, and the installed candidate must be exercised to verify the choices before any acceptance claim.\ncli/src/sidecar.ts:86:  private pendingCheckpointChoice?: { id: string; settle: (choice: \"read_only\" | \"without_checkpoint\" | \"allow_sensitive\" | \"cancel\" | \"other\") => void };\ncli/src/sidecar.ts:559:            this.emit({ type: \"notice\", text: \"Creating a checkpoint that may persist sensitive workspace content, as requested.\" });\ncli/src/sidecar.ts:661:  private requestCheckpointChoice(turnId: string, signal: AbortSignal): Promise<\"read_only\" | \"without_checkpoint\" | \"allow_sensitive\" | \"cancel\" | \"other\"> {\ncli/src/sidecar.ts:665:      const settle = (choice: \"read_only\" | \"without_checkpoint\" | \"allow_sensitive\" | \"cancel\" | \"other\") => {\ncli/src/sidecar.ts:677:        message: \"Sensitive content blocked the checkpoint. Choose 1 read-only, 2 continue without a rollback checkpoint, 3 create a checkpoint anyway (may persist sensitive content), 4 cancel this turn, or 5 re-enter the instruction.\",\ncli/src/sidecar.ts:682:  private resolveCheckpointChoice(id: string, choice: \"read_only\" | \"without_checkpoint\" | \"allow_sensitive\" | \"cancel\" | \"other\"): void {\ncore/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_view.rs:2643:        feed(&mut state, &[r#\"{\"v\":1,\"type\":\"checkpoint.choice.request\",\"id\":\"choice-1\",\"turn_id\":\"t1\",\"message\":\"Sensitive content blocked the checkpoint. Choose 1 read-only, 2 continue without a rollback checkpoint, 3 create a checkpoint anyway (may persist sensitive content), 4 cancel this turn, or 5 re-enter the instruction.\"}\"#]);\ncli/src/agent.ts:967:  /** User-selected read-only mode after a sensitive pre-turn checkpoint was declined. */\ncli/test/repl_checkpoint_choices.test.ts:34:test(\"REPL asks how to proceed when sensitive content blocks a turn checkpoint\", async () => {\ncli/test/repl_checkpoint_choices.test.ts:48:    assert.equal(sensitiveRetry, expectedSensitiveRetry, `choice ${choice} sensitive checkpoint retry`);\ncli/test/persistence_protection.test.ts:248:    assert.throws(() => new CheckpointManager(workspace).createCheckpoint(\"sensitive checkpoint\"), /sensitive/i);\ncli/test/persistence_protection.test.ts:313:test(\"non-git checkpoint refuses to copy sensitive workspace files\", () => {\ncli/test/sidecar.test.ts:363:  test(\"sensitive checkpoint rejection asks before starting a read-only review turn\", async () => {\ncli/test/sidecar.test.ts:444:  test(\"operator can explicitly create a checkpoint that may contain sensitive workspace content\", async () => {\ncli/test/sidecar.test.ts:448:      await send({ type: \"prompt.submit\", id: \"t-sensitive-checkpoint\", text: \"review the codebase\" });\ncli/test/sidecar.test.ts:451:      assert.match(request.message, /1 read-only.*2 continue without a rollback checkpoint.*3 create a checkpoint anyway \\(may persist sensitive content\\).*4 cancel this turn.*5 re-enter the instruction/);\ncli/test/sidecar.test.ts:452:      await send({ type: \"checkpoint.choice\", id: request.id, choice: \"allow_sensitive\" });\ncli/test/sidecar.test.ts:453:      await waitUntil(() => events.some((event) => event.type === \"turn.result\" && event.turn_id === \"t-sensitive-checkpoint\"));\ncli/src/core/persistence_protection.ts:12:    super(`Sensitive content prevents durable persistence to ${destination}.`);\ncli/src/protocol.ts:169:  | { type: \"checkpoint.choice\"; id: string; choice: \"read_only\" | \"without_checkpoint\" | \"allow_sensitive\" | \"cancel\" | \"other\" }\ncli/src/protocol.ts:232:      const choices = [\"read_only\", \"without_checkpoint\", \"allow_sensitive\", \"cancel\", \"other\"] as const;\ncli/src/core/app.ts:470:   * Checkpoints state to durable persistence.\ncli/src/repl.ts:197:  /** Ask before a turn when a rollback checkpoint would persist sensitive workspace content. */\ncli/src/repl.ts:215:    console.log(\"  3. Create the checkpoint anyway (may persist sensitive content)\");\ncli/src/repl.ts:233:        console.log(pc.yellow(\"Creating a checkpoint that may persist sensitive workspace content, as requested.\\n\"));\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":75993828}},"started_at_ms":1792895214902,"completed_at_ms":1792895215979}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T02:26:56.894Z","ordinal":320677,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a170e1-ecfe-79c3-ab52-1f24f80c3f23","call_id":"call_967972ef078e4b29b059753d11bbd59e","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:9:**RC3, checkpoint choice, and Doctor:** RC3 remains the latest published prerelease, tagged at `1b9791f07d301c885fe48f04a796203583ab5a5c`; its archive digest and provenance are recorded in the snapshot below. The operator's `Sensitive content prevents durable persistence to checkpoint` failure occurred on immutable RC1, which predates the interactive choice flow. RC3 source contains the five choices: read-only, continue in the configured mode without a rollback checkpoint, create a checkpoint with the sensitivity risk acknowledged, cancel, or re-enter the instruction. Current RC3 source also scans saved-state metadata asynchronously in bounded batches, accepts schema-2 task `messageLog` records, and treats a configured model absent from `/models` as unverified rather than unavailable; a `--deep` inference probe can verify it. The interrupted-write temporary file reported by Doctor is a separate real warning and is not automatically repaired. These source checks and existing tests do not substitute for exercising the exact installed candidate on the operator's own state.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:49:**Checkpoint failure and remediation:** The operator reports every launch attempt on installed RC1 fails before the turn starts with `Sensitive content prevents durable persistence to checkpoint`. This is confirmed as an RC1 limitation: immutable RC1 source predates the checkpoint-choice flow. PR #153 integrates that flow in current main, offering read-only, continue without a rollback checkpoint, create the checkpoint despite sensitive content, cancel, or re-enter the instruction. This is source-integrated behavior only; the installed candidate must exercise the prompt and selected actions before acceptance. RC1 and RC2 remain unchanged and do not contain this behavior.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:65:**Checkpoint failure and remediation:** The operator reports that every attempt to start Nexus RC1 fails with `Sensitive content prevents durable persistence to checkpoint`. This is consistent with RC1's exact source predating PR #147's checkpoint-choice flow. PR #147 is integrated in current main and its exact-head CI and CodeQL passed; the interactive TUI now offers read-only, continue without a rollback checkpoint, create the checkpoint anyway with a sensitivity warning, cancel, or re-enter the instruction. RC1 and RC2 are immutable and do not contain this behavior. The next candidate must include the fix, and the installed candidate must be exercised to verify the choices before any acceptance claim.\ncli/src/sidecar.ts:86:  private pendingCheckpointChoice?: { id: string; settle: (choice: \"read_only\" | \"without_checkpoint\" | \"allow_sensitive\" | \"cancel\" | \"other\") => void };\ncli/src/sidecar.ts:559:            this.emit({ type: \"notice\", text: \"Creating a checkpoint that may persist sensitive workspace content, as requested.\" });\ncli/src/sidecar.ts:661:  private requestCheckpointChoice(turnId: string, signal: AbortSignal): Promise<\"read_only\" | \"without_checkpoint\" | \"allow_sensitive\" | \"cancel\" | \"other\"> {\ncli/src/sidecar.ts:665:      const settle = (choice: \"read_only\" | \"without_checkpoint\" | \"allow_sensitive\" | \"cancel\" | \"other\") => {\ncli/src/sidecar.ts:677:        message: \"Sensitive content blocked the checkpoint. Choose 1 read-only, 2 continue without a rollback checkpoint, 3 create a checkpoint anyway (may persist sensitive content), 4 cancel this turn, or 5 re-enter the instruction.\",\ncli/src/sidecar.ts:682:  private resolveCheckpointChoice(id: string, choice: \"read_only\" | \"without_checkpoint\" | \"allow_sensitive\" | \"cancel\" | \"other\"): void {\ncore/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_view.rs:2643:        feed(&mut state, &[r#\"{\"v\":1,\"type\":\"checkpoint.choice.request\",\"id\":\"choice-1\",\"turn_id\":\"t1\",\"message\":\"Sensitive content blocked the checkpoint. Choose 1 read-only, 2 continue without a rollback checkpoint, 3 create a checkpoint anyway (may persist sensitive content), 4 cancel this turn, or 5 re-enter the instruction.\"}\"#]);\ncli/src/agent.ts:967:  /** User-selected read-only mode after a sensitive pre-turn checkpoint was declined. */\ncli/test/repl_checkpoint_choices.test.ts:34:test(\"REPL asks how to proceed when sensitive content blocks a turn checkpoint\", async () => {\ncli/test/repl_checkpoint_choices.test.ts:48:    assert.equal(sensitiveRetry, expectedSensitiveRetry, `choice ${choice} sensitive checkpoint retry`);\ncli/test/persistence_protection.test.ts:248:    assert.throws(() => new CheckpointManager(workspace).createCheckpoint(\"sensitive checkpoint\"), /sensitive/i);\ncli/test/persistence_protection.test.ts:313:test(\"non-git checkpoint refuses to copy sensitive workspace files\", () => {\ncli/test/sidecar.test.ts:363:  test(\"sensitive checkpoint rejection asks before starting a read-only review turn\", async () => {\ncli/test/sidecar.test.ts:444:  test(\"operator can explicitly create a checkpoint that may contain sensitive workspace content\", async () => {\ncli/test/sidecar.test.ts:448:      await send({ type: \"prompt.submit\", id: \"t-sensitive-checkpoint\", text: \"review the codebase\" });\ncli/test/sidecar.test.ts:451:      assert.match(request.message, /1 read-only.*2 continue without a rollback checkpoint.*3 create a checkpoint anyway \\(may persist sensitive content\\).*4 cancel this turn.*5 re-enter the instruction/);\ncli/test/sidecar.test.ts:452:      await send({ type: \"checkpoint.choice\", id: request.id, choice: \"allow_sensitive\" });\ncli/test/sidecar.test.ts:453:      await waitUntil(() => events.some((event) => event.type === \"turn.result\" && event.turn_id === \"t-sensitive-checkpoint\"));\ncli/src/core/persistence_protection.ts:12:    super(`Sensitive content prevents durable persistence to ${destination}.`);\ncli/src/protocol.ts:169:  | { type: \"checkpoint.choice\"; id: string; choice: \"read_only\" | \"without_checkpoint\" | \"allow_sensitive\" | \"cancel\" | \"other\" }\ncli/src/protocol.ts:232:      const choices = [\"read_only\", \"without_checkpoint\", \"allow_sensitive\", \"cancel\", \"other\"] as const;\ncli/src/core/app.ts:470:   * Checkpoints state to durable persistence.\ncli/src/repl.ts:197:  /** Ask before a turn when a rollback checkpoint would persist sensitive workspace content. */\ncli/src/repl.ts:215:    console.log(\"  3. Create the checkpoint anyway (may persist sensitive content)\");\ncli/src/repl.ts:233:        console.log(pc.yellow(\"Creating a checkpoint that may persist sensitive workspace content, as requested.\\n\"));\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a170d0-7672-79e2-b11d-117e84b3ea44","create_time":1792895216.8947637}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
