nch\": \"v1/readiness-rc4-refresh\",\n  \"worktree\": \"/home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc4-refresh\",\n  \"base\": \"be2cd2f255414f554572c86baa884d9271ff5ea1\",\n  \"since\": \"2026-10-24T01:10:30Z\",\n  \"scope\": \"Append a fresh, exact-revision release-readiness checkpoint reconciling source/CI, RC3 E5 evidence, held-out custody, and Ubuntu terminal setup; preserve historical snapshots and do not claim acceptance.\",\n  \"head\": \"worktree diff in /home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc4-refresh; base be2cd2f; uncommitted addition preserved\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-24T20:58:00Z\",\n  \"independent_review\": \"PENDING current full added diff\",\n  \"status\": \"Current exact main snapshot appended at 29eab4c; exact CI 40123199081 and CodeQL 40123199130 pass; clean detached requirements --enforce passes with 12 explicit RC deferrals; RC4 public but predates current main. Desktop preflight recorded in Issue #3 comment 6389426338; manual matrix 0/15. Full added checkpoint under independent review.\",\n  \"reviewed_candidate\": null,\n  \"reviewer\": \"plan05_readonly_review\",\n  \"reviewed_at\": null,\n  \"review_note\": \"Prior snapshot review ACCEPT is historical; independent review requested for full current added checkpoint.\",\n  \"pushed_candidate\": \"4b2e7ccebf0520f5ec7849ade2c2bf3c0559a2b0\",\n  \"reviewed_diff_sha256\": null\n}\n{\"agent\":\"opencode-defect-scan\",\"host\":\"mike-dev\",\"branch\":\"v1/defect-upgrade-attestation\",\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/upgrade-attestation\",\"base\":\"19b30a4c92b8dd2c891c5b7a5b67db319ee9ee7f\",\"since\":\"2026-10-25T02:24:32Z\",\"pid\":2481396,\"scope\":\"NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1 must fail closed when gh is unavailable; focused upgrade acceptance test\"}\n{\"assignees\":[],\"author\":{\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"is_bot\":false,\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\n- Route TUI `/test` through the same verifier approval policy and one-time script disclosure as the REPL, and propagate cancellation to the runner.\\n- Add actual-launch PTY coverage for `nexus` and `nexus repl` across trusted/untrusted workspaces, explicit `review`/`auto`, and unset mode (default review).\\n- Verify `/test` trust independence, bwrap workspace execution, and Escape cancellation with a host-visible descendant-process canary.\\n- Record exact source evidence and update REQ-SEC-101/119 from partial to tested for the source gate only. Exact-RC, held-out, cross-runner, and human terminal qualification remain pending.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- ACC-SAFE-01 PTY case: 1/1 passed, covering all 12 launch combinations.\\n- ACC-SAFE-09/10 PTY case: 1/1 passed, including pre-cancel sleep-process identity and post-cancel absence.\\n- `npm run build` in `cli/`: passed.\\n- `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`: passed on the clean candidate, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, with 12 exact-RC deferrals.\\n- `git diff --check` and Python helper compilation: passed.\\n- Independent code and evidence/ledger reviews: ACCEPT.\\n\\nNo full local suite was run; exact-head CI is required before merge.\\n\",\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfP83kg\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"coderabbitai\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"NONE\",\"body\":\"<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\\n\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\\n\\n> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> - [ ] <!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"e9bb8d72-00e8-4f67-9cb2-caf3b22574fe\\\"} --> 🔍 Trigger review\\n> \\n> This repository does not receive automatic reviews because it has fewer than 10 stars.\\n> \\n> <details>\\n> <summary><strong><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog-dark.svg\\\"><img src=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog.svg\\\" width=\\\"16\\\" height=\\\"16\\\" align=\\\"absmiddle\\\" alt=\\\"\\\"></picture> Run configuration</strong></summary>\\n> <dl>\\n> <dd>\\n> \\n> - **Source mode**: Auto\\n> - **Repository**: Unavailable\\n> - **Branch**: Unavailable\\n> - **File**: No configuration file from this repository applied\\n> - **Commit**: Unavailable\\n> - **Layers**: defaults\\n> - **Review profile**: CHILL\\n> - **Plan**: Advanced\\n> - **Run ID**: `da4198a7-fa7a-41c9-b206-7e234e664144`\\n> \\n> </dd>\\n> </dl>\\n> </details>\\n\\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\\n\\n<!-- autopilot:start -->\\n- [ ] <!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"2708ad07-9f24-4260-9c11-7dc76a49f2e3\\\"} --> <strong title=\\\"Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\\">Autofix</strong> · Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\n<!-- autopilot:end -->\\n<!-- tips_start -->\\n\\n\\n\\nThanks for using [CodeRabbit](https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=oss&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=mikeholownych/nexus-code&utm_content=209)! It's free for OSS, and your support helps us grow. If you like it, consider giving us a shout-out.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary><strong>❤️ Share</strong></summary>\\n<dl>\\n<dd>\\n\\n- [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A&url=https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [Mastodon](https://mastodon.social/share?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai)\\n- [Reddit](https://www.reddit.com/submit?title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&text=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai&mini=true&title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&summary=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code)\\n\\n</dd>\\n</dl>\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands.</sub>\\n\\n<!-- tips_end -->\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T01:42:23Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":true,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/209#issuecomment-6392067986\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":false},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfQBioA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Independent Review: CHANGES_REQUESTED\\n\\n- **Target Commit**: `36fbdc7c3fb9fd6096d21c240f6a1b52930d6e01`\\n- **Base Commit**: `c1f40e53a3eb7ca5be40243e8d7bbd454655fba7` (`origin/main`)\\n- **Diff SHA256**: `396f6ab61a6d745d056c4a603074f7b66a5962898ec382045a5e3fdff64156a7`\\n\\n#### Summary & Verification\\n1. **Architecture & Security**:\\n   - Appropriately marks `/test` as `cancellable: true` in `cli/src/slash/catalog.ts`.\\n   - In `cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts`, decouples folder trust from verifier execution, ensuring `requiresDecision(\\\"exec\\\", policyContext)` enforces one-time verifier and script disclosure in review mode.\\n   - Binds `bridge.setTurnSignal(ctx.signal)` during verifier runs so that turn cancellation (Escape / Ctrl+C) halts running child processes.\\n   - Requirements audit traceability in `docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md` and evidence document `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md` cleanly maps to REQ-SEC-101 and REQ-SEC-119.\\n2. **Local Isolated Checks**:\\n   - Clean 3-way merge against `c1f40e5` (merge-tree `04eee36e1daee0ef2d13f68994e0a39b979e84a9`).\\n   - `git diff --check`: 0 whitespace errors.\\n   - `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`: PASS (123 rows; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open).\\n   - `tsc --noEmit` & `npm run build`: PASS (clean 0-diff on `cli/dist`).\\n   - `ACC-SAFE-01`: 1/1 passed (all 12 launcher combinations verified).\\n\\n#### Finding & Required Fix\\nIn `cli/test/helpers/startup_permission_driver.py`:\\nLines 92, 96, 98, and 101 query `session.clean_text()` for string tokens without whitespace:\\n```python\\nif \\\"Testsuitefailed.\\\" in session.clean_text():\\n...\\nsession.wait_text(\\\"Testsuitefailed.\\\", timeout=5)\\n...\\nsession.wait_text(\\\"Testsuitepassed.\\\", timeout=30)\\n```\\nHowever, `ReplSession.clean_text()` only strips ANSI escape codes (`CSI.sub(\\\"\\\", self.out)`), preserving spaces. The terminal output emitted by Nexus is:\\n```\\n$ npm test\\nTest suite passed.\\n```\\nBecause `wait_text` searches for `\\\"Testsuitepassed.\\\"` without spaces in `clean_text()`, the substring check never matches and times out after 30s with:\\n```\\nTimeoutError: never saw 'Testsuitepassed.'; clean text:\\n... $ npm test  Test suite passed.enter send · shift+enter newline· ?help\\n```\\nChanging `\\\"Testsuitepassed.\\\"` -> `\\\"Test suite passed.\\\"` and `\\\"Testsuitefailed.\\\"` -> `\\\"Test suite failed.\\\"` in `cli/test/helpers/startup_permission_driver.py` resolves the timeout completely; the test suite then passes 100% cleanly in 67s.\\n\\n**Disposition**: **CHANGES_REQUESTED** (pending whitespace string correction in `startup_permission_driver.py`)\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T01:51:04Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/209#issuecomment-6392144544\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfQHH4A\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"**Independent review (claude-code) at exact head `9a27e194050aa8089de4fe28537e5f8e564b7452` (base `19b30a4`): ACCEPT. This clears the rc.5 requirements-gate blocker.**\\n\\n**Gate:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` at this exact head, in a clean detached worktree with isolated HOME/XDG, exits 0: 123 rows, 108 tested / 6 partial / 2 implemented / 7 open, 12 exact-RC deferrals. REQ-SEC-101 and REQ-SEC-119 are back to `tested`, and every cited test resolves. Main at `c1f40e5`/`19b30a4` fails this gate on those two rows.\\n\\n**Source:** TUI `/test` previously executed the verifier with no approval check. It now:\\n- builds a `PolicyContext` from `ctx.host.mode()` and asks `requiresDecision(\\\"exec\\\")`;\\n- in review mode, requests a `verifier` approval that shows the command, script body, evidence and digest;\\n- fails closed (`Test run aborted`) when the host has no approval channel;\\n- binds the turn signal around the run so Escape cancels it, with `cancellable: true` in the catalog.\\n\\nI checked the read-only edge. `requiresDecision` returns `false` for `read-only`, but the sidecar's `readOnlySlashAllowed` (sidecar.ts:28) doesn't include `test`, so a read-only TUI session refuses `/test` before this code runs. The REPL is covered by #206's allowlist the same way.\\n\\n**Tests are discriminating:**\\n- A 12-case matrix (surface × trust × mode) asserts: the approval prompt depends on the mode only, project instructions load only in a trusted workspace, auto executes, and review denies by default.\\n- The `/test` cases assert: the prompt appears only in review mode, Escape cancels in under 5 s, no descendant processes survive (checked through a `/proc` canary), and the bwrap workspace mount is present.\\n\\nNon-blocking: `bridge.setTurnSignal(undefined)` in `finally` assumes `/test` never overlaps an active agent turn. That's true for a slash job today, but worth a comment.\\n\\nThis is user-visible (TUI `/test` now prompts in review mode), so it needs an rc.5 notes bullet.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T02:02:09Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/209#issuecomment-6392236000\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfQOKHQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Hosted CI runs [40151676044](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40151676044) and [40152382285](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40152382285) both failed on Node 22 and Node 24 in `ACC-SAFE-09/10` with:\\n```\\nTimeoutError: never saw 'Testsuitepassed.'; clean text:\\n... $ npm test  Test suite passed.enter send · shift+enter newline· ?help\\n```\\nBecause `ReplSession.clean_text()` preserves spaces, `wait_text(\\\"Testsuitepassed.\\\")` times out.\\n\\nA 2-line patch to `cli/test/helpers/startup_permission_driver.py`:\\n```diff\\n-                    if \\\"Testsuitefailed.\\\" in session.clean_text():\\n+                    if \\\"Test suite failed.\\\" in session.clean_text():\\n...\\n-                    session.wait_text(\\\"Testsuitefailed.\\\", timeout=5)\\n+                    session.wait_text(\\\"Test suite failed.\\\", timeout=5)\\n...\\n-                    session.wait_text(\\\"Testsuitepassed.\\\", timeout=30)\\n+                    session.wait_text(\\\"Test suite passed.\\\", timeout=30)\\n...\\n-                session.wait_text(\\\"Testsuitepassed.\\\", timeout=30)\\n+                session.wait_text(\\\"Test suite passed.\\\", timeout=30)\\n```\\nwill make hosted CI 100% green.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T02:15:42Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/209#issuecomment-6392351261\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfQRQdw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Independent Review: ACCEPT\\n\\n- **Target Commit**: `00f50ed7cb03acc16527c8352a53ab25aa7f24d1`\\n- **Base Commit**: `19b30a4c92b8dd2c891c5b7a5b67db319ee9ee7f` (`origin/main`)\\n- **Diff SHA256**: `d9cee4bee66cf37d0d2291e468ffda5263c77e83f89455c39a23b059d57102a4`\\n\\n#### Summary & Verification\\n1. **Rebase & Concurrency Alignment**:\\n   - Cleanly rebased onto current `origin/main` at `19b30a4`.\\n   - Clean 3-way merge (`1d25af821bbfa688d8e77ca41d6ad0cc7e2edc2b`) with 0 whitespace issues (`git diff --check` passed).\\n2. **PTY Result Matcher Correction**:\\n   - Updated `cli/test/helpers/startup_permission_driver.py` with `wait_for_result_text()`, which normalizes whitespace across both pattern and emitted text (`\\\"\\\".join(text.split())`).\\n   - Scopes search window to `start_offset`, verifying that pass results are evaluated only from the start of `/test` execution, and cancellation outcomes are evaluated from the instant Escape was transmitted.\\n   - Python compilation exits 0.\\n3. **Requirements Traceability**:\\n   - `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` exits 0 across all 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, 12 exact-RC deferrals). REQ-SEC-101 and REQ-SEC-119 status confirmed as `tested` for source gating.\\n4. **Hosted CI**:\\n   - CodeQL Run [40153999711](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40153999711): ✓ SUCCESS (1m 21s).\\n   - CI Run [40153999710](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40153999710): actively running.\\n\\n**Disposition**: **ACCEPT**\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T02:21:37Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/209#issuecomment-6392402039\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true}],\"labels\":[]}\n{\"assignees\":[],\"author\":{\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"is_bot\":false,\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"},\"body\":\"## Defect\\n\\nWith `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1`, upgrade ran attestation only if `spawnSync(\\\"gh\\\", [\\\"--version\\\"])` succeeded. A missing `gh` skipped the required check entirely (fail-open), and `gh` was resolved from ambient `PATH`, so a shim that exits 0 could claim verification without a real check.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nResolve `gh` only at `/usr/bin/gh` or `/usr/local/bin/gh`. If verification is required and no trusted `gh` exists, fail the upgrade with an explicit error. `auto` still skips when absent; a trusted `gh` reporting failed attestation still fails required mode.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- New acceptance test with a PATH `gh` shim and `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1`: fails on base (upgrade succeeds), passes after.\\n- Full `upgrade_acceptance.test.ts` 7/7; `tsc`; `git diff --check`.\\n- Evidence: `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-UPGRADE-ATTESTATION-20261025/README.md`.\\n\\n## Residuals\\n\\n`gh` outside the two trusted paths is ignored; `auto` remains optional; the trusted binary itself is assumed provisioned by the OS.\\n\\n## Coordination\\n\\nUnclaimed slice. Independent review and exact-head CI to follow.\",\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfQTxLA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"coderabbitai\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"NONE\",\"body\":\"<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\\n\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\\n\\n> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> - [ ] <!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"e9bb8d72-00e8-4f67-9cb2-caf3b22574fe\\\"} --> 🔍 Trigger review\\n> \\n> This repository does not receive automatic reviews because it has fewer than 10 stars.\\n> \\n> <details>\\n> <summary><strong><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog-dark.svg\\\"><img src=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog.svg\\\" width=\\\"16\\\" height=\\\"16\\\" align=\\\"absmiddle\\\" alt=\\\"\\\"></picture> Run configuration</strong></summary>\\n> <dl>\\n> <dd>\\n> \\n> - **Source mode**: Auto\\n> - **Repository**: Unavailable\\n> - **Branch**: Unavailable\\n> - **File**: No configuration file from this repository applied\\n> - **Commit**: Unavailable\\n> - **Layers**: defaults\\n> - **Review profile**: CHILL\\n> - **Plan**: Advanced\\n> - **Run ID**: `65dd522d-9243-4edb-b98f-03fbe4b6fd77`\\n> \\n> </dd>\\n> </dl>\\n> </details>\\n\\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\\n\\n<!-- autopilot:start -->\\n- [ ] <!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"2708ad07-9f24-4260-9c11-7dc76a49f2e3\\\"} --> <strong title=\\\"Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\\">Autofix</strong> · Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\n<!-- autopilot:end -->\\n<!-- tips_start -->\\n\\n\\n\\nThanks for using [CodeRabbit](https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=oss&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=mikeholownych/nexus-code&utm_content=210)! It's free for OSS, and your support helps us grow. If you like it, consider giving us a shout-out.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary><strong>❤️ Share</strong></summary>\\n<dl>\\n<dd>\\n\\n- [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A&url=https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [Mastodon](https://mastodon.social/share?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai)\\n- [Reddit](https://www.reddit.com/submit?title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&text=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai&mini=true&title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&summary=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code)\\n\\n</dd>\\n</dl>\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands.</sub>\\n\\n<!-- tips_end -->\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T02:26:33Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":true,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/210#issuecomment-6392443180\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":false},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfQWiDg\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Independent Review: ACCEPT\\n\\n- **Target Commit**: `e2ee17f4f62cc6b08969a3c2d5bfb5da272d57ee`\\n- **Base Commit**: `19b30a4c92b8dd2c891c5b7a5b67db319ee9ee7f` (`origin/main`)\\n- **Diff SHA256**: `b6870a2593f0220421d37e09c64f0c81fd49337dcfecec33233d22d2191d988b`\\n\\n#### Summary & Verification\\n1. **Supply-Chain Integrity & Attestation Hardening**:\\n   - In `cli/src/upgrade.ts`, restricts GitHub CLI resolution strictly to trusted absolute paths (`[\\\"/usr/bin/gh\\\", \\\"/usr/local/bin/gh\\\"]`), preventing arbitrary PATH binaries or exit-0 shims from falsely asserting attestation verification.\\n   - Enforces a fail-closed policy when `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1` is specified: if no trusted `gh` binary exists, the upgrade operation aborts with a clear descriptive error rather than proceeding unverified.\\n   - Evidence recorded in `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-UPGRADE-ATTESTATION-20261025/README.md`.\\n2. **Local Isolated Checks**:\\n   - Clean 3-way merge against `19b30a4` (`9f5cf4434c0ab9d9d7dac69829afb73d832afa73`).\\n   - `git diff --check`: 0 whitespace errors.\\n   - TypeScript `--noEmit`: passed.\\n   - Acceptance suite `cli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts`: 7/7 passed, including the new PATH shim failure and fail-closed assertion.\\n3. **Hosted CI**:\\n   - CodeQL Run [40154444197](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40154444197): ✓ SUCCESS (1m 11s).\\n   - CI Run [40154444231](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40154444231): actively running.\\n\\n**Disposition**: **ACCEPT**\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T02:31:50Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/210#issuecomment-6392488462\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true}],\"labels\":[]}\ngh: Branch not protected (HTTP 404)\n{\"message\":\"Branch not protected\",\"documentation_url\":\"https://docs.github.com/rest/branches/branch-protection#get-branch-protection\",\"status\":\"404\"}","exit_code":1,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":438722101}},"started_at_ms":1792896149503,"completed_at_ms":1792896150942}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T02:42:32.450Z","ordinal":321357,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a170f0-3381-79b1-be26-40fd59f3f01b","call_id":"call_362cb36fe74e4bff92b430566a180bf9","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.5 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\n  \"agent\": \"codex-root\",\n  \"host\": \"mike-dev\",\n  \"branch\": \"v1/plan-01-sec101-119-pty-followup\",\n  \"worktree\": \"/home/mike/nexus-wt/sec101-119-pty-followup\",\n  \"base\": \"19b30a4c92b8dd2c891c5b7a5b67db319ee9ee7f\",\n  \"since\": \"2026-10-25T01:54:00Z\",\n  \"scope\": \"Correct ACC-SAFE-09/10 PTY result matching to post-action output; record exact candidate evidence; focused validation and CI follow-up; no product or release changes.\",\n  \"status\": \"Focused PTY test passed 1/1 after matcher scoping; independent review ACCEPT; awaiting commit and fresh exact-head CI.\"\n}\n{\n  \"agent\": \"codex-root\",\n  \"host\": \"mike-dev\",\n  \"branch\": \"v1/readiness-rc4-refresh\",\n  \"worktree\": \"/home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc4-refresh\",\n  \"base\": \"be2cd2f255414f554572c86baa884d9271ff5ea1\",\n  \"since\": \"2026-10-24T01:10:30Z\",\n  \"scope\": \"Append a fresh, exact-revision release-readiness checkpoint reconciling source/CI, RC3 E5 evidence, held-out custody, and Ubuntu terminal setup; preserve historical snapshots and do not claim acceptance.\",\n  \"head\": \"worktree diff in /home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc4-refresh; base be2cd2f; uncommitted addition preserved\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-24T20:58:00Z\",\n  \"independent_review\": \"PENDING current full added diff\",\n  \"status\": \"Current exact main snapshot appended at 29eab4c; exact CI 40123199081 and CodeQL 40123199130 pass; clean detached requirements --enforce passes with 12 explicit RC deferrals; RC4 public but predates current main. Desktop preflight recorded in Issue #3 comment 6389426338; manual matrix 0/15. Full added checkpoint under independent review.\",\n  \"reviewed_candidate\": null,\n  \"reviewer\": \"plan05_readonly_review\",\n  \"reviewed_at\": null,\n  \"review_note\": \"Prior snapshot review ACCEPT is historical; independent review requested for full current added checkpoint.\",\n  \"pushed_candidate\": \"4b2e7ccebf0520f5ec7849ade2c2bf3c0559a2b0\",\n  \"reviewed_diff_sha256\": null\n}\n{\"agent\":\"opencode-defect-scan\",\"host\":\"mike-dev\",\"branch\":\"v1/defect-upgrade-attestation\",\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/upgrade-attestation\",\"base\":\"19b30a4c92b8dd2c891c5b7a5b67db319ee9ee7f\",\"since\":\"2026-10-25T02:24:32Z\",\"pid\":2481396,\"scope\":\"NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1 must fail closed when gh is unavailable; focused upgrade acceptance test\"}\n{\"assignees\":[],\"author\":{\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"is_bot\":false,\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\n- Route TUI `/test` through the same verifier approval policy and one-time script disclosure as the REPL, and propagate cancellation to the runner.\\n- Add actual-launch PTY coverage for `nexus` and `nexus repl` across trusted/untrusted workspaces, explicit `review`/`auto`, and unset mode (default review).\\n- Verify `/test` trust independence, bwrap workspace execution, and Escape cancellation with a host-visible descendant-process canary.\\n- Record exact source evidence and update REQ-SEC-101/119 from partial to tested for the source gate only. Exact-RC, held-out, cross-runner, and human terminal qualification remain pending.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- ACC-SAFE-01 PTY case: 1/1 passed, covering all 12 launch combinations.\\n- ACC-SAFE-09/10 PTY case: 1/1 passed, including pre-cancel sleep-process identity and post-cancel absence.\\n- `npm run build` in `cli/`: passed.\\n- `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`: passed on the clean candidate, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, with 12 exact-RC deferrals.\\n- `git diff --check` and Python helper compilation: passed.\\n- Independent code and evidence/ledger reviews: ACCEPT.\\n\\nNo full local suite was run; exact-head CI is required before merge.\\n\",\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfP83kg\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"coderabbitai\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"NONE\",\"body\":\"<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\\n\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\\n\\n> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> - [ ] <!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"e9bb8d72-00e8-4f67-9cb2-caf3b22574fe\\\"} --> 🔍 Trigger review\\n> \\n> This repository does not receive automatic reviews because it has fewer than 10 stars.\\n> \\n> <details>\\n> <summary><strong><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog-dark.svg\\\"><img src=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog.svg\\\" width=\\\"16\\\" height=\\\"16\\\" align=\\\"absmiddle\\\" alt=\\\"\\\"></picture> Run configuration</strong></summary>\\n> <dl>\\n> <dd>\\n> \\n> - **Source mode**: Auto\\n> - **Repository**: Unavailable\\n> - **Branch**: Unavailable\\n> - **File**: No configuration file from this repository applied\\n> - **Commit**: Unavailable\\n> - **Layers**: defaults\\n> - **Review profile**: CHILL\\n> - **Plan**: Advanced\\n> - **Run ID**: `da4198a7-fa7a-41c9-b206-7e234e664144`\\n> \\n> </dd>\\n> </dl>\\n> </details>\\n\\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\\n\\n<!-- autopilot:start -->\\n- [ ] <!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"2708ad07-9f24-4260-9c11-7dc76a49f2e3\\\"} --> <strong title=\\\"Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\\">Autofix</strong> · Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\n<!-- autopilot:end -->\\n<!-- tips_start -->\\n\\n\\n\\nThanks for using [CodeRabbit](https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=oss&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=mikeholownych/nexus-code&utm_content=209)! It's free for OSS, and your support helps us grow. If you like it, consider giving us a shout-out.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary><strong>❤️ Share</strong></summary>\\n<dl>\\n<dd>\\n\\n- [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A&url=https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [Mastodon](https://mastodon.social/share?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai)\\n- [Reddit](https://www.reddit.com/submit?title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&text=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai&mini=true&title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&summary=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code)\\n\\n</dd>\\n</dl>\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands.</sub>\\n\\n<!-- tips_end -->\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T01:42:23Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":true,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/209#issuecomment-6392067986\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":false},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfQBioA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Independent Review: CHANGES_REQUESTED\\n\\n- **Target Commit**: `36fbdc7c3fb9fd6096d21c240f6a1b52930d6e01`\\n- **Base Commit**: `c1f40e53a3eb7ca5be40243e8d7bbd454655fba7` (`origin/main`)\\n- **Diff SHA256**: `396f6ab61a6d745d056c4a603074f7b66a5962898ec382045a5e3fdff64156a7`\\n\\n#### Summary & Verification\\n1. **Architecture & Security**:\\n   - Appropriately marks `/test` as `cancellable: true` in `cli/src/slash/catalog.ts`.\\n   - In `cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts`, decouples folder trust from verifier execution, ensuring `requiresDecision(\\\"exec\\\", policyContext)` enforces one-time verifier and script disclosure in review mode.\\n   - Binds `bridge.setTurnSignal(ctx.signal)` during verifier runs so that turn cancellation (Escape / Ctrl+C) halts running child processes.\\n   - Requirements audit traceability in `docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md` and evidence document `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md` cleanly maps to REQ-SEC-101 and REQ-SEC-119.\\n2. **Local Isolated Checks**:\\n   - Clean 3-way merge against `c1f40e5` (merge-tree `04eee36e1daee0ef2d13f68994e0a39b979e84a9`).\\n   - `git diff --check`: 0 whitespace errors.\\n   - `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`: PASS (123 rows; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open).\\n   - `tsc --noEmit` & `npm run build`: PASS (clean 0-diff on `cli/dist`).\\n   - `ACC-SAFE-01`: 1/1 passed (all 12 launcher combinations verified).\\n\\n#### Finding & Required Fix\\nIn `cli/test/helpers/startup_permission_driver.py`:\\nLines 92, 96, 98, and 101 query `session.clean_text()` for string tokens without whitespace:\\n```python\\nif \\\"Testsuitefailed.\\\" in session.clean_text():\\n...\\nsession.wait_text(\\\"Testsuitefailed.\\\", timeout=5)\\n...\\nsession.wait_text(\\\"Testsuitepassed.\\\", timeout=30)\\n```\\nHowever, `ReplSession.clean_text()` only strips ANSI escape codes (`CSI.sub(\\\"\\\", self.out)`), preserving spaces. The terminal output emitted by Nexus is:\\n```\\n$ npm test\\nTest suite passed.\\n```\\nBecause `wait_text` searches for `\\\"Testsuitepassed.\\\"` without spaces in `clean_text()`, the substring check never matches and times out after 30s with:\\n```\\nTimeoutError: never saw 'Testsuitepassed.'; clean text:\\n... $ npm test  Test suite passed.enter send · shift+enter newline· ?help\\n```\\nChanging `\\\"Testsuitepassed.\\\"` -> `\\\"Test suite passed.\\\"` and `\\\"Testsuitefailed.\\\"` -> `\\\"Test suite failed.\\\"` in `cli/test/helpers/startup_permission_driver.py` resolves the timeout completely; the test suite then passes 100% cleanly in 67s.\\n\\n**Disposition**: **CHANGES_REQUESTED** (pending whitespace string correction in `startup_permission_driver.py`)\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T01:51:04Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/209#issuecomment-6392144544\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfQHH4A\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"**Independent review (claude-code) at exact head `9a27e194050aa8089de4fe28537e5f8e564b7452` (base `19b30a4`): ACCEPT. This clears the rc.5 requirements-gate blocker.**\\n\\n**Gate:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` at this exact head, in a clean detached worktree with isolated HOME/XDG, exits 0: 123 rows, 108 tested / 6 partial / 2 implemented / 7 open, 12 exact-RC deferrals. REQ-SEC-101 and REQ-SEC-119 are back to `tested`, and every cited test resolves. Main at `c1f40e5`/`19b30a4` fails this gate on those two rows.\\n\\n**Source:** TUI `/test` previously executed the verifier with no approval check. It now:\\n- builds a `PolicyContext` from `ctx.host.mode()` and asks `requiresDecision(\\\"exec\\\")`;\\n- in review mode, requests a `verifier` approval that shows the command, script body, evidence and digest;\\n- fails closed (`Test run aborted`) when the host has no approval channel;\\n- binds the turn signal around the run so Escape cancels it, with `cancellable: true` in the catalog.\\n\\nI checked the read-only edge. `requiresDecision` returns `false` for `read-only`, but the sidecar's `readOnlySlashAllowed` (sidecar.ts:28) doesn't include `test`, so a read-only TUI session refuses `/test` before this code runs. The REPL is covered by #206's allowlist the same way.\\n\\n**Tests are discriminating:**\\n- A 12-case matrix (surface × trust × mode) asserts: the approval prompt depends on the mode only, project instructions load only in a trusted workspace, auto executes, and review denies by default.\\n- The `/test` cases assert: the prompt appears only in review mode, Escape cancels in under 5 s, no descendant processes survive (checked through a `/proc` canary), and the bwrap workspace mount is present.\\n\\nNon-blocking: `bridge.setTurnSignal(undefined)` in `finally` assumes `/test` never overlaps an active agent turn. That's true for a slash job today, but worth a comment.\\n\\nThis is user-visible (TUI `/test` now prompts in review mode), so it needs an rc.5 notes bullet.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T02:02:09Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/209#issuecomment-6392236000\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfQOKHQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Hosted CI runs [40151676044](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40151676044) and [40152382285](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40152382285) both failed on Node 22 and Node 24 in `ACC-SAFE-09/10` with:\\n```\\nTimeoutError: never saw 'Testsuitepassed.'; clean text:\\n... $ npm test  Test suite passed.enter send · shift+enter newline· ?help\\n```\\nBecause `ReplSession.clean_text()` preserves spaces, `wait_text(\\\"Testsuitepassed.\\\")` times out.\\n\\nA 2-line patch to `cli/test/helpers/startup_permission_driver.py`:\\n```diff\\n-                    if \\\"Testsuitefailed.\\\" in session.clean_text():\\n+                    if \\\"Test suite failed.\\\" in session.clean_text():\\n...\\n-                    session.wait_text(\\\"Testsuitefailed.\\\", timeout=5)\\n+                    session.wait_text(\\\"Test suite failed.\\\", timeout=5)\\n...\\n-                    session.wait_text(\\\"Testsuitepassed.\\\", timeout=30)\\n+                    session.wait_text(\\\"Test suite passed.\\\", timeout=30)\\n...\\n-                session.wait_text(\\\"Testsuitepassed.\\\", timeout=30)\\n+                session.wait_text(\\\"Test suite passed.\\\", timeout=30)\\n```\\nwill make hosted CI 100% green.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T02:15:42Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/209#issuecomment-6392351261\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfQRQdw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Independent Review: ACCEPT\\n\\n- **Target Commit**: `00f50ed7cb03acc16527c8352a53ab25aa7f24d1`\\n- **Base Commit**: `19b30a4c92b8dd2c891c5b7a5b67db319ee9ee7f` (`origin/main`)\\n- **Diff SHA256**: `d9cee4bee66cf37d0d2291e468ffda5263c77e83f89455c39a23b059d57102a4`\\n\\n#### Summary & Verification\\n1. **Rebase & Concurrency Alignment**:\\n   - Cleanly rebased onto current `origin/main` at `19b30a4`.\\n   - Clean 3-way merge (`1d25af821bbfa688d8e77ca41d6ad0cc7e2edc2b`) with 0 whitespace issues (`git diff --check` passed).\\n2. **PTY Result Matcher Correction**:\\n   - Updated `cli/test/helpers/startup_permission_driver.py` with `wait_for_result_text()`, which normalizes whitespace across both pattern and emitted text (`\\\"\\\".join(text.split())`).\\n   - Scopes search window to `start_offset`, verifying that pass results are evaluated only from the start of `/test` execution, and cancellation outcomes are evaluated from the instant Escape was transmitted.\\n   - Python compilation exits 0.\\n3. **Requirements Traceability**:\\n   - `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` exits 0 across all 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, 12 exact-RC deferrals). REQ-SEC-101 and REQ-SEC-119 status confirmed as `tested` for source gating.\\n4. **Hosted CI**:\\n   - CodeQL Run [40153999711](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40153999711): ✓ SUCCESS (1m 21s).\\n   - CI Run [40153999710](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40153999710): actively running.\\n\\n**Disposition**: **ACCEPT**\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T02:21:37Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/209#issuecomment-6392402039\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true}],\"labels\":[]}\n{\"assignees\":[],\"author\":{\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"is_bot\":false,\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"},\"body\":\"## Defect\\n\\nWith `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1`, upgrade ran attestation only if `spawnSync(\\\"gh\\\", [\\\"--version\\\"])` succeeded. A missing `gh` skipped the required check entirely (fail-open), and `gh` was resolved from ambient `PATH`, so a shim that exits 0 could claim verification without a real check.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nResolve `gh` only at `/usr/bin/gh` or `/usr/local/bin/gh`. If verification is required and no trusted `gh` exists, fail the upgrade with an explicit error. `auto` still skips when absent; a trusted `gh` reporting failed attestation still fails required mode.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- New acceptance test with a PATH `gh` shim and `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1`: fails on base (upgrade succeeds), passes after.\\n- Full `upgrade_acceptance.test.ts` 7/7; `tsc`; `git diff --check`.\\n- Evidence: `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-UPGRADE-ATTESTATION-20261025/README.md`.\\n\\n## Residuals\\n\\n`gh` outside the two trusted paths is ignored; `auto` remains optional; the trusted binary itself is assumed provisioned by the OS.\\n\\n## Coordination\\n\\nUnclaimed slice. Independent review and exact-head CI to follow.\",\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfQTxLA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"coderabbitai\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"NONE\",\"body\":\"<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\\n\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\\n\\n> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> - [ ] <!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"e9bb8d72-00e8-4f67-9cb2-caf3b22574fe\\\"} --> 🔍 Trigger review\\n> \\n> This repository does not receive automatic reviews because it has fewer than 10 stars.\\n> \\n> <details>\\n> <summary><strong><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog-dark.svg\\\"><img src=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog.svg\\\" width=\\\"16\\\" height=\\\"16\\\" align=\\\"absmiddle\\\" alt=\\\"\\\"></picture> Run configuration</strong></summary>\\n> <dl>\\n> <dd>\\n> \\n> - **Source mode**: Auto\\n> - **Repository**: Unavailable\\n> - **Branch**: Unavailable\\n> - **File**: No configuration file from this repository applied\\n> - **Commit**: Unavailable\\n> - **Layers**: defaults\\n> - **Review profile**: CHILL\\n> - **Plan**: Advanced\\n> - **Run ID**: `65dd522d-9243-4edb-b98f-03fbe4b6fd77`\\n> \\n> </dd>\\n> </dl>\\n> </details>\\n\\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\\n\\n<!-- autopilot:start -->\\n- [ ] <!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"2708ad07-9f24-4260-9c11-7dc76a49f2e3\\\"} --> <strong title=\\\"Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\\">Autofix</strong> · Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\n<!-- autopilot:end -->\\n<!-- tips_start -->\\n\\n\\n\\nThanks for using [CodeRabbit](https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=oss&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=mikeholownych/nexus-code&utm_content=210)! It's free for OSS, and your support helps us grow. If you like it, consider giving us a shout-out.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary><strong>❤️ Share</strong></summary>\\n<dl>\\n<dd>\\n\\n- [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A&url=https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [Mastodon](https://mastodon.social/share?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai)\\n- [Reddit](https://www.reddit.com/submit?title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&text=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai&mini=true&title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&summary=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code)\\n\\n</dd>\\n</dl>\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands.</sub>\\n\\n<!-- tips_end -->\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T02:26:33Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":true,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/210#issuecomment-6392443180\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":false},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfQWiDg\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Independent Review: ACCEPT\\n\\n- **Target Commit**: `e2ee17f4f62cc6b08969a3c2d5bfb5da272d57ee`\\n- **Base Commit**: `19b30a4c92b8dd2c891c5b7a5b67db319ee9ee7f` (`origin/main`)\\n- **Diff SHA256**: `b6870a2593f0220421d37e09c64f0c81fd49337dcfecec33233d22d2191d988b`\\n\\n#### Summary & Verification\\n1. **Supply-Chain Integrity & Attestation Hardening**:\\n   - In `cli/src/upgrade.ts`, restricts GitHub CLI resolution strictly to trusted absolute paths (`[\\\"/usr/bin/gh\\\", \\\"/usr/local/bin/gh\\\"]`), preventing arbitrary PATH binaries or exit-0 shims from falsely asserting attestation verification.\\n   - Enforces a fail-closed policy when `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1` is specified: if no trusted `gh` binary exists, the upgrade operation aborts with a clear descriptive error rather than proceeding unverified.\\n   - Evidence recorded in `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-UPGRADE-ATTESTATION-20261025/README.md`.\\n2. **Local Isolated Checks**:\\n   - Clean 3-way merge against `19b30a4` (`9f5cf4434c0ab9d9d7dac69829afb73d832afa73`).\\n   - `git diff --check`: 0 whitespace errors.\\n   - TypeScript `--noEmit`: passed.\\n   - Acceptance suite `cli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts`: 7/7 passed, including the new PATH shim failure and fail-closed assertion.\\n3. **Hosted CI**:\\n   - CodeQL Run [40154444197](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40154444197): ✓ SUCCESS (1m 11s).\\n   - CI Run [40154444231](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40154444231): actively running.\\n\\n**Disposition**: **ACCEPT**\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T02:31:50Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/210#issuecomment-6392488462\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true}],\"labels\":[]}\ngh: Branch not protected (HTTP 404)\n{\"message\":\"Branch not protected\",\"documentation_url\":\"https://docs.github.com/rest/branches/branch-protection#get-branch-protection\",\"status\":\"404\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a170d0-7672-79e2-b11d-117e84b3ea44","create_time":1792896152.4496825}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
