{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T02:48:12.424Z","ordinal":321534,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a170f5-6388-7cb3-b6cf-d0037b24f99e","call_id":"call_5cd0491ea99d406d81dc69abf71643ae","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT.** The missing trusted-`gh` path is covered deterministically: the test injects an empty trusted-path list, places a success-returning shim in `PATH`, and confirms the shim is not executed and rejection happens before journal or staging creation. The separate test covers a trusted `gh` that fails attestation. The documented behavior change for `gh` outside the fixed system paths presents no additional blocker.\\n\\nBase: `19b30a4`  \\nHead: `94ad942bd492ee6586bf73a595bbb642f8f73757`  \\nDiff SHA-256: `f40941e0ead3aba1babb4dbc920e03ef5bc09d0fffd5b7825435636eea2b94e8`\\n\\nRead-only review; no tests were run.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/pr207_independent_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** for the amended candidate against base `19b30a4`.\\n\\nThe ancestor walk treats only `ENOENT` as an absent marker and fails closed on other filesystem errors. It covers nested normal and linked worktrees when Git is unavailable, while non-repository paths remain a no-op. The existing read-only exclude behavior is unchanged.\\n\\n`git diff --check` is clean. I did not run tests; the reported 23/23 focused result is owner-supplied. The reviewed candidate is `f2d7b7d` plus uncommitted changes.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a170f2-3e90-7ad2-8d66-c8179982613b","create_time":1792896492.424213}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
