ode 20/22/24 jobs successful; `linux-x86_64` remains in progress. The custodian recorded an 8/8-task T3 corpus seal at 10:43:02 UTC, with corrected private manifest digest `dcbd794ed2998423787fdead4957b38b0c4a8a641855d87304d065d01c3fae37` at 10:43:22 UTC, and released both authoring claims. This is sealed, custodian-validated corpus evidence; no T3 qualification run has occurred. PR #24's real-terminal procedure is integrated, but all required five environments × three sizes still require the exact installed RC and genuine operator evidence; no matrix cell is claimed complete.\n- **RC and publication:** Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`; PR #8 remains a draft integration-to-main candidate. No RC artifact, exact-RC test, cross-runner RC comparison, installed provider/standalone run, T2/T3/T4 qualification, or independent RC acceptance exists. Final stable publication remains authorized but gated on all mandatory exact-RC acceptance and release checks.\n\n## Superseded checkpoint (2026-10-18, `a7126aa`)\n\n- **Authoritative integration revision and CI:** `origin/v1/integration` is at `a7126aa811044b45357440b5aee9228500a480a8` (draft PR [#8](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/8) targeting `main`). GitHub Actions CI run [39108774170](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39108774170) on `a7126aa` completed with **success** across all five jobs (`cloudflare-contest-contract`, `test-matrix (20)`, `test-matrix (22)`, `test-matrix (24)`, and `linux-x86_64`: Rust 281/281, CLI 1,152/1,152 with 0 skipped, security gates, deterministic double-build packaging, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke). Source CI is green; installed-RC product qualification has not yet executed.\n- **Sealed held-out T2 corpus (`heldout-v2`, PR [#16](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/16), merged at `f776903`):**\n  - Committed public manifest: `eval/heldout-manifest.json` (SHA-256 `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`), containing 40 external-repository T2 tasks pinned to full 40-hex baseline commits across Go (10), JavaScript (10), Python (10), and Rust (10), and across bugfix (10), debug (10), feature (10), and refactor (10).\n  - Custody record: `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md` (updated at `ce3f590`).\n  - **Distinction of evidence:** Independent public metadata review (`codex-lead`) verified and accepted the committed manifest digest (`50895b84…`), 40 unique task IDs, 10×4 class/language balance, 40 full pinned commits, and schema/digest fields without inspecting private payloads. Private payload validation (2 rounds per task in bounded `SUITE` windows: fresh clone → checkout → setup → pre-patch regression pass → pre-patch hidden fail → reference patch apply → post-patch hidden pass → post-patch regression pass), rejection/quarantine of one provenance-contaminated batch (`author-b9` at `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2-quarantine/b9-contaminated-2026-10-18T0235Z/`), per-session exec-log audits for clean replacement authors (`author-b8c`, `author-b9c`), and store access tightening (`/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2` mode `0700`, `tasks/` and `reference/` mode `0500` read-only) are custodian-attested in `custody-report-2026-10-18.md`. Earlier author-exposed packages (`v12`, `v15`, `v16`, `v17`, `v18`) recorded in historical sections below are superseded development/pilot artifacts and are never used for held-out qualification.\n- **Evaluator isolation and kernel resource contract (PRs [#10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/10), [#18](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/18), [#19](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/19)):**\n  - `blackbox-v1` oracle separation (`2c70d39`, PR #10) runs private oracle checks outside the candidate workspace while mounting the candidate workspace read-only (`--ro-bind`), superseding the historical shared-workspace oracle exposure noted in the 2026-10-17 review below.\n  - Repository workspace history isolation (`96aeef2`, PR #18, `eval/workspace.mjs`) stages external-repo tasks via `git init` + ancestor-only fetch (`--no-tags`, `--no-write-fetch-head`) without `--shared`, `objects/info/alternates`, remotes, tags, or post-baseline commits, preventing candidates from reading upstream fix commits in git history.\n  - Kernel-enforced resource contract (`91406bd`, PR #19, `eval/resources.mjs`, `eval/cgroup_supervisor.mjs`, `scripts/ensure-ci-user-cgroups.sh`) executes each task phase (setup, candidate sandbox, hidden/regression, oracle) inside a transient delegated `systemd --user` scope with verified cgroup v2 `CPUQuota`, `MemoryMax`, `MemorySwapMax=0`, `TasksMax`, `memory.oom.group=1`, dedicated size-capped tmpfs `workspaceRoot` storage enforcement, and `cgroup.kill` process-tree cleanup verified to `populated == 0`. These controls are source-implemented, independently reviewed, and CI-tested (`1,152/1,152` on `0cee0b7`, run `39104943950`), not live qualification results. Qualification-host provisioning (`nexus-eval` account, narrow sudoers rule, dedicated tmpfs mount, and frozen `config.resources` profile) remains a prerequisite before running held-out T2/T3/T4 workloads.\n- **Governance, tokenizer, and acceptance lifecycle reconciliations (PRs [#11](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/11)–[#15](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/15), [#17](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/17)):**\n  - `DEC-05` amendment (`f771a3c`, PR #11) and `ACCEPTANCE.md` §6.2 (`77102c5`, PR #13) resolve the historical eight-vs-nine T4 denominator conflict by retaining all **9 fault classes × 5 runs** (including SIGTERM + `run --resume`).\n  - `DEC-17` (`f771a3c`, PR #11), `REQ-AGT-118` reconciliation (`d2c4bfc`, PR #12), and published independent review records (`19dedc6`, PR #14; `f8e19e4`, PR #15; `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-11_PR-11d_REVIEW_AGT-118/`) resolve the CJK/Hangul admission-safety floor vs `≤ 1.5×` accuracy band conflict: the `≥ 1` token/character safety floor takes precedence, `≤ 1.5×` applies to corpora not dominated by the floor, and recorded Chinese (`2.00×`) and Hangul (`1.67×`) exceptions remain preserved. `REQ-AGT-118` is `tested` at the source level (`tokens.test.ts` 3/3 pass); this does not claim installed-RC product qualification.\n  - `REQ-AGT-010` and historical `CTX-001` rows (`f68b5bc`, PR #17) are reconciled with `DEC-04`: the v1 subset (`ACC-TRUST-04` trust gating and source/trust annotations in `workspace_trust.test.ts`, 5/5 pass) is source-tested and independently accepted, while the full provenance graph and `CTX-002` remain post-v1.\n  - `ACCEPTANCE.md` §1.1 (`77102c5`, PR #13) defines the five-stage RC lifecycle binding source gates, workflow-built RC artifact construction, RC artifact gates (`ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08`), installed-RC qualification, and version-only stable promotion.\n- **Supply-chain reproducibility and draft-then-publish release workflow (PRs [#20](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/20), [#21](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/21)):**\n  - `.github/workflows/repro.yml` and `scripts/repro-identity.mjs` (`86bdbe6`, PR #20) enforce fail-closed tag/commit/clean-tree/version identity across independent Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 builders.\n  - `.github/workflows/release.yml` and `scripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs` (`a7126aa`, PR #21) build RC tags (`vX.Y.Z-rc.N`) as prereleases and build stable tags (`vX.Y.Z`) as **unpublished drafts** (`draft: true`), requiring via the RC's own checker that a stable tag is a single commit directly on its `vX.Y.Z-rc.N` parent changing only synchronized version metadata.\n\n## Historical evidence: Corrected Node 20 full-suite result (2026-10-17 07:40 UTC; superseded for branch status above)\n\n- PR #10 follow-up commit `4439b7e61dd51a60f4674bddbfdd1621386cce53` includes both fixes identified by the exact Node 20 run on `bb8e673`: packaged doctor evidence no longer prints an external launcher target, and `hasExecutedTests()` recognizes Node 20 TAP summaries only when at least one test passed or failed. It includes regression coverage for an external `nexus` symlink, ordinary TAP, all-skipped TAP, zero-test TAP, and cancelled-only TAP. Independent code review accepted these changes. (Subsequently integrated via PR #10 at `2c70d39`.)\n- A complete `npm --prefix cli test` on the corrected exact source tree completed under Node 20.20.2/npm 10.8.2 with **1,104 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped** across 193 suites; shell exit 0; reported duration 1,615,366 ms. The preserved log is `/tmp/nexus-p10g-node20-full-corrected.log`. Build ran before the suite, and the source tree was committed without changes while the test ran, binding the result to `4439b7e`.\n- This full pass supersedes neither the real pre-fix failure on `bb8e673` (1,097 passed, 7 failed) nor its history. The intentionally interrupted pre-correction run remains classified as interrupted. The package leak and parser edge cases were fixed before this corrected run; tests were not skipped or relaxed.\n- At 07:40 UTC, PR #10 checks were run `39014385063` on `4439b7e` and PR #9 checks were run `39012957463` on `6220e14`; superseded runs `39010821988`, `39010709839`, and `39006853703` were cancelled after newer commits replaced their heads.\n\n## Historical evidence: Node 20 full-suite follow-up (2026-10-17 07:13 UTC)\n\n- A complete `npm --prefix cli test` run on exact PR #10 commit `bb8e673637231aa38ab04b6f07a4498a88bdc132`, using Node 20.20.2/npm 10.8.2 and an isolated home, completed with **1,097 passed, 7 failed, 0 skipped**. The preserved log is `/tmp/nexus-p10g-node20-full-bb8e673.log`. The failures include a packaged-doctor evidence disclosure of an external launcher target and valid Node 20 TAP summaries being misread as zero executed tests. This is an actual source-suite failure and supersedes any implication that the full cross-version test set had not yet been exercised locally.\n- A four-file follow-up in the PR #10 worktree avoids exposing external launcher paths in packaged doctor evidence and recognizes Node 20 TAP summaries while rejecting zero-test, all-skipped, and cancelled-only summaries. The cancelled-only edge case was found during independent review and fixed before acceptance; the reviewer accepted the corrected parser/test diff. Build succeeded, the focused four-file selection passed **47/47**, staged `git diff --check` passed, and staged Gitleaks found zero findings.\n- One full-suite attempt on the pre-correction working tree was intentionally interrupted after review found the cancelled-only edge case. It is classified as interrupted, not passed or failed. The prior 1,097/7 result remains historical evidence and is not erased.\n\n## Historical evidence: Release validation update (2026-10-17 06:40 UTC)\n\n- A focused Node 20.20.2 run of `npm --prefix cli test -- test/security_gates.test.ts` against PR #10's pre-fix snapshot reproduced an SBOM test failure: nested `npx` exited with `ENOENT` for the absent `cli/lib` directory after inheriting npm's `npm_config_local_prefix` and `npm_config_prefix`. A prior supplemental command labeled Node 20 was invalid because `node` resolved to Node 24; it is not counted as Node 20 evidence.\n- PR #10 commit `bb8e673637231aa38ab04b6f07a4498a88bdc132` (and `59dc522` on integration) clears the lowercase and uppercase prefix variables only for the nested CycloneDX `npx` call and adds a regression that injects the lowercase values set by `npm --prefix cli`. The focused security-gate suite then passed 10/10 under Node 20.20.2/npm 10.8.2 and 10/10 under Node 24.11.1/npm 11.19.0. `bash -n`, `git diff --check`, and staged Gitleaks also passed. Independent review accepted the scoped fix and confirmed Linux CI compatibility.\n\n## Historical evidence: Review update (2026-10-17 03:10 UTC; pilot packages superseded by `heldout-v2` above)\n\nThis section records the historical inspection at `e1759cae9cf399e2d2586d05bfea3f86b757c412`. The pilot package attempts and their failures remain historical evidence and are not erased; the active sealed held-out corpus is `heldout-v2` (`eval/heldout-manifest.json`, SHA-256 `50895b84…`, PR #16).\n\n- At 03:10 UTC on 2026-10-17, `v1/integration` was `e1759cae9cf399e2d2586d05bfea3f86b757c412` and `v1/candidate-1` was `6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a`.\n- Independent inspection of pilot candidate v17 verified manifest digest `ce44dd2066dc4dec6c5e1f56021e3b442aa293510cbf9f217cf2c2e2256d83fe`, all 227 listed file hashes/sizes, no unlisted package files, 40 parseable tasks, 20 repository/20 fixture tasks, and 80/80 validator-command digest coverage. That author-exposed set was not independently held out or accepted and was retired as development/pilot material when `heldout-v2` was commissioned.\n- Independent inspection of Node 24.11.1 supplement v2 verified its manifest digest (`fc8fe753272bdd2b66e17e84f6f910b1aa4230b4f9284f022e09eff0df0afd7c`), payload `SUPPLEMENTARY_VALIDATION.json` digest (`aec9651dac09d38867201d0c37163fb25213222f912114bfbda49f50e096ce36`), and binding to v17. Its three specified tasks passed the recorded base-failure/reference-pass checks.\n- A separate harmless synthetic canary reproduction against the pre-PR-#10 `runIsolated()` boundary confirmed a material hidden-oracle integrity defect at `e1759ca`: candidate-like code executed by a checker could read and overwrite a hidden file copied into the same writable `/workspace`; its canary appeared in captured output and would be persisted in `hidden.log`. No host escape was demonstrated, and no held-out payload or model candidate was used in that reproduction. (Subsequently remediated at the source level by `blackbox-v1` oracle separation in PR #10 `2c70d39`, workspace history isolation in PR #18 `96aeef2`, and kernel resource isolation in PR #19 `91406bd`.)\n\n## Historical evidence: Security and T2 update (2026-10-17)\n\n- PR [#10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/10), initial commit `aa2cd6228303b850f1406de94c5c9ee044ff9bf5` (merged at `2c70d39`), added the `blackbox-v1` oracle boundary and regression coverage.\n- The earlier corpus author supplied pilot overlay v18 at `/tmp/nexus-v1-heldout-author/DEC-05-v1-blackbox-dev-v18` (`SHA256SUMS.json` digest `e830c82c60a7767d4d235cc53764d8298abadc2d22107a5e6ee7ed3664509dd4`), with seven fixture tasks migrated and 33 unmigrated. That overlay remains unsealed historical pilot material and is superseded by the sealed 40-task external-repository corpus `heldout-v2` (`eval/heldout-manifest.json`, PR #16).\n- On historical integration `e1759ca`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs` reported 121 rows (106 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), and `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` reported all versioned components at `0.1.0-alpha.2`.\n\n## Historical evidence: Earlier state checkpoint (2026-10-17 02:51 UTC)\n\n- At 02:51 UTC on 2026-10-17, `v1/integration` was at `8c9994596144c5674d9be8e011ad1feb4109ffb4` and `v1/candidate-1` was at `6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a`.\n- A confirmed CI dependency defect was fixed at `642ba37`: the contest-contract job builds the CLI after installing dependencies and before running demo tests, because `cli/dist` is generated and untracked. The prior run at `10fe416` failed when `demo/lib/real-agent-runner.mjs` could not import `cli/dist/client.js`; that failure remains historical evidence.\n- `rust-toolchain.toml` is tracked and pins Rust `1.95.0` with `rustfmt` and `clippy`.\n- `REQ-DX-106` is satisfied on the integration branch: GitHub milestone [v1.0.0](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/milestone/1) has seven open plan-group issues ([#1–#7](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1)).\n- The earlier v12 (`82886448799cb9c63d28a8f5f28b940229b981a51982c49bad80b7f7d2c73092`), v15 (`6f78983cc860a4ed616f5aa5375b8d3fec5b7335ea6bac47a448924dc91af06d`), and v16 T2 pilot packages and their failed Docker validation attempts remain historical evidence only.\n\n## Historical evidence at `6151a23`\n\n- At that historical inspection, `v1/integration` and `v1/candidate-1` identified the same commit (`6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a`).\n- `make build` completed successfully in an isolated candidate worktree. The produced TUI and CLI entrypoint hashes were respectively `ca20da9214db8dcb130cfa35f25f2e76f9caad63dcf3dfbefe49132fcaa9e52f` and `8da0ccf909d5432de22d62459168f21a22b4360607cbf47259338cc144758f42`.\n- After the build, isolated `make test` passed: Rust 281/281; CLI 1087/1087 across 193 suites; zero failures and zero skipped. Runtime was Node 24.11.1. `scripts/security_gates.sh` passed its npm audit (zero high/critical), Rust advisory/license, credential-scan, diff-hygiene and documentation checks. Output is retained outside the repository at `/tmp/nexus-v1-make-test-built-6151.log` (SHA-256 `b72e0e15819985fc48f39998d2adc5ce90e9dd125519784c25a2a2b4d2db9521`).\n- The earlier unbuilt `make test` failed (Rust 281 passed; CLI 1060/1087 passed, 27 failed, zero skipped) because required generated build outputs were absent. It is preserved at `/tmp/nexus-v1-make-test-6151.log` (SHA-256 `7c4a364daedc3b26bd6b0392f6e0466c581c33ae5ef9d04c11348129e0abbb31`) and is superseded only for the source-suite result by the correctly ordered build-then-test run.\n- Automated PTY acceptance tests are included in the passing CLI suite. This is not human interaction in each required terminal emulator.\n- The source suite includes the T1 evaluator smoke and two-fault T4 smoke. These do not establish the full T2, T3, T4 qualification thresholds.\n\n## Requirements below their required gate (reconciled at `a7126aa`)\n\n| ID | Current state | Remaining behavior or evidence | Dependency | Owner role | Exact next action |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `REQ-AGT-002` | partial | Zero false `VERIFIED` across the frozen qualification workloads; source regression tests pass (`1,152/1,152` at `a7126aa`) but no held-out evaluation exists. | T2/T3/T4 RC runs | Qualification operator | Run the preregistered acceptance set on an installed RC and retain per-run evidence; fix and repeat any false `VERIFIED`. |\n| `REQ-AGT-004` | tested (depth 0; work-unit mechanism landed in PR-4b) | `AGT-02a` archive→task→session commit ordering is applied to durable work units by PR-4b (`agent.ts:3339-3402`, `operation_runner.ts:566`, `durable_continuity.test.ts:359`, `dispositions.md` M2); work-unit pressure-forced compaction + SIGKILL crash-boundary test is in flight under `PLAN-04 PR-4g`, and live long-task `ACC-CONT-10` remains pending RC qualification. | `PLAN-04 PR-4g` (`ACC-CONT-03` SIGKILL), `ACC-CONT-10` on installed RC | Continuity implementer, independent reviewer, and qualification operator | Land and independently review `PLAN-04 PR-4g` (M1/M3/L5), then execute `ACC-CONT-10` on the installed RC during M5. |\n| `REQ-AGT-010` | partial (RR; v1 subset independently accepted at `f68b5bc`) | `ACC-TRUST-04` v1 subset (workspace skills/knowledge trust gating and source/trust annotations in `workspace_trust.test.ts`, 5/5 pass) is source-tested and independently accepted (PR #17 `f68b5bc`); `DEC-04` defers the full `CTX-001` provenance graph and `CTX-002` to post-v1. | Installed-RC verification; post-v1 deferral recorded | Requirement owner | Preserve the `DEC-04` v1 subset / post-v1 boundary in release notes and verify no regression on the installed RC. |\n| `REQ-AGT-111` | open (post-v1 shared-loop refactor; v1 behavior still required) | `PLAN-04` defers the full shared step implementation, while v1 requires documented main/subagent divergences and `measureAdmission` in the subagent loop. Calls exist in both loops, and divergence documentation is tracked under `PLAN-04`. | `PLAN-04` task 6 and source evidence | Continuity implementer, then requirement owner | Verify both `measureAdmission` calls satisfy strict-counting behavior and ensure main/subagent divergence documentation is reconciled in the ledger. |\n| `REQ-PRV-003` | implemented | Standalone behavior has scripted tests but no qualifying live standalone evidence (HIST-08). | Installed RC; standalone matrix | Provider qualification operator | Run `ACCEPTANCE.md` §4 for supported server profiles and archive sanitized receipts. |\n| `REQ-REL-005` | partial (RR) | Candidate source security gates passed on `a7126aa` (run `39108774170`); exact-RC artifact/security evidence is pending RC tag construction. `security_gates.sh` requires `cargo-deny` or `cargo-audit` and fails closed when neither is installed (`ACC-SUP-04`). | Exact RC and `ACC-SUP-05` release CI matrix | Release engineering | On the frozen RC tag, run and archive the release workflow security evidence. |\n| `REQ-REL-106` | open (post-v1; manual path defined for v1) | `SPEC-06` marks self-uninstall/prune post-v1 and retains the quickstart manual uninstall as the v1 path. The ledger's open status is a roadmap deferral, not a v1 implementation blocker. | Post-v1 scope; release documentation | Release/documentation owner | Preserve the documented manual uninstall path for v1 and record this item as explicitly deferred in the final release ledger. |\n| `REQ-AGT-118` | tested (source level; `DEC-17` exceptions preserved) | Conflict resolved by `DEC-17` (PR #11 `f771a3c`): the `≥ 1` token-per-CJK/Hangul-character admission-safety floor takes precedence over the `≤ 1.5×` band, which applies to corpora not dominated by the floor; Chinese (`2.00×`) and Hangul (`1.67×`) floor exceptions remain recorded. Source tests (`tokens.test.ts` 3/3) and independent review records (PRs #12, #14, #15) are integrated. | Installed-RC qualification | Qualification operator | Retain the `DEC-17` exception record; source-level `tested` status does not substitute for installed-RC product qualification. |\n| `REQ-AGT-110` | open | Independent continuity/compaction/truncation acceptance under `ACCEPTANCE.md` §8, including an independent long task with two compactions and kill/resume. | Installed RC and reviewer who did not implement the work | Owner-supplied independent reviewer | After RC freeze, execute the reviewer procedure and archive a per-area verdict; this cannot be self-signed. |\n| `REQ-PER-107` | implemented (post-v1 optional item) | `SPEC-08` marks parent-directory fsync post-v1 and optional. Source evidence exists; this is not a v1 gate under the accepted spec. | Post-v1 scope | Persistence implementer and requirement owner | Keep recorded as optional post-v1 scope. |\n| `REQ-PRV-111` | partial | RC-pinned live provider verification is incomplete. Historical OpenRouter/ChatGPT evidence is not RC evidence; OpenRouter must use a pinned model. OpenAI API-key and Anthropic paths have no configured authorization. | Installed RC; available provider authorization | Provider qualification operator | On the RC, run `providers verify` for OpenRouter with a pinned model and complete one live small §6-style bug-fix task with a correct outcome. Repeat ChatGPT sign-in verification and retain PASS on the RC; keep ChatGPT, OpenAI API-key, and Anthropic experimental unless separately verified. |\n| `REQ-REL-114` | open (workflow enforced at `86bdbe6`; RC run pending) | `.github/workflows/repro.yml` and `scripts/repro-identity.mjs` (PR #20 `86bdbe6`) enforce fail-closed tag/commit/clean-tree/toolchain/artifact identity across Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 builders, covered by `repro_identity.test.ts`. Live execution on an actual RC tag remains pending RC construction. | Final RC tag and `.github/workflows/repro.yml` run | Release engineering | Dispatch `repro.yml` against the exact `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag/commit and archive both runner manifests and comparison evidence. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-101` | tested (corpus sealed at `f776903`; live T2 run pending) | The 40-task external-repository T2 corpus (`heldout-v2`) is sealed and committed in `eval/heldout-manifest.json` (SHA-256 `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`, PR #16 `f776903`, custody record `ce3f590`). Independent metadata review (`codex-lead`) accepted the public manifest structure/digest; private payload validation (40/40, 2 rounds each) and author-isolation audits are custodian-recorded with store permissions `0700`/`0500`. | Qualification-host provisioning, frozen resource config, installed RC, peer calibration | Custodian and qualification operator | Keep `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2` restricted from implementation agents; complete qualification-host provisioning and execute the 5-run T2 matrix on the installed RC. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-107` | open | No accepted live standalone/proxy matrix or RC-pinned provider verification. | RC, qualifying held-out subset, provider access, serial gateway window | Qualification operator | Execute `ACCEPTANCE.md` §4 through the approved stripped proxy and collect E5 provider verification receipts on the installed RC. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-102` | tested as harness control | Missing fingerprint and mismatched comparison settings are rejected by tests; no live matched model/configuration record exists. | Frozen RC, identified model/server, task corpus | Qualification operator | Before each comparison, record and verify exact RC, weights hash, server build, sampling, context/output limits, allowlisted environment and equal task budgets in every run manifest. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-103` | tested as harness control | Five-run pair validation and peer configuration forwarding are tested; no live matched T2 results exist. | Sealed T2 set, RC, peers on same model | Qualification operator | Run five serial repetitions for each task/configuration for Nexus, Goose and OpenCode; retain original and replacement records and paired score inputs. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-104` | tested as scorer control | The separate metrics and scorer are tested; threshold outcomes and zero-false-`VERIFIED` have not been measured on qualification workloads. | Completed T2/T3/T4 evidence | Qualification operator | Score every preregistered metric separately and apply the fixed thresholds and confidence intervals; any false `VERIFIED` fails the hard gate. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-105` | tested as injector/smoke (`DEC-05` 9-class count resolved) | `DEC-05` amendment (`f771a3c`) and `ACCEPTANCE.md` §6.2 (`77102c5`) resolve the scenario count to **9 fault classes × 5 runs** (retaining SIGTERM + `run --resume`). Injector and two-fault smoke pass in CI; full 9×5 RC evidence is pending M5 execution. | Installed RC and gateway window | Qualification operator | Execute and score all 9 fault classes × 5 runs against the installed RC. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-106` | tested as harness/isolation controls (live M5 audit pending) | `blackbox-v1` oracle separation (`2c70d39`, PR #10), ancestor-only repository workspace staging (`96aeef2`, PR #18), and delegated cgroup v2 CPU/memory/pids/tmpfs-storage enforcement with `cgroup.kill` cleanup (`91406bd`, PR #19) are integrated, independently reviewed, and CI-tested (`1,152/1,152`). Live qualification-host provisioning and full-run inclusion/exclusion audit remain pending M5 execution. | Qualification-host provisioning (`nexus-eval` user, dedicated tmpfs mount, frozen `config.resources`), installed RC, completed M5 | Evaluator/host operator and independent reviewer | Provision the qualification host and freeze `config.resources`; run M5 with unreadable hidden tests and enforced cgroup/tmpfs bounds; archive every inclusion, exclusion, and replacement reason for independent review. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-108` | partial | Automated PTY suite passes on `a7126aa`; the human matrix is absent for xterm, kitty (keyboard protocol enabled), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60. | Human terminal access and RC install | Human acceptance operator | Execute the `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3 manual matrix on the installed RC across all required terminal×size cells and archive screenshots and verdicts. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-109` | open | No T3 evidence for 8 tasks × 5 runs, each ≥60 steps with ≥2 compactions and steering; thresholds are false-absence 0 and steering ≥95%. | Frozen T3 workload, RC, gateway capacity | Qualification operator | Freeze/register T3 tasks before execution, then run all repetitions and score using the accepted rules. |\n\nAt `a7126aa`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs` passes in report mode: **121 rows; 107 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open**. In `--enforce` mode (the G6 release gate), the checker remains fail-closed until the remaining blocker and release-required rows above reach their required post-qualification states.\n\n## Gate reconciliation (at `a7126aa`)\n\n| Gate | Evidence at `a7126aa` | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| G0 clean-clone/isolation | CI run `39108774170` passed across Node 20/22/24 and Ubuntu 22.04 with isolated HOME/cgroups/bubblewrap. | Source gate green on `v1/integration`; repeat on exact pre-tag commit on `main`. |\n| G1 safety | Full source suite (`1,152/1,152` CLI, `281/281` Rust, 0 skipped) and `scripts/security_gates.sh` pass in CI run `39108774170`. | Source gate green; artifact-bound checks run at Stage 3 after RC construction. |\n| G2 package | `linux-x86_64` job in run `39108774170` passed double-build byte comparison, CycloneDX SBOM validation, `smoke-package.sh`, and `installer-smoke.sh`; `repro.yml` (`86bdbe6`) and draft-then-publish `release.yml` (`a7126aa`) are integrated. | Source/CI packaging green; Stage 2/3 workflow-built RC archive and cross-runner `repro.yml` dispatch pending RC tag. |\n| G3 continuity/inference/verification/eval | Source suite, T1 self-test, T4 smoke, `blackbox-v1` oracle isolation, repo history isolation, cgroup v2 resource contract, and sealed 40-task T2 manifest (`50895b84…`) are integrated. `PLAN-04 PR-4g` (continuity M1/M3/L5) and qualification-host provisioning (`PLAN-10 QUAL-HOST` / `PR-10j`) are in flight. | Partial; live T2/T3/full T4 and standalone/provider matrices pending Stage 4 installed-RC execution. |\n| G4 persistence | Source persistence and retention tests pass in CI (`39108774170`). | Source gate green; independent RC acceptance (§8) pending Stage 4. |\n\n## Release and qualification sequence (`ACCEPTANCE.md` §1.1)\n\n1. **Close remaining source & host prerequisites on `v1/integration`:** Land and independently review `PLAN-04 PR-4g` (Continuity M1/M3/L5), `PLAN-10 PR-10j` (dedicated-tmpfs storage preflight & canary), and `PLAN-10 QUAL-HOST` (qualification-host provisioning bundle and frozen resource profile); update the stale `ACCEPTANCE.md` §1.1 sentence now that PR #21 (`a7126aa`) implements draft-then-publish for stable tags.\n2. **Stage 1 — Pre-RC source gates & integration to `main`:** Merge `v1/integration` to `main` (PR #8) once all pre-RC source checks pass, synchronize version metadata to `1.0.0-rc.1` (`scripts/sync-version.mjs`), add `docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.1.md`, and verify green source CI on `main`.\n3. **Stage 2 — RC artifact construction:** Tag `v1.0.0-rc.1` on the verified `main` commit and build/publish the prerelease RC candidate via `.github/workflows/release.yml`, recording the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance attestation.\n4. **Stage 3 — RC artifact gates:** Run `ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08` and dispatch `.github/workflows/repro.yml` (`REQ-REL-114`) against the exact `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag and commit.\n5. **Stage 4 — Installed-RC qualification:** Install the workflow-produced `v1.0.0-rc.1` package via the documented installer and execute `ACCEPTANCE.md` §§4–8 (standalone/provider matrix, CI/scripted/manual terminal matrix, T2 40×5 held-out comparison, T4 9×5 fault matrix, T3 8×5 long-task matrix, install matrix, SPEC-09 §3.2 docs checklist, and §8 independent acceptance). Archive all evidence under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/v1.0.0-rc.1/`.\n6. **Stage 5 — G6 decision, version-only stable promotion, draft verification, and publication:** After G6 passes on the accepted RC, create the version-only `v1.0.0` commit directly on the accepted RC commit (enforced by `scripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs` in `release.yml`), run source CI, tag `v1.0.0` to build the unpublished draft release, complete Stage 5 stable artifact/install/attestation checks, record the signed G6 and Stage 5 disposition, and publish the draft release (`gh release edit v1.0.0 --draft=false`).\n3:This is the procedure that decides whether a release candidate (RC) may become v1.0.0. It defines:\n15:| **Product qualification** | Did the RC meet these gates on real workflows? |\n18:A gate passes only on archived evidence bound to the source commit or installed RC artifact that the gate evaluates. Source-level evidence names the exact source commit; installed-RC evidence names both that commit and the installed package digest. A green test suite alone never qualifies the product.\n24:1. **Pre-RC source gates.** Before creating an RC tag, run required source CI and every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method evaluates source, a source-built test binary, or an environment without requiring a published RC. Record the full commit ID and check results. Source checks do not establish behavior of the installed package.\n25:2. **RC artifact construction.** After the required owner authorization, create the version-matched RC tag on that exact source commit and use the repository release workflow to build and publish the RC artifacts. Record the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance. The workflow-produced artifacts are the candidates for qualification; a local build or a different commit is not interchangeable. RC artifact publication is not product qualification or final release acceptance.\n26:3. **RC artifact gates.** Before installed-RC product qualification, run every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method requires the RC archive, RC attestation/release, or workflow-produced artifact. This includes ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08. ACC-PKG checks that explicitly require an installed package run against this RC as specified by their test method. Record the RC tag commit, workflow run, artifact digests, and each check result. A source-level analogue does not replace an artifact-bound check.\n27:4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\n28:5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\n30:The final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\n32:Exact-RC requirements records identify at least one implementer and an independent reviewer. For a blocking requirement recorded as `tested` instead of `product-qualified`, the cited decision must be explicitly allowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\n34:The post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. At G6, the exact-RC invocation must provide a record meeting the normal B/RR status threshold and digest-bound evidence for every criterion in this table. The table also supplies the criterion mapping for rows whose ledger points to an ACCEPTANCE section instead of naming ACC IDs. The source ledger is never rewritten by the record. Any below-tested required row omitted from this table still fails.\n36:<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:START -->\n37:### Qualification-only requirements for exact-RC enforcement\n39:| Requirement | Acceptance criteria required in the exact-RC record | Remaining stage |\n41:| REQ-REL-003 | ACC-PLAT | Installed-RC platform and Node-version matrix |\n42:| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\n44:| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\n45:| REQ-REL-005 | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | Exact-RC security and dependency artifact checks |\n46:| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\n47:| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\n48:| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\n49:| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n50:| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n51:| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\n52:| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n53:<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\n55:<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\n56:### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\n60:<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:END -->\n64:1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\n65:2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n81:| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n82:| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n83:| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n87:Every ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\n97:| Supply chain | ACC-SUP-01 to ACC-SUP-08 (artifact-bound ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08 after RC construction) | SPEC-07 |\n114:| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\n115:| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\n119:| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n120:| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n121:| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\n123:## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n128:2. Install the RC with the documented command.\n135:4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\n142:| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\n154:| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\n155:| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\n176:### 5.2 Scripted PTY scenarios against the installed RC (E3, mock gateway)\n190:### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\n192:Terminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\n194:For each terminal × size, check:\n201:6. Ctrl-C twice (clean terminal restore: echo on, no stray escape codes).\n204:Record PASS/FAIL per cell, with a screenshot of the approval panel and the post-exit terminal state.\n212:### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\n214:- 40 sealed tasks. The manifest is committed before RC1, and authorship is recorded (agent-authored, DEC-05).\n215:- 5 runs × {Nexus RC, Goose, OpenCode}.\n216:- Before execution, freeze three qualification configs at `eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json`, `eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json`, and `eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json`. Each must set `qualification: true`, identify the same model fingerprint and sampling settings, and record equal context/output and task budgets; the Nexus config must identify the installed RC and its package digest. Do not derive these files from the pilot configs by silently inheriting or changing settings.\n217:- Set `T2_TASKS` to the custodian-approved, sealed task directory and `T2_OUT` to a new, empty, run-specific output directory. Do not use the disclosed `eval/tasks` development set as held-out evidence. Preserve all three outputs and their manifests; never reuse an output directory for a retry.\n231:  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\n233:### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\n235:9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\n255:| False VERIFIED (T2 + T3 + T4) | **= 0** |\n260:| T4 truthful outcome | = 100% |\n261:| T4 hang beyond budget + 5 min | = 0 |\n273:| Fresh install, each image with Node ≥ 22 | Documented one-line command with `NEXUS_VERSION=<rc>`, then the no-version command after v1.0.0 is published | Installed. `nexus --version` equals the RC. `nexus doctor` shows no version warning and an empty stderr. |\n275:| Upgrade alpha.2 → RC | Same, with the tag | Symlink swapped. Old version retained. User state intact. |\n276:| Rollback RC → alpha.2 | Same, with the old tag | Works. |\n292:- the RC package;\n308:   - 2 T4 classes.\n309:2. One live long task (≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions) on the RC through the gateway, including one kill and resume.\n329:G6 passes only when every item below holds. It authorizes a version-only stable commit from the accepted RC source, followed by its source checks, stable tag, and unpublished draft candidate; it does not authorize making stable assets publicly available. RC tags are candidate construction inputs governed by §1.1; an RC tag or its successful build does not satisfy this release decision.\n331:- [ ] G0–G4 automated gates pass on the final RC commit (§3).\n332:- [ ] RC artifact gates pass on the workflow-produced RC, including ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08; record the exact source commit, workflow run, and artifact digest.\n333:- [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\n334:- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: CI, scripted and manual gates PASS.\n338:- [ ] The pre-RC source gate passes from a clean source worktree: `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`. Every B/RR source row outside the §1.1 qualification-only map must be ≥ `tested`. A mapped row below `tested` is reported as deferred; this result does not accept or qualify it.\n339:- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\n341:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\n343:- [ ] Release notes state the standalone scope (DEC-16), the provider tiers (DEC-06), the experimental surfaces (DEC-03, DEC-07) and the known limitations.\nv1.0.0-rc.4\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.4\t2026-10-24T11:54:37Z\nv1.0.0-rc.3\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.3\t2026-10-23T09:06:11Z\nv1.0.0-rc.1\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.1\t2026-10-21T18:54:41Z\nv0.1.0-alpha.2\tPre-release\tv0.1.0-alpha.2\t2026-10-14T09:10:47Z\nv0.1.0-alpha.1\tPre-release\tv0.1.0-alpha.1\t2026-10-13T20:11:01Z\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":436420796}},"started_at_ms":1792897297264,"completed_at_ms":1792897297702}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T03:01:38.800Z","ordinal":321798,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17101-b170-7500-9005-f2cabf7bbc30","call_id":"call_4e767ab1c3c74900ad9547147415340d","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.8 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 12628)\nTotal output lines: 204\n\n- **Continuity PR #25:** Latest head is `db44e0b`; exact CI run [39119984308](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39119984308) is running. Previous exact head `8907703` failed Node 20/22/24 matrices (run `39118809319`); Node 24 reported 9 behavioral failures among 1,157 tests, including convergence recovery and tester-verifier completion cases. The owner has been given the exact failures; no merge is authorized until the latest head is green and independently reviewed.\n- **T3 and terminal lanes:** PR #27 T3 harness head `12edf74` has independent code review ACCEPT. Its CI run [39119197191](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39119197191) has the contest-contract and Node 20/22/24 jobs successful; `linux-x86_64` remains in progress. The custodian recorded an 8/8-task T3 corpus seal at 10:43:02 UTC, with corrected private manifest digest `dcbd794ed2998423787fdead4957b38b0c4a8a641855d87304d065d01c3fae37` at 10:43:22 UTC, and released both authoring claims. This is sealed, custodian-validated corpus evidence; no T3 qualification run has occurred. PR #24's real-terminal procedure is integrated, but all required five environments × three sizes still require the exact installed RC and genuine operator evidence; no matrix cell is claimed complete.\n- **RC and publication:** Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`; PR #8 remains a draft integration-to-main candidate. No RC artifact, exact-RC test, cross-runner RC comparison, installed provider/standalone run, T2/T3/T4 qualification, or independent RC acceptance exists. Final stable publication remains authorized but gated on all mandatory exact-RC acceptance and release checks.\n\n## Superseded checkpoint (2026-10-18, `a7126aa`)\n\n- **Authoritative integration revision and CI:** `origin/v1/integration` is at `a7126aa811044b45357440b5aee9228500a480a8` (draft PR [#8](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/8) targeting `main`). GitHub Actions CI run [39108774170](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39108774170) on `a7126aa` completed with **success** across all five jobs (`cloudflare-contest-contract`, `test-matrix (20)`, `test-matrix (22)`, `test-matrix (24)`, and `linux-x86_64`: Rust 281/281, CLI 1,152/1,152 with 0 skipped, security gates, deterministic double-build packaging, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke). Source CI is green; installed-RC product qualification has not yet executed.\n- **Sealed held-out T2 corpus (`heldout-v2`, PR [#16](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/16), merged at `f776903`):**\n  - Committed public manifest: `eval/heldout-manifest.json` (SHA-256 `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`), containing 40 external-repository T2 tasks pinned to full 40-hex baseline commits across Go (10), JavaScript (10), Python (10), and Rust (10), and across bugfix (10), debug (10), feature (10), and refactor (10).\n  - Custody record: `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md` (updated at `ce3f590`).\n  - **Distinction of evidence:** Independent public metadata review (`codex-lead`) verified and accepted the committed manifest digest (`50895b84…`), 40 unique task IDs, 10×4 class/language balance, 40 full pinned commits, and schema/digest fields without inspecting private payloads. Private payload validation (2 rounds per task in bounded `SUITE` windows: fresh clone → checkout → setup → pre-patch regression pass → pre-patch hidden fail → reference patch apply → post-patch hidden pass → post-patch regression pass), rejection/quarantine of one provenance-contaminated batch (`author-b9` at `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2-quarantine/b9-contaminated-2026-10-18T0235Z/`), per-session exec-log audits for clean replacement authors (`author-b8c`, `author-b9c`), and store access tightening (`/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2` mode `0700`, `tasks/` and `reference/` mode `0500` read-only) are custodian-attested in `custody-report-2026-10-18.md`. Earlier author-exposed packages (`v12`, `v15`, `v16`, `v17`, `v18`) recorded in historical sections below are superseded development/pilot artifacts and are never used for held-out qualification.\n- **Evaluator isolation and kernel resource contract (PRs [#10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/10), [#18](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/18), [#19](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/19)):**\n  - `blackbox-v1` oracle separation (`2c70d39`, PR #10) runs private oracle checks outside the candidate workspace while mounting the candidate workspace read-only (`--ro-bind`), superseding the historical shared-workspace oracle exposure noted in the 2026-10-17 review below.\n  - Repository workspace history isolation (`96aeef2`, PR #18, `eval/workspace.mjs`) stages external-repo tasks via `git init` + ancestor-only fetch (`--no-tags`, `--no-write-fetch-head`) without `--shared`, `objects/info/alternates`, remotes, tags, or post-baseline commits, preventing candidates from reading upstream fix commits in git history.\n  - Kernel-enforced resource contract (`91406bd`, PR #19, `eval/resources.mjs`, `eval/cgroup_supervisor.mjs`, `scripts/ensure-ci-user-cgroups.sh`) executes each task phase (setup, candidate sandbox, hidden/regression, oracle) inside a transient delegated `systemd --user` scope with verified cgroup v2 `CPUQuota`, `MemoryMax`, `MemorySwapMax=0`, `TasksMax`, `memory.oom.group=1`, dedicated size-capped tmpfs `workspaceRoot` storage enforcement, and `cgroup.kill` process-tree cleanup verified to `populated == 0`. These controls are source-implemented, independently reviewed, and CI-tested (`1,152/1,152` on `0cee0b7`, run `39104943950`), not live qualification results. Qualification-host provisioning (`nexus-eval` account, narrow sudoers rule, dedicated tmpfs mount, and frozen `config.resources` profile) remains a prerequisite before running held-out T2/T3/T4 workloads.\n- **Governance, tokenizer, and acceptance lifecycle reconciliations (PRs [#11](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/11)–[#15](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/15), [#17](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/17)):**\n  - `DEC-05` amendment (`f771a3c`, PR #11) and `ACCEPTANCE.md` §6.2 (`77102c5`, PR #13) resolve the historical eight-vs-nine T4 denominator conflict by retaining all **9 fault classes × 5 runs** (including SIGTERM + `run --resume`).\n  - `DEC-17` (`f771a3c`, PR #11), `REQ-AGT-118` reconciliation (`d2c4bfc`, PR #12), and published independent review records (`19dedc6`, PR #14; `f8e19e4`, PR #15; `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-11_PR-11d_REVIEW_AGT-118/`) resolve the CJK/Hangul admission-safety floor vs `≤ 1.5×` accuracy band conflict: the `≥ 1` token/character safety floor takes precedence, `≤ 1.5×` applies to corpora not dominated by the floor, and recorded Chinese (`2.00×`) and Hangul (`1.67×`) exceptions remain preserved. `REQ-AGT-118` is `tested` at the source level (…9128 tokens truncated… (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\n176:### 5.2 Scripted PTY scenarios against the installed RC (E3, mock gateway)\n190:### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\n192:Terminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\n194:For each terminal × size, check:\n201:6. Ctrl-C twice (clean terminal restore: echo on, no stray escape codes).\n204:Record PASS/FAIL per cell, with a screenshot of the approval panel and the post-exit terminal state.\n212:### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\n214:- 40 sealed tasks. The manifest is committed before RC1, and authorship is recorded (agent-authored, DEC-05).\n215:- 5 runs × {Nexus RC, Goose, OpenCode}.\n216:- Before execution, freeze three qualification configs at `eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json`, `eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json`, and `eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json`. Each must set `qualification: true`, identify the same model fingerprint and sampling settings, and record equal context/output and task budgets; the Nexus config must identify the installed RC and its package digest. Do not derive these files from the pilot configs by silently inheriting or changing settings.\n217:- Set `T2_TASKS` to the custodian-approved, sealed task directory and `T2_OUT` to a new, empty, run-specific output directory. Do not use the disclosed `eval/tasks` development set as held-out evidence. Preserve all three outputs and their manifests; never reuse an output directory for a retry.\n231:  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\n233:### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\n235:9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\n255:| False VERIFIED (T2 + T3 + T4) | **= 0** |\n260:| T4 truthful outcome | = 100% |\n261:| T4 hang beyond budget + 5 min | = 0 |\n273:| Fresh install, each image with Node ≥ 22 | Documented one-line command with `NEXUS_VERSION=<rc>`, then the no-version command after v1.0.0 is published | Installed. `nexus --version` equals the RC. `nexus doctor` shows no version warning and an empty stderr. |\n275:| Upgrade alpha.2 → RC | Same, with the tag | Symlink swapped. Old version retained. User state intact. |\n276:| Rollback RC → alpha.2 | Same, with the old tag | Works. |\n292:- the RC package;\n308:   - 2 T4 classes.\n309:2. One live long task (≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions) on the RC through the gateway, including one kill and resume.\n329:G6 passes only when every item below holds. It authorizes a version-only stable commit from the accepted RC source, followed by its source checks, stable tag, and unpublished draft candidate; it does not authorize making stable assets publicly available. RC tags are candidate construction inputs governed by §1.1; an RC tag or its successful build does not satisfy this release decision.\n331:- [ ] G0–G4 automated gates pass on the final RC commit (§3).\n332:- [ ] RC artifact gates pass on the workflow-produced RC, including ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08; record the exact source commit, workflow run, and artifact digest.\n333:- [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\n334:- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: CI, scripted and manual gates PASS.\n338:- [ ] The pre-RC source gate passes from a clean source worktree: `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`. Every B/RR source row outside the §1.1 qualification-only map must be ≥ `tested`. A mapped row below `tested` is reported as deferred; this result does not accept or qualify it.\n339:- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\n341:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\n343:- [ ] Release notes state the standalone scope (DEC-16), the provider tiers (DEC-06), the experimental surfaces (DEC-03, DEC-07) and the known limitations.\nv1.0.0-rc.4\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.4\t2026-10-24T11:54:37Z\nv1.0.0-rc.3\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.3\t2026-10-23T09:06:11Z\nv1.0.0-rc.1\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.1\t2026-10-21T18:54:41Z\nv0.1.0-alpha.2\tPre-release\tv0.1.0-alpha.2\t2026-10-14T09:10:47Z\nv0.1.0-alpha.1\tPre-release\tv0.1.0-alpha.1\t2026-10-13T20:11:01Z\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a170f2-3e90-7ad2-8d66-c8179982613b","create_time":1792897298.8002145}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
