in` and run exact-head CI then.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T02:50:05Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"**Independent review (claude-code) at exact head `94ad942bd492ee6586bf73a595bbb642f8f73757` (base `19b30a4`): ACCEPT, with two non-blocking follow-ups.**\\n\\nThe fix is correct:\\n- `gh` is no longer resolved from PATH, so a shim that exits 0 can't produce `attestationVerified = true`.\\n- With `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1` and no trusted `gh`, the upgrade fails **before** any download or journal staging. The in-flow branch also fails closed, which covers a trusted path that disappears mid-run.\\n- Both the archive and the `SHA256SUMS` attestation must pass.\\n\\nFollow-ups:\\n1. **Silent downgrade in `auto` mode.** Only `/usr/bin/gh` and `/usr/local/bin/gh` are trusted. Users whose `gh` lives at `/snap/bin/gh`, `/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin/gh` or `~/.local/bin/gh` used to get verification through PATH and now get none. `attestationVerified` stays `undefined`, and nothing in `cli/src` outside `upgrade.ts` reads it, so the user isn't told. Suggest an `onProgress`/notice line such as \\\"provenance attestation not checked: no trusted gh found (set NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1 to require it)\\\". Consider adding `/snap/bin/gh` (root-owned) to the default list.\\n2. **Environment hardening.** `spawnSync(trustedGh, …)` inherits the caller's environment, so `GH_HOST` and similar variables can point `gh` at a different API host. Sigstore signature and identity checks should still reject forged bundles, but passing an explicit minimal env (or deleting `GH_HOST`/`GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN`) would keep the verification target fixed to github.com.\\n\\nThis is user-visible (upgrade behaviour with `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1`), so it needs an rc.5 notes bullet if it merges before the tag.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T02:51:26Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"PR #209 is now merged as `4e7297f545538e6422ca3890334a7036f58287ca`. The exact PR #209 workflow compl