{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T03:42:53.825Z","ordinal":322564,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a170f2-3e90-7ad2-8d66-c8179982613b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-402a0a67-a463-43e2-a960-1f651fc9ad9d","process_id":"1160","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","cat /home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-latest-resume-corruption/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/defect-latest-resume-corruption/README.md && git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-latest-resume-corruption diff --stat origin/main..HEAD && git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-latest-resume-corruption show --format= --name-only 0123a15"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"cat /home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-latest-resume-corruption/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/defect-latest-resume-corruption/README.md && git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-latest-resume-corruption diff --stat origin/main..HEAD && git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-latest-resume-corruption show --format= --name-only 0123a15"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# Corrupt latest-task resume fallback\n\n## Scope and identity\n\n- Source base: `4adc61ac98616c5e1dccaf6065e7f2332443d468`.\n- Reviewed source commit: `0123a15` (`fix(state): report corrupt task records when listing`).\n- Branch: `v1/defect-latest-resume-corruption`.\n\n## Defect and fix\n\nA safe fixture with a valid older task and malformed newer task showed `listTasks` returning only the older record. Both bare-latest resume paths select the first listed task, so this silent skip could resume the wrong older task or falsely report that no task exists.\n\n`listTasks` now quarantines malformed JSON and throws `CorruptStateError`, rejects non-object records through the same typed path, and propagates other I/O errors unchanged. The original corrupt bytes are preserved by rename. A subsequent listing can succeed explicitly after quarantine rather than silently hiding the failure. This implements the corruption reporting and quarantine requirements in REQ-PER-104 without changing either resume entry point.\n\n## Validation\n\nAll commands used isolated `HOME` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` directories; no live inference or credentials were used.\n\n- Direct reproduction before the fix: listing returned only `older`, with `newestCorruptRecordSkipped: true`.\n- Regression before the fix: expected `CorruptStateError` was not thrown.\n- `node scripts/run_tests.mjs test/state.test.ts test/durable_continuity.test.ts test/state_migration.test.ts` passed 59/59 after building the required Rust engine and CLI. An initial run without the fresh worktree's engine produced 12 setup failures and was not counted as a product result.\n- `make build` / CLI build and `tsc --noEmit` passed.\n- `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 exact-RC qualification deferrals. This is a source gate, not installed-RC qualification.\n- Full snapshot `make test` on `27415c8`: **failed**, with 1,660/1,663 passing. Failures were the already-fixed evaluator resource-order fixture (fixed separately at `36b702f`), the CI-only capped-storage prerequisite, and the intermittent upgrade download failure. The corrupt-resume focused regression remains passing; this is not a green full-suite result.\n\n## Independent review and integration\n\nAn independent reviewer returned **ACCEPT** for exact source commit `0123a15`, confirming typed corruption reporting, byte-preserving quarantine, unchanged non-parse error handling, and coverage of both bare-latest callers through their shared `listTasks` path. Review was read-only and did not rerun tests.\n\nNo push, pull-request integration, release qualification, or installed-candidate acceptance is claimed.\n .github/workflows/repro.yml                        |  18 +-\n cli/src/agent.ts                                   |  16 +-\n cli/src/config.ts                                  |   7 +-\n cli/src/core/approval_policy.ts                    |  21 +--\n cli/src/core/state.ts                              |  14 +-\n cli/src/doctor.ts                                  |   2 +-\n cli/src/index.ts                                   |   6 +-\n cli/src/repl.ts                                    |  36 +---\n cli/src/sidecar.ts                                 |   4 +-\n cli/src/slash/catalog.ts                           |   2 +-\n cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts                |  43 +----\n cli/src/startup_trust.ts                           |  13 +-\n cli/src/tar_safety.ts                              |  10 +-\n cli/src/types.ts                                   |   2 +-\n cli/test/approval_policy.test.ts                   |  81 +--------\n cli/test/config.test.ts                            |  19 --\n cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts                    | 140 ---------------\n cli/test/helpers/repl_approval_driver.py           |  29 ---\n cli/test/helpers/startup_permission_driver.py      | 133 --------------\n cli/test/readonly_mode_escalation.test.ts          |  85 ---------\n cli/test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts                 | 199 ---------------------\n cli/test/repl_readonly_commands.test.ts            |  24 ---\n cli/test/repl_readonly_e2e.test.ts                 |  65 -------\n cli/test/repro_identity.test.ts                    |  39 +---\n cli/test/startup_trust_prompt.test.ts              |   4 -\n cli/test/state.test.ts                             |  22 +++\n cli/test/tar_safety.test.ts                        | 116 +-----------\n cli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts                   | 158 +++++++---------\n core/src/cst.rs                                    |  52 ++----\n docs/ARCHITECTURE.md                               |   2 +-\n docs/USER_MANUAL.md                                |  16 +-\n docs/releases/v1.0.0.md                            |  17 +-\n .../v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md    |  45 -----\n .../v1/DEFECT-CST-UNBOUNDED-20261024/README.md     |   7 +-\n .../README.md                                      |  55 ------\n .../v1/DEFECT-REPL-READONLY-20261024/README.md     |  64 -------\n .../v1/DEFECT-TAR-AMBIENT-ENV-20261024/README.md   |  58 ------\n .../v1/defect-latest-resume-corruption/README.md   |  30 ++++\n docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md                           |   8 +-\n docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md                        |   4 +-\n .../plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md       |  18 +-\n .../specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md       |  28 ++-\n quickstart.md                                      |   6 +-\n scripts/package-linux.sh                           |  13 +-\n scripts/repro-identity.mjs                         |  18 +-\n 45 files changed, 256 insertions(+), 1493 deletions(-)\ncli/src/core/state.ts\ncli/test/state.test.ts\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":39158}},"started_at_ms":1792899773825,"completed_at_ms":1792899773825}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T03:42:54.862Z","ordinal":322565,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17127-798d-7530-9ccd-0ef2c1c38ca5","call_id":"call_a7eb0ea9263d4327bae4de5e9d1162bf","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"# Corrupt latest-task resume fallback\n\n## Scope and identity\n\n- Source base: `4adc61ac98616c5e1dccaf6065e7f2332443d468`.\n- Reviewed source commit: `0123a15` (`fix(state): report corrupt task records when listing`).\n- Branch: `v1/defect-latest-resume-corruption`.\n\n## Defect and fix\n\nA safe fixture with a valid older task and malformed newer task showed `listTasks` returning only the older record. Both bare-latest resume paths select the first listed task, so this silent skip could resume the wrong older task or falsely report that no task exists.\n\n`listTasks` now quarantines malformed JSON and throws `CorruptStateError`, rejects non-object records through the same typed path, and propagates other I/O errors unchanged. The original corrupt bytes are preserved by rename. A subsequent listing can succeed explicitly after quarantine rather than silently hiding the failure. This implements the corruption reporting and quarantine requirements in REQ-PER-104 without changing either resume entry point.\n\n## Validation\n\nAll commands used isolated `HOME` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` directories; no live inference or credentials were used.\n\n- Direct reproduction before the fix: listing returned only `older`, with `newestCorruptRecordSkipped: true`.\n- Regression before the fix: expected `CorruptStateError` was not thrown.\n- `node scripts/run_tests.mjs test/state.test.ts test/durable_continuity.test.ts test/state_migration.test.ts` passed 59/59 after building the required Rust engine and CLI. An initial run without the fresh worktree's engine produced 12 setup failures and was not counted as a product result.\n- `make build` / CLI build and `tsc --noEmit` passed.\n- `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 exact-RC qualification deferrals. This is a source gate, not installed-RC qualification.\n- Full snapshot `make test` on `27415c8`: **failed**, with 1,660/1,663 passing. Failures were the already-fixed evaluator resource-order fixture (fixed separately at `36b702f`), the CI-only capped-storage prerequisite, and the intermittent upgrade download failure. The corrupt-resume focused regression remains passing; this is not a green full-suite result.\n\n## Independent review and integration\n\nAn independent reviewer returned **ACCEPT** for exact source commit `0123a15`, confirming typed corruption reporting, byte-preserving quarantine, unchanged non-parse error handling, and coverage of both bare-latest callers through their shared `listTasks` path. Review was read-only and did not rerun tests.\n\nNo push, pull-request integration, release qualification, or installed-candidate acceptance is claimed.\n .github/workflows/repro.yml                        |  18 +-\n cli/src/agent.ts                                   |  16 +-\n cli/src/config.ts                                  |   7 +-\n cli/src/core/approval_policy.ts                    |  21 +--\n cli/src/core/state.ts                              |  14 +-\n cli/src/doctor.ts                                  |   2 +-\n cli/src/index.ts                                   |   6 +-\n cli/src/repl.ts                                    |  36 +---\n cli/src/sidecar.ts                                 |   4 +-\n cli/src/slash/catalog.ts                           |   2 +-\n cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts                |  43 +----\n cli/src/startup_trust.ts                           |  13 +-\n cli/src/tar_safety.ts                              |  10 +-\n cli/src/types.ts                                   |   2 +-\n cli/test/approval_policy.test.ts                   |  81 +--------\n cli/test/config.test.ts                            |  19 --\n cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts                    | 140 ---------------\n cli/test/helpers/repl_approval_driver.py           |  29 ---\n cli/test/helpers/startup_permission_driver.py      | 133 --------------\n cli/test/readonly_mode_escalation.test.ts          |  85 ---------\n cli/test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts                 | 199 ---------------------\n cli/test/repl_readonly_commands.test.ts            |  24 ---\n cli/test/repl_readonly_e2e.test.ts                 |  65 -------\n cli/test/repro_identity.test.ts                    |  39 +---\n cli/test/startup_trust_prompt.test.ts              |   4 -\n cli/test/state.test.ts                             |  22 +++\n cli/test/tar_safety.test.ts                        | 116 +-----------\n cli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts                   | 158 +++++++---------\n core/src/cst.rs                                    |  52 ++----\n docs/ARCHITECTURE.md                               |   2 +-\n docs/USER_MANUAL.md                                |  16 +-\n docs/releases/v1.0.0.md                            |  17 +-\n .../v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md    |  45 -----\n .../v1/DEFECT-CST-UNBOUNDED-20261024/README.md     |   7 +-\n .../README.md                                      |  55 ------\n .../v1/DEFECT-REPL-READONLY-20261024/README.md     |  64 -------\n .../v1/DEFECT-TAR-AMBIENT-ENV-20261024/README.md   |  58 ------\n .../v1/defect-latest-resume-corruption/README.md   |  30 ++++\n docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md                           |   8 +-\n docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md                        |   4 +-\n .../plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md       |  18 +-\n .../specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md       |  28 ++-\n quickstart.md                                      |   6 +-\n scripts/package-linux.sh                           |  13 +-\n scripts/repro-identity.mjs                         |  18 +-\n 45 files changed, 256 insertions(+), 1493 deletions(-)\ncli/src/core/state.ts\ncli/test/state.test.ts\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a170f2-3e90-7ad2-8d66-c8179982613b","create_time":1792899774.8619542}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
