ts_open_the_review() {\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-phase3a-interaction-core.md:1542:        state.apply(ev(r#\"{\"v\":1,\"type\":\"approval.request\",\"id\":\"approval-1\",\"turn_id\":\"t1\",\"tool\":\"write_file\",\"subject\":\"x.txt\",\"preview\":\"{}\"}\"#));\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-phase3a-interaction-core.md:1563:    const APPROVAL: &str = r#\"{\"v\":1,\"type\":\"approval.request\",\"id\":\"approval-1\",\"turn_id\":\"t1\",\"tool\":\"write_file\",\"subject\":\"x.txt\",\"preview\":\"{}\",\"review\":{\"kind\":\"change\",\"path\":\"x.txt\",\"before\":null,\"after\":\"hi\\n\",\"created\":true,\"truncated\":false}}\"#;\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-phase3a-interaction-core.md:2461:    fn approval(review: &str) -> String {\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-phase3a-interaction-core.md:2463:            r#\"{{\"v\":1,\"type\":\"approval.request\",\"id\":\"approval-1\",\"turn_id\":\"t1\",\"tool\":\"edit_file\",\"subject\":\"src/x.txt\",\"preview\":\"{{}}\",\"review\":{review}}}\"#\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-phase3a-interaction-core.md:2610:/// Draws the approval modal; returns the rows available to the review and the largest useful scroll.\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-phase3a-interaction-core.md:2736:echo '{{\"v\":1,\"type\":\"approval.request\",\"id\":\"approval-1\",\"turn_id\":\"t1\",\"tool\":\"write_file\",\"subject\":\"x.txt\",\"preview\":\"{{}}\",\"review\":{{\"kind\":\"change\",\"path\":\"x.txt\",\"before\":null,\"after\":\"hi\",\"created\":true,\"truncated\":false}}}}'\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-phase3a-interaction-core.md:3090:2. **Approval with a fake sidecar:** a `sh` fake that emits an `approval.request` with a `change` review for `src/app.ts` (before `a\\nb\\n`, after `a\\nB\\n`) after the first prompt, then expects `approve` with `\"always\":false`. Expect \"Approval needed\", `-b` and `+B`; press `y`; expect \"✓ approved Edit src/app.ts\" and the banner.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:41:| 4 | Replace the `autoApprove` booleans with `HarnessConfig.approvalMode`. Default resolution per DEC-01 C: `--yes`/`NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE` → explicit, else trusted → auto, else review. CLI flags: `--approve`, `--yes`, `--read-only`, `--mode <m>`. | `config.ts:107`, `types.ts`, `index.ts:93,115`, `repl.ts:69,281,644-648`, `sidecar.ts:53,66,478,638,935` | 3 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:42:| 5 | Route verifier executions through the policy as `exec`. When not trusted and no prior approval exists, emit the approval with `kind: \"verifier\"`, the command, and the resolved script body (read `package.json` `scripts.test`, the Makefile `test:` recipe, `Cargo.toml`/`pytest.ini` presence). Cache the approval per (workspace, command, script digest) for the session. | `agent.ts:1602-1630,3432-3436,4034`; `tester.ts:113-136` (add `describeVerifier()`); `approval_review.ts` (new kind) | 3 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:51:| 14 | Docs: USER_MANUAL approvals/modes, quickstart \"review requested actions\", ARCHITECTURE §3 controls-and-limits, release notes entry. | docs | 1-13 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:30:- Model tool call -> `agent.dispatchToolCall` (agent.ts:3880). Vault `restore()` puts real secrets back into args for non-egress tools (agent.ts:3899-3906). Flight recorder logs args. The **approval gate runs only when an `onConfirm` handler exists and the capability is `mutating`** (agent.ts:3946-3947). The handler auto-approves unless `--approve` / `/mode review` is set: repl.ts:69,281; index.ts:93,115; sidecar.ts:935.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:49:| SEC-01 | S1 | every interactive/sidecar run | repl.ts:69,80,281; index.ts:93,115; sidecar.ts:935; tools.ts:755 | SOURCE. Default = autonomous: no approval for any tool, and no sandbox (`sandbox` is undefined unless `--sandbox`; config.ts:107). `run_command` executes arbitrary `bash -c` on the host as the user. The only guard is a substring denylist (SEC-02). | A prompt injection (file contents, fetched page, skill, MCP output) can run any host command without the operator seeing a prompt. The documented posture (ARCHITECTURE sec. 3) implies containment that does not exist by default. | BLOCKER for v1: either default to review mode for run_command/egress, or default to an enforced sandbox, and document the default plainly at startup. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:51:| SEC-03 | S2 | fetch_web (unapproved even in review mode) | tools.ts:52-111, 653-658 | RUNTIME (Repro R4). The SSRF guard is a hostname-string check with no DNS resolution and no redirect control (`fetch` follows redirects). `http://localtest.me:18731/` and `http://[::ffff:127.0.0.1]:18731/` both fetched a loopback-only server. Also not blocked: fd00::/8, fe80::/10, 100.64/10. The response body is read fully before truncation (tools.ts:662). | The model can reach loopback and LAN services (homelab gateway, admin UIs) and exfiltrate data in the URL query. There is no approval prompt, because fetch_web is non-mutating. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: resolve and pin the IP, check every redirect hop (`redirect: \"manual\"`), block all of v4/v6 private, ULA, link-local and mapped ranges, and cap the body size. Consider requiring approval for egress in review mode. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:130:| HIST-05 | S2 | Review mode / egress | cli/src/core/capabilities.ts (`fetch_web`, `search_web`, `browser_navigate`, `browser_click` → `\"mutating\": false`); cli/src/agent.ts:3946-3947 | SOURCE: approval gate is `onConfirm && isMutating`; network/browser tools are non-mutating so review mode never asks before egress. TOP_TIER T-12 still open; B1 \"every egress capability gated\" unmet | `--approve` users may assume outbound actions need approval; browser_click can act on external sites | Add an egress/exec effect class gated in review mode, or document explicitly |\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-sidecar-protocol.md:473:  | { type: \"approval.request\"; id: string; turn_id: string; tool: string; subject: string; preview: string }\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:52:| VER-01 | S2 | Any session on a cloned/untrusted repo, including `--approve` review mode | agent.ts:1602-1617 (baseline), 3432-3436 (oracle), 1630 (independence copy run); tester.ts:113-136 | SOURCE. Before the first file edit (agent.ts:4034, after the edit's own approval) and at every `task_completed`, Nexus runs `make test` / `npm test` / `cargo test` / `pytest` through `bridge.executeTool` directly. These run arbitrary repo-defined code with no approval prompt and no workspace-trust check (unlike MCP/plugins, workspace_trust.ts), and unsandboxed unless `--sandbox`. Review mode shows an approval for `edit_file` but never for the hidden repo script that follows. Builds on SEC-01; it is a separate path because it bypasses even review mode. | Cloning a hostile repo and asking for any edit runs its test script on the host without a prompt. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: gate discovered verifiers on workspace trust or a one-time approval of the exact command (shown with its script body), and run them sandboxed when one is available. Document this. |\ncli/test/sidecar.test.ts:227:  test(\"the approval preview redacts quoted secrets in arguments\", async () => {\ndocs/cloudflare/AGENT_NATIVE_COLLABORATION_RESEARCH.md:133:| Accepted-only integration | ADAPT | Exact candidate disposition and stale-ref checks are useful; avoid making a PR/approval queue canonical or hard-coding human reviewer roles. |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/trust_inference.md:34:### T-02 Subagents run every tool with no approval in review mode\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/trust_inference.md:107:### T-06 `run_tests.filter` is interpolated into a shell command and `run_tests` is not approval-gated: arbitrary command executio