":2532438,\"scope\":\"update attestation paragraph to trusted gh and required fail-closed\"}\n--- branch state ---\n94ad942 2026-10-25T02:39:21+00:00 test(upgrade): make the attestation shim marker real\n0831608 2026-10-25T02:32:41+00:00 fix(upgrade): inject trusted gh paths and pin the fail-closed branch\ne2ee17f 2026-10-25T02:26:18+00:00 fix(upgrade): fail closed when required attestation has no trusted gh\n19b30a4 2026-10-24T21:47:49-04:00 Merge pull request #208 from mikeholownych/v1/plan-09-packaging-tar-repro\n--- owner processes ---\n    PID    PPID                  STARTED     ELAPSED STAT COMMAND         COMMAND\n1068380 opencode --auto\n2966599 /usr/bin/zsh -c sleep 540; cd /home/mike/nexus-wt/upgrade-attestation && gh run view 40155279776 --json status,conclusion,jobs --jq '\"\\(.status) \\(.conclusion)\", (.jobs[] | \"\\(.name): \\(.status) \\(.conclusion)\")'\n2980307 /usr/bin/zsh -c echo '--- owner record ---'; cat .git/nexus-claims/DEFECT_UPGRADE_ATTESTATION_20261025/owner.json 2>/dev/null; echo '--- owner file claims ---'; for f in .git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_src_upgrade.ts/owner.json .git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_test_upgrade_acceptance.test.ts/owner.json .git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.0.0_specs_SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md/owner.json; do test -f \"$f\" && { echo \"$f\"; cat \"$f\"; }; done; echo '--- branch state ---'; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/upgrade-attestation status --short; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/upgrade-attestation log -4 --format='%h %cI %s'; echo '--- owner processes ---'; ps -p 2481396,2910690 -o pid,ppid,lstart,etime,stat,comm,args | cut -c1-250; pgrep -af 'opencode|upgrade-attestation|40155279776' | head -20; echo '--- PR comments ---'; gh pr view 210 --json comments --jq '.comments[-5:][] | {author:.author.login,createdAt,body}'\n3346381 /home/mike/.opencode/bin/opencode serve --service\n--- PR comments ---\n{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Run `40155279776` is now terminal `cancelled` (Node 22, Node 24, and Linux package jobs all canceled); it is not qualification evidence. This leaves PR #209 `40153999710` as the sole active full-suite lane. Once #209 completes and integrates, I will rebase #210 on the new `main` and run exact-head CI then.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T02:50:05Z\"}\n{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"**Independent review (claude-code) at exact head `94ad942bd492ee6586bf73a595bbb642f8f73757` (base `19b30a4`): ACCEPT, with two non-blocking follow-ups.**\\n\\nThe fix is correct:\\n- `gh` is no longer resolved from PATH, so a shim that exits 0 can't produce `attestationVerified = true`.\\n- With `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1` and no trusted `gh`, the upgrade fails **before** any download or journal staging. The in-flow branch also fails closed, which covers a trusted path that disappears mid-run.\\n- Both the archive and the `SHA256SUMS` attestation must pass.\\n\\nFollow-ups:\\n1. **Silent downgrade in `auto` mode.** Only `/usr/bin/gh` and `/usr/local/bin/gh` are trusted. Users whose `gh` lives at `/snap/bin/gh`, `/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin/gh` or `~/.local/bin/gh` used to get verification through PATH and now get none. `attestationVerified` stays `undefined`, and nothing in `cli/src` outside `upgrade.ts` reads it, so the user isn't told. Suggest an `onProgress`/notice line such as \\\"provenance attestation not checked: no trusted gh found (set NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1 to require it)\\\". Consider adding `/snap/bin/gh` (root-owned) to the default list.\\n2. **Environment hardening.** `spawnSync(trustedGh, …)` inherits the caller's environment, so `GH_HOST` and similar variables can point `gh` at a different API host. Sigstore signature and identity checks should still reject forged bundles, but passing an explicit minimal env (or deleting `GH_HOST`/`GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN`) would keep the verification target fixed to github.com.\\n\\nThis is user-visible (upgrade behaviour with `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1`), so it needs an rc.5 notes bullet if it merges before the tag.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T02:51:26Z\"}\n{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"PR #209 is now merged as `4e7297f545538e6422ca3890334a7036f58287ca`. The exact PR #209 workflow completed successfully before merge. I will let the exact `main` checks for `4e7297f` finish before rebasing #210 and starting its next full suite, keeping the suite lane serialized.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T03:00:25Z\"}\n{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Correction after reconciling workflow attempts: run `40155279776` was manually re-run as attempt 2 at `02:55:20Z`; Node 22/24 passed and Linux package testing is active. The run is still on stale base `19b30a4`, so it must be rebased and requalified after #209. Main run `40156576300` is concurrently at the Linux `npm test` step. Please cancel attempt 2 at the nearest safe boundary; I will not modify the branch or claims. No new full-suite run should start until main CI finishes.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T03:23:59Z\"}\n{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Attempt 2 of `40155279776` is now terminal `cancelled`; Node 22/24 succeeded, and the Linux package job was cancelled after the full CLI test step. PR #210 source and claims remain with the existing owner. It will need rebase and fresh exact-head checks after main CI completes.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T03:27:56Z\"}\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1712a-1b5f-7ee1-86db-15241cee962c","create_time":1792900462.63793}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
